dies. The fish have adapted to a variety of water parameters, as well as varying quantities of vegetation and light.<\\/span><\\/p><p><span data-preserver-spaces=\\\"true\\\">The bodies of zebra danios are thin and torpedo-shaped, with striking horizontal stripes running from head to tail. Zebra danios are lively, peaceful, and playful fish that do not cause problems when housed with appropriate species.<\\/span><\\/p><p><span data-preserver-spaces=\\\"true\\\">Zebra danios are tiny fish with zebra-like stripes on their bodies. The fish are silvery-gold in color with blue stripes in the wild. Males are more golden in hue than females, who are silvery-white.<\\/span><\\/p><p><span data-preserver-spaces=\\\"true\\\">The small, rounded fins and rounded tail of the common zebra danio.&nbsp;<\\/span><\\/p><p><span data-preserver-spaces=\\\"true\\\">The longfin zebra danio is a captive-bred aquarium fish with long, flowing fins and a long tail that is approximately three times the length of the fins and tail of the common zebra danio.<\\/span><\\/p><p><i><strong>I. Size<\\/strong><\\/i><\\/p><ul><li>Average Adult Size: 4 cm [1.5 inches]<\\/li><li>Maximum Adult Size: 1.5 inches<\\/li><li>Swimming Level: &nbsp;surface oriented<\\/li><\\/ul><p><i><span data-preserver-spaces=\\\"true\\\"><strong>II. You would love the fish because\\u2026<\\/strong><\\/span><\\/i><\\/p><p><span data-preserver-spaces=\\\"true\\\">Zebra danio \\u2013 Yellow is available in a variety of hues in the aquarium market, including silvery-green, pink, blue, and purple bodies. All zebra danios have white stripes with black borders and varied colored stripes \\u2014 such as blue \\u2014 between these stripes.<\\/span><\\/p><p><span data-preserver-spaces=\\\"true\\\">GloFish danios, neon counterparts of the zebra danio, are also available in a variety of colors, including Sunburst Orange, Galactic Purple, Starfire Red, Electric Green, and Cosmic Blue.<\\/span><\\/p><p><span data-preserver-spaces=\\\"true\\\">White-gold bodies and crimson eyes distinguish albino zebra danios. These fish are uncommon in the wild due to their bright coloring, but they are rather popular in the fish trade.<\\/span><\\/p><p><span data-preserver-spaces=\\\"true\\\">Zebra danios lose their coloring when stressed. Male and female zebra danios have brighter, bolder stripes when trying to impress their mates during the breeding season.<\\/span><\\/p><p><span data-preserver-spaces=\\\"true\\\">Zebra danios are active, playful fish that get on well with most fish in a community tank. The zebra danios swim quickly around the upper and middle sections of the tank, and are diurnal, meaning they\\u2019re more active during the day than at night.<\\/span><\\/p><p><span data-preserver-spaces=\\\"true\\\">As shoaling fish, zebra danios are bravest in groups of five or more. Getting the balance right is important \\u2014 too few zebra danios can cause stress, while too many zebra danios can cause hyperactivity and territorial behavior<\\/span><\\/p><p><i><strong>III. Is this fish species peaceful or hostile?<\\/strong><\\/i><\\/p><ul><li>Recommended: 6 and more<\\/li><li>Recommended Male\\/Female \\u2013 1:1<\\/li><li>Overall hostility: Peaceful<\\/li><li class=\\\"TrT0Xe\\\">Hostility towards own species: Peaceful<\\/li><li class=\\\"TrT0Xe\\\">Hostility towards other Species: Peaceful<\\/li><\\/ul><p>.However they nibble the fins of certain species. Angelfish, bettas, and guppies, as well as any fish with long-flowing fins, are potential prey for the energetic zebra danio.<\\/p><p><i><span data-preserver-spaces=\\\"true\\\"><strong>IV. Species compatibility<\\/strong><\\/span><\\/i><\\/p><p><span data-preserver-spaces=\\\"true\\\">Ember tetras<\\/span><\\/p><p><span data-preserver-spaces=\\\"true\\\">guppies<\\/span><\\/p><p><span data-preserver-spaces=\\\"true\\\">plecos,<\\/span><\\/p><p><span data-preserver-spaces=\\\"true\\\">Tetras<\\/span><\\/p><p><span data-preserver-spaces=\\\"true\\\">Zebra danios can pretty much live happily with most other types of fish, as long as they have plenty of space.<\\/span><\\/p><p><i><span data-preserver-spaces=\\\"true\\\"><strong>V. How to feed this species?<\\/strong><\\/span><\\/i><\\/p><p><span data-preserver-spaces=\\\"true\\\">The majority of danios are omnivorous and thrive on Aqueon Tropical Flakes, Color Flakes, Tropical Granules, and Shrimp Pellets. Frozen and live foods can also be given as treats or to aid in the induction of spawning. To achieve the greatest results, rotate their diet regularly and feed them only what they can take in under 2 minutes once or twice a day.<\\/span><\\/p><p><i>Recommended food<\\/i><\\/p><ul><li><p class=\\\"oxy-product-title product_title entry-title oxy-woo-element\\\" id=\\\"-product-title-53-111764\\\"><span data-preserver-spaces=\\\"true\\\">Aqueon Tropical Flakes<\\/span><\\/p><\\/li><li><p class=\\\"a-size-large a-spacing-none\\\" id=\\\"title\\\"><span class=\\\"a-size-large product-title-word-break\\\" id=\\\"productTitle\\\">WA Cichlid Vital Pellets<\\/span><\\/p><\\/li><\\/ul>\",\"content\":null,\"images\":[null,\"yellow-danio-min-300x300.jpg\"],\"product_type\":\"physical\",\"sale_type\":\"0\",\"sku\":null,\"price\":\"0\",\"sale_price\":null,\"start_date\":null,\"end_date\":null,\"cost_per_item\":\"0\",\"product_id\":null,\"barcode\":null,\"with_storehouse_management\":\"0\",\"quantity\":\"0\",\"allow_checkout_when_out_of_stock\":\"0\",\"stock_status\":\"in_stock\",\"weight\":\"0\",\"length\":\"0\",\"wide\":\"0\",\"height\":\"0\",\"is_added_attributes\":\"0\",\"has_product_options\":\"1\",\"related_products\":null,\"faq_schema_config\":\"[]\",\"seo_meta\":{\"seo_title\":null,\"seo_description\":null,\"index\":\"index\"},\"seo_meta_image\":null,\"layout\":null,\"is_popular\":\"0\",\"status\":\"published\",\"store_id\":null,\"is_featured\":\"0\",\"categories\":[\"33\"],\"brand_id\":null,\"image\":null,\"minimum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"maximum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"tag\":null,\"submitter\":\"save\"}', 'created', 'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/129.0.0.0 Safari/537.36', '2409:40e0:1b0:d388:c8c7:d8b9:da3c:acb8', 3, 419, 'YELLOW DANIO', 'info', '2024-10-24 16:38:10', '2024-10-24 16:38:10'),
(2339, 3, 'product', '{\"name\":\"GERMAN RAMIREZI\",\"model\":\"Botble\\\\Ecommerce\\\\Models\\\\Product\",\"slug\":\"german-ramirezi\",\"slug_id\":\"0\",\"is_slug_editable\":\"1\",\"description\":\"<div>German Blue Ram Cichlids are known throughout the aquarium hobby not only for their fantastically iridescent colors, but also for their charming and playful personalities.&nbsp; These little beauties feature yellow-green bodies dotted with stunning electric blue markings.&nbsp; These fish also have a dark stripe that runs vertically through their blood red eyes, which is sometimes accompanied by more vertical stripes across the body.&nbsp; Some specimens also have shimmering pink bellies.&nbsp; Their large, spiky fins are trimmed in red and black, which may make these friendly fish appear much more intimidating than they actually are.&nbsp; German Blue Ram Cichlids range from 1 to 2 inches in length.<\\/div><div>&nbsp;<\\/div><div>These cichlids hail from the river basins of Venezuela and Colombia, so their natural environment consists of warm and slow-moving waters.&nbsp; When keeping these fish, it is very important to maintain high quality of water in your tank and to keep it within the recommended water parameters.&nbsp; Like most fish, they do best in tanks that have live plants, rocks, or driftwood that provides them with cover.&nbsp; Under ideal conditions, German Blue Ram Cichlids may mate with each other and will try to lay their eggs in a secure hiding place, such as a cave.&nbsp; If no hiding places are provided, they may become aggressive toward other aquarium inhabitants in order to protect their eggs.<\\/div><div>&nbsp;<\\/div><p>Otherwise, German Blue Ram Cichlids are very peaceful and totally safe to keep with larger species of shrimp, snails, live plants, and other non-aggressive fish.&nbsp; We sell these fish in groups because they are known to do best in groups of 3 or more.&nbsp; These fish are omnivores, but they may be finicky about food upon being introduced to a new tank.&nbsp; It\'s a good idea to start them on foods like brine shrimp, bloodworms, and frozen or live mosquito larvae.&nbsp; Then you can gradually introduce them to easier foods like fish flakes or pellets.<\\/p><div><div><strong>What We Like About This Fish:<\\/strong><\\/div><div><ul><li>Remarkable and exotic colors and patterns<\\/li><li>Charming and playful personality<\\/li><li>Safe with plants<\\/li><li>Completely peaceful<\\/li><\\/ul><div><strong>&nbsp;<\\/strong><\\/div><div><strong>RECOMMENDED TANK PARAMETERS:&nbsp;<\\/strong><\\/div><div><ul><li>Temperature:&nbsp;&nbsp;78.8\\u00b0 - 86\\u00b0 F (26\\u00b0 - 30\\u00b0 C), although 82\\u00b0+ F (28\\u00b0+ C) is optimal<\\/li><li>pH:&nbsp; 5.5 - 7.0<\\/li><li>KH:&nbsp; 2 - 10 dKH<\\/li><li>Minimum tank size:&nbsp; 10 gallons per fish (30 gallons for 3)<\\/li><\\/ul><\\/div><\\/div><div><strong>&nbsp;<\\/strong><\\/div><div><strong>CARE GUIDELINES:<\\/strong><\\/div><div><ul><li>Diet:&nbsp; Omnivorous.&nbsp; More likely to accept brine shrimp, bloodworms, and frozen or live mosquito larvae, and most will eventually eat fish flakes or pellets as well.<\\/li><li>Social behavior:&nbsp; Peaceful, schooling\\/shoaling.<\\/li><li>Origin:&nbsp; Tank-bred, but indigenous to rivers in Venezuela and Columbia<\\/li><li>Average adult size:&nbsp; 1 - 2 inches (2.5 - 5 cm)<\\/li><li>Average purchase size:&nbsp; .75 - 1.5 inches (1.9 - 3.8 cm)<\\/li><\\/ul><\\/div><\\/div>\",\"content\":null,\"images\":[null,\"german-ramirosey-min-300x300.jpg\"],\"product_type\":\"physical\",\"sale_type\":\"0\",\"sku\":null,\"price\":\"0\",\"sale_price\":null,\"start_date\":null,\"end_date\":null,\"cost_per_item\":\"0\",\"product_id\":null,\"barcode\":null,\"with_storehouse_management\":\"0\",\"quantity\":\"0\",\"allow_checkout_when_out_of_stock\":\"0\",\"stock_status\":\"in_stock\",\"weight\":\"0\",\"length\":\"0\",\"wide\":\"0\",\"height\":\"0\",\"is_added_attributes\":\"0\",\"has_product_options\":\"1\",\"related_products\":null,\"faq_schema_config\":\"[]\",\"seo_meta\":{\"seo_title\":null,\"seo_description\":null,\"index\":\"index\"},\"seo_meta_image\":null,\"layout\":null,\"is_popular\":\"0\",\"status\":\"published\",\"store_id\":null,\"is_featured\":\"0\",\"categories\":[\"33\"],\"brand_id\":null,\"image\":null,\"minimum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"maximum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"tag\":null,\"submitter\":\"save\"}', 'created', 'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/129.0.0.0 Safari/537.36', '2409:40e0:1b0:d388:c8c7:d8b9:da3c:acb8', 3, 420, 'GERMAN RAMIREZI', 'info', '2024-10-24 16:42:08', '2024-10-24 16:42:08'),
(2340, 3, 'product', '{\"name\":\"THAISILK RAMIREZI\",\"model\":\"Botble\\\\Ecommerce\\\\Models\\\\Product\",\"slug\":\"thaisilk-ramirezi\",\"slug_id\":\"0\",\"is_slug_editable\":\"1\",\"description\":\"<p><strong>Appearance:<\\/strong>&nbsp;The Thai Silk Blue Ramirezi Fish is a breathtaking variant of the Ramirezi Dwarf Cichlid known for its vibrant and iridescent blue coloration. These fish have a sleek, elongated body with a shimmering, metallic blue hue that covers their entire body, giving them a striking and eye-catching appearance. Their large, expressive eyes and delicate finnage add to their overall allure, making them a favorite among aquarists.<\\/p><p>&nbsp;<\\/p><p><strong>Body Shape:<\\/strong>&nbsp;Thai Silk Blue Ramirezi Fish have a compact, oval-shaped body with a slightly pointed head. Their dorsal and anal fins are elongated and flow gracefully, enhancing their elegant look. The caudal fin is fan-shaped, adding to their visual appeal when they swim.<\\/p><p>&nbsp;<\\/p><p><strong>Temperament:<\\/strong>&nbsp;Known for their peaceful and calm demeanor, Thai Silk Blue Ramirezi Fish are excellent community fish. They get along well with other non-aggressive tank mates and can be kept in pairs or small groups. While they are generally peaceful, they may exhibit some territorial behavior, especially during breeding.<\\/p><p>&nbsp;<\\/p><p><strong>Tank Requirements:<\\/strong>&nbsp;To ensure the well-being of Thai Silk Blue Ramirezi Fish, an aquarium with a minimum capacity of 20 gallons is recommended. They thrive in well-maintained tanks with stable water conditions. The ideal water temperature for these fish ranges from 78\\u00b0F to 85\\u00b0F (25\\u00b0C to 29\\u00b0C), with a slightly acidic to neutral pH level (6.0 to 7.5). Providing plenty of plants, hiding spots, and soft substrate will help create a comfortable and enriching environment.<\\/p><p>&nbsp;<\\/p><p><strong>Diet:<\\/strong>&nbsp;Thai Silk Blue Ramirezi Fish are omnivorous and have a varied diet. A high-quality flake or pellet food should form the basis of their diet, supplemented with live or frozen foods such as brine shrimp, daphnia, and bloodworms. They also enjoy blanched vegetables like spinach and zucchini, which provide essential nutrients and variety.<\\/p><p>&nbsp;<\\/p><p><strong>Care:<\\/strong>&nbsp;Caring for Thai Silk Blue Ramirezi Fish involves maintaining pristine water quality through regular water changes and monitoring of water parameters. They are sensitive to poor water conditions, so consistent tank maintenance is crucial. Providing a balanced diet and a stress-free environment with plenty of hiding spots will ensure their health and happiness.<\\/p>\",\"content\":null,\"images\":[null,\"thaisilk-remirosey-300x300.jpg\"],\"product_type\":\"physical\",\"sale_type\":\"0\",\"sku\":null,\"price\":\"0\",\"sale_price\":null,\"start_date\":null,\"end_date\":null,\"cost_per_item\":\"0\",\"product_id\":null,\"barcode\":null,\"with_storehouse_management\":\"0\",\"quantity\":\"0\",\"allow_checkout_when_out_of_stock\":\"0\",\"stock_status\":\"in_stock\",\"weight\":\"0\",\"length\":\"0\",\"wide\":\"0\",\"height\":\"0\",\"is_added_attributes\":\"0\",\"has_product_options\":\"1\",\"related_products\":null,\"faq_schema_config\":\"[]\",\"seo_meta\":{\"seo_title\":null,\"seo_description\":null,\"index\":\"index\"},\"seo_meta_image\":null,\"layout\":null,\"is_popular\":\"0\",\"status\":\"published\",\"store_id\":null,\"is_featured\":\"0\",\"categories\":[\"33\"],\"brand_id\":null,\"image\":null,\"minimum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"maximum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"tag\":null,\"submitter\":\"save\"}', 'created', 'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/129.0.0.0 Safari/537.36', '2409:40e0:1b0:d388:c8c7:d8b9:da3c:acb8', 3, 421, 'THAISILK RAMIREZI', 'info', '2024-10-24 16:43:56', '2024-10-24 16:43:56');
