(2341, 3, 'product', '{\"name\":\"YELLOW SNAIL\",\"model\":\"Botble\\\\Ecommerce\\\\Models\\\\Product\",\"slug\":\"yellow-snail\",\"slug_id\":\"0\",\"is_slug_editable\":\"1\",\"description\":\"<p>Pomacea canaliculata, commonly known as the golden apple snail or the channeled apple snail, is a species of large freshwater snail with gills and an operculum, an aquatic gastropod mollusc in the family Ampullariidae, the apple snails.<\\/p>\",\"content\":null,\"images\":[null,\"yellow-snail-min-300x300.jpg\"],\"product_type\":\"physical\",\"sale_type\":\"0\",\"sku\":null,\"price\":\"0\",\"sale_price\":null,\"start_date\":null,\"end_date\":null,\"cost_per_item\":\"0\",\"product_id\":null,\"barcode\":null,\"with_storehouse_management\":\"0\",\"quantity\":\"0\",\"allow_checkout_when_out_of_stock\":\"0\",\"stock_status\":\"in_stock\",\"weight\":\"0\",\"length\":\"0\",\"wide\":\"0\",\"height\":\"0\",\"is_added_attributes\":\"0\",\"has_product_options\":\"1\",\"related_products\":null,\"faq_schema_config\":\"[]\",\"seo_meta\":{\"seo_title\":null,\"seo_description\":null,\"index\":\"index\"},\"seo_meta_image\":null,\"layout\":null,\"is_popular\":\"0\",\"status\":\"published\",\"store_id\":null,\"is_featured\":\"0\",\"categories\":[\"33\"],\"brand_id\":null,\"image\":null,\"minimum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"maximum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"tag\":null,\"submitter\":\"save\"}', 'created', 'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/129.0.0.0 Safari/537.36', '2409:40e0:1b0:d388:c8c7:d8b9:da3c:acb8', 3, 422, 'YELLOW SNAIL', 'info', '2024-10-24 16:46:29', '2024-10-24 16:46:29'),
(2342, 3, 'product', '{\"name\":\"BALLON MOLLY\",\"model\":\"Botble\\\\Ecommerce\\\\Models\\\\Product\",\"slug\":\"ballon-molly\",\"slug_id\":\"0\",\"is_slug_editable\":\"1\",\"description\":\"<p>The Baloon Molly (<i>Poecilia latipinna\\/velifera<\\/i>) is one of the most celebrated and beautiful livebearers in the aquarium world, boasting a variety of stunning colour forms.&nbsp; It is affectionately known and named for the large, impressive dorsal fin displayed by males.&nbsp; This species has been bred extensively for decades and has been developed into nearly endless colour varieties including black, green, dalmatian, golden, harlequin\\/calico, chocolate, albino, creamsicle, and many others.&nbsp; While this fish originated from fresh, brackish, and saltwater habitats in southern North America, the tank-raised specimens available are almost exclusively raised and thrive in alkaline freshwater.&nbsp; This fish could be considered a larger fish in the world of small community fish because it grows to an size of 4 to 5 inches as an adult.&nbsp; Despite its large size, it has a generally peaceful yet outgoing disposition, and it makes a great addition to many mixed-species aquariums.<\\/p><p>The Baloon Molly compatible with most other peaceful aquarium species in a relatively spacious &nbsp;aquarium.&nbsp; It is an omnivore, so it will potentially prey on smaller dwarf shrimp and their fry, but it is otherwise safe to keep with peaceful invertebrates as well.&nbsp; This fish is not a picky eater and it will accept a variety of high quality dry foods, but these should be supplemented with a variety of frozen foods as well.&nbsp; It will mostly occupy the middle and upper regions of the aquarium, and it does have the ability to jump out of the water, especially while in the early stages of acclimating to a new aquarium.&nbsp; As a result, a secure lid is highly recommended to ensure that this fish does not jump out of the tank.<\\/p><p>Plants are not absolutely necessary for the Baloon Molly, but they will certainly be appreciated.&nbsp; All hardy stem plants, rooted plants, Marimo Moss Balls, and mosses are generally safe to keep with this fish as long as the Baloon Molly well fed.&nbsp; The Baloon Molly is an excellent fish for beginners as well as experts!<\\/p><p><strong>What We Like About This Fish:<\\/strong><\\/p><ul><li>Hardy and adaptable<\\/li><li>Beautiful variety of colours<\\/li><li>Excellent for medium and larger planted aquariums<\\/li><li>Peaceful disposition<\\/li><\\/ul><p>&nbsp;<\\/p><p><strong>RECOMMENDED TANK PARAMETERS:&nbsp;<\\/strong><\\/p><ul><li><u>Temperature<\\/u>:&nbsp; 72\\u00b0 - 80\\u00b0 F (22\\u00b0 - 26.7\\u00b0 C)<\\/li><li><u>pH<\\/u>:&nbsp;&nbsp;7.0 - 8.5, though 7.5 or higher is ideal<\\/li><li><u>KH<\\/u>:&nbsp; 15 - 35 dKH<\\/li><li><u>Minimum tank size<\\/u>:&nbsp; 10 gallons for a single specimen, 30+ gallons for a group<\\/li><\\/ul><p>&nbsp;<\\/p><p><strong>CARE GUIDELINES:<\\/strong><\\/p><ul><li><u>Diet<\\/u>:&nbsp; High quality flake foods and frozen foods, especially those high in plant matter.<\\/li><li><u>Social behaviour<\\/u>:&nbsp; Shoaling, peaceful with most species.<\\/li><\\/ul>\",\"content\":null,\"images\":[null,\"ballon-molly-min-300x300.jpg\"],\"product_type\":\"physical\",\"sale_type\":\"0\",\"sku\":null,\"price\":\"0\",\"sale_price\":null,\"start_date\":null,\"end_date\":null,\"cost_per_item\":\"0\",\"product_id\":null,\"barcode\":null,\"with_storehouse_management\":\"0\",\"quantity\":\"0\",\"allow_checkout_when_out_of_stock\":\"0\",\"stock_status\":\"in_stock\",\"weight\":\"0\",\"length\":\"0\",\"wide\":\"0\",\"height\":\"0\",\"is_added_attributes\":\"0\",\"has_product_options\":\"1\",\"related_products\":null,\"faq_schema_config\":\"[]\",\"seo_meta\":{\"seo_title\":null,\"seo_description\":null,\"index\":\"index\"},\"seo_meta_image\":null,\"layout\":null,\"is_popular\":\"0\",\"status\":\"published\",\"store_id\":null,\"is_featured\":\"0\",\"categories\":[\"33\"],\"brand_id\":null,\"image\":null,\"minimum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"maximum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"tag\":null,\"submitter\":\"save\"}', 'created', 'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/129.0.0.0 Safari/537.36', '2409:40e0:1b0:d388:c8c7:d8b9:da3c:acb8', 3, 423, 'BALLON MOLLY', 'info', '2024-10-24 16:48:32', '2024-10-24 16:48:32'),
(2343, 3, 'product', '{\"name\":\"RED BALLON PLATY\",\"model\":\"Botble\\\\Ecommerce\\\\Models\\\\Product\",\"slug\":\"red-ballon-platy\",\"slug_id\":\"0\",\"is_slug_editable\":\"1\",\"description\":\"<p>The Balloon Red Platy Fish is a delightful addition to any freshwater aquarium, known for its vibrant red color and unique balloon-like body shape. This livebearer fish is not only visually appealing but also easy to care for, making it an ideal choice for both beginner and experienced aquarists.<\\/p><p><strong>Features:<\\/strong><\\/p><ul><li><strong>Scientific Name:<\\/strong>&nbsp;Xiphophorus maculatus<\\/li><li><strong>Common Names:<\\/strong>&nbsp;Balloon Platy, Red Balloon Platy<\\/li><li><strong>Size:<\\/strong>&nbsp;Up to 2.5 inches (6 cm)<\\/li><li><strong>Lifespan:<\\/strong>&nbsp;2-3 years<\\/li><li><strong>Temperament:<\\/strong>&nbsp;Peaceful<\\/li><li><strong>Diet:<\\/strong>&nbsp;Omnivorous<\\/li><li><strong>Optimal Water Conditions:<\\/strong><ul><li><strong>Temperature:<\\/strong>&nbsp;70-82\\u00b0F (21-28\\u00b0C)<\\/li><li><strong>pH Level:<\\/strong>&nbsp;7.0-8.2<\\/li><li><strong>Hardness:<\\/strong>&nbsp;10-25 dGH<\\/li><\\/ul><\\/li><\\/ul><p><strong>Care Instructions:<\\/strong><\\/p><ol><li><strong>Tank Setup:<\\/strong><ul><li><strong>Tank Size:<\\/strong>&nbsp;Minimum 10 gallons (40 liters) for a small group.<\\/li><li><strong>Substrate:<\\/strong>&nbsp;Fine gravel or sand.<\\/li><li><strong>Plants:<\\/strong>&nbsp;Include plenty of live plants such as Java Fern, Anubias, and Hornwort to provide hiding spots and enhance the natural environment.<\\/li><li><strong>Decorations:<\\/strong>&nbsp;Add driftwood and rocks for additional hiding places and to create a stimulating environment.<\\/li><\\/ul><\\/li><li><strong>Water Quality:<\\/strong><ul><li>Perform regular water changes (25-30% weekly) to maintain high water quality.<\\/li><li>Use a reliable filter to keep the water clean and well-oxygenated.<\\/li><\\/ul><\\/li><li><strong>Feeding:<\\/strong><ul><li>Feed a varied diet consisting of high-quality flake food, frozen or live brine shrimp, daphnia, and bloodworms.<\\/li><li>Supplement with vegetable matter such as blanched spinach or spirulina flakes.<\\/li><\\/ul><\\/li><li><strong>Compatibility:<\\/strong><ul><li>Balloon Red Platy Fish are peaceful and can be kept with other non-aggressive fish such as Tetras, Guppies, Mollies, and Corydoras.<\\/li><li>Avoid keeping them with large or aggressive fish that may harm them.<\\/li><\\/ul><\\/li><li><strong>Breeding:<\\/strong><ul><li>Balloon Platies are livebearers, meaning they give birth to free-swimming fry.<\\/li><li>Provide plenty of plants or breeding boxes to protect the fry from being eaten by adult fish.<\\/li><li>Separate pregnant females into a breeding tank to ensure the safety of the fry.<\\/li><\\/ul><\\/li><\\/ol><p>You will get a pair (Male and Female) of Balloon Red platy fish. The packet is fully sealed with pure oxygen and it is safe to travel long distances for 5-7 days. Buying Balloon Red platy fishes online from aquastore is totally safe, we are delivering you with 100% satisfaction.<\\/p>\",\"content\":null,\"images\":[null,\"red-ballon-platy-min-300x300.jpg\"],\"product_type\":\"physical\",\"sale_type\":\"0\",\"sku\":null,\"price\":\"0\",\"sale_price\":null,\"start_date\":null,\"end_date\":null,\"cost_per_item\":\"0\",\"product_id\":null,\"barcode\":null,\"with_storehouse_management\":\"0\",\"quantity\":\"0\",\"allow_checkout_when_out_of_stock\":\"0\",\"stock_status\":\"in_stock\",\"weight\":\"0\",\"length\":\"0\",\"wide\":\"0\",\"height\":\"0\",\"is_added_attributes\":\"0\",\"has_product_options\":\"1\",\"related_products\":null,\"faq_schema_config\":\"[]\",\"seo_meta\":{\"seo_title\":null,\"seo_description\":null,\"index\":\"index\"},\"seo_meta_image\":null,\"layout\":null,\"is_popular\":\"0\",\"status\":\"published\",\"store_id\":null,\"is_featured\":\"0\",\"categories\":[\"33\"],\"brand_id\":null,\"image\":null,\"minimum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"maximum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"tag\":null,\"submitter\":\"save\"}', 'created', 'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/129.0.0.0 Safari/537.36', '2409:40e0:1b0:d388:c8c7:d8b9:da3c:acb8', 3, 424, 'RED BALLON PLATY', 'info', '2024-10-24 16:50:29', '2024-10-24 16:50:29'),
(2344, 3, 'product', '{\"name\":\"RED TIGER BARB\",\"model\":\"Botble\\\\Ecommerce\\\\Models\\\\Product\",\"slug\":\"red-tiger-barb\",\"slug_id\":\"0\",\"is_slug_editable\":\"1\",\"description\":\"<p>GloFish fluorescent fish are wonderful fish that add brilliant color and excitement to any aquarium. They are born with their harmless, life-long color (they\\u2019re not dyed, injected, or painted). They require the same care as other freshwater tropical fish. The Long-Fin Barbs swim slower than normal barbs and can be a great addition to a community tank.<\\/p><p>Please note that this purchase includes only the fish, so you will need to have an aquarium available for them when they arrive.<\\/p><p><strong>Care Note:<\\/strong>&nbsp;GloFish Fin Barbs should be kept in groups of five or more, as they can become aggressive toward other fish when they are in smaller groups.<\\/p>\",\"content\":null,\"images\":[null,\"untitled-design-min-300x300.jpg\"],\"product_type\":\"physical\",\"sale_type\":\"0\",\"sku\":null,\"price\":\"0\",\"sale_price\":null,\"start_date\":null,\"end_date\":null,\"cost_per_item\":\"0\",\"product_id\":null,\"barcode\":null,\"with_storehouse_management\":\"0\",\"quantity\":\"0\",\"allow_checkout_when_out_of_stock\":\"0\",\"stock_status\":\"in_stock\",\"weight\":\"0\",\"length\":\"0\",\"wide\":\"0\",\"height\":\"0\",\"is_added_attributes\":\"0\",\"has_product_options\":\"1\",\"related_products\":null,\"faq_schema_config\":\"[]\",\"seo_meta\":{\"seo_title\":null,\"seo_description\":null,\"index\":\"index\"},\"seo_meta_image\":null,\"layout\":null,\"is_popular\":\"0\",\"status\":\"published\",\"store_id\":null,\"is_featured\":\"0\",\"categories\":[\"33\"],\"brand_id\":null,\"image\":null,\"minimum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"maximum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"tag\":null,\"submitter\":\"save\"}', 'created', 'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/129.0.0.0 Safari/537.36', '2409:40e0:1b0:d388:c8c7:d8b9:da3c:acb8', 3, 425, 'RED TIGER BARB', 'info', '2024-10-24 16:52:07', '2024-10-24 16:52:07'),
(2345, 3, 'product', '{\"name\":\"GREEN TIGER BARB\",\"model\":\"Botble\\\\Ecommerce\\\\Models\\\\Product\",\"slug\":\"green-tiger-barb\",\"slug_id\":\"0\",\"is_slug_editable\":\"1\",\"description\":\"<p>The Green Tiger Barb (<i>Pethia nigrofasciata<\\/i>) is a very&nbsp;peaceful species that is an excellent fish for the community planted aquarium. It is known for its small size and black striping, but is most desired for the brilliant ruby coloration that males develop during spawning behaviour. This fish is also rather versatile regarding water conditions.<\\/p><p>The Green Tiger Barb typically occupies the top and middle level of the water column, although it can often be seen swimming and feeding in the middle and bottom levels as well. It is safe with other peaceful, small fish. It may prey on smaller dwarf shrimp and their fry. Larger, peaceful invertebrates can make good tank mates. The Green Tiger Barb must be kept in groups of 6 or more, although larger groups are more ideal so that subdominant specimens are not bullied by dominant individuals during breeding behaviour. Its natural habitat is tropical rainforest areas that typically have clear water. It requires clean water to thrive and it will display optimal coloration and health in a planted aquarium with dark substrate.<\\/p><p>&nbsp;<\\/p><p>While not a picky eater, The Green Tiger Barb will thrive and remain very colourful on a varied diet of&nbsp;omnivorous foods. High-quality flake food, pellets, and live, frozen, or freeze-dried&nbsp;<i>Artemia<\\/i>, microworms,&nbsp;<i>Tubifex<\\/i>, and finely chopped bloodworms will all be readily accepted. Some vegetable matter, especially dry food high in vegetable content, is essential for optimal health and coloration.<\\/p><div class=\\\"rte sm:text-start text-start js-product-description\\\"><p>What We Like About This Fish:<\\/p><ul><li>Males develop beautiful green coloration with maturity<\\/li><li>Peaceful disposition with fish and peaceful invertebrates too large to be considered prey<\\/li><li>Very active and noticeable fish in any aquarium<\\/li><li>Ideal for planted aquariums<\\/li><\\/ul><p>&nbsp;<\\/p><p><strong>RECOMMENDED TANK PARAMETERS:<\\/strong><\\/p><p>&nbsp;<\\/p><ul><li>Temperature: 68 - 81\\u00b0 F (20\\u00b0-27\\u00b0 C)<\\/li><li>pH:&nbsp;5.5 - 7.5<\\/li><li>KH: 3 - 12 dKH<\\/li><li>Minimum Tank Size: 20 gallons for a group of 6 \\u2013 8<\\/li><\\/ul><p>&nbsp;<\\/p><p><strong>CARE INFORMATION:<\\/strong><\\/p><ul><li>Diet: Omnivore\\/Micropredator. Will easily accept high quality dry and frozen foods of appropriate size. Requires a varied diet, including vegetable matter, for optimal health and coloration.<\\/li><li><u>Social Behaviour:<\\/u>&nbsp;Peaceful, schooling\\/shoaling.<\\/li><\\/ul><\\/div><div class=\\\"dbtfy-back-in-stock-container\\\"><div class=\\\"dbtfy-back-in-stock\\\" data-product-id=\\\"4746472882265\\\">&nbsp;<\\/div><\\/div>\",\"content\":null,\"images\":[null,\"green-tiger-barb-min-300x300.jpg\"],\"product_type\":\"physical\",\"sale_type\":\"0\",\"sku\":null,\"price\":\"0\",\"sale_price\":null,\"start_date\":null,\"end_date\":null,\"cost_per_item\":\"0\",\"product_id\":null,\"barcode\":null,\"with_storehouse_management\":\"0\",\"quantity\":\"0\",\"allow_checkout_when_out_of_stock\":\"0\",\"stock_status\":\"in_stock\",\"weight\":\"0\",\"length\":\"0\",\"wide\":\"0\",\"height\":\"0\",\"is_added_attributes\":\"0\",\"has_product_options\":\"1\",\"related_products\":null,\"faq_schema_config\":\"[]\",\"seo_meta\":{\"seo_title\":null,\"seo_description\":null,\"index\":\"index\"},\"seo_meta_image\":null,\"layout\":null,\"is_popular\":\"0\",\"status\":\"published\",\"store_id\":null,\"is_featured\":\"0\",\"categories\":[\"33\"],\"brand_id\":null,\"image\":null,\"minimum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"maximum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"tag\":null,\"submitter\":\"save\"}', 'created', 'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/129.0.0.0 Safari/537.36', '2409:40e0:1b0:d388:c8c7:d8b9:da3c:acb8', 3, 426, 'GREEN TIGER BARB', 'info', '2024-10-24 16:58:28', '2024-10-24 16:58:28'),
(2346, 3, 'product', '{\"name\":\"CALICO ORANDA\",\"model\":\"Botble\\\\Ecommerce\\\\Models\\\\Product\",\"slug\":\"calico-oranda\",\"slug_id\":\"0\",\"is_slug_editable\":\"1\",\"description\":\"<p>The Calico Oranda features a festive, confetti-like blend of reds, oranges, white, and black. This coloration gives the Calico Oranda wonderful character and adds instant visual interest. The Calico Oranda closely resembles Veil Tail goldfish varieties in the shape and length of the tail, and is one of many varieties of what is collectively known as ornamental or fancy goldfish;&nbsp;<i>Carassius auratus auratus<\\/i>. Originally from parts of Asia, Japan, and China, Fancy Goldfish enjoy worldwide distribution due to controlled breeding programs.<\\/p><p>As a member of the carp family, the Calico Oranda is generally quite hardy. They will do well in 30 gallon aquariums or larger, as well as backyard garden ponds of 180 gallons or more. In addition to a fine gravel bottom or well-rounded river rocks, the Calico Oranda will appreciate hardy, cold water plants. Keep in mind that goldfish are diggers and will scatter the fine sand onto leaves, injuring thin and less hardy plants.<\\/p><p>There appears to be a definite courtship ritual when goldfish breed. Breeding often results in up to 1,000 eggs, with fry hatching in five to six days. They should be fed small pieces of live or prepared foods designed for egg-laying fish.<\\/p><p>Goldfish are omnivorous and will eat all types of dried and live foods. However, limit protein intake to 30% of the diet. Goldfish flake or pellet food will provide these fish with the proper nutrition.<\\/p>\",\"content\":null,\"images\":[null,\"calico-oranda-min-300x300.jpg\"],\"product_type\":\"physical\",\"sale_type\":\"0\",\"sku\":null,\"price\":\"0\",\"sale_price\":null,\"start_date\":null,\"end_date\":null,\"cost_per_item\":\"0\",\"product_id\":null,\"barcode\":null,\"with_storehouse_management\":\"0\",\"quantity\":\"0\",\"allow_checkout_when_out_of_stock\":\"0\",\"stock_status\":\"in_stock\",\"weight\":\"0\",\"length\":\"0\",\"wide\":\"0\",\"height\":\"0\",\"is_added_attributes\":\"0\",\"has_product_options\":\"1\",\"related_products\":null,\"faq_schema_config\":\"[]\",\"seo_meta\":{\"seo_title\":null,\"seo_description\":null,\"index\":\"index\"},\"seo_meta_image\":null,\"layout\":null,\"is_popular\":\"0\",\"status\":\"published\",\"store_id\":null,\"is_featured\":\"0\",\"categories\":[\"33\"],\"brand_id\":null,\"image\":null,\"minimum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"maximum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"tag\":null,\"submitter\":\"save\"}', 'created', 'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/129.0.0.0 Safari/537.36', '2409:40e0:1b0:d388:c8c7:d8b9:da3c:acb8', 3, 427, 'CALICO ORANDA', 'info', '2024-10-24 17:07:10', '2024-10-24 17:07:10'),
(2347, 3, 'product', '{\"name\":\"TROCOLOUR ORANDA\",\"model\":\"Botble\\\\Ecommerce\\\\Models\\\\Product\",\"slug\":\"trocolour-oranda\",\"slug_id\":\"0\",\"is_slug_editable\":\"1\",\"description\":\"<p>The Tri-Color Oranda is a distinctive and visually striking variety of the Oranda Goldfish (Carassius auratus). Oranda Goldfish are known for their unique appearance, characterized by a prominent growth on the head called a \\u201cwen\\u201d or \\u201chood,\\u201d which can cover their entire head. The Tri-Color Oranda, as the name suggests, is recognized for its tri-coloration and impressive wen growth. Here are some key features and information about the Tri-Color Oranda:<\\/p><p>Tri-Color Orandas have a tri-colored pattern, typically consisting of red, white, and black markings. The red coloration can appear on the body, while the white and black colors are often on the fins, tail, and head. The exact distribution of colors may vary among individual fish.<\\/p><p>One of the standout features of the Tri-Color Oranda is the growth of the wen or hood. The wen covers the head and can develop into a substantial and fleshy mass, giving the fish a unique and charming appearance. The wen\\u2019s coloration may vary but often matches the body color.<\\/p><p>Oranda Goldfish, including the Tri-Color variety, can grow relatively large. They can reach lengths of up to 8 to 12 inches (20 to 30 centimeters) or even more in well-maintained aquariums or ponds.<\\/p><p>Tri-Color Orandas require a spacious aquarium with ample room to swim, as well as good water quality. They are hardy fish, but their wen growth requires careful attention. The wen is sensitive and prone to injury, so it\\u2019s essential to maintain excellent water conditions to prevent infections or injuries.<\\/p><p>Provide your Tri-Color Oranda with a well-planted aquarium with hiding places and open swimming areas. Ensure that the tank has a suitable filtration system to maintain water quality.<\\/p><p>Oranda Goldfish are generally peaceful and sociable. They are known for their curious and friendly nature, making them enjoyable to observe in a community tank.<\\/p><p>Tri-Color Orandas are beloved by fish enthusiasts for their unique and eye-catching appearance. Their striking coloration, distinctive wen growth, and friendly disposition make them a popular choice for aquarium keepers who are looking to add a touch of elegance to their aquatic displays. Proper care and attention to water quality are essential to ensure the health and well-being of these remarkable fish.<\\/p><p><span data-preserver-spaces=\\\"true\\\"><strong>III. Is this fish species peaceful or hostile?<\\/strong><\\/span><\\/p><p><span data-preserver-spaces=\\\"true\\\">Extremely peaceful fish.<\\/span><\\/p><p><i><span data-preserver-spaces=\\\"true\\\"><strong>IV. Species compatibility<\\/strong><\\/span><\\/i><\\/p><p>When keeping Tri-Color Orandas, choose tank mates that are peaceful and won\\u2019t nip at their long fins or disturb their wen growth. Other goldfish varieties, such as other Orandas or fancy goldfish, can make suitable companions.<\\/p><p>Avoid keeping them with aggressive or fin-nipping fish, as their delicate fins can be easily damaged.<\\/p><p><i><span data-preserver-spaces=\\\"true\\\"><strong>V. How to feed this species?<\\/strong><\\/span><\\/i><\\/p><p>These goldfish are omnivorous and enjoy a varied diet. You can feed them high-quality pellets or flakes formulated for goldfish, as well as occasional treats such as live or frozen foods like brine shrimp, bloodworms, and vegetables like peas.<\\/p>\",\"content\":null,\"images\":[null,\"trocolour-oranda-min-300x300.jpg\"],\"product_type\":\"physical\",\"sale_type\":\"0\",\"sku\":null,\"price\":\"0\",\"sale_price\":null,\"start_date\":null,\"end_date\":null,\"cost_per_item\":\"0\",\"product_id\":null,\"barcode\":null,\"with_storehouse_management\":\"0\",\"quantity\":\"0\",\"allow_checkout_when_out_of_stock\":\"0\",\"stock_status\":\"in_stock\",\"weight\":\"0\",\"length\":\"0\",\"wide\":\"0\",\"height\":\"0\",\"is_added_attributes\":\"0\",\"has_product_options\":\"1\",\"related_products\":null,\"faq_schema_config\":\"[]\",\"seo_meta\":{\"seo_title\":null,\"seo_description\":null,\"index\":\"index\"},\"seo_meta_image\":null,\"layout\":null,\"is_popular\":\"0\",\"status\":\"published\",\"store_id\":null,\"is_featured\":\"0\",\"categories\":[\"33\"],\"brand_id\":null,\"image\":null,\"minimum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"maximum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"tag\":null,\"submitter\":\"save\"}', 'created', 'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/129.0.0.0 Safari/537.36', '2409:40e0:1b0:d388:c8c7:d8b9:da3c:acb8', 3, 428, 'TROCOLOUR ORANDA', 'info', '2024-10-24 17:15:35', '2024-10-24 17:15:35'),
(2348, 3, 'product', '{\"name\":\"ASSAMISE BADIS\",\"model\":\"Botble\\\\Ecommerce\\\\Models\\\\Product\",\"slug\":\"assamise-badis\",\"slug_id\":\"0\",\"is_slug_editable\":\"1\",\"description\":\"<p class=\\\"\\\">The Badis assamensis, commonly known as the Assam Badis, is a captivating freshwater fish species native to parts of India and Bangladesh. Specifically found in the Brahmaputra River basin, they inhabit slow-moving waters, including streams and swamps.<\\/p><p class=\\\"\\\">Physically, the Assam Badis is characterized by its elongated body and vibrant coloration. Males typically display more intense colors, featuring shades of red, blue, and green, especially during courtship and spawning. They typically grow to a size of about 2 to 3 inches (5-7.5 cm).<\\/p><p class=\\\"\\\">In their natural habitat, Assam Badis thrive in densely planted aquariums with areas for swimming and hiding spots provided by plants and small caves. They prefer soft to slightly hard water conditions, and maintaining a stable and clean environment with proper filtration contributes to their overall well-being.<\\/p><p class=\\\"\\\">Known for their territorial behavior, Assam Badis are best kept in a species-only tank or with very small, peaceful tankmates. They are not suitable for community aquariums due to their territorial nature. A well-balanced diet, including live or frozen foods like small insects and microorganisms, meets their nutritional needs.<\\/p><p class=\\\"\\\">Maintaining water conditions within the range of 72-79\\u00b0F (22-26\\u00b0C) and a pH level between 6.0 to 7.5 is advisable. Regular water changes and proper filtration contribute to their health and vitality.<\\/p><p class=\\\"\\\">Breeding Assam Badis in captivity is possible but can be challenging due to their specific requirements. Creating a breeding tank with soft, acidic water and providing hiding spots with dense vegetation encourage successful spawning. Males intensify their colors during courtship.<\\/p><p class=\\\"\\\">In summary, the Assam Badis is a captivating and colorful addition to aquariums, appreciated for its vibrant hues and unique behaviors. Recreating their natural habitat from the Brahmaputra River basin and adhering to proper care conditions contribute to their well-being in captivity.<\\/p>\",\"content\":null,\"images\":[null,\"assamise-badis-min-300x300.jpg\"],\"product_type\":\"physical\",\"sale_type\":\"0\",\"sku\":null,\"price\":\"0\",\"sale_price\":null,\"start_date\":null,\"end_date\":null,\"cost_per_item\":\"0\",\"product_id\":null,\"barcode\":null,\"with_storehouse_management\":\"0\",\"quantity\":\"0\",\"allow_checkout_when_out_of_stock\":\"0\",\"stock_status\":\"in_stock\",\"weight\":\"0\",\"length\":\"0\",\"wide\":\"0\",\"height\":\"0\",\"is_added_attributes\":\"0\",\"has_product_options\":\"1\",\"related_products\":null,\"faq_schema_config\":\"[]\",\"seo_meta\":{\"seo_title\":null,\"seo_description\":null,\"index\":\"index\"},\"seo_meta_image\":null,\"layout\":null,\"is_popular\":\"0\",\"status\":\"published\",\"store_id\":null,\"is_featured\":\"0\",\"categories\":[\"34\"],\"brand_id\":null,\"image\":null,\"minimum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"maximum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"tag\":null,\"submitter\":\"save\"}', 'created', 'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/129.0.0.0 Safari/537.36', '2409:40e0:1b0:d388:c8c7:d8b9:da3c:acb8', 3, 429, 'ASSAMISE BADIS', 'info', '2024-10-24 17:17:51', '2024-10-24 17:17:51'),
(2349, 3, 'product', '{\"name\":\"NBLUE BADIS\",\"model\":\"Botble\\\\Ecommerce\\\\Models\\\\Product\",\"slug\":\"nblue-badis\",\"slug_id\":\"0\",\"is_slug_editable\":\"1\",\"description\":\"<p>The Blue Badis (<i>Badis badis<\\/i>), also commonly known as the Chameleon Fish, is a nano-sized member of the perch family indigenous to the Ganges River system of India.&nbsp; The \\u201cchameleon fish\\u201d name refers to the unique ability of this fish, particularly adult males, to dramatically change colors during breeding and territorial behavior.&nbsp; The initial color in juveniles is mottled brown, tan, and red vertical striping.&nbsp; As the Blue Badis reaches maturity, males will often display more intense red and iridescent blue coloration on its fins.<\\/p><p>The Blue Badis is a micropredator requiring a diet of meaty foods.&nbsp; Many specimens will not accept dry flake and pellet foods, so live and frozen foods should be regularly offered.&nbsp; In nature, this fish eats various small worms, small crustaceans, insects and insect larvae.&nbsp; In the aquarium, glassworms, enriched Artemia, and Daphnia will make an excellent staple diet.&nbsp; Bloodworms and Tubifex worms can be fed on occasion, but should not be fed as a regular diet since they can lead to obesity problems with this species.<\\/p><p>The aquarium of the Blue Badis should include plenty of rockwork and driftwood.&nbsp; This fish is a cave spawner, so it is also a good idea to shape some d\\u00e9cor into cave-like structures.&nbsp; During spawning, the male will guard the eggs and newly-hatched fry, but any adults should be removed thereafter if you want to avoid cannibalism of the fry by the parents.<\\/p><p>The Blue Badis will thrive in a planted aquarium with relatively mild to moderate water flow and is generally peaceful with other species of fish.&nbsp; Though it is a predator, its small size makes it safe with all but the very tiniest fish.&nbsp; It can be housed with some invertebrates such as snails and larger shrimp, but it may eat most&nbsp;<i>Caridina<\\/i>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<i>Neocaridina<\\/i>&nbsp;shrimp. It may hybridize with other Badis species, although it is unlikely to do so with the Scarlet Badis (<i>Dario dario<\\/i>) due to the size difference.<\\/p><p><strong>What We Like About This Fish:<\\/strong><\\/p><ul><li>Iridescent blue and red coloration in males during courtship and territorial behavior<\\/li><li>Peaceful disposition with most fish<\\/li><li>Hardy and adaptable<\\/li><li>Very active in middle and lower levels of the aquarium<\\/li><\\/ul><p><strong>&nbsp;<\\/strong><\\/p><p><strong>RECOMMENDED TANK PARAMETERS:<\\/strong><\\/p><ul><li><u>Temperature<\\/u>:&nbsp; 59\\u00b0 - 77\\u00b0 F (15\\u00b0 - 25\\u00b0 C)<\\/li><li><u>pH<\\/u>:&nbsp; 6.0 - 7.5<\\/li><li><u>KH<\\/u>:&nbsp; 10 - 15 dKH<\\/li><li><u>Minimum tank size<\\/u>:&nbsp; 20 gallons<\\/li><\\/ul><p><strong>&nbsp;<\\/strong><\\/p><p><strong>CARE GUIDELINES:&nbsp;<\\/strong><\\/p><ul><li><u>Diet<\\/u>:&nbsp; Meaty foods, especially frozen foods such as Daphnia and Artemia, Bloodworms and Tubifex worms on occasion only. &nbsp;Dry foods will often be ignored.<\\/li><li><u>Social behavior<\\/u>:&nbsp; Mostly peaceful, loosely schooling\\/shoaling in small groups. Adult males can be territorial with other males.<\\/li><\\/ul>\",\"content\":null,\"images\":[null,\"nblue-badis-min-300x300.jpg\"],\"product_type\":\"physical\",\"sale_type\":\"0\",\"sku\":null,\"price\":\"0\",\"sale_price\":null,\"start_date\":null,\"end_date\":null,\"cost_per_item\":\"0\",\"product_id\":null,\"barcode\":null,\"with_storehouse_management\":\"0\",\"quantity\":\"0\",\"allow_checkout_when_out_of_stock\":\"0\",\"stock_status\":\"in_stock\",\"weight\":\"0\",\"length\":\"0\",\"wide\":\"0\",\"height\":\"0\",\"is_added_attributes\":\"0\",\"has_product_options\":\"1\",\"related_products\":null,\"faq_schema_config\":\"[]\",\"seo_meta\":{\"seo_title\":null,\"seo_description\":null,\"index\":\"index\"},\"seo_meta_image\":null,\"layout\":null,\"is_popular\":\"0\",\"status\":\"published\",\"store_id\":null,\"is_featured\":\"0\",\"categories\":[\"34\"],\"brand_id\":null,\"image\":null,\"minimum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"maximum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"tag\":null,\"submitter\":\"save\"}', 'created', 'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/129.0.0.0 Safari/537.36', '2409:40e0:1b0:d388:c8c7:d8b9:da3c:acb8', 3, 430, 'NBLUE BADIS', 'info', '2024-10-24 17:27:07', '2024-10-24 17:27:07'),
(2350, 3, 'product', '{\"name\":\"RED BADIS\",\"model\":\"Botble\\\\Ecommerce\\\\Models\\\\Product\",\"slug\":\"red-badis\",\"slug_id\":\"0\",\"is_slug_editable\":\"1\",\"description\":\"<p>Red Badis: One of our favorite nano fishes that you may find is the scarlet badi, a very popular freshwater fish.<\\/p><p>Red Badis are quite entertaining to watch because of their beauty, degree of energy, and behaviour. Additionally, they don\\u2019t need much effort to be healthy!<\\/p><p>Having said that, there are several essential aspects of caring for Scarlet Badis that you should be aware of if you want them to prosper and lead a full, stress-free existence.<\\/p><p>These tiny fish will do well in constrained situations. The males will grow to a length of 0.8 inches. The females are much more little, growing to only 0.5 inches in length.<\\/p><p>They are known as micro fish because they may be kept in tanks as tiny as 10 gallons.<\\/p><p>The bodies of the males are alternately striped in red and turquoise. Despite their diminutive size, they are really attractive.<\\/p><p>It is simple to see why Scarlet Badis are also referred to as Gem Badis. Although the ladies are less vibrant, they are nonetheless stunning.<\\/p><p>Additionally, the female draws attention to the male\\u2019s vivid colours when they are swimming together.<\\/p><p><i><strong>II. You would love the fish because\\u2026<\\/strong><\\/i><\\/p><p>Red Badis is a little fish called the Scarlet Badis.<\\/p><p>Males are considerably smaller than females and rarely grow to a length of 1 inch.<\\/p><p>Additionally, the hues of men and females differ. Sexual dimorphism is the term for this distinction.<\\/p><p>Male adults are vivid red or rusty orange in colour. They have seven bands that extend from their flanks to their fins.<\\/p><p>Eight lines of silvery blue alternate with these stripes, and both lines extend along the fins.<\\/p><p>The ventral fins are typically bluish-white in hue with a white outline.<\\/p><p>One of the tiniest fish species is the scarlet badi, which belongs to the percoid superfamily, which also includes well-known species like the yellow perch<\\/p><p>(a gamefish native to North America) and the marine basslets.<\\/p><p>Small streams in India with modest water movement are their natural habitat. Specifically, the Brahmaputra River\\u2019s tributaries and tributaries.<\\/p><p>The Scarlet Badis may also be referred to as Badis bengalensis, an earlier name that has since been supplanted by Dario dario, depending on how ancient your sources are.<\\/p><p>It was previously placed in the genus alongside the larger, more similar-looking Blue Badis, Badis badis.<\\/p><p><i><strong>III. Is this fish species peaceful or hostile?<\\/strong><\\/i><\\/p><p>Is a peaceful fish.<\\/p><p><i><strong>IV. Species compatibility<\\/strong><\\/i><\\/p><p>Pearl danios (Peaceful temperament and small)&nbsp;Neon &amp; Small Tetras (Peaceful temperament and small)<\\/p><p><i><strong>V. How to feed this species?<\\/strong><\\/i><\\/p><p>Include fresh vegetables like spinach, cooked peas, and lettuce in a varied diet for optimal health.When preparing fish for breeding, live foods like blackworms, brine shrimp, and glass worms should be used as treats.<\\/p>\",\"content\":null,\"images\":[null,\"red-badis-min-300x300.jpg\"],\"product_type\":\"physical\",\"sale_type\":\"0\",\"sku\":null,\"price\":\"0\",\"sale_price\":null,\"start_date\":null,\"end_date\":null,\"cost_per_item\":\"0\",\"product_id\":null,\"barcode\":null,\"with_storehouse_management\":\"0\",\"quantity\":\"0\",\"allow_checkout_when_out_of_stock\":\"0\",\"stock_status\":\"in_stock\",\"weight\":\"0\",\"length\":\"0\",\"wide\":\"0\",\"height\":\"0\",\"is_added_attributes\":\"0\",\"has_product_options\":\"1\",\"related_products\":null,\"faq_schema_config\":\"[]\",\"seo_meta\":{\"seo_title\":null,\"seo_description\":null,\"index\":\"index\"},\"seo_meta_image\":null,\"layout\":null,\"is_popular\":\"0\",\"status\":\"published\",\"store_id\":null,\"is_featured\":\"0\",\"categories\":[\"34\"],\"brand_id\":null,\"image\":null,\"minimum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"maximum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"tag\":null,\"submitter\":\"save\"}', 'created', 'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/129.0.0.0 Safari/537.36', '2409:40e0:1b0:d388:c8c7:d8b9:da3c:acb8', 3, 431, 'RED BADIS', 'info', '2024-10-24 17:40:27', '2024-10-24 17:40:27'),
(2351, 3, 'product', '{\"name\":\"GREEN SHRIMP\",\"model\":\"Botble\\\\Ecommerce\\\\Models\\\\Product\",\"slug\":\"green-shrimp\",\"slug_id\":\"0\",\"is_slug_editable\":\"1\",\"description\":\"<p><strong>Overview:&nbsp;<\\/strong>Green Shrimp could be a wonderful addition to your tank, especially when you want to make it colorful and bring vividness with different aquarium species. While fish are dominant in the tank, green shrimps make things look more attractive. The scientific name of green shrimp is Caridina cf. Babaulti and is believed to be originated in India and Malaysia. With the undemanding nature and greenish look, green shrimp is always in high demand. It is easy to care for and maintain until the water parameters are under control. This shrimp remain happy and healthy and make the tank look beautiful.<\\/p><p><strong>Distribution and Habitat<\\/strong>: Green Shrimps are freshwater shrimps and have wider adaptability. They can live in freshwater tanks with no hassles. Although called green shrimps, they have a tinge of orange and neon green color, making them look more vibrant. When introduced in the tank, green shrimps flash eye-catching contrast color with the dark-colored aquarium substrate and make it look more appealing. The best part is green shrimps have an extremely adaptable nature making them easy to maintain and care for in the tanks. Remember not to put shrimps with aggressive fish like angelfish or aggressive barbs that can kill and eat them in anger.<\\/p><p><strong>Temperature:&nbsp;<\\/strong>24 to 28 degrees Celsius is the most appropriate temperature range for the Green Shrimps. When provided the right temperature, the shrimps live happily and healthily in the freshwater tank.<\\/p><p><strong>Water conditions<\\/strong>: Green shrimps are peculiar about certain water conditions, among which water pH is one. The right pH level range is from 6.8 to 7.8, wherein the water types should be- kH 0-10; gH 4-14; and TDS 80-200. Under the right water conditions, shrimps can grow up to the size of about 1.4 inches in length. However, the most common maximum length is about 1 inch.<\\/p><p><strong>Feeding<\\/strong>: Green Shrimps are omnivorous in nature, which means they can feed on a variety of food, both plants, and greens. They are also a great algae eater. So, even if you are not providing them anything or enough to eat, they will just start munching on the aquarium algae and fill their stomach. Or else, they can also feed on anything that you feed your fish- blanched vegetables, egg yolk, or any other fish food. In general, shrimps eat very little; for instance, one fish flake the size of a dime every day is enough for ten or more shrimp.<\\/p><p><strong>Breeding<\\/strong>: Green shrimps breed easily and lay quite a few eggs around the leaves or on the substrate. Generally, the eggs of green shrimps are smaller than other shrimps, which is why the baby shrimps are also smaller in size and a bit hard to raise. Although these shrimp breed in large numbers, they are not the easiest to breed!<\\/p><p><strong>Do you know<\\/strong>: Green shrimps are algae eater and therefore work as a cleaning crew of the tank. They can easily manage the waste and control algae growth.<\\/p>\",\"content\":null,\"images\":[null,\"green-shrimp-min-300x300.jpg\"],\"product_type\":\"physical\",\"sale_type\":\"0\",\"sku\":null,\"price\":\"0\",\"sale_price\":null,\"start_date\":null,\"end_date\":null,\"cost_per_item\":\"0\",\"product_id\":null,\"barcode\":null,\"with_storehouse_management\":\"0\",\"quantity\":\"0\",\"allow_checkout_when_out_of_stock\":\"0\",\"stock_status\":\"in_stock\",\"weight\":\"0\",\"length\":\"0\",\"wide\":\"0\",\"height\":\"0\",\"is_added_attributes\":\"0\",\"has_product_options\":\"1\",\"related_products\":null,\"faq_schema_config\":\"[]\",\"seo_meta\":{\"seo_title\":null,\"seo_description\":null,\"index\":\"index\"},\"seo_meta_image\":null,\"layout\":null,\"is_popular\":\"0\",\"status\":\"published\",\"store_id\":null,\"is_featured\":\"0\",\"categories\":[\"34\"],\"brand_id\":null,\"image\":null,\"minimum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"maximum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"tag\":null,\"submitter\":\"save\"}', 'created', 'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/129.0.0.0 Safari/537.36', '2409:40e0:1b0:d388:c8c7:d8b9:da3c:acb8', 3, 432, 'GREEN SHRIMP', 'info', '2024-10-24 17:41:38', '2024-10-24 17:41:38'),
(2352, 3, 'product', '{\"name\":\"YELLOW SHRIMP\",\"model\":\"Botble\\\\Ecommerce\\\\Models\\\\Product\",\"slug\":\"yellow-shrimp\",\"slug_id\":\"0\",\"is_slug_editable\":\"1\",\"description\":\"<p>Golden Back Yellow shrimp are a higher grade of Neon Yellow Shrimp that feature a brilliant, neon yellow \\\"racing\\\" stripe down the back.&nbsp; Their gorgeous coloration draws the eye directly to these dynamic little shrimp and adds charm and cheer to any aquarium set-up.&nbsp; These shrimp look great, clean your tank, and are a blast to watch!&nbsp; They are very active and breed quickly.<\\/p><p>We generally ship young adult shrimp that are already of breeding age.&nbsp; Golden Back Yellow Shrimp are fairly adaptable creatures that can live in almost any freshwater aquarium with the right water parameters.&nbsp; Younger shrimp may have not reached their full potential yet and will grow into a bright yellow color as long as they are comfortable in the tank.&nbsp; Lower intensity lighting and dark substrate also helps them achieve the most vibrant yellows.<\\/p><div><p><strong>What We Like About This Shrimp:<\\/strong><\\/p><ul><li>Bright and cheery yellow coloration with iridescent stripe down the back<\\/li><li>Completely peaceful with all non-aggressive tankmates<\\/li><li>Safe with all plants<\\/li><li>Excellent scavenger<\\/li><\\/ul><\\/div><div>&nbsp;<\\/div><div>&nbsp;<\\/div><div><strong>RECOMMENDED TANK PARAMETERS:<\\/strong><\\/div><div><ul><li>Temperature: 64\\u00b0 - 84\\u00b0 F (17.8\\u00b0 - 28.8\\u00b0 C)<\\/li><li>pH: 6.8 - 7.5<\\/li><li>KH: 0 - 10 dKH<\\/li><li>Minimum tank size: 2 gallons<\\/li><\\/ul><\\/div><div>&nbsp;<\\/div><div>&nbsp;<\\/div><div><strong>CARE GUIDELINES:<\\/strong><\\/div><div><ul><li>Diet: Scavenger that feeds continually.&nbsp; Requires very little feeding in a well-established aquarium containing algae, biofilm, or decaying plant matter.&nbsp; In less mature aquariums, high quality dry foods with high plant content can be fed multiple times daily.<\\/li><li>Social behavior: Peaceful.&nbsp; A small group can continually replenish and grow its population<\\/li><li>Origin: Tank-bred , but wild populations indigenous to Taiwan<\\/li><li>Average adult size: 1 - 1.5 inches (2.5 - 3.8 cm)<\\/li><li>Average purchase size: 1\\/2 - 3\\/4 inch (1.3 - 1.9 cm)<\\/li><\\/ul><\\/div>\",\"content\":null,\"images\":[null,\"yellow-shrimp-min-300x300.jpg\"],\"product_type\":\"physical\",\"sale_type\":\"0\",\"sku\":null,\"price\":\"0\",\"sale_price\":null,\"start_date\":null,\"end_date\":null,\"cost_per_item\":\"0\",\"product_id\":null,\"barcode\":null,\"with_storehouse_management\":\"0\",\"quantity\":\"0\",\"allow_checkout_when_out_of_stock\":\"0\",\"stock_status\":\"in_stock\",\"weight\":\"0\",\"length\":\"0\",\"wide\":\"0\",\"height\":\"0\",\"is_added_attributes\":\"0\",\"has_product_options\":\"1\",\"related_products\":null,\"faq_schema_config\":\"[]\",\"seo_meta\":{\"seo_title\":null,\"seo_description\":null,\"index\":\"index\"},\"seo_meta_image\":null,\"layout\":null,\"is_popular\":\"0\",\"status\":\"published\",\"store_id\":null,\"is_featured\":\"0\",\"categories\":[\"34\"],\"brand_id\":null,\"image\":null,\"minimum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"maximum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"tag\":null,\"submitter\":\"save\"}', 'created', 'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/129.0.0.0 Safari/537.36', '2409:40e0:1b0:d388:c8c7:d8b9:da3c:acb8', 3, 433, 'YELLOW SHRIMP', 'info', '2024-10-24 17:42:45', '2024-10-24 17:42:45'),
(2353, 3, 'product', '{\"name\":\"RED SHRIMP\",\"model\":\"Botble\\\\Ecommerce\\\\Models\\\\Product\",\"slug\":\"red-shrimp\",\"slug_id\":\"0\",\"is_slug_editable\":\"1\",\"description\":\"<p>Price is for a single piece shrimp. A Red Cherry Shrimp can be a great little&nbsp;freshwater shrimp&nbsp;to add to an aquarium. Their bright red color really adds beauty to a tank, especially one loaded with live green aquarium plants and black gravel or substrate. Cherry Shrimp or Neocaridina heteropoda, also known simply as Cherry Shrimp, are natives of Taiwan. But most available in stores today are bread in captivity as they can reproduce in fresh water. Red Cherry Shrimp are active and interesting to watch<\\/p>\",\"content\":null,\"images\":[null,\"red-shrimp-min-300x300.jpg\"],\"product_type\":\"physical\",\"sale_type\":\"0\",\"sku\":null,\"price\":\"0\",\"sale_price\":null,\"start_date\":null,\"end_date\":null,\"cost_per_item\":\"0\",\"product_id\":null,\"barcode\":null,\"with_storehouse_management\":\"0\",\"quantity\":\"0\",\"allow_checkout_when_out_of_stock\":\"0\",\"stock_status\":\"in_stock\",\"weight\":\"0\",\"length\":\"0\",\"wide\":\"0\",\"height\":\"0\",\"is_added_attributes\":\"0\",\"has_product_options\":\"1\",\"related_products\":null,\"faq_schema_config\":\"[]\",\"seo_meta\":{\"seo_title\":null,\"seo_description\":null,\"index\":\"index\"},\"seo_meta_image\":null,\"layout\":null,\"is_popular\":\"0\",\"status\":\"published\",\"store_id\":null,\"is_featured\":\"0\",\"categories\":[\"34\"],\"brand_id\":null,\"image\":null,\"minimum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"maximum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"tag\":null}', 'created', 'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/129.0.0.0 Safari/537.36', '2409:40e0:1b0:d388:c8c7:d8b9:da3c:acb8', 3, 434, 'RED SHRIMP', 'info', '2024-10-24 17:44:02', '2024-10-24 17:44:02'),
(2354, 3, 'product', '{\"name\":\"RED SHRIMP\",\"model\":\"Botble\\\\Ecommerce\\\\Models\\\\Product\",\"slug\":\"red-shrimp\",\"slug_id\":\"470\",\"is_slug_editable\":\"1\",\"description\":\"<p>Price is for a single piece shrimp. A Red Cherry Shrimp can be a great little&nbsp;freshwater shrimp&nbsp;to add to an aquarium. Their bright red color really adds beauty to a tank, especially one loaded with live green aquarium plants and black gravel or substrate. Cherry Shrimp or Neocaridina heteropoda, also known simply as Cherry Shrimp, are natives of Taiwan. But most available in stores today are bread in captivity as they can reproduce in fresh water. Red Cherry Shrimp are active and interesting to watch<\\/p>\",\"content\":null,\"images\":[null,\"red-shrimp-min-300x300.jpg\"],\"product_type\":\"physical\",\"sale_type\":\"0\",\"sku\":null,\"price\":\"0\",\"sale_price\":null,\"start_date\":null,\"end_date\":null,\"cost_per_item\":\"0\",\"product_id\":\"434\",\"barcode\":null,\"with_storehouse_management\":\"0\",\"quantity\":\"0\",\"allow_checkout_when_out_of_stock\":\"0\",\"stock_status\":\"in_stock\",\"weight\":\"0\",\"length\":\"0\",\"wide\":\"0\",\"height\":\"0\",\"is_added_attributes\":\"0\",\"has_product_options\":\"1\",\"related_products\":null,\"faq_schema_config\":[[{\"key\":\"question\",\"value\":null},{\"key\":\"answer\",\"value\":null}]],\"seo_meta\":{\"seo_title\":null,\"seo_description\":null,\"index\":\"index\"},\"seo_meta_image\":null,\"language\":\"en_US\",\"layout\":null,\"is_popular\":\"0\",\"status\":\"published\",\"store_id\":null,\"is_featured\":\"0\",\"categories\":[\"34\"],\"brand_id\":null,\"image\":\"red-shrimp-min-300x300.jpg\",\"minimum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"maximum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"tag\":null,\"submitter\":\"save\"}', 'updated', 'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/129.0.0.0 Safari/537.36', '2409:40e0:1b0:d388:c8c7:d8b9:da3c:acb8', 3, 434, 'RED SHRIMP', 'primary', '2024-10-24 17:44:17', '2024-10-24 17:44:17');
