(2359, 3, 'product', '{\"_method\":\"delete\"}', 'deleted', 'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/129.0.0.0 Safari/537.36', '2409:40e0:1b0:d388:c8c7:d8b9:da3c:acb8', 3, 437, 'MOUNTAIN MINNOW', 'danger', '2024-10-24 17:58:39', '2024-10-24 17:58:39'),
(2360, 3, 'product', '{\"name\":\"OTOCINCLUS\",\"model\":\"Botble\\\\Ecommerce\\\\Models\\\\Product\",\"slug\":\"otocinclus\",\"slug_id\":\"0\",\"is_slug_editable\":\"1\",\"description\":\"<p><strong>The Otocinclus Catfish is one of THE most peaceful fish for the nano, community, or planted aquarium. It is also an effective algae eater and scavenger!<\\/strong><\\/p><p>&nbsp;<\\/p><p>Whether or not you have an algae problem in your tank, Otocinclus Catfish make a great addition to any aquarium community.&nbsp; Also known as Otto Cats, otos, or dwarf suckermouth catfish, these fish use their sucker-mouths to attack algae on the aquarium glass, plants, and decorations.&nbsp; In fact, they are widely considered one of the best algae-eating fish in the world, and groups of them form quite the cleanup crew with their voracious appetite for algae.<strong>&nbsp; <\\/strong>They come from fast-moving rivers in South America, so they do best in aquariums with strong currents (which can be achieved with good water filters or powerheads), good filtration, and plenty of aeration.<\\/p><p>Otocinclus Catfish are recognizable by the rows of armor-like plating along their bodies.&nbsp; They often have a variety of neutral colors on their bodies (such as browns, grays, and black) that form attractive patterns.&nbsp; We sell these fish in schools of 3 and 5 because they are known to do best in groups of 3 or more.&nbsp; These are small catfish, growing up to a maximum of 2 inches in length. &nbsp;They have very social personalities and are quite peaceful, making them completely safe to keep with other non-aggressive fish, shrimp, snails, and live plants.<\\/p><p>If algae is not present in your aquarium, the Otocinclus\' diets can be supplemented with algae wafers or vegetable-based flake food.<\\/p><p><strong>What We Like About This Fish:<\\/strong><\\/p><ul><li>Widely considered the best algae-eating fish in the freshwater aquarium hobby<\\/li><li>Very social personalities<\\/li><li>Safe with plants<\\/li><li>Completely peaceful<\\/li><\\/ul><p>&nbsp;<\\/p><p><strong>RECOMMENDED TANK PARAMETERS:&nbsp;<\\/strong><\\/p><ul><li><u>Temperature<\\/u>:&nbsp; 74\\u00b0 - 79\\u00b0 F (23\\u00b0 - 26\\u00b0 C)<\\/li><li><u>pH<\\/u>:&nbsp; 6.8 - 7.5<\\/li><li><u>KH<\\/u>:&nbsp; 2 - 10 dKH<\\/li><li><u>Minimum tank size<\\/u>:&nbsp; 10 gallons<\\/li><\\/ul><p>&nbsp;<\\/p><p><strong>CARE GUIDELINES:<\\/strong><\\/p><ul><li><u>Diet<\\/u>:&nbsp; Can mostly sustain themselves on algae.&nbsp; If algae is not present in your aquarium, their diets can be supplemented with algae wafers or vegetable-based flake foods.<\\/li><\\/ul><p><u>Social behavior<\\/u>:&nbsp; Peaceful, schooling\\/shoaling.<\\/p>\",\"content\":null,\"images\":[null,\"otocinclus-300x300.jpg\"],\"product_type\":\"physical\",\"sale_type\":\"0\",\"sku\":null,\"price\":\"0\",\"sale_price\":null,\"start_date\":null,\"end_date\":null,\"cost_per_item\":\"0\",\"product_id\":null,\"barcode\":null,\"with_storehouse_management\":\"0\",\"quantity\":\"0\",\"allow_checkout_when_out_of_stock\":\"0\",\"stock_status\":\"in_stock\",\"weight\":\"0\",\"length\":\"0\",\"wide\":\"0\",\"height\":\"0\",\"is_added_attributes\":\"0\",\"has_product_options\":\"1\",\"related_products\":null,\"faq_schema_config\":\"[]\",\"seo_meta\":{\"seo_title\":null,\"seo_description\":null,\"index\":\"index\"},\"seo_meta_image\":null,\"layout\":null,\"is_popular\":\"0\",\"status\":\"published\",\"store_id\":null,\"is_featured\":\"0\",\"categories\":[\"34\"],\"brand_id\":null,\"image\":null,\"minimum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"maximum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"tag\":null,\"submitter\":\"save\"}', 'created', 'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/129.0.0.0 Safari/537.36', '2409:40e0:1b0:d388:c8c7:d8b9:da3c:acb8', 3, 438, 'OTOCINCLUS', 'info', '2024-10-24 18:01:05', '2024-10-24 18:01:05'),
(2361, 3, 'product', '{\"name\":\"SIAMESE ALGAE EATER\",\"model\":\"Botble\\\\Ecommerce\\\\Models\\\\Product\",\"slug\":\"siamese-algae-eater\",\"slug_id\":\"0\",\"is_slug_editable\":\"1\",\"description\":\"<p><strong>The Siamese Algae Eater is one of the best algae-eating fish in the aquarium hobby, and it is one of the very few fish that will eat the dreaded black beard algae!<\\/strong><\\/p><p>&nbsp;<\\/p><div>The Siamese Algae Eater&nbsp;(<i>Crossocheilus siamensis<\\/i>)&nbsp;is a longtime favorite in the aquarium hobby due to its active nature and its voracious appetite for various types of nuisance algae, including pesky black beard algae. It is a mostly herviborous fish that is gregarious as a juvenile, but is shoaling (rather than schooling) as an adult. As it matures, a distinct hierarchy develops within a group of this species, and stress and aggression are likely when the group contains less than 6 specimens.<\\/div><div>Care is simple for the Siamese Algae Eater. It is tolerant of a wide range of water parameters, but it will thrive in an aquarium with ample filtration and moderate to high water flow. This active fish is known to jump occasionally, so a secure aquarium lid is recommended. It will readily eat most high-quality dry foods rich in vegetable matter, but it should also be offered fresh vegetables such as zucchini and cucumber as well. Meaty foods should be kept to a minimum with this fish.<\\/div><div>As stated above, the Siamese Algae Eater is a generally peaceful fish, but it will prey on dwarf shrimp and other very small invertebrates. It does not seem to bother most snails, and we have found it to be generally peaceful with most larger shrimp (such as Amano, Flower, Green Lace, and Vampire Shrimp) as long as they are too large to be considered easy prey. The Siamese Algae Eater is a schooling fish&nbsp;as a juvenile, but can become more territorial with its own kind and similar-looking species as it matures. It must be kept in groups of at least 6 fish to avoid harrassment of subdominant specimens, or else it should be kept singly.&nbsp;Aggression can be kept to a minimum in a larger tank with plenty of territory and cover for each fish.<\\/div><div><div><strong>What We Like About This Fish:<\\/strong><\\/div><div><ul><li>Voracious algae eater<\\/li><li>Will not eat ornamental plants<\\/li><li>Generally peaceful disposition with fish and peaceful larger invertebrates<\\/li><li>Very active and noticeable fish in any aquarium<\\/li><li>Very hardy<\\/li><\\/ul><\\/div><div>&nbsp;<\\/div><div>&nbsp;<\\/div><div><strong>RECOMMENDED TANK PARAMETERS:<\\/strong><\\/div><div><ul><li>Temperature:&nbsp; 72\\u00b0 - 79\\u00b0 F (22\\u00b0 - 26\\u00b0 C)<\\/li><li>pH:&nbsp; 6.5 - 7.5<\\/li><li>KH:&nbsp; 4 - 15 dKH<\\/li><li><p>Minimum tank size:&nbsp; 50 gallons<\\/p><div><strong>CARE GUIDELINES:<\\/strong><\\/div><div><ul><li>Diet:&nbsp; Omnivorous. Will easily accept high quality dry and frozen foods as well as fresh vegetables. Should be fed mostly vegetable matter.<\\/li><li>Social behavior:&nbsp; Generally peaceful, schooling\\/shoaling as a juvenile. Can be somewhat territoral with its own kind or similar fish as an adult<\\/li><\\/ul><\\/div><\\/li><\\/ul><\\/div><\\/div>\",\"content\":null,\"images\":[null,\"siamese-algae-eater-min-300x300.jpg\"],\"product_type\":\"physical\",\"sale_type\":\"0\",\"sku\":null,\"price\":\"0\",\"sale_price\":null,\"start_date\":null,\"end_date\":null,\"cost_per_item\":\"0\",\"product_id\":null,\"barcode\":null,\"with_storehouse_management\":\"0\",\"quantity\":\"0\",\"allow_checkout_when_out_of_stock\":\"0\",\"stock_status\":\"in_stock\",\"weight\":\"0\",\"length\":\"0\",\"wide\":\"0\",\"height\":\"0\",\"is_added_attributes\":\"0\",\"has_product_options\":\"1\",\"related_products\":null,\"faq_schema_config\":\"[]\",\"seo_meta\":{\"seo_title\":null,\"seo_description\":null,\"index\":\"index\"},\"seo_meta_image\":null,\"layout\":null,\"is_popular\":\"0\",\"status\":\"published\",\"store_id\":null,\"is_featured\":\"0\",\"categories\":[\"34\"],\"brand_id\":null,\"image\":null,\"minimum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"maximum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"tag\":null,\"submitter\":\"save\"}', 'created', 'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/129.0.0.0 Safari/537.36', '2409:40e0:1b0:d388:c8c7:d8b9:da3c:acb8', 3, 439, 'SIAMESE ALGAE EATER', 'info', '2024-10-24 18:04:14', '2024-10-24 18:04:14'),
(2362, 3, 'product', '{\"name\":\"CHERRY BARB\",\"model\":\"Botble\\\\Ecommerce\\\\Models\\\\Product\",\"slug\":\"cherry-barb\",\"slug_id\":\"0\",\"is_slug_editable\":\"1\",\"description\":\"<p>Named for the males\' vibrant red color during spawning season, the Cherry Barb makes a great schooling addition to many freshwater community tanks. These slender fish are common in this pet hobby and are easy to manage for most beginner aquarists. These smaller fish tend to be shy around larger, aggressive fish, so keep them in a group and choose their tank mates carefully.<\\/p><h2 class=\\\"comp mntl-sc-block lifestyle-sc-block-heading mntl-sc-block-heading u-how-to-title-align\\\" id=\\\"mntl-sc-block_18-0\\\"><span class=\\\"mntl-sc-block-heading__text\\\">Cherry Barb Habitat and Care<\\/span><\\/h2><p class=\\\"comp mntl-sc-block lifestyle-sc-block-html mntl-sc-block-html text-passage u-how-to-title-align\\\" id=\\\"mntl-sc-block_19-0\\\">Being a shyer fish, the Cherry Barb likes to have lots of places to hide in their home aquarium. They should be added to your aquarium first, so they can get settled and not have to compete for hiding places.<\\/p><div class=\\\"comp mntl-sc-block lifestyle-sc-block-adslot mntl-sc-block-adslot mntl-block u-no-article-width-restriction\\\" id=\\\"mntl-sc-block_20-0\\\">&nbsp;<\\/div><p class=\\\"comp mntl-sc-block lifestyle-sc-block-html mntl-sc-block-html text-passage u-how-to-title-align\\\" id=\\\"mntl-sc-block_21-0\\\">Since they like to stick in a group, you may need to make lots of hiding places to accommodate more than one fish at a time. Planted tanks or aquascapes make a great home for Cherry Barbs with good water quality and lots of places to hide.<\\/p><div class=\\\"comp mntl-sc-block lifestyle-sc-block-adslot mntl-sc-block-adslot mntl-block u-no-article-width-restriction\\\" id=\\\"mntl-sc-block_22-0\\\">&nbsp;<\\/div><p class=\\\"comp mntl-sc-block lifestyle-sc-block-html mntl-sc-block-html text-passage u-how-to-title-align\\\" id=\\\"mntl-sc-block_23-0\\\">Cherry Barbs are relatively easy to care for as long as you keep up with your regular maintenance. In planted tanks, be sure to remove dead plant material regularly and pay attention to any pH changes between day and night.<\\/p>\",\"content\":null,\"images\":[null,\"cherry-barb-300x300.jpg\"],\"product_type\":\"physical\",\"sale_type\":\"0\",\"sku\":null,\"price\":\"0\",\"sale_price\":null,\"start_date\":null,\"end_date\":null,\"cost_per_item\":\"0\",\"product_id\":null,\"barcode\":null,\"with_storehouse_management\":\"0\",\"quantity\":\"0\",\"allow_checkout_when_out_of_stock\":\"0\",\"stock_status\":\"in_stock\",\"weight\":\"0\",\"length\":\"0\",\"wide\":\"0\",\"height\":\"0\",\"is_added_attributes\":\"0\",\"has_product_options\":\"1\",\"related_products\":null,\"faq_schema_config\":\"[]\",\"seo_meta\":{\"seo_title\":null,\"seo_description\":null,\"index\":\"index\"},\"seo_meta_image\":null,\"layout\":null,\"is_popular\":\"0\",\"status\":\"published\",\"store_id\":null,\"is_featured\":\"0\",\"categories\":[\"34\"],\"brand_id\":null,\"image\":null,\"minimum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"maximum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"tag\":null,\"submitter\":\"save\"}', 'created', 'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/129.0.0.0 Safari/537.36', '2409:40e0:1b0:d388:c8c7:d8b9:da3c:acb8', 3, 440, 'CHERRY BARB', 'info', '2024-10-24 18:07:44', '2024-10-24 18:07:44'),
(2363, 3, 'product', '{\"name\":\"PURPLE WIDOW\",\"model\":\"Botble\\\\Ecommerce\\\\Models\\\\Product\",\"slug\":\"purple-widow\",\"slug_id\":\"0\",\"is_slug_editable\":\"1\",\"description\":\"<p><span data-preserver-spaces=\\\"true\\\">Glo Tetra \\u2013 Purple: Tetras have several bones linking the inner ear to the swim bladder, which gives them a great hearing. They also have a small, rounded fin between the dorsal and tail fins.<\\/span><\\/p><p><span data-preserver-spaces=\\\"true\\\">Genetically altered Galactic Purple Tetras are fluorescent purple. Typically, these fish measure 2.4 inches. The water\\u2019s pH level and temperature range should be between 6.0 and 7.0 for these fish to be kept in captivity.<\\/span><\\/p><p><span data-preserver-spaces=\\\"true\\\">Given that these fish are jumpers, the tank should include dense vegetation, open places for swimming, a cover, floating plants to assist filter the light, and a gravel or sand substrate.<\\/span><\\/p><p><span data-preserver-spaces=\\\"true\\\">Smaller fish may get their fins bit by the tetra, however, the fin-nipping tendency of the tetra can be remedied by keeping it in a group of at least six. These fish can be housed in a communal tank with larger fish. For a small party, a minimum recommended tank size of 15 gallons and 20 inches long is advised.<\\/span><\\/p><p><i><span data-preserver-spaces=\\\"true\\\"><strong>II. You would love the fish because\\u2026<\\/strong><\\/span><\\/i><\\/p><p><span data-preserver-spaces=\\\"true\\\">The new collection of Tetras from Fluorescent GloFish\\u00ae is available in six bright colors, including Starfire Red\\u00ae, Electric Green\\u00ae, Sunburst Orange\\u00ae, Cosmic Blue\\u00ae, Galactic Purple\\u00ae, and Moonrise Pink\\u00ae. GloFish\\u00ae is not dyed, and the color they were born with does not deteriorate with time.<\\/span><\\/p><p><span data-preserver-spaces=\\\"true\\\">To aid in the detection of environmental toxins and advance scientific study, the first generations of GloFish\\u00ae were genetically modified as embryos. Now, every GloFish\\u00ae generation is born with its stunning color! A naturally occurring fluorescent protein gene in some marine species is responsible for the dazzling colors.<\\/span><\\/p><p><span data-preserver-spaces=\\\"true\\\">Maintaining GloFish\\u00ae is as simple as maintaining Tetras. Keep this tranquil fish alone in tiny aquariums or small schools with other equally peaceful fish for the best care. Feed GloFish\\u00ae a broad diet of flake and frozen meals because they are omnivores.<\\/span><\\/p><p><i><span data-preserver-spaces=\\\"true\\\"><strong>III. Is this fish species peaceful or hostile?<\\/strong><\\/span><\\/i><\\/p><p><span data-preserver-spaces=\\\"true\\\">A very peaceful and easy-going fish.<\\/span><\\/p><p><i><span data-preserver-spaces=\\\"true\\\"><strong>IV. Species compatibility<\\/strong><\\/span><\\/i><span data-preserver-spaces=\\\"true\\\">Neon Tetra, Tiger Barb, Plecos, original Danio, and the Dwarf Cichlid<\\/span><\\/p><p>&nbsp;<\\/p><p><span data-preserver-spaces=\\\"true\\\">V. How to feed this species?<\\/span><\\/p><p><span data-preserver-spaces=\\\"true\\\">Flakes, pellets, and frozen or freeze-dried meals make up a well-balanced GloFish diet. a diversified diet that includes items high in carotenoids and beta carotene to help maintain your fish\\u2019s beautiful color and guarantee optimum nutritional balance.<\\/span><\\/p>\",\"content\":null,\"images\":[null,\"purple-widow-300x300-1.jpg\"],\"product_type\":\"physical\",\"sale_type\":\"0\",\"sku\":null,\"price\":\"0\",\"sale_price\":null,\"start_date\":null,\"end_date\":null,\"cost_per_item\":\"0\",\"product_id\":null,\"barcode\":null,\"with_storehouse_management\":\"0\",\"quantity\":\"0\",\"allow_checkout_when_out_of_stock\":\"0\",\"stock_status\":\"in_stock\",\"weight\":\"0\",\"length\":\"0\",\"wide\":\"0\",\"height\":\"0\",\"is_added_attributes\":\"0\",\"has_product_options\":\"1\",\"related_products\":null,\"faq_schema_config\":\"[]\",\"seo_meta\":{\"seo_title\":null,\"seo_description\":null,\"index\":\"index\"},\"seo_meta_image\":null,\"layout\":null,\"is_popular\":\"0\",\"status\":\"published\",\"store_id\":null,\"is_featured\":\"0\",\"categories\":[\"34\"],\"brand_id\":null,\"image\":null,\"minimum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"maximum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"tag\":null,\"submitter\":\"save\"}', 'created', 'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/129.0.0.0 Safari/537.36', '2409:40e0:1b0:d388:c8c7:d8b9:da3c:acb8', 3, 441, 'PURPLE WIDOW', 'info', '2024-10-24 18:10:18', '2024-10-24 18:10:18'),
(2364, 3, 'product', '{\"name\":\"YELLOW WIDOW\",\"model\":\"Botble\\\\Ecommerce\\\\Models\\\\Product\",\"slug\":\"yellow-widow\",\"slug_id\":\"0\",\"is_slug_editable\":\"1\",\"description\":\"<p><span data-preserver-spaces=\\\"true\\\">Glo Tetra \\u2013 Yellow: The glowlight tetra is astonishingly simple to care for and very stunning. It is a calm, laid-back fish that originated in the rivers of Guyana. It can live in a variety of aquarium conditions. You ought to preserve at least six glowlight tetras because they are school.<\\/span><\\/p><p><span data-preserver-spaces=\\\"true\\\">Glo Tetra \\u2013 Yellow:originated from The Essequibo basin in Guyanabeen discovered in the Essequibo, Mazaruni, and Potaro Rivers. The tannins produced by the breakdown of plant materials give the river waters of South America their natural softness and acidity.<\\/span><\\/p><p><i><span data-preserver-spaces=\\\"true\\\"><strong>II. You would love the fish because\\u2026<\\/strong><\\/span><\\/i><\\/p><p><span data-preserver-spaces=\\\"true\\\">Depending on the breed of the color, they appear in various fluorescent colors like Glo Tetra \\u2013 Yellow<\\/span><\\/p><p><span data-preserver-spaces=\\\"true\\\">One of the most well-liked tetras is the glowlight tetra, which is calm and simple to care for.<\\/span><\\/p><p><span data-preserver-spaces=\\\"true\\\">They grow barely an inch and a half long as adults, making them tiny and skinny. The glowlight tetra\\u2019s translucent, silvery-peach body is split by an iridescent red-gold stripe that extends from the nose to the tail.<\\/span><\\/p><p><span data-preserver-spaces=\\\"true\\\">The stripe mimics a light bulb\\u2019s or glowlight\\u2019s glowing filament. The anal and pelvic fins are bordered in white, while the leading edge of the dorsal fin is the same iridescent red color. in the dark and then exposed to blue light.<\\/span><\\/p><p><span data-preserver-spaces=\\\"true\\\">The red line or glowlight rasbora, a kind of rasbora, and the glowlight tetra both have distinctive stripes, and the two fish are occasionally mistaken for one another.<\\/span><\\/p><p><span data-preserver-spaces=\\\"true\\\">The two species, however, do not belong to the same genus. The absence of an adipose fin in the rasbora is the most noticeable distinction between the two.<\\/span><\\/p><p><i><span data-preserver-spaces=\\\"true\\\"><strong>III. Is this fish species peaceful or hostile?<\\/strong><\\/span><\\/i><\\/p><p><span data-preserver-spaces=\\\"true\\\">A very peaceful and easy-going fish.<\\/span><\\/p><p><i><span data-preserver-spaces=\\\"true\\\"><strong>IV. Species compatibility<\\/strong><\\/span><\\/i><\\/p><p><span data-preserver-spaces=\\\"true\\\">Neon Tetra, Tiger Barb, Plecos, original Danio, and the Dwarf Cichlid<\\/span><\\/p><p><i><span data-preserver-spaces=\\\"true\\\"><strong>V. How to feed this species?<\\/strong><\\/span><\\/i><\\/p><p><span data-preserver-spaces=\\\"true\\\">Flakes, pellets, and frozen or freeze-dried meals make up a well-balanced GloFish diet. a diversified diet that includes items high in carotenoids and beta carotene to help maintain your fish\\u2019s beautiful color and guarantee optimum nutritional balance.<\\/span><\\/p><p>&nbsp;<\\/p>\",\"content\":null,\"images\":[null,\"yellow-widow-300x300.jpg\"],\"product_type\":\"physical\",\"sale_type\":\"0\",\"sku\":null,\"price\":\"0\",\"sale_price\":null,\"start_date\":null,\"end_date\":null,\"cost_per_item\":\"0\",\"product_id\":null,\"barcode\":null,\"with_storehouse_management\":\"0\",\"quantity\":\"0\",\"allow_checkout_when_out_of_stock\":\"0\",\"stock_status\":\"in_stock\",\"weight\":\"0\",\"length\":\"0\",\"wide\":\"0\",\"height\":\"0\",\"is_added_attributes\":\"0\",\"has_product_options\":\"1\",\"related_products\":null,\"faq_schema_config\":\"[]\",\"seo_meta\":{\"seo_title\":null,\"seo_description\":null,\"index\":\"index\"},\"seo_meta_image\":null,\"layout\":null,\"is_popular\":\"0\",\"status\":\"published\",\"store_id\":null,\"is_featured\":\"0\",\"categories\":[\"34\"],\"brand_id\":null,\"image\":null,\"minimum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"maximum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"tag\":null}', 'created', 'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/129.0.0.0 Safari/537.36', '2409:40e0:1b0:d388:c8c7:d8b9:da3c:acb8', 3, 442, 'YELLOW WIDOW', 'info', '2024-10-24 18:12:08', '2024-10-24 18:12:08'),
