(2366, 3, 'product', '{\"name\":\"GREEN WIDOW\",\"model\":\"Botble\\\\Ecommerce\\\\Models\\\\Product\",\"slug\":\"green-widow\",\"slug_id\":\"0\",\"is_slug_editable\":\"1\",\"description\":\"<ul class=\\\"tabs wc-tabs product-tabs small-nav-collapse nav nav-uppercase nav-line nav-left\\\" role=\\\"tablist\\\"><li class=\\\"description_tab active\\\" id=\\\"tab-title-description\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\"><a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/fish.splashyfin.com\\/shop\\/glo-tetra-green\\/#tab-description\\\" role=\\\"tab\\\" aria-selected=\\\"true\\\" aria-controls=\\\"tab-description\\\">Description<\\/a><\\/li><li class=\\\"additional_information_tab\\\" id=\\\"tab-title-additional_information\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\"><a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/fish.splashyfin.com\\/shop\\/glo-tetra-green\\/#tab-additional_information\\\" tabindex=\\\"-1\\\" role=\\\"tab\\\" aria-selected=\\\"false\\\" aria-controls=\\\"tab-additional_information\\\">Additional information<\\/a><\\/li><\\/ul><div class=\\\"tab-panels\\\"><div class=\\\"woocommerce-Tabs-panel woocommerce-Tabs-panel--description panel entry-content active\\\" id=\\\"tab-description\\\" role=\\\"tabpanel\\\" aria-labelledby=\\\"tab-title-description\\\"><p><span data-preserver-spaces=\\\"true\\\">Glo Tetra \\u2013 Green are fish that have been genetically altered. They have vivid fluorescent colors, as their name suggests.<\\/span><\\/p><p><span data-preserver-spaces=\\\"true\\\">They are nothing more than luminous variations of the wild species like Zebra danios, Rainbow sharks, Tiger barbs, Bettas, and Black skirt tetras that are naturally found.<\\/span><\\/p><p><span data-preserver-spaces=\\\"true\\\">The gentle Glo Tetra-Green prefers to live in shoaling groups of five or more. A solitary specimen is prone to experience stress and isolate itself.<\\/span><\\/p><p><span data-preserver-spaces=\\\"true\\\">The best and required solution is to keep them together in groups. They are gentle fish that make great tank mates for other little fish due to their disposition.<\\/span><\\/p><p><span data-preserver-spaces=\\\"true\\\">To long-finned fish, however, are semi-aggressive as long as they are sluggish, not too big, and aggressive. They begin to nibble in response to the lengthy fins.<\\/span><\\/p><p><span data-preserver-spaces=\\\"true\\\">Their intergroup hostility is also triggered if the female in a group of two or more males exhibits spawning behavior, and every male tends to pair up with the female.<\\/span><\\/p><p><span data-preserver-spaces=\\\"true\\\">If you wish to breed glofish, separate the female at this time and place her in a different setup. You can add the male afterward. The glofish tetras are otherwise calm and have distinguished themselves from the other community fishes.<\\/span><\\/p><p><i><span data-preserver-spaces=\\\"true\\\"><strong>II. You would love the fish because\\u2026<\\/strong><\\/span><\\/i><\\/p><p><span data-preserver-spaces=\\\"true\\\">Depending on the breed of the color, they appear in various fluorescent colors. However, these fish share the same overall appearance as a black skirt tetra.<\\/span><\\/p><p><span data-preserver-spaces=\\\"true\\\">Their bodies are generally quadrilateral, with a rounded forehead. Their lower end goes pointed inward and meets the tail at the second half section. Their top end is streamlined and curled.<\\/span><\\/p><p><span data-preserver-spaces=\\\"true\\\">They have highly noticeable fins, which add to their overall sheen. The dorsal fin is tiny and has an appearance of a square with a pointed top. The forked tail fin has a more \\u201cV\\u201d-shaped look. The body\\u2019s bottom half is covered by the anal fin.<\\/span><\\/p><p><span data-preserver-spaces=\\\"true\\\">Glo Tetra \\u2013 Green comes in several vividly colored varieties. All seven colors of the rainbow are represented by these colors.<\\/span><\\/p><p><span data-preserver-spaces=\\\"true\\\">If your tank has color variations, they enhance its brilliance and make it appear like a luminous ornamental item in your guest room.<\\/span><\\/p><p><span data-preserver-spaces=\\\"true\\\">All of these variations appear normal in white light, yet they glow in the dark and when exposed to blue light.<\\/span><\\/p><p><i><span data-preserver-spaces=\\\"true\\\"><strong>III. Is this fish species peaceful or hostile?<\\/strong><\\/span><\\/i><\\/p><p><span data-preserver-spaces=\\\"true\\\">A very peaceful and friendly nature.<\\/span><\\/p><p><i><span data-preserver-spaces=\\\"true\\\"><strong>IV. Species compatibility<\\/strong><\\/span><\\/i><\\/p><p><span data-preserver-spaces=\\\"true\\\">Tetras, Guppies, Platys, Corydoras Catfish, and Gouramis.<\\/span><\\/p><p><i><span data-preserver-spaces=\\\"true\\\"><strong>V. How to feed this species?<\\/strong><\\/span><\\/i><\\/p><p><span data-preserver-spaces=\\\"true\\\">In the wild, red phantom tetras are omnivores and will consume both decaying plant matter and small animals like young shrimp, larvae, and snails. In captivity, these fish thrive on fine-grained subtropical fish flakes.<\\/span><\\/p><\\/div><\\/div>\",\"content\":null,\"images\":[null,\"green-widow-300x300.jpg\"],\"product_type\":\"physical\",\"sale_type\":\"0\",\"sku\":null,\"price\":\"0\",\"sale_price\":null,\"start_date\":null,\"end_date\":null,\"cost_per_item\":\"0\",\"product_id\":null,\"barcode\":null,\"with_storehouse_management\":\"0\",\"quantity\":\"0\",\"allow_checkout_when_out_of_stock\":\"0\",\"stock_status\":\"in_stock\",\"weight\":\"0\",\"length\":\"0\",\"wide\":\"0\",\"height\":\"0\",\"is_added_attributes\":\"0\",\"has_product_options\":\"1\",\"related_products\":null,\"faq_schema_config\":\"[]\",\"seo_meta\":{\"seo_title\":null,\"seo_description\":null,\"index\":\"index\"},\"seo_meta_image\":null,\"layout\":null,\"is_popular\":\"0\",\"status\":\"published\",\"store_id\":null,\"is_featured\":\"0\",\"categories\":[\"34\"],\"brand_id\":null,\"image\":null,\"minimum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"maximum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"tag\":null,\"submitter\":\"save\"}', 'created', 'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/129.0.0.0 Safari/537.36', '2409:40e0:1b0:d388:c8c7:d8b9:da3c:acb8', 3, 443, 'GREEN WIDOW', 'info', '2024-10-24 18:13:43', '2024-10-24 18:13:43');
INSERT INTO `audit_histories` (`id`, `user_id`, `module`, `request`, `action`, `user_agent`, `ip_address`, `reference_user`, `reference_id`, `reference_name`, `type`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
(2367, 3, 'product', '{\"name\":\"RED WIDOW\",\"model\":\"Botble\\\\Ecommerce\\\\Models\\\\Product\",\"slug\":\"red-widow\",\"slug_id\":\"0\",\"is_slug_editable\":\"1\",\"description\":\"<p>Red widow fish are brilliantly colored and beautiful fish. Widow tetras are an undemanding species that adapt to a range of conditions, though subdued lighting and neutral-colored gravel substrates are preferred.&nbsp; Hardy and easy to care for. A schooling fish by nature, widow tetras are best kept in groups of six or more. They make an excellent community fish due to their peaceful nature.<\\/p><ul><li><strong>TEMPERATURE<\\/strong>&nbsp;<strong>RANGE<\\/strong>&nbsp;: 21 \\u00b0C \\u2013 27\\u00b0C<\\/li><li><strong>PH RANGE<\\/strong>&nbsp;: 6 \\u2013 7<\\/li><li><strong>TANK MATES &amp; COMPATIBILITY<\\/strong>:- Tetras are peaceful and passive, making them suitable tank mates for a variety of fish species. Similarly-sized, bottom-dwelling, non-aggressive fish can be added to a community tank with tetras. Tetras are a schooling species, so make sure your neon tetras are housed in groups of six or more before considering other fish species for the tank.<\\/li><li><strong>FEEDING<\\/strong>:- In the wild, Tetras are omnivores, eating a varied diet of meat and fish. Depending on the food source available in the fish\\u2019s habitat, a neon tetra will feed on insect larvae, small insects, algae, and other plant matter. Good-quality fish flakes that are fortified with vitamins and minerals are a staple food to feed tetras. Several times per week, feed neon tetras live or frozen foods like bloodworms, daphnia, tubifex, and brine shrimp. Cut live food into small pieces to prevent the neon tetras from having problems swallowing the food.<\\/li><li><strong>CARE<\\/strong>:- Caring for tetras is easy. Tetras are hardy fish that can adapt to brackish and clearwater environments, but a clean freshwater tank setup will ensure that the fish thrive in captivity. Tetras are omnivores and have a varied diet in the wild, which you should replicate in your home aquarium. Decorate your neon tetra tank with floating plants like&nbsp;<a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.fishkeepingworld.com\\/hornwort\\/\\\">hornwort&nbsp;<\\/a>and&nbsp;<a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.fishkeepingworld.com\\/java-moss\\/\\\">Java moss<\\/a>. These plants create shady, secluded hideaways that neon tetras enjoy. Driftwood can also be used to provide hiding places for the fish.<\\/li><\\/ul>\",\"content\":null,\"images\":[null,\"red-widow-300x300.jpg\"],\"product_type\":\"physical\",\"sale_type\":\"0\",\"sku\":null,\"price\":\"0\",\"sale_price\":null,\"start_date\":null,\"end_date\":null,\"cost_per_item\":\"0\",\"product_id\":null,\"barcode\":null,\"with_storehouse_management\":\"0\",\"quantity\":\"0\",\"allow_checkout_when_out_of_stock\":\"0\",\"stock_status\":\"in_stock\",\"weight\":\"0\",\"length\":\"0\",\"wide\":\"0\",\"height\":\"0\",\"is_added_attributes\":\"0\",\"has_product_options\":\"1\",\"related_products\":null,\"faq_schema_config\":\"[]\",\"seo_meta\":{\"seo_title\":null,\"seo_description\":null,\"index\":\"index\"},\"seo_meta_image\":null,\"layout\":null,\"is_popular\":\"0\",\"status\":\"published\",\"store_id\":null,\"is_featured\":\"0\",\"categories\":[\"34\"],\"brand_id\":null,\"image\":null,\"minimum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"maximum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"tag\":null,\"submitter\":\"save\"}', 'created', 'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/129.0.0.0 Safari/537.36', '2409:40e0:1b0:d388:c8c7:d8b9:da3c:acb8', 3, 444, 'RED WIDOW', 'info', '2024-10-24 18:14:41', '2024-10-24 18:14:41'),
(2368, 3, 'product', '{\"name\":\"LEMON\",\"model\":\"Botble\\\\Ecommerce\\\\Models\\\\Product\",\"slug\":\"lemon\",\"slug_id\":\"0\",\"is_slug_editable\":\"1\",\"description\":\"<p>This species\\u2019 distribution is somewhat confusing. The type locality is vague (see below), and the majority of subsequent reports pertain to&nbsp;the rio Tapaj\\u00f3s&nbsp;basins&nbsp;in central Brazil, one of the primary affluents of the lower Amazon River basin. The species is thus often assumed to be endemic to this watershed, but at least one&nbsp;field observation suggests that it also occurs in&nbsp;the rio Xingu system which borders the Tapaj\\u00f3s to the east<\\/p><p>Perhaps looks best&nbsp;in an arrangement comprising a sandy substrate plus some driftwood roots and branches, or heavily-planted planted set-up.<\\/p><p>The addition of dried leaf litter would further emphasise the natural feel and as well as offering additional cover for the fish brings with it the growth of microbe colonies as decomposition occurs.<\\/p><p>The latter are useful since they provide an additional food source for both adults and fry while the humic substances released by decaying leaves are also considered beneficial.<\\/p>\",\"content\":null,\"images\":[null,\"lemon-min-300x300.jpg\"],\"product_type\":\"physical\",\"sale_type\":\"0\",\"sku\":null,\"price\":\"0\",\"sale_price\":null,\"start_date\":null,\"end_date\":null,\"cost_per_item\":\"0\",\"product_id\":null,\"barcode\":null,\"with_storehouse_management\":\"0\",\"quantity\":\"0\",\"allow_checkout_when_out_of_stock\":\"0\",\"stock_status\":\"in_stock\",\"weight\":\"0\",\"length\":\"0\",\"wide\":\"0\",\"height\":\"0\",\"is_added_attributes\":\"0\",\"has_product_options\":\"1\",\"related_products\":null,\"faq_schema_config\":\"[]\",\"seo_meta\":{\"seo_title\":null,\"seo_description\":null,\"index\":\"index\"},\"seo_meta_image\":null,\"layout\":null,\"is_popular\":\"0\",\"status\":\"published\",\"store_id\":null,\"is_featured\":\"0\",\"categories\":[\"34\"],\"brand_id\":null,\"image\":null,\"minimum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"maximum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"tag\":null,\"submitter\":\"save\"}', 'created', 'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/129.0.0.0 Safari/537.36', '2409:40e0:1b0:d388:c8c7:d8b9:da3c:acb8', 3, 445, 'LEMON', 'info', '2024-10-24 18:18:48', '2024-10-24 18:18:48'),
(2369, 3, 'product', '{\"name\":\"GLOW LIGHT\",\"model\":\"Botble\\\\Ecommerce\\\\Models\\\\Product\",\"slug\":\"glow-light\",\"slug_id\":\"0\",\"is_slug_editable\":\"1\",\"description\":\"<p>The glowlight&nbsp;<a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.thesprucepets.com\\/emperor-tetra-1381832\\\" data-component=\\\"link\\\" data-source=\\\"inlineLink\\\" data-type=\\\"internalLink\\\" data-ordinal=\\\"1\\\">tetra<\\/a>&nbsp;is absolutely gorgeous and surprisingly easy to care for. Originating in the Essequibo River of Guyana, it is easygoing and peaceful and can survive in a fairly wide range of aquarium environments. Because they are schooling fish, you\'ll want to keep at least six glowlight tetras in your aquarium.<\\/p>\",\"content\":null,\"images\":[null,\"glowlight-min-300x300.jpg\"],\"product_type\":\"physical\",\"sale_type\":\"0\",\"sku\":null,\"price\":\"0\",\"sale_price\":null,\"start_date\":null,\"end_date\":null,\"cost_per_item\":\"0\",\"product_id\":null,\"barcode\":null,\"with_storehouse_management\":\"0\",\"quantity\":\"0\",\"allow_checkout_when_out_of_stock\":\"0\",\"stock_status\":\"in_stock\",\"weight\":\"0\",\"length\":\"0\",\"wide\":\"0\",\"height\":\"0\",\"is_added_attributes\":\"0\",\"has_product_options\":\"1\",\"related_products\":null,\"faq_schema_config\":\"[]\",\"seo_meta\":{\"seo_title\":null,\"seo_description\":null,\"index\":\"index\"},\"seo_meta_image\":null,\"layout\":null,\"is_popular\":\"0\",\"status\":\"published\",\"store_id\":null,\"is_featured\":\"0\",\"categories\":[\"34\"],\"brand_id\":null,\"image\":null,\"minimum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"maximum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"tag\":null,\"submitter\":\"save\"}', 'created', 'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/129.0.0.0 Safari/537.36', '2409:40e0:1b0:d388:c8c7:d8b9:da3c:acb8', 3, 446, 'GLOW LIGHT', 'info', '2024-10-24 18:19:44', '2024-10-24 18:19:44'),
(2370, 3, 'product', '{\"name\":\"RED PENCIL\",\"model\":\"Botble\\\\Ecommerce\\\\Models\\\\Product\",\"slug\":\"red-pencil\",\"slug_id\":\"0\",\"is_slug_editable\":\"1\",\"description\":\"<p>Red Pencil Tetra is one of the most beautiful species of pencilfish. Its adaptable has a pleasant demeanor and may just be the perfect aquarium fish.<\\/p><p><span data-preserver-spaces=\\\"true\\\">Red Pencil Tetra: This is a very popular smaller pencil fish called the Red Pencilfish (Nannostomus beckfordi) has a crimson upper half, a black stripe, and a white bottom.<\\/span><\\/p><p><span data-preserver-spaces=\\\"true\\\">The \\u201cnose\\u201d of the male has a crimson mark on it. Both genders have bluish\\/white bottom fins. They originate from Guyana, Suriname, and French Guiana, as well as the eastern Amazon drainage in the Brazilian states of Amap\\u00e1 and Par\\u00e1.<\\/span><\\/p><p><span data-preserver-spaces=\\\"true\\\">These are captive-raised with an emphasis on increased red coloration. They are perfect community fish with other similar-sized fish.<\\/span><\\/p><p><span data-preserver-spaces=\\\"true\\\">Adult size for them is less than 1.5 inches. They are the ideal addition to a tank that is at least 10 gallons in size and has calm fish of the same size, such as little tetras and rasboras.<\\/span><\\/p><p><span data-preserver-spaces=\\\"true\\\">They benefit from living plants since they like being around them. For them to feel at home in their aquariums, it is recommended that they be kept in groups of at least ten.<\\/span><\\/p><p><span data-preserver-spaces=\\\"true\\\">When men and females are together, the males will have more vibrant colors to stand out from the other members of the group.<\\/span><\\/p><p><span data-preserver-spaces=\\\"true\\\">The aquarium should have rockwork, vegetation, and driftwood to mimic their natural habitat. It is highly advised to utilize Indian Almond or Guava leaves because they also like tannins in their water.<\\/span><\\/p><p><span data-preserver-spaces=\\\"true\\\">They also prefer a darkened aquarium, so keeping floating plants is advised to reduce the amount of light that reaches them. The use of a sponge filter is advised for gentle filtration. Because the red pencil fish is likely to eat young shrimp, we do not advise keeping this fish near shrimp colonies.<\\/span><\\/p><p><i><span data-preserver-spaces=\\\"true\\\"><strong>II. You would love the fish because\\u2026<\\/strong><\\/span><\\/i><\\/p><p><span data-preserver-spaces=\\\"true\\\">You will be intrigued by this species because of its striking red coloring.<\\/span><\\/p><p><span data-preserver-spaces=\\\"true\\\">The demand for this fish, which is excellent for such a setup, has increased as a result of the exploding popularity of planted micro tanks.<\\/span><\\/p><p><span data-preserver-spaces=\\\"true\\\">Its habitat and population are allegedly severely constrained, but fortunately, the availability of specimens through tank breeding has reduced the need for wild collection.<\\/span><\\/p><p><span data-preserver-spaces=\\\"true\\\">A very active and a schooling specie, this should always be maintained in groups to prevent aggression. A tank with plants is ideal. Any fish that isn\\u2019t too big to consume can be kept with them.<\\/span><\\/p><p><i><span data-preserver-spaces=\\\"true\\\"><strong>III. Is this fish species peaceful or hostile?<\\/strong><\\/span><\\/i><\\/p><p><span data-preserver-spaces=\\\"true\\\">Overall peaceful fish.<\\/span><\\/p><p><i><span data-preserver-spaces=\\\"true\\\"><strong>IV. Species compatibility<\\/strong><\\/span><\\/i><\\/p><p><span data-preserver-spaces=\\\"true\\\">Danios, Corydoras, Discus fish, most Livebearers, and some peaceful Dwarf Cichlids, such as Apistogramma.<\\/span><\\/p><p><i><span data-preserver-spaces=\\\"true\\\"><strong>V. How to feed this species?<\\/strong><\\/span><\\/i><\\/p><p><span data-preserver-spaces=\\\"true\\\">Little pellets, prepared fish food, flake food, frozen food, dry food, and anything else that fish can consume in general will be enjoyed by it.<\\/span><\\/p>\",\"content\":null,\"images\":[null,\"red-pencil-min-300x300.jpg\"],\"product_type\":\"physical\",\"sale_type\":\"0\",\"sku\":null,\"price\":\"0\",\"sale_price\":null,\"start_date\":null,\"end_date\":null,\"cost_per_item\":\"0\",\"product_id\":null,\"barcode\":null,\"with_storehouse_management\":\"0\",\"quantity\":\"0\",\"allow_checkout_when_out_of_stock\":\"0\",\"stock_status\":\"in_stock\",\"weight\":\"0\",\"length\":\"0\",\"wide\":\"0\",\"height\":\"0\",\"is_added_attributes\":\"0\",\"has_product_options\":\"1\",\"related_products\":null,\"faq_schema_config\":\"[]\",\"seo_meta\":{\"seo_title\":null,\"seo_description\":null,\"index\":\"index\"},\"seo_meta_image\":null,\"layout\":null,\"is_popular\":\"0\",\"status\":\"published\",\"store_id\":null,\"is_featured\":\"0\",\"categories\":[\"34\"],\"brand_id\":null,\"image\":null,\"minimum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"maximum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"tag\":null,\"submitter\":\"save\"}', 'created', 'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/129.0.0.0 Safari/537.36', '2409:40e0:1b0:d388:c8c7:d8b9:da3c:acb8', 3, 447, 'RED PENCIL', 'info', '2024-10-24 18:21:29', '2024-10-24 18:21:29'),
(2371, 3, 'product', '{\"name\":\"CARDINAL\",\"model\":\"Botble\\\\Ecommerce\\\\Models\\\\Product\",\"slug\":\"cardinal\",\"slug_id\":\"0\",\"is_slug_editable\":\"1\",\"description\":\"<p class=\\\"comp mntl-sc-block lifestyle-sc-block-html mntl-sc-block-html text-passage u-how-to-title-align\\\" id=\\\"mntl-sc-block_1-0\\\">Arguably the most popular of the small tetras, the cardinal tetra is similar in appearance to a longtime aquarium favorite, the&nbsp;<a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.thesprucepets.com\\/neon-tetra-paracheirodon-1381835\\\" data-component=\\\"link\\\" data-source=\\\"inlineLink\\\" data-type=\\\"internalLink\\\" data-ordinal=\\\"1\\\">neon tetra<\\/a>\\u2014you can tell them apart by one particular detail: a slight difference in their red stripe.&nbsp;Cardinal tetras are active schooling fish, and they live&nbsp;peacefully in a community aquarium.<\\/p><div class=\\\"comp mntl-sc-block lifestyle-sc-block-adslot mntl-sc-block-adslot mntl-block u-no-article-width-restriction\\\" id=\\\"mntl-sc-block_2-0\\\">&nbsp;<\\/div><p class=\\\"comp mntl-sc-block lifestyle-sc-block-html mntl-sc-block-html text-passage u-how-to-title-align\\\" id=\\\"mntl-sc-block_3-0\\\">Although they are difficult to breed in captivity, tetras remain a very popular aquarium fish. Here\\u2019s everything you need to know to keep cardinal tetras happy and healthy in your tank.<\\/p>\",\"content\":null,\"images\":[null,\"cardinal-min-300x300.jpg\"],\"product_type\":\"physical\",\"sale_type\":\"0\",\"sku\":null,\"price\":\"0\",\"sale_price\":null,\"start_date\":null,\"end_date\":null,\"cost_per_item\":\"0\",\"product_id\":null,\"barcode\":null,\"with_storehouse_management\":\"0\",\"quantity\":\"0\",\"allow_checkout_when_out_of_stock\":\"0\",\"stock_status\":\"in_stock\",\"weight\":\"0\",\"length\":\"0\",\"wide\":\"0\",\"height\":\"0\",\"is_added_attributes\":\"0\",\"has_product_options\":\"1\",\"related_products\":null,\"faq_schema_config\":\"[]\",\"seo_meta\":{\"seo_title\":null,\"seo_description\":null,\"index\":\"index\"},\"seo_meta_image\":null,\"layout\":null,\"is_popular\":\"0\",\"status\":\"published\",\"store_id\":null,\"is_featured\":\"0\",\"categories\":[\"34\"],\"brand_id\":null,\"image\":null,\"minimum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"maximum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"tag\":null,\"submitter\":\"save\"}', 'created', 'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/129.0.0.0 Safari/537.36', '2409:40e0:1b0:d388:c8c7:d8b9:da3c:acb8', 3, 448, 'CARDINAL', 'info', '2024-10-24 18:22:53', '2024-10-24 18:22:53'),
(2372, 3, 'product', '{\"name\":\"NEON\",\"model\":\"Botble\\\\Ecommerce\\\\Models\\\\Product\",\"slug\":\"neon\",\"slug_id\":\"0\",\"is_slug_editable\":\"1\",\"description\":\"<p><strong>Common Names:<\\/strong>&nbsp;Neon tetra, neon fish<\\/p><p><strong>Scientific Name:&nbsp;<\\/strong><i>Paracheirodon innesi<\\/i><\\/p><p><strong>Adult Size:&nbsp;<\\/strong>1.5 inches (4 centimeters)<\\/p><p><strong>Life Expectancy:&nbsp;<\\/strong>5 to 10 years<\\/p>\",\"content\":null,\"images\":[null,\"neon-min-300x300.jpg\"],\"product_type\":\"physical\",\"sale_type\":\"0\",\"sku\":null,\"price\":\"0\",\"sale_price\":null,\"start_date\":null,\"end_date\":null,\"cost_per_item\":\"0\",\"product_id\":null,\"barcode\":null,\"with_storehouse_management\":\"0\",\"quantity\":\"0\",\"allow_checkout_when_out_of_stock\":\"0\",\"stock_status\":\"in_stock\",\"weight\":\"0\",\"length\":\"0\",\"wide\":\"0\",\"height\":\"0\",\"is_added_attributes\":\"0\",\"has_product_options\":\"1\",\"related_products\":null,\"faq_schema_config\":\"[]\",\"seo_meta\":{\"seo_title\":null,\"seo_description\":null,\"index\":\"index\"},\"seo_meta_image\":null,\"layout\":null,\"is_popular\":\"0\",\"status\":\"published\",\"store_id\":null,\"is_featured\":\"0\",\"categories\":[\"34\"],\"brand_id\":null,\"image\":null,\"minimum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"maximum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"tag\":null,\"submitter\":\"save\"}', 'created', 'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/129.0.0.0 Safari/537.36', '2409:40e0:1b0:d388:c8c7:d8b9:da3c:acb8', 3, 449, 'NEON', 'info', '2024-10-24 18:26:47', '2024-10-24 18:26:47'),
