(2492, 3, 'product', '{\"name\":\"CARDINAL\",\"model\":\"Botble\\\\Ecommerce\\\\Models\\\\Product\",\"slug\":\"cardinal\",\"slug_id\":\"484\",\"is_slug_editable\":\"1\",\"description\":\"<p class=\\\"comp mntl-sc-block lifestyle-sc-block-html mntl-sc-block-html text-passage u-how-to-title-align\\\" id=\\\"mntl-sc-block_1-0\\\">Arguably the most popular of the small tetras, the cardinal tetra is similar in appearance to a longtime aquarium favorite, the&nbsp;<a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.thesprucepets.com\\/neon-tetra-paracheirodon-1381835\\\">neon tetra<\\/a>\\u2014you can tell them apart by one particular detail: a slight difference in their red stripe.&nbsp;Cardinal tetras are active schooling fish, and they live&nbsp;peacefully in a community aquarium.<\\/p><div class=\\\"comp mntl-sc-block lifestyle-sc-block-adslot mntl-sc-block-adslot mntl-block u-no-article-width-restriction\\\" id=\\\"mntl-sc-block_2-0\\\">&nbsp;<\\/div><p class=\\\"comp mntl-sc-block lifestyle-sc-block-html mntl-sc-block-html text-passage u-how-to-title-align\\\" id=\\\"mntl-sc-block_3-0\\\">Although they are difficult to breed in captivity, tetras remain a very popular aquarium fish. Here\\u2019s everything you need to know to keep cardinal tetras happy and healthy in your tank.<\\/p>\",\"content\":null,\"images\":[null,\"cardinal-min-300x300.jpg\"],\"product_type\":\"physical\",\"sale_type\":\"0\",\"sku\":null,\"price\":\"0\",\"sale_price\":null,\"start_date\":null,\"end_date\":null,\"cost_per_item\":\"0\",\"product_id\":\"448\",\"barcode\":null,\"with_storehouse_management\":\"0\",\"quantity\":\"0\",\"allow_checkout_when_out_of_stock\":\"0\",\"stock_status\":\"in_stock\",\"weight\":\"0\",\"length\":\"0\",\"wide\":\"0\",\"height\":\"0\",\"is_added_attributes\":\"0\",\"has_product_options\":\"1\",\"related_products\":null,\"faq_schema_config\":[[{\"key\":\"question\",\"value\":null},{\"key\":\"answer\",\"value\":null}]],\"seo_meta\":{\"seo_title\":null,\"seo_description\":null,\"index\":\"ind