(2531, 3, 'product', '{\"name\":\"TROCOLOUR ORANDA\",\"model\":\"Botble\\\\Ecommerce\\\\Models\\\\Product\",\"slug\":\"trocolour-oranda\",\"slug_id\":\"464\",\"is_slug_editable\":\"1\",\"description\":\"<p>The Tri-Color Oranda is a distinctive and visually striking variety of the Oranda Goldfish (Carassius auratus). Oranda Goldfish are known for their unique appearance, characterized by a prominent growth on the head called a \\u201cwen\\u201d or \\u201chood,\\u201d which can cover their entire head. The Tri-Color Oranda, as the name suggests, is recognized for its tri-coloration and impressive wen growth. Here are some key features and information about the Tri-Color Oranda:<\\/p><p>Tri-Color Orandas have a tri-colored pattern, typically consisting of red, white, and black markings. The red coloration can appear on the body, while the white and black colors are often on the fins, tail, and head. The exact distribution of colors may vary among individual fish.<\\/p><p>One of the standout features of the Tri-Color Oranda is the growth of the wen or hood. The wen covers the head and can develop into a substantial and fleshy mass, giving the fish a unique and charming appearance. The wen\\u2019s coloration may vary but often matches the body color.<\\/p><p>Oranda Goldfish, including the Tri-Color variety, can grow relatively large. They can reach lengths of up to 8 to 12 inches (20 to 30 centimeters) or even more in well-maintained aquariums or ponds.<\\/p><p>Tri-Color Orandas require a spacious aquarium with ample room to swim, as well as good water quality. They are hardy fish, but their wen growth requires careful attention. The wen is sensitive and prone to injury, so it\\u2019s essential to maintain excellent water conditions to prevent infections or injuries.<\\/p><p>Provide your Tri-Color Oranda with a well-planted aquarium with hiding places and open swimming areas. Ensure that the tank has a suitable filtration system to maintain water quality.<\\/p><p>Oranda Goldfish are generally peaceful and sociable. They are known for their curious and friendly nature, making them enjoyable to observe in a community tank.<\\/p><p>Tri-Color Orandas are beloved by fish enthusiasts for their unique and eye-catching appearance. Their striking coloration, distinctive wen growth, and friendly disposition make them a popular choice for aquarium keepers who are looking to add a touch of elegance to their aquatic displays. Proper care and attention to water quality are essential to ensure the health and well-being of these remarkable fish.<\\/p><p><span><strong>III. Is this fish species peaceful or hostile?<\\/strong><\\/span><\\/p><p><span>Extremely peaceful fish.<\\/span><\\/p><p><i><span><strong>IV. Species compatibility<\\/strong><\\/span><\\/i><\\/p><p>When keeping Tri-Color Orandas, choose tank mates that are peaceful and won\\u2019t nip at their long fins or disturb their wen growth. Other goldfish varieties, such as other Orandas or fancy goldfish, can make suitable companions.<\\/p><p>Avoid keeping them with aggressive or fin-nipping fish, as their delicate fins can be easily damaged.<\\/p><p><i><span><strong>V. How to feed this species?<\\/strong><\\/span><\\/i><\\/p><p>These goldfish are omnivorous and enjoy a varied diet. You can feed them high-quality pellets or flakes formulated for goldfish, as well as occasional treats such as live or frozen foods like brine shrimp, bloodworms, and vegetables like peas.<\\/p>\",\"content\":null,\"images\":[null,\"trocolour-oranda-min-300x300.jpg\"],\"product_type\":\"physical\",\"botble-ecommerce-tables-product-variation-table-428_length\":\"10\",\"has_product_options\":\"1\",\"related_products\":null,\"faq_schema_config\":[[{\"key\":\"question\",\"value\":null},{\"key\":\"answer\",\"value\":null}]],\"seo_meta\":{\"seo_title\":null,\"seo_description\":null,\"index\":\"index\"},\"seo_meta_image\":null,\"language\":\"en_US\",\"layout\":null,\"is_popular\":\"0\",\"status\":\"published\",\"store_id\":null,\"is_featured\":\"0\",\"categories\":[\"48\"],\"brand_id\":null,\"sku\":null,\"image\":\"trocolour-oranda-min-300x300.jpg\",\"product_labels\":[\"2\"],\"minimum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"maximum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"tag\":null,\"submitter\":\"save\"}', 'updated', 'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/129.0.0.0 Safari/537.36', '43.231.241.174', 3, 428, 'TROCOLOUR ORANDA', 'primary', '2024-10-28 13:10:02', '2024-10-28 13:10:02'),
(2532, 3, 'product', '{\"name\":\"ASSAMISE BADIS\",\"model\":\"Botble\\\\Ecommerce\\\\Models\\\\Product\",\"slug\":\"assamise-badis\",\"slug_id\":\"465\",\"is_slug_editable\":\"1\",\"description\":\"<p>The Badis assamensis, commonly known as the Assam Badis, is a captivating freshwater fish species native to parts of India and Bangladesh. Specifically found in the Brahmaputra River basin, they inhabit slow-moving waters, including streams and swamps.<\\/p><p>Physically, the Assam Badis is characterized by its elongated body and vibrant coloration. Males typically display more intense colors, featuring shades of red, blue, and green, especially during courtship and spawning. They typically grow to a size of about 2 to 3 inches (5-7.5 cm).<\\/p><p>In their natural habitat, Assam Badis thrive in densely planted aquariums with areas for swimming and hiding spots provided by plants and small caves. They prefer soft to slightly hard water conditions, and maintaining a stable and clean environment with proper filtration contributes to their overall well-being.<\\/p><p>Known for their territorial behavior, Assam Badis are best kept in a species-only tank or with very small, peaceful tankmates. They are not suitable for community aquariums due to their territorial nature. A well-balanced diet, including live or frozen foods like small insects and microorganisms, meets their nutritional needs.<\\/p><p>Maintaining water conditions within the range of 72-79\\u00b0F (22-26\\u00b0C) and a pH level between 6.0 to 7.5 is advisable. Regular water changes and proper filtration contribute to their health and vitality.<\\/p><p>Breeding Assam Badis in captivity is possible but can be challenging due to their specific requirements. Creating a breeding tank with soft, acidic water and providing hiding spots with dense vegetation encourage successful spawning. Males intensify their colors during courtship.<\\/p><p>In summary, the Assam Badis is a captivating and colorful addition to aquariums, appreciated for its vibrant hues and unique behaviors. Recreating their natural habitat from the Brahmaputra River basin and adhering to proper care conditions contribute to their well-being in captivity.<\\/p>\",\"content\":null,\"images\":[null,\"assamise-badis-min-300x300.jpg\"],\"product_type\":\"physical\",\"sale_type\":\"0\",\"sku\":null,\"price\":\"0\",\"sale_price\":null,\"start_date\":null,\"end_date\":null,\"cost_per_item\":\"0\",\"product_id\":\"429\",\"barcode\":null,\"with_storehouse_management\":\"0\",\"quantity\":\"0\",\"allow_checkout_when_out_of_stock\":\"0\",\"stock_status\":\"in_stock\",\"weight\":\"0\",\"length\":\"0\",\"wide\":\"0\",\"height\":\"0\",\"is_added_attributes\":\"0\",\"has_product_options\":\"1\",\"related_products\":null,\"faq_schema_config\":[[{\"key\":\"question\",\"value\":null},{\"key\":\"answer\",\"value\":null}]],\"seo_meta\":{\"seo_title\":null,\"seo_description\":null,\"index\":\"index\"},\"seo_meta_image\":null,\"language\":\"en_US\",\"layout\":null,\"is_popular\":\"0\",\"status\":\"published\",\"store_id\":null,\"is_featured\":\"0\",\"categories\":[\"45\",\"46\",\"47\",\"48\",\"49\"],\"brand_id\":null,\"image\":\"assamise-badis-min-300x300.jpg\",\"minimum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"maximum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"tag\":null,\"submitter\":\"save\"}', 'updated', 'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/129.0.0.0 Safari/537.36', '43.231.241.174', 3, 429, 'ASSAMISE BADIS', 'primary', '2024-10-28 13:11:14', '2024-10-28 13:11:14'),
(2533, 3, 'product', '{\"name\":\"GREEN TIGER BARB\",\"model\":\"Botble\\\\Ecommerce\\\\Models\\\\Product\",\"slug\":\"green-tiger-barb\",\"slug_id\":\"462\",\"is_slug_editable\":\"1\",\"description\":\"<p>The Green Tiger Barb (<i>Pethia nigrofasciata<\\/i>) is a very&nbsp;peaceful species that is an excellent fish for the community planted aquarium. It is known for its small size and black striping, but is most desired for the brilliant ruby coloration that males develop during spawning behaviour. This fish is also rather versatile regarding water conditions.<\\/p><p>The Green Tiger Barb typically occupies the top and middle level of the water column, although it can often be seen swimming and feeding in the middle and bottom levels as well. It is safe with other peaceful, small fish. It may prey on smaller dwarf shrimp and their fry. Larger, peaceful invertebrates can make good tank mates. The Green Tiger Barb must be kept in groups of 6 or more, although larger groups are more ideal so that subdominant specimens are not bullied by dominant individuals during breeding behaviour. Its natural habitat is tropical rainforest areas that typically have clear water. It requires clean water to thrive and it will display optimal coloration and health in a planted aquarium with dark substrate.<\\/p><p>&nbsp;<\\/p><p>While not a picky eater, The Green Tiger Barb will thrive and remain very colourful on a varied diet of&nbsp;omnivorous foods. High-quality flake food, pellets, and live, frozen, or freeze-dried&nbsp;<i>Artemia<\\/i>, microworms,&nbsp;<i>Tubifex<\\/i>, and finely chopped bloodworms will all be readily accepted. Some vegetable matter, especially dry food high in vegetable content, is essential for optimal health and coloration.<\\/p><div class=\\\"rte sm:text-start text-start js-product-description\\\"><p>What We Like About This Fish:<\\/p><ul><li>Males develop beautiful green coloration with maturity<\\/li><li>Peaceful disposition with fish and peaceful invertebrates too large to be considered prey<\\/li><li>Very active and noticeable fish in any aquarium<\\/li><li>Ideal for planted aquariums<\\/li><\\/ul><p>&nbsp;<\\/p><p><strong>RECOMMENDED TANK PARAMETERS:<\\/strong><\\/p><p>&nbsp;<\\/p><ul><li>Temperature: 68 - 81\\u00b0 F (20\\u00b0-27\\u00b0 C)<\\/li><li>pH:&nbsp;5.5 - 7.5<\\/li><li>KH: 3 - 12 dKH<\\/li><li>Minimum Tank Size: 20 gallons for a group of 6 \\u2013 8<\\/li><\\/ul><p>&nbsp;<\\/p><p><strong>CARE INFORMATION:<\\/strong><\\/p><ul><li>Diet: Omnivore\\/Micropredator. Will easily accept high quality dry and frozen foods of appropriate size. Requires a varied diet, including vegetable matter, for optimal health and coloration.<\\/li><li><u>Social Behaviour:<\\/u>&nbsp;Peaceful, schooling\\/shoaling.<\\/li><\\/ul><\\/div><div class=\\\"dbtfy-back-in-stock-container\\\"><div class=\\\"dbtfy-back-in-stock\\\">&nbsp;<\\/div><\\/div>\",\"content\":null,\"images\":[null,\"green-tiger-barb-min-300x300.jpg\"],\"product_type\":\"physical\",\"sale_type\":\"0\",\"sku\":null,\"price\":\"0\",\"sale_price\":null,\"start_date\":null,\"end_date\":null,\"cost_per_item\":\"0\",\"product_id\":\"426\",\"barcode\":null,\"with_storehouse_management\":\"0\",\"quantity\":\"0\",\"allow_checkout_when_out_of_stock\":\"0\",\"stock_status\":\"in_stock\",\"weight\":\"0\",\"length\":\"0\",\"wide\":\"0\",\"height\":\"0\",\"is_added_attributes\":\"0\",\"has_product_options\":\"1\",\"related_products\":null,\"faq_schema_config\":[[{\"key\":\"question\",\"value\":null},{\"key\":\"answer\",\"value\":null}]],\"seo_meta\":{\"seo_title\":null,\"seo_description\":null,\"index\":\"index\"},\"seo_meta_image\":null,\"language\":\"en_US\",\"layout\":null,\"is_popular\":\"0\",\"status\":\"published\",\"store_id\":null,\"is_featured\":\"0\",\"categories\":[\"45\",\"46\",\"47\",\"48\",\"49\"],\"brand_id\":null,\"image\":\"green-tiger-barb-min-300x300.jpg\",\"minimum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"maximum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"tag\":null,\"submitter\":\"save\"}', 'updated', 'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/129.0.0.0 Safari/537.36', '43.231.241.174', 3, 426, 'GREEN TIGER BARB', 'primary', '2024-10-28 13:13:02', '2024-10-28 13:13:02'),
