(2648, 3, 'product', '{\"name\":\"UARU CICHLID\",\"model\":\"Botble\\\\Ecommerce\\\\Models\\\\Product\",\"slug\":\"uaru-cichlid-1\",\"slug_id\":\"494\",\"is_slug_editable\":\"1\",\"description\":\"<p>A fish with real character which needs a large, well-filtered, softwater aquarium and frequent partial water changes to remain in good health.Best kept in groups with non-aggressive tankmates.<\\/p><h2 id=\\\"section_care\\\">Care<\\/h2><p>Uaru are gentle giants which congregate in small social groups within their natural blackwater habitat. The water is warm, and very soft and acidic, and these conditions must be recreated in the home aquarium (peat filtration highly recommended) in order for this species to do well. In the wild, these majestic fish prefer the safety of shady areas amongst vegetation and fallen trees, so this should be replicated in the home aquarium as best as possible. The tank must be at least 48\\\" long and should incorporate dark substrate and decor. Lighting should be dim. The aquarium should be aquascaped with plenty of bogwood and robust plants such as&nbsp;<i>Microsorum pteropus<\\/i>, or plastic\\/silk varieties. Uaru very much enjoy eating fine-leaved or soft-leaved plants; indeed their faces will almost appear to \\\"light up\\\" if you present them with some&nbsp;<i>Cabomba caroliniana<\\/i>&nbsp;from time to time, a particular favourite! Uaru are peaceful fish and can be kept alongside other medium-large sized peaceable species. They should not be housed with aggressive or boisterous fish. The only time they are likely to become confrontational is if two of the fish pair off, at which time they should be separated from the rest of the group. Uaru are very susceptible to poor water conditions, so good filtration and frequent partial water changes are a must. Ideally they will only be added to mature aquaria. Not recommended for beginners. Young specimens show a \\\"spotted\\\" pattern and undergo a dramatic transformation into their adult form. May also be seen on sale as Triangle Cichlid.<\\/p><h2 id=\\\"section_feeding\\\">Feeding<\\/h2><p>It is important that Uaru receive a varied diet, incorporating a good amount of vegetable matter. They can sometimes be a little picky, but will generally feed on: flake, green flake, slow-sinking pellets\\/granular foods, lettuce, spinach, kale, cucumber, soft-leaved aquatic plants (such as&nbsp;<i>Cabomba caroliniana<\\/i>), frozen foods such as mosquito larvae, Mysis shrimp, Krill, chopped prawns (salad shrimp) etc.<\\/p>\",\"content\":null,\"images\":[null,\"uaru-cichlid-min-300x300-1.jpg\"],\"product_type\":\"physical\",\"sale_type\":\"0\",\"sku\":null,\"price\":\"1500\",\"sale_price\":null,\"start_date\":null,\"end_date\":null,\"cost_per_item\":\"0\",\"product_id\":\"452\",\"barcode\":null,\"with_storehouse_management\":\"0\",\"quantity\":\"0\",\"allow_checkout_when_out_of_stock\":\"0\",\"stock_status\":\"in_stock\",\"weight\":\"0\",\"length\":\"0\",\"wide\":\"0\",\"height\":\"0\",\"is_added_attributes\":\"0\",\"has_product_options\":\"1\",\"related_products\":null,\"faq_schema_config\":[[{\"key\":\"question\",\"value\":null},{\"key\":\"answer\",\"value\":null}]],\"seo_meta\":{\"seo_title\":null,\"seo_description\":null,\"index\":\"index\"},\"seo_meta_image\":null,\"language\":\"en_US\",\"layout\":null,\"is_popular\":\"0\",\"status\":\"published\",\"store_id\":null,\"is_featured\":\"0\",\"categories\":[\"45\"],\"brand_id\":null,\"image\":\"uaru-cichlid-min-300x300-1.jpg\",\"minimum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"maximum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"tag\":null,\"submitter\":\"apply\"}', 'updated', 'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/130.0.0.0 Safari/537.36', '2405:201:800e:d0d0:ad7b:3351:47bb:df30', 3, 452, 'UARU CICHLID', 'primary', '2024-11-05 16:06:21', '2024-11-05 16:06:21'),
(2649, 3, 'product', '{\"name\":\"UARU CICHLID\",\"model\":\"Botble\\\\Ecommerce\\\\Models\\\\Product\",\"slug\":\"uaru-cichlid-1\",\"slug_id\":\"494\",\"is_slug_editable\":\"1\",\"description\":\"<p>A fish with real character which needs a large, well-filtered, softwater aquarium and frequent partial water changes to remain in good health.Best kept in groups with non-aggressive tankmates.<\\/p><h2 id=\\\"section_care\\\">Care<\\/h2><p>Uaru are gentle giants which congregate in small social groups within their natural blackwater habitat. The water is warm, and very soft and acidic, and these conditions must be recreated in the home aquarium (peat filtration highly recommended) in order for this species to do well. In the wild, these majestic fish prefer the safety of shady areas amongst vegetation and fallen trees, so this should be replicated in the home aquarium as best as possible. The tank must be at least 48\\\" long and should incorporate dark substrate and decor. Lighting should be dim. The aquarium should be aquascaped with plenty of bogwood and robust plants such as&nbsp;<i>Microsorum pteropus<\\/i>, or plastic\\/silk varieties. Uaru very much enjoy eating fine-leaved or soft-leaved plants; indeed their faces will almost appear to \\\"light up\\\" if you present them with some&nbsp;<i>Cabomba caroliniana<\\/i>&nbsp;from time to time, a particular favourite! Uaru are peaceful fish and can be kept alongside other medium-large sized peaceable species. They should not be housed with aggressive or boisterous fish. The only time they are likely to become confrontational is if two of the fish pair off, at which time they should be separated from the rest of the group. Uaru are very susceptible to poor water conditions, so good filtration and frequent partial water changes are a must. Ideally they will only be added to mature aquaria. Not recommended for beginners. Young specimens show a \\\"spotted\\\" pattern and undergo a dramatic transformation into their adult form. May also be seen on sale as Triangle Cichlid.<\\/p><h2 id=\\\"section_feeding\\\">Feeding<\\/h2><p>It is important that Uaru receive a varied diet, incorporating a good amount of vegetable matter. They can sometimes be a little picky, but will generally feed on: flake, green flake, slow-sinking pellets\\/granular foods, lettuce, spinach, kale, cucumber, soft-leaved aquatic plants (such as&nbsp;<i>Cabomba caroliniana<\\/i>), frozen foods such as mosquito larvae, Mysis shrimp, Krill, chopped prawns (salad shrimp) etc.<\\/p>\",\"content\":null,\"images\":[null,\"uaru-cichlid-min-300x300-1.jpg\"],\"product_type\":\"physical\",\"sale_type\":\"0\",\"sku\":null,\"price\":\"1500\",\"sale_price\":null,\"start_date\":null,\"end_date\":null,\"cost_per_item\":\"0\",\"product_id\":\"452\",\"barcode\":null,\"with_storehouse_management\":\"0\",\"quantity\":\"0\",\"allow_checkout_when_out_of_stock\":\"0\",\"stock_status\":\"in_stock\",\"weight\":\"0\",\"length\":\"0\",\"wide\":\"0\",\"height\":\"0\",\"is_added_attributes\":\"0\",\"has_product_options\":\"1\",\"related_products\":null,\"faq_schema_config\":[[{\"key\":\"question\",\"value\":null},{\"key\":\"answer\",\"value\":null}]],\"seo_meta\":{\"seo_title\":null,\"seo_description\":null,\"index\":\"index\"},\"seo_meta_image\":null,\"language\":\"en_US\",\"layout\":null,\"is_popular\":\"0\",\"status\":\"published\",\"store_id\":null,\"is_featured\":\"0\",\"categories\":[\"45\"],\"brand_id\":null,\"image\":\"uaru-cichlid-min-300x300-1.jpg\",\"minimum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"maximum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"tag\":null,\"submitter\":\"save\"}', 'updated', 'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/130.0.0.0 Safari/537.36', '2405:201:800e:d0d0:ad7b:3351:47bb:df30', 3, 452, 'UARU CICHLID', 'primary', '2024-11-05 16:06:32', '2024-11-05 16:06:32'),
(2650, 3, 'product', '{\"name\":\"RANI LOACH\",\"model\":\"Botble\\\\Ecommerce\\\\Models\\\\Product\",\"slug\":\"rani-loach-1\",\"slug_id\":\"493\",\"is_slug_editable\":\"1\",\"description\":\"<p><i><strong>Botia dario<\\/strong><\\/i>&nbsp;(<strong>Bengal loach<\\/strong>&nbsp;or&nbsp;<strong>queen loach<\\/strong>) is a species of fish in the loach family Botiidae found in the Brahmaputra and Ganges basins in Bangladesh, Bhutan and northern India. The species is overall widespread.<\\/p><p><i>Botia dario<\\/i> is a good fish to have in tropical aquariums, quickly taking care of pest snail populations and less shy than B. striata. They get as long as 6 inches (150 mm) and are commonly kept in groups of 4 or more. They are omnivores and are fed sinking pellets as well as algae wafers. They also enjoy fresh vegetables, such as cucumber, zucchini, and frozen foods like bloodworms and brine shrimp.<\\/p>\",\"content\":null,\"images\":[null,\"rani-loach-min-300x300-1.jpg\"],\"product_type\":\"physical\",\"sale_type\":\"0\",\"sku\":null,\"price\":\"0\",\"sale_price\":null,\"start_date\":null,\"end_date\":null,\"cost_per_item\":\"0\",\"product_id\":\"451\",\"barcode\":null,\"with_storehouse_management\":\"0\",\"quantity\":\"0\",\"allow_checkout_when_out_of_stock\":\"0\",\"stock_status\":\"in_stock\",\"weight\":\"0\",\"length\":\"0\",\"wide\":\"0\",\"height\":\"0\",\"is_added_attributes\":\"0\",\"has_product_options\":\"1\",\"related_products\":null,\"faq_schema_config\":[[{\"key\":\"question\",\"value\":null},{\"key\":\"answer\",\"value\":null}]],\"seo_meta\":{\"seo_title\":null,\"seo_description\":null,\"index\":\"index\"},\"seo_meta_image\":null,\"language\":\"en_US\",\"layout\":null,\"is_popular\":\"0\",\"status\":\"draft\",\"store_id\":null,\"is_featured\":\"0\",\"categories\":[\"45\"],\"brand_id\":null,\"image\":\"rani-loach-min-300x300-1.jpg\",\"minimum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"maximum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"tag\":null,\"submitter\":\"save\"}', 'updated', 'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/130.0.0.0 Safari/537.36', '2405:201:800e:d0d0:ad7b:3351:47bb:df30', 3, 451, 'RANI LOACH', 'primary', '2024-11-05 16:07:10', '2024-11-05 16:07:10'),
(2651, 3, 'product', '{\"name\":\"RANI LOACH\",\"model\":\"Botble\\\\Ecommerce\\\\Models\\\\Product\",\"slug\":\"rani-loach-1\",\"slug_id\":\"493\",\"is_slug_editable\":\"1\",\"description\":\"<p><i><strong>Botia dario<\\/strong><\\/i>&nbsp;(<strong>Bengal loach<\\/strong>&nbsp;or&nbsp;<strong>queen loach<\\/strong>) is a species of fish in the loach family Botiidae found in the Brahmaputra and Ganges basins in Bangladesh, Bhutan and northern India. The species is overall widespread.<\\/p><p><i>Botia dario<\\/i> is a good fish to have in tropical aquariums, quickly taking care of pest snail populations and less shy than B. striata. They get as long as 6 inches (150 mm) and are commonly kept in groups of 4 or more. They are omnivores and are fed sinking pellets as well as algae wafers. They also enjoy fresh vegetables, such as cucumber, zucchini, and frozen foods like bloodworms and brine shrimp.<\\/p>\",\"content\":null,\"images\":[null,\"rani-loach-min-300x300-1.jpg\"],\"product_type\":\"physical\",\"sale_type\":\"0\",\"sku\":null,\"price\":\"100\",\"sale_price\":null,\"start_date\":null,\"end_date\":null,\"cost_per_item\":\"0\",\"product_id\":\"451\",\"barcode\":null,\"with_storehouse_management\":\"0\",\"quantity\":\"0\",\"allow_checkout_when_out_of_stock\":\"0\",\"stock_status\":\"in_stock\",\"weight\":\"0\",\"length\":\"0\",\"wide\":\"0\",\"height\":\"0\",\"is_added_attributes\":\"0\",\"has_product_options\":\"1\",\"related_products\":null,\"faq_schema_config\":[[{\"key\":\"question\",\"value\":null},{\"key\":\"answer\",\"value\":null}]],\"seo_meta\":{\"seo_title\":null,\"seo_description\":null,\"index\":\"index\"},\"seo_meta_image\":null,\"language\":\"en_US\",\"layout\":null,\"is_popular\":\"0\",\"status\":\"published\",\"store_id\":null,\"is_featured\":\"0\",\"categories\":[\"45\"],\"brand_id\":null,\"image\":\"rani-loach-min-300x300-1.jpg\",\"minimum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"maximum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"tag\":null,\"submitter\":\"apply\"}', 'updated', 'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/130.0.0.0 Safari/537.36', '2405:201:800e:d0d0:ad7b:3351:47bb:df30', 3, 451, 'RANI LOACH', 'primary', '2024-11-05 16:07:47', '2024-11-05 16:07:47'),
(2652, 3, 'product', '{\"name\":\"RANI LOACH\",\"model\":\"Botble\\\\Ecommerce\\\\Models\\\\Product\",\"slug\":\"rani-loach-1\",\"slug_id\":\"493\",\"is_slug_editable\":\"1\",\"description\":\"<p><i><strong>Botia dario<\\/strong><\\/i>&nbsp;(<strong>Bengal loach<\\/strong>&nbsp;or&nbsp;<strong>queen loach<\\/strong>) is a species of fish in the loach family Botiidae found in the Brahmaputra and Ganges basins in Bangladesh, Bhutan and northern India. The species is overall widespread.<\\/p><p><i>Botia dario<\\/i> is a good fish to have in tropical aquariums, quickly taking care of pest snail populations and less shy than B. striata. They get as long as 6 inches (150 mm) and are commonly kept in groups of 4 or more. They are omnivores and are fed sinking pellets as well as algae wafers. They also enjoy fresh vegetables, such as cucumber, zucchini, and frozen foods like bloodworms and brine shrimp.<\\/p>\",\"content\":null,\"images\":[null,\"rani-loach-min-300x300-1.jpg\"],\"product_type\":\"physical\",\"sale_type\":\"0\",\"sku\":null,\"price\":\"100\",\"sale_price\":null,\"start_date\":null,\"end_date\":null,\"cost_per_item\":\"0\",\"product_id\":\"451\",\"barcode\":null,\"with_storehouse_management\":\"0\",\"quantity\":\"0\",\"allow_checkout_when_out_of_stock\":\"0\",\"stock_status\":\"in_stock\",\"weight\":\"0\",\"length\":\"0\",\"wide\":\"0\",\"height\":\"0\",\"is_added_attributes\":\"0\",\"has_product_options\":\"1\",\"related_products\":null,\"faq_schema_config\":[[{\"key\":\"question\",\"value\":null},{\"key\":\"answer\",\"value\":null}]],\"seo_meta\":{\"seo_title\":null,\"seo_description\":null,\"index\":\"index\"},\"seo_meta_image\":null,\"language\":\"en_US\",\"layout\":null,\"is_popular\":\"0\",\"status\":\"published\",\"store_id\":null,\"is_featured\":\"0\",\"categories\":[\"45\"],\"brand_id\":null,\"image\":\"rani-loach-min-300x300-1.jpg\",\"minimum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"maximum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"tag\":null,\"submitter\":\"save\"}', 'updated', 'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/130.0.0.0 Safari/537.36', '2405:201:800e:d0d0:ad7b:3351:47bb:df30', 3, 451, 'RANI LOACH', 'primary', '2024-11-05 16:07:49', '2024-11-05 16:07:49'),
(2653, 3, 'product', '{\"name\":\"BRONZE CORY CAT\",\"model\":\"Botble\\\\Ecommerce\\\\Models\\\\Product\",\"slug\":\"bronze-cory-cat-1\",\"slug_id\":\"492\",\"is_slug_editable\":\"1\",\"description\":\"<p>The bronze corydoras&nbsp;<i>(Corydoras aeneus)<\\/i>, also known as the bronze cory&nbsp;and green corydoras, is a small, tropical catfish that ranks among the most popular catfish kept in home aquariums.. They are native to South America and can found from Argentina in the south, all the way up to Columbia in the north.<\\/p><p>The Bronze Corydora Catfish (<i>Corydoras eques<\\/i>)&nbsp;is one of the most coveted, but rare&nbsp;<i>Corydoras<\\/i>&nbsp;species, especially when it comes to tank-bred specimens. It develops increasingly bright bronze coloration along its gills and back as it matures. This Bronze creates a very striking contrast with the metallic blue-green slate coloration along the sides of the body of the fish. While it is very rarely available and considered difficult to breed, it is truly exceptional in every way and it makes a marvelous addition to the nano, planted, and community aquarium.<\\/p><p>They primarily tend to inhabit slow moving rivers and streams, and prefer areas with shallow, muddy water. With that being said, they can also be found in everything from fast flowing rivers, to nearly stagnant pond and marshes.<\\/p><p>They are one of only a handful of fish that can thrive in stagnant water, and they do this by utilizing their specialized ability to breath air from the surface of the water. Even in the home aquarium, you will often see them darting to the surface to take a quick gulp of air, and then diving back down to the bottom.<\\/p>\",\"content\":null,\"images\":[null,\"bronze-cory-cat-min-300x300-1.jpg\"],\"product_type\":\"physical\",\"sale_type\":\"0\",\"sku\":null,\"price\":\"50\",\"sale_price\":null,\"start_date\":null,\"end_date\":null,\"cost_per_item\":\"0\",\"product_id\":\"450\",\"barcode\":null,\"with_storehouse_management\":\"0\",\"quantity\":\"0\",\"allow_checkout_when_out_of_stock\":\"0\",\"stock_status\":\"in_stock\",\"weight\":\"0\",\"length\":\"0\",\"wide\":\"0\",\"height\":\"0\",\"is_added_attributes\":\"0\",\"has_product_options\":\"1\",\"related_products\":null,\"faq_schema_config\":[[{\"key\":\"question\",\"value\":null},{\"key\":\"answer\",\"value\":null}]],\"seo_meta\":{\"seo_title\":null,\"seo_description\":null,\"index\":\"index\"},\"seo_meta_image\":null,\"language\":\"en_US\",\"layout\":null,\"is_popular\":\"0\",\"status\":\"published\",\"store_id\":null,\"is_featured\":\"0\",\"categories\":[\"45\"],\"brand_id\":null,\"image\":\"bronze-cory-cat-min-300x300-1.jpg\",\"minimum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"maximum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"tag\":null,\"submitter\":\"save\"}', 'updated', 'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/130.0.0.0 Safari/537.36', '2405:201:800e:d0d0:ad7b:3351:47bb:df30', 3, 450, 'BRONZE CORY CAT', 'primary', '2024-11-05 16:08:12', '2024-11-05 16:08:12'),
(2654, 3, 'product', '{\"name\":\"NEON\",\"model\":\"Botble\\\\Ecommerce\\\\Models\\\\Product\",\"slug\":\"neon\",\"slug_id\":\"485\",\"is_slug_editable\":\"1\",\"description\":\"<p><strong>Common Names:<\\/strong>&nbsp;Neon tetra, neon fish<\\/p><p><strong>Scientific Name:&nbsp;<\\/strong><i>Paracheirodon innesi<\\/i><\\/p><p><strong>Adult Size:&nbsp;<\\/strong>1.5 inches (4 centimeters)<\\/p><p><strong>Life Expectancy:&nbsp;<\\/strong>5 to 10 years<\\/p>\",\"content\":null,\"images\":[null,\"neon-min-300x300.jpg\"],\"product_type\":\"physical\",\"sale_type\":\"0\",\"sku\":null,\"price\":\"30\",\"sale_price\":null,\"start_date\":null,\"end_date\":null,\"cost_per_item\":\"0\",\"product_id\":\"449\",\"barcode\":null,\"with_storehouse_management\":\"0\",\"quantity\":\"0\",\"allow_checkout_when_out_of_stock\":\"0\",\"stock_status\":\"in_stock\",\"weight\":\"0\",\"length\":\"0\",\"wide\":\"0\",\"height\":\"0\",\"is_added_attributes\":\"0\",\"has_product_options\":\"1\",\"related_products\":null,\"faq_schema_config\":[[{\"key\":\"question\",\"value\":null},{\"key\":\"answer\",\"value\":null}]],\"seo_meta\":{\"seo_title\":null,\"seo_description\":null,\"index\":\"index\"},\"seo_meta_image\":null,\"language\":\"en_US\",\"layout\":null,\"is_popular\":\"0\",\"status\":\"published\",\"store_id\":null,\"is_featured\":\"1\",\"categories\":[\"45\"],\"brand_id\":null,\"image\":\"neon-min-300x300.jpg\",\"minimum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"maximum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"tag\":null,\"submitter\":\"save\"}', 'updated', 'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/130.0.0.0 Safari/537.36', '2405:201:800e:d0d0:ad7b:3351:47bb:df30', 3, 449, 'NEON', 'primary', '2024-11-05 16:08:46', '2024-11-05 16:08:46'),
(2655, 3, 'product', '{\"name\":\"CARDINAL\",\"model\":\"Botble\\\\Ecommerce\\\\Models\\\\Product\",\"slug\":\"cardinal\",\"slug_id\":\"484\",\"is_slug_editable\":\"1\",\"description\":\"<p class=\\\"comp mntl-sc-block lifestyle-sc-block-html mntl-sc-block-html text-passage u-how-to-title-align\\\" id=\\\"mntl-sc-block_1-0\\\">Arguably the most popular of the small tetras, the cardinal tetra is similar in appearance to a longtime aquarium favorite, the&nbsp;<a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.thesprucepets.com\\/neon-tetra-paracheirodon-1381835\\\">neon tetra<\\/a>\\u2014you can tell them apart by one particular detail: a slight difference in their red stripe.&nbsp;Cardinal tetras are active schooling fish, and they live&nbsp;peacefully in a community aquarium.<\\/p><div class=\\\"comp mntl-sc-block lifestyle-sc-block-adslot mntl-sc-block-adslot mntl-block u-no-article-width-restriction\\\" id=\\\"mntl-sc-block_2-0\\\">&nbsp;<\\/div><p class=\\\"comp mntl-sc-block lifestyle-sc-block-html mntl-sc-block-html text-passage u-how-to-title-align\\\" id=\\\"mntl-sc-block_3-0\\\">Although they are difficult to breed in captivity, tetras remain a very popular aquarium fish. Here\\u2019s everything you need to know to keep cardinal tetras happy and healthy in your tank.<\\/p>\",\"content\":null,\"images\":[null,\"cardinal-min-300x300.jpg\"],\"product_type\":\"physical\",\"sale_type\":\"0\",\"sku\":null,\"price\":\"60\",\"sale_price\":null,\"start_date\":null,\"end_date\":null,\"cost_per_item\":\"0\",\"product_id\":\"448\",\"barcode\":null,\"with_storehouse_management\":\"0\",\"quantity\":\"0\",\"allow_checkout_when_out_of_stock\":\"0\",\"stock_status\":\"in_stock\",\"weight\":\"0\",\"length\":\"0\",\"wide\":\"0\",\"height\":\"0\",\"is_added_attributes\":\"0\",\"has_product_options\":\"1\",\"related_products\":null,\"faq_schema_config\":[[{\"key\":\"question\",\"value\":null},{\"key\":\"answer\",\"value\":null}]],\"seo_meta\":{\"seo_title\":null,\"seo_description\":null,\"index\":\"index\"},\"seo_meta_image\":null,\"language\":\"en_US\",\"layout\":null,\"is_popular\":\"0\",\"status\":\"published\",\"store_id\":null,\"is_featured\":\"0\",\"categories\":[\"45\"],\"brand_id\":null,\"image\":\"cardinal-min-300x300.jpg\",\"minimum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"maximum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"tag\":null,\"submitter\":\"save\"}', 'updated', 'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/130.0.0.0 Safari/537.36', '2405:201:800e:d0d0:ad7b:3351:47bb:df30', 3, 448, 'CARDINAL', 'primary', '2024-11-05 16:09:27', '2024-11-05 16:09:27'),
(2656, 3, 'product', '{\"name\":\"RED PENCIL\",\"model\":\"Botble\\\\Ecommerce\\\\Models\\\\Product\",\"slug\":\"red-pencil\",\"slug_id\":\"483\",\"is_slug_editable\":\"1\",\"description\":\"<p>Red Pencil Tetra is one of the most beautiful species of pencilfish. Its adaptable has a pleasant demeanor and may just be the perfect aquarium fish.<\\/p><p><span>Red Pencil Tetra: This is a very popular smaller pencil fish called the Red Pencilfish (Nannostomus beckfordi) has a crimson upper half, a black stripe, and a white bottom.<\\/span><\\/p><p><span>The \\u201cnose\\u201d of the male has a crimson mark on it. Both genders have bluish\\/white bottom fins. They originate from Guyana, Suriname, and French Guiana, as well as the eastern Amazon drainage in the Brazilian states of Amap\\u00e1 and Par\\u00e1.<\\/span><\\/p><p><span>These are captive-raised with an emphasis on increased red coloration. They are perfect community fish with other similar-sized fish.<\\/span><\\/p><p><span>Adult size for them is less than 1.5 inches. They are the ideal addition to a tank that is at least 10 gallons in size and has calm fish of the same size, such as little tetras and rasboras.<\\/span><\\/p><p><span>They benefit from living plants since they like being around them. For them to feel at home in their aquariums, it is recommended that they be kept in groups of at least ten.<\\/span><\\/p><p><span>When men and females are together, the males will have more vibrant colors to stand out from the other members of the group.<\\/span><\\/p><p><span>The aquarium should have rockwork, vegetation, and driftwood to mimic their natural habitat. It is highly advised to utilize Indian Almond or Guava leaves because they also like tannins in their water.<\\/span><\\/p><p><span>They also prefer a darkened aquarium, so keeping floating plants is advised to reduce the amount of light that reaches them. The use of a sponge filter is advised for gentle filtration. Because the red pencil fish is likely to eat young shrimp, we do not advise keeping this fish near shrimp colonies.<\\/span><\\/p><p><i><span><strong>II. You would love the fish because\\u2026<\\/strong><\\/span><\\/i><\\/p><p><span>You will be intrigued by this species because of its striking red coloring.<\\/span><\\/p><p><span>The demand for this fish, which is excellent for such a setup, has increased as a result of the exploding popularity of planted micro tanks.<\\/span><\\/p><p><span>Its habitat and population are allegedly severely constrained, but fortunately, the availability of specimens through tank breeding has reduced the need for wild collection.<\\/span><\\/p><p><span>A very active and a schooling specie, this should always be maintained in groups to prevent aggression. A tank with plants is ideal. Any fish that isn\\u2019t too big to consume can be kept with them.<\\/span><\\/p><p><i><span><strong>III. Is this fish species peaceful or hostile?<\\/strong><\\/span><\\/i><\\/p><p><span>Overall peaceful fish.<\\/span><\\/p><p><i><span><strong>IV. Species compatibility<\\/strong><\\/span><\\/i><\\/p><p><span>Danios, Corydoras, Discus fish, most Livebearers, and some peaceful Dwarf Cichlids, such as Apistogramma.<\\/span><\\/p><p><i><span><strong>V. How to feed this species?<\\/strong><\\/span><\\/i><\\/p><p><span>Little pellets, prepared fish food, flake food, frozen food, dry food, and anything else that fish can consume in general will be enjoyed by it.<\\/span><\\/p>\",\"content\":null,\"images\":[null,\"red-pencil-min-300x300.jpg\"],\"product_type\":\"physical\",\"sale_type\":\"0\",\"sku\":null,\"price\":\"60\",\"sale_price\":null,\"start_date\":null,\"end_date\":null,\"cost_per_item\":\"0\",\"product_id\":\"447\",\"barcode\":null,\"with_storehouse_management\":\"0\",\"quantity\":\"0\",\"allow_checkout_when_out_of_stock\":\"0\",\"stock_status\":\"in_stock\",\"weight\":\"0\",\"length\":\"0\",\"wide\":\"0\",\"height\":\"0\",\"is_added_attributes\":\"0\",\"has_product_options\":\"1\",\"related_products\":null,\"faq_schema_config\":[[{\"key\":\"question\",\"value\":null},{\"key\":\"answer\",\"value\":null}]],\"seo_meta\":{\"seo_title\":null,\"seo_description\":null,\"index\":\"index\"},\"seo_meta_image\":null,\"language\":\"en_US\",\"layout\":null,\"is_popular\":\"0\",\"status\":\"published\",\"store_id\":null,\"is_featured\":\"0\",\"categories\":[\"45\"],\"brand_id\":null,\"image\":\"red-pencil-min-300x300.jpg\",\"minimum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"maximum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"tag\":null,\"submitter\":\"save\"}', 'updated', 'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/130.0.0.0 Safari/537.36', '2405:201:800e:d0d0:ad7b:3351:47bb:df30', 3, 447, 'RED PENCIL', 'primary', '2024-11-05 16:13:55', '2024-11-05 16:13:55'),
(2657, 3, 'product', '{\"name\":\"GLOW LIGHT\",\"model\":\"Botble\\\\Ecommerce\\\\Models\\\\Product\",\"slug\":\"glow-light\",\"slug_id\":\"482\",\"is_slug_editable\":\"1\",\"description\":\"<p>The glowlight&nbsp;<a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.thesprucepets.com\\/emperor-tetra-1381832\\\">tetra<\\/a>&nbsp;is absolutely gorgeous and surprisingly easy to care for. Originating in the Essequibo River of Guyana, it is easygoing and peaceful and can survive in a fairly wide range of aquarium environments. Because they are schooling fish, you\'ll want to keep at least six glowlight tetras in your aquarium.<\\/p>\",\"content\":null,\"images\":[null,\"glowlight-min-300x300.jpg\"],\"product_type\":\"physical\",\"sale_type\":\"0\",\"sku\":null,\"price\":\"50\",\"sale_price\":null,\"start_date\":null,\"end_date\":null,\"cost_per_item\":\"0\",\"product_id\":\"446\",\"barcode\":null,\"with_storehouse_management\":\"0\",\"quantity\":\"0\",\"allow_checkout_when_out_of_stock\":\"0\",\"stock_status\":\"in_stock\",\"weight\":\"0\",\"length\":\"0\",\"wide\":\"0\",\"height\":\"0\",\"is_added_attributes\":\"0\",\"has_product_options\":\"1\",\"related_products\":null,\"faq_schema_config\":[[{\"key\":\"question\",\"value\":null},{\"key\":\"answer\",\"value\":null}]],\"seo_meta\":{\"seo_title\":null,\"seo_description\":null,\"index\":\"index\"},\"seo_meta_image\":null,\"language\":\"en_US\",\"layout\":null,\"is_popular\":\"0\",\"status\":\"published\",\"store_id\":null,\"is_featured\":\"0\",\"categories\":[\"45\"],\"brand_id\":null,\"image\":\"glowlight-min-300x300.jpg\",\"minimum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"maximum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"tag\":null,\"submitter\":\"save\"}', 'updated', 'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/130.0.0.0 Safari/537.36', '2405:201:800e:d0d0:ad7b:3351:47bb:df30', 3, 446, 'GLOW LIGHT', 'primary', '2024-11-05 16:15:08', '2024-11-05 16:15:08'),
(2658, 3, 'product', '{\"name\":\"LEMON\",\"model\":\"Botble\\\\Ecommerce\\\\Models\\\\Product\",\"slug\":\"lemon\",\"slug_id\":\"481\",\"is_slug_editable\":\"1\",\"description\":\"<p>This species\\u2019 distribution is somewhat confusing. The type locality is vague (see below), and the majority of subsequent reports pertain to&nbsp;the rio Tapaj\\u00f3s&nbsp;basins&nbsp;in central Brazil, one of the primary affluents of the lower Amazon River basin. The species is thus often assumed to be endemic to this watershed, but at least one&nbsp;field observation suggests that it also occurs in&nbsp;the rio Xingu system which borders the Tapaj\\u00f3s to the east<\\/p><p>Perhaps looks best&nbsp;in an arrangement comprising a sandy substrate plus some driftwood roots and branches, or heavily-planted planted set-up.<\\/p><p>The addition of dried leaf litter would further emphasise the natural feel and as well as offering additional cover for the fish brings with it the growth of microbe colonies as decomposition occurs.<\\/p><p>The latter are useful since they provide an additional food source for both adults and fry while the humic substances released by decaying leaves are also considered beneficial.<\\/p>\",\"content\":null,\"images\":[null,\"lemon-min-300x300.jpg\"],\"product_type\":\"physical\",\"sale_type\":\"0\",\"sku\":null,\"price\":\"50\",\"sale_price\":null,\"start_date\":null,\"end_date\":null,\"cost_per_item\":\"0\",\"product_id\":\"445\",\"barcode\":null,\"with_storehouse_management\":\"0\",\"quantity\":\"0\",\"allow_checkout_when_out_of_stock\":\"0\",\"stock_status\":\"in_stock\",\"weight\":\"0\",\"length\":\"0\",\"wide\":\"0\",\"height\":\"0\",\"is_added_attributes\":\"0\",\"has_product_options\":\"1\",\"related_products\":null,\"faq_schema_config\":[[{\"key\":\"question\",\"value\":null},{\"key\":\"answer\",\"value\":null}]],\"seo_meta\":{\"seo_title\":null,\"seo_description\":null,\"index\":\"index\"},\"seo_meta_image\":null,\"language\":\"en_US\",\"layout\":null,\"is_popular\":\"0\",\"status\":\"published\",\"store_id\":null,\"is_featured\":\"0\",\"categories\":[\"45\"],\"brand_id\":null,\"image\":\"lemon-min-300x300.jpg\",\"minimum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"maximum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"tag\":null,\"submitter\":\"save\"}', 'updated', 'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/130.0.0.0 Safari/537.36', '2405:201:800e:d0d0:ad7b:3351:47bb:df30', 3, 445, 'LEMON', 'primary', '2024-11-05 16:15:47', '2024-11-05 16:15:47'),
(2659, 3, 'product', '{\"name\":\"RED WIDOW\",\"model\":\"Botble\\\\Ecommerce\\\\Models\\\\Product\",\"slug\":\"red-widow\",\"slug_id\":\"480\",\"is_slug_editable\":\"1\",\"description\":\"<p>Red widow fish are brilliantly colored and beautiful fish. Widow tetras are an undemanding species that adapt to a range of conditions, though subdued lighting and neutral-colored gravel substrates are preferred.&nbsp; Hardy and easy to care for. A schooling fish by nature, widow tetras are best kept in groups of six or more. They make an excellent community fish due to their peaceful nature.<\\/p><ul><li><strong>TEMPERATURE<\\/strong>&nbsp;<strong>RANGE<\\/strong>&nbsp;: 21 \\u00b0C \\u2013 27\\u00b0C<\\/li><li><strong>PH RANGE<\\/strong>&nbsp;: 6 \\u2013 7<\\/li><li><strong>TANK MATES &amp; COMPATIBILITY<\\/strong>:- Tetras are peaceful and passive, making them suitable tank mates for a variety of fish species. Similarly-sized, bottom-dwelling, non-aggressive fish can be added to a community tank with tetras. Tetras are a schooling species, so make sure your neon tetras are housed in groups of six or more before considering other fish species for the tank.<\\/li><li><strong>FEEDING<\\/strong>:- In the wild, Tetras are omnivores, eating a varied diet of meat and fish. Depending on the food source available in the fish\\u2019s habitat, a neon tetra will feed on insect larvae, small insects, algae, and other plant matter. Good-quality fish flakes that are fortified with vitamins and minerals are a staple food to feed tetras. Several times per week, feed neon tetras live or frozen foods like bloodworms, daphnia, tubifex, and brine shrimp. Cut live food into small pieces to prevent the neon tetras from having problems swallowing the food.<\\/li><li><strong>CARE<\\/strong>:- Caring for tetras is easy. Tetras are hardy fish that can adapt to brackish and clearwater environments, but a clean freshwater tank setup will ensure that the fish thrive in captivity. Tetras are omnivores and have a varied diet in the wild, which you should replicate in your home aquarium. Decorate your neon tetra tank with floating plants like&nbsp;<a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.fishkeepingworld.com\\/hornwort\\/\\\">hornwort&nbsp;<\\/a>and&nbsp;<a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.fishkeepingworld.com\\/java-moss\\/\\\">Java moss<\\/a>. These plants create shady, secluded hideaways that neon tetras enjoy. Driftwood can also be used to provide hiding places for the fish.<\\/li><\\/ul>\",\"content\":null,\"images\":[null,\"red-widow-300x300.jpg\"],\"product_type\":\"physical\",\"sale_type\":\"0\",\"sku\":null,\"price\":\"30\",\"sale_price\":null,\"start_date\":null,\"end_date\":null,\"cost_per_item\":\"0\",\"product_id\":\"444\",\"barcode\":null,\"with_storehouse_management\":\"0\",\"quantity\":\"0\",\"allow_checkout_when_out_of_stock\":\"0\",\"stock_status\":\"in_stock\",\"weight\":\"0\",\"length\":\"0\",\"wide\":\"0\",\"height\":\"0\",\"is_added_attributes\":\"0\",\"has_product_options\":\"1\",\"related_products\":null,\"faq_schema_config\":[[{\"key\":\"question\",\"value\":null},{\"key\":\"answer\",\"value\":null}]],\"seo_meta\":{\"seo_title\":null,\"seo_description\":null,\"index\":\"index\"},\"seo_meta_image\":null,\"language\":\"en_US\",\"layout\":null,\"is_popular\":\"0\",\"status\":\"published\",\"store_id\":null,\"is_featured\":\"0\",\"categories\":[\"45\"],\"brand_id\":null,\"image\":\"red-widow-300x300.jpg\",\"minimum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"maximum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"tag\":null,\"submitter\":\"save\"}', 'updated', 'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/130.0.0.0 Safari/537.36', '2405:201:800e:d0d0:ad7b:3351:47bb:df30', 3, 444, 'RED WIDOW', 'primary', '2024-11-05 16:16:19', '2024-11-05 16:16:19'),
(2660, 3, 'product', '{\"name\":\"GREEN WIDOW\",\"model\":\"Botble\\\\Ecommerce\\\\Models\\\\Product\",\"slug\":\"green-widow\",\"slug_id\":\"479\",\"is_slug_editable\":\"1\",\"description\":\"<ul class=\\\"tabs wc-tabs product-tabs small-nav-collapse nav nav-uppercase nav-line nav-left\\\"><li class=\\\"description_tab active\\\" id=\\\"tab-title-description\\\"><a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/fish.splashyfin.com\\/shop\\/glo-tetra-green\\/#tab-description\\\">Description<\\/a><\\/li><li class=\\\"additional_information_tab\\\" id=\\\"tab-title-additional_information\\\"><a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/fish.splashyfin.com\\/shop\\/glo-tetra-green\\/#tab-additional_information\\\">Additional information<\\/a><\\/li><\\/ul><div class=\\\"tab-panels\\\"><div class=\\\"woocommerce-Tabs-panel woocommerce-Tabs-panel--description panel entry-content active\\\" id=\\\"tab-description\\\"><p><span>Glo Tetra \\u2013 Green are fish that have been genetically altered. They have vivid fluorescent colors, as their name suggests.<\\/span><\\/p><p><span>They are nothing more than luminous variations of the wild species like Zebra danios, Rainbow sharks, Tiger barbs, Bettas, and Black skirt tetras that are naturally found.<\\/span><\\/p><p><span>The gentle Glo Tetra-Green prefers to live in shoaling groups of five or more. A solitary specimen is prone to experience stress and isolate itself.<\\/span><\\/p><p><span>The best and required solution is to keep them together in groups. They are gentle fish that make great tank mates for other little fish due to their disposition.<\\/span><\\/p><p><span>To long-finned fish, however, are semi-aggressive as long as they are sluggish, not too big, and aggressive. They begin to nibble in response to the lengthy fins.<\\/span><\\/p><p><span>Their intergroup hostility is also triggered if the female in a group of two or more males exhibits spawning behavior, and every male tends to pair up with the female.<\\/span><\\/p><p><span>If you wish to breed glofish, separate the female at this time and place her in a different setup. You can add the male afterward. The glofish tetras are otherwise calm and have distinguished themselves from the other community fishes.<\\/span><\\/p><p><i><span><strong>II. You would love the fish because\\u2026<\\/strong><\\/span><\\/i><\\/p><p><span>Depending on the breed of the color, they appear in various fluorescent colors. However, these fish share the same overall appearance as a black skirt tetra.<\\/span><\\/p><p><span>Their bodies are generally quadrilateral, with a rounded forehead. Their lower end goes pointed inward and meets the tail at the second half section. Their top end is streamlined and curled.<\\/span><\\/p><p><span>They have highly noticeable fins, which add to their overall sheen. The dorsal fin is tiny and has an appearance of a square with a pointed top. The forked tail fin has a more \\u201cV\\u201d-shaped look. The body\\u2019s bottom half is covered by the anal fin.<\\/span><\\/p><p><span>Glo Tetra \\u2013 Green comes in several vividly colored varieties. All seven colors of the rainbow are represented by these colors.<\\/span><\\/p><p><span>If your tank has color variations, they enhance its brilliance and make it appear like a luminous ornamental item in your guest room.<\\/span><\\/p><p><span>All of these variations appear normal in white light, yet they glow in the dark and when exposed to blue light.<\\/span><\\/p><p><i><span><strong>III. Is this fish species peaceful or hostile?<\\/strong><\\/span><\\/i><\\/p><p><span>A very peaceful and friendly nature.<\\/span><\\/p><p><i><span><strong>IV. Species compatibility<\\/strong><\\/span><\\/i><\\/p><p><span>Tetras, Guppies, Platys, Corydoras Catfish, and Gouramis.<\\/span><\\/p><p><i><span><strong>V. How to feed this species?<\\/strong><\\/span><\\/i><\\/p><p><span>In the wild, red phantom tetras are omnivores and will consume both decaying plant matter and small animals like young shrimp, larvae, and snails. In captivity, these fish thrive on fine-grained subtropical fish flakes.<\\/span><\\/p><\\/div><\\/div>\",\"content\":null,\"images\":[null,\"green-widow-300x300.jpg\"],\"product_type\":\"physical\",\"sale_type\":\"0\",\"sku\":null,\"price\":\"30\",\"sale_price\":null,\"start_date\":null,\"end_date\":null,\"cost_per_item\":\"0\",\"product_id\":\"443\",\"barcode\":null,\"with_storehouse_management\":\"0\",\"quantity\":\"0\",\"allow_checkout_when_out_of_stock\":\"0\",\"stock_status\":\"in_stock\",\"weight\":\"0\",\"length\":\"0\",\"wide\":\"0\",\"height\":\"0\",\"is_added_attributes\":\"0\",\"has_product_options\":\"1\",\"related_products\":null,\"faq_schema_config\":[[{\"key\":\"question\",\"value\":null},{\"key\":\"answer\",\"value\":null}]],\"seo_meta\":{\"seo_title\":null,\"seo_description\":null,\"index\":\"index\"},\"seo_meta_image\":null,\"language\":\"en_US\",\"layout\":null,\"is_popular\":\"0\",\"status\":\"published\",\"store_id\":null,\"is_featured\":\"0\",\"categories\":[\"45\"],\"brand_id\":null,\"image\":\"green-widow-300x300.jpg\",\"minimum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"maximum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"tag\":null,\"submitter\":\"save\"}', 'updated', 'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/130.0.0.0 Safari/537.36', '2405:201:800e:d0d0:ad7b:3351:47bb:df30', 3, 443, 'GREEN WIDOW', 'primary', '2024-11-05 16:16:42', '2024-11-05 16:16:42'),
(2661, 3, 'product', '{\"name\":\"YELLOW WIDOW\",\"model\":\"Botble\\\\Ecommerce\\\\Models\\\\Product\",\"slug\":\"yellow-widow\",\"slug_id\":\"478\",\"is_slug_editable\":\"1\",\"description\":\"<p><span>Glo Tetra \\u2013 Yellow: The glowlight tetra is astonishingly simple to care for and very stunning. It is a calm, laid-back fish that originated in the rivers of Guyana. It can live in a variety of aquarium conditions. You ought to preserve at least six glowlight tetras because they are school.<\\/span><\\/p><p><span>Glo Tetra \\u2013 Yellow:originated from The Essequibo basin in Guyanabeen discovered in the Essequibo, Mazaruni, and Potaro Rivers. The tannins produced by the breakdown of plant materials give the river waters of South America their natural softness and acidity.<\\/span><\\/p><p><i><span><strong>II. You would love the fish because\\u2026<\\/strong><\\/span><\\/i><\\/p><p><span>Depending on the breed of the color, they appear in various fluorescent colors like Glo Tetra \\u2013 Yellow<\\/span><\\/p><p><span>One of the most well-liked tetras is the glowlight tetra, which is calm and simple to care for.<\\/span><\\/p><p><span>They grow barely an inch and a half long as adults, making them tiny and skinny. The glowlight tetra\\u2019s translucent, silvery-peach body is split by an iridescent red-gold stripe that extends from the nose to the tail.<\\/span><\\/p><p><span>The stripe mimics a light bulb\\u2019s or glowlight\\u2019s glowing filament. The anal and pelvic fins are bordered in white, while the leading edge of the dorsal fin is the same iridescent red color. in the dark and then exposed to blue light.<\\/span><\\/p><p><span>The red line or glowlight rasbora, a kind of rasbora, and the glowlight tetra both have distinctive stripes, and the two fish are occasionally mistaken for one another.<\\/span><\\/p><p><span>The two species, however, do not belong to the same genus. The absence of an adipose fin in the rasbora is the most noticeable distinction between the two.<\\/span><\\/p><p><i><span><strong>III. Is this fish species peaceful or hostile?<\\/strong><\\/span><\\/i><\\/p><p><span>A very peaceful and easy-going fish.<\\/span><\\/p><p><i><span><strong>IV. Species compatibility<\\/strong><\\/span><\\/i><\\/p><p><span>Neon Tetra, Tiger Barb, Plecos, original Danio, and the Dwarf Cichlid<\\/span><\\/p><p><i><span><strong>V. How to feed this species?<\\/strong><\\/span><\\/i><\\/p><p><span>Flakes, pellets, and frozen or freeze-dried meals make up a well-balanced GloFish diet. a diversified diet that includes items high in carotenoids and beta carotene to help maintain your fish\\u2019s beautiful color and guarantee optimum nutritional balance.<\\/span><\\/p><p>&nbsp;<\\/p>\",\"content\":null,\"images\":[null,\"yellow-widow-300x300.jpg\"],\"product_type\":\"physical\",\"sale_type\":\"0\",\"sku\":null,\"price\":\"30\",\"sale_price\":null,\"start_date\":null,\"end_date\":null,\"cost_per_item\":\"0\",\"product_id\":\"442\",\"barcode\":null,\"with_storehouse_management\":\"0\",\"quantity\":\"0\",\"allow_checkout_when_out_of_stock\":\"0\",\"stock_status\":\"in_stock\",\"weight\":\"0\",\"length\":\"0\",\"wide\":\"0\",\"height\":\"0\",\"is_added_attributes\":\"0\",\"has_product_options\":\"1\",\"related_products\":null,\"faq_schema_config\":[[{\"key\":\"question\",\"value\":null},{\"key\":\"answer\",\"value\":null}]],\"seo_meta\":{\"seo_title\":null,\"seo_description\":null,\"index\":\"index\"},\"seo_meta_image\":null,\"language\":\"en_US\",\"layout\":null,\"is_popular\":\"0\",\"status\":\"published\",\"store_id\":null,\"is_featured\":\"0\",\"categories\":[\"45\"],\"brand_id\":null,\"image\":\"yellow-widow-300x300.jpg\",\"minimum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"maximum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"tag\":null,\"submitter\":\"save\"}', 'updated', 'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/130.0.0.0 Safari/537.36', '2405:201:800e:d0d0:ad7b:3351:47bb:df30', 3, 442, 'YELLOW WIDOW', 'primary', '2024-11-05 16:18:36', '2024-11-05 16:18:36');
