(2662, 3, 'product', '{\"name\":\"PURPLE WIDOW\",\"model\":\"Botble\\\\Ecommerce\\\\Models\\\\Product\",\"slug\":\"purple-widow\",\"slug_id\":\"477\",\"is_slug_editable\":\"1\",\"description\":\"<p><span>Glo Tetra \\u2013 Purple: Tetras have several bones linking the inner ear to the swim bladder, which gives them a great hearing. They also have a small, rounded fin between the dorsal and tail fins.<\\/span><\\/p><p><span>Genetically altered Galactic Purple Tetras are fluorescent purple. Typically, these fish measure 2.4 inches. The water\\u2019s pH level and temperature range should be between 6.0 and 7.0 for these fish to be kept in captivity.<\\/span><\\/p><p><span>Given that these fish are jumpers, the tank should include dense vegetation, open places for swimming, a cover, floating plants to assist filter the light, and a gravel or sand substrate.<\\/span><\\/p><p><span>Smaller fish may get their fins bit by the tetra, however, the fin-nipping tendency of the tetra can be remedied by keeping it in a group of at least six. These fish can be housed in a communal tank with larger fish. For a small party, a minimum recommended tank size of 15 gallons and 20 inches long is advised.<\\/span><\\/p><p><i><span><strong>II. You would love the fish because\\u2026<\\/strong><\\/span><\\/i><\\/p><p><span>The new collection of Tetras from Fluorescent GloFish\\u00ae is available in six bright colors, including Starfire Red\\u00ae, Electric Green\\u00ae, Sunburst Orange\\u00ae, Cosmic Blue\\u00ae, Galactic Purple\\u00ae, and Moonrise Pink\\u00ae. GloFish\\u00ae is not dyed, and the color they were born with does not deteriorate with time.<\\/span><\\/p><p><span>To aid in the detection of environmental toxins and advance scientific study, the first generations of GloFish\\u00ae were genetically modified as embryos. Now, every GloFish\\u00ae generation is born with its stunning color! A naturally occurring fluorescent protein gene in some marine species is responsible for the dazzling colors.<\\/span><\\/p><p><span>Maintaining GloFish\\u00ae is as simple as maintaining Tetras. Keep this tranquil fish alone in tiny aquariums or small schools with other equally peaceful fish for the best care. Feed GloFish\\u00ae a broad diet of flake and frozen meals because they are omnivores.<\\/span><\\/p><p><i><span><strong>III. Is this fish species peaceful or hostile?<\\/strong><\\/span><\\/i><\\/p><p><span>A very peaceful and easy-going fish.<\\/span><\\/p><p><i><span><strong>IV. Species compatibility<\\/strong><\\/span> <\\/i><span>Neon Tetra, Tiger Barb, Plecos, original Danio, and the Dwarf Cichlid<\\/span><\\/p><p>&nbsp;<\\/p><p><span>V. How to feed this species?<\\/span><\\/p><p><span>Flakes, pellets, and frozen or freeze-dried meals make up a well-balanced GloFish diet. a diversified diet that includes items high in carotenoids and beta carotene to help maintain your fish\\u2019s beautiful color and guarantee optimum nutritional balance.<\\/span><\\/p>\",\"content\":null,\"images\":[null,\"purple-widow-300x300-1.jpg\"],\"product_type\":\"physical\",\"sale_type\":\"0\",\"sku\":null,\"price\":\"30\",\"sale_price\":null,\"start_date\":null,\"end_date\":null,\"cost_per_item\":\"0\",\"product_id\":\"441\",\"barcode\":null,\"with_storehouse_management\":\"0\",\"quantity\":\"0\",\"allow_checkout_when_out_of_stock\":\"0\",\"stock_status\":\"in_stock\",\"weight\":\"0\",\"length\":\"0\",\"wide\":\"0\",\"height\":\"0\",\"is_added_attributes\":\"0\",\"has_product_options\":\"1\",\"related_products\":null,\"faq_schema_config\":[[{\"key\":\"question\",\"value\":null},{\"key\":\"answer\",\"value\":null}]],\"seo_meta\":{\"seo_title\":null,\"seo_description\":null,\"index\":\"index\"},\"seo_meta_image\":null,\"language\":\"en_US\",\"layout\":null,\"is_popular\":\"0\",\"status\":\"published\",\"store_id\":null,\"is_featured\":\"0\",\"categories\":[\"45\"],\"brand_id\":null,\"image\":\"purple-widow-300x300-1.jpg\",\"minimum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"maximum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"tag\":null,\"submitter\":\"save\"}', 'updated', 'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/130.0.0.0 Safari/537.36', '2405:201:800e:d0d0:ad7b:3351:47bb:df30', 3, 441, 'PURPLE WIDOW', 'primary', '2024-11-05 16:18:52', '2024-11-05 16:18:52'),
(2663, 3, 'product', '{\"name\":\"CHERRY BARB\",\"model\":\"Botble\\\\Ecommerce\\\\Models\\\\Product\",\"slug\":\"cherry-barb\",\"slug_id\":\"476\",\"is_slug_editable\":\"1\",\"description\":\"<p>Named for the males\' vibrant red color during spawning season, the Cherry Barb makes a great schooling addition to many freshwater community tanks. These slender fish are common in this pet hobby and are easy to manage for most beginner aquarists. These smaller fish tend to be shy around larger, aggressive fish, so keep them in a group and choose their tank mates carefully.<\\/p><h2 class=\\\"comp mntl-sc-block lifestyle-sc-block-heading mntl-sc-block-heading u-how-to-title-align\\\" id=\\\"mntl-sc-block_18-0\\\"><span class=\\\"mntl-sc-block-heading__text\\\">Cherry Barb Habitat and Care<\\/span><\\/h2><p class=\\\"comp mntl-sc-block lifestyle-sc-block-html mntl-sc-block-html text-passage u-how-to-title-align\\\" id=\\\"mntl-sc-block_19-0\\\">Being a shyer fish, the Cherry Barb likes to have lots of places to hide in their home aquarium. They should be added to your aquarium first, so they can get settled and not have to compete for hiding places.<\\/p><div class=\\\"comp mntl-sc-block lifestyle-sc-block-adslot mntl-sc-block-adslot mntl-block u-no-article-width-restriction\\\" id=\\\"mntl-sc-block_20-0\\\">&nbsp;<\\/div><p class=\\\"comp mntl-sc-block lifestyle-sc-block-html mntl-sc-block-html text-passage u-how-to-title-align\\\" id=\\\"mntl-sc-block_21-0\\\">Since they like to stick in a group, you may need to make lots of hiding places to accommodate more than one fish at a time. Planted tanks or aquascapes make a great home for Cherry Barbs with good water quality and lots of places to hide.<\\/p><div class=\\\"comp mntl-sc-block lifestyle-sc-block-adslot mntl-sc-block-adslot mntl-block u-no-article-width-restriction\\\" id=\\\"mntl-sc-block_22-0\\\">&nbsp;<\\/div><p class=\\\"comp mntl-sc-block lifestyle-sc-block-html mntl-sc-block-html text-passage u-how-to-title-align\\\" id=\\\"mntl-sc-block_23-0\\\">Cherry Barbs are relatively easy to care for as long as you keep up with your regular maintenance. In planted tanks, be sure to remove dead plant material regularly and pay attention to any pH changes between day and night.<\\/p>\",\"content\":null,\"images\":[null,\"cherry-barb-300x300.jpg\"],\"product_type\":\"physical\",\"sale_type\":\"0\",\"sku\":null,\"price\":\"50\",\"sale_price\":null,\"start_date\":null,\"end_date\":null,\"cost_per_item\":\"0\",\"product_id\":\"440\",\"barcode\":null,\"with_storehouse_management\":\"0\",\"quantity\":\"0\",\"allow_checkout_when_out_of_stock\":\"0\",\"stock_status\":\"in_stock\",\"weight\":\"0\",\"length\":\"0\",\"wide\":\"0\",\"height\":\"0\",\"is_added_attributes\":\"0\",\"has_product_options\":\"1\",\"related_products\":null,\"faq_schema_config\":[[{\"key\":\"question\",\"value\":null},{\"key\":\"answer\",\"value\":null}]],\"seo_meta\":{\"seo_title\":null,\"seo_description\":null,\"index\":\"index\"},\"seo_meta_image\":null,\"language\":\"en_US\",\"layout\":null,\"is_popular\":\"0\",\"status\":\"published\",\"store_id\":null,\"is_featured\":\"0\",\"categories\":[\"45\"],\"brand_id\":null,\"image\":\"cherry-barb-300x300.jpg\",\"minimum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"maximum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"tag\":null,\"submitter\":\"save\"}', 'updated', 'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/130.0.0.0 Safari/537.36', '2405:201:800e:d0d0:ad7b:3351:47bb:df30', 3, 440, 'CHERRY BARB', 'primary', '2024-11-05 16:20:43', '2024-11-05 16:20:43'),
(2664, 3, 'product', '{\"name\":\"SIAMESE ALGAE EATER\",\"model\":\"Botble\\\\Ecommerce\\\\Models\\\\Product\",\"slug\":\"siamese-algae-eater\",\"slug_id\":\"475\",\"is_slug_editable\":\"1\",\"description\":\"<p><strong>The Siamese Algae Eater is one of the best algae-eating fish in the aquarium hobby, and it is one of the very few fish that will eat the dreaded black beard algae!<\\/strong><\\/p><p>&nbsp;<\\/p><div>The Siamese Algae Eater&nbsp;(<i>Crossocheilus siamensis<\\/i>)&nbsp;is a longtime favorite in the aquarium hobby due to its active nature and its voracious appetite for various types of nuisance algae, including pesky black beard algae. It is a mostly herviborous fish that is gregarious as a juvenile, but is shoaling (rather than schooling) as an adult. As it matures, a distinct hierarchy develops within a group of this species, and stress and aggression are likely when the group contains less than 6 specimens.<\\/div><div>Care is simple for the Siamese Algae Eater. It is tolerant of a wide range of water parameters, but it will thrive in an aquarium with ample filtration and moderate to high water flow. This active fish is known to jump occasionally, so a secure aquarium lid is recommended. It will readily eat most high-quality dry foods rich in vegetable matter, but it should also be offered fresh vegetables such as zucchini and cucumber as well. Meaty foods should be kept to a minimum with this fish.<\\/div><div>As stated above, the Siamese Algae Eater is a generally peaceful fish, but it will prey on dwarf shrimp and other very small invertebrates. It does not seem to bother most snails, and we have found it to be generally peaceful with most larger shrimp (such as Amano, Flower, Green Lace, and Vampire Shrimp) as long as they are too large to be considered easy prey. The Siamese Algae Eater is a schooling fish&nbsp;as a juvenile, but can become more territorial with its own kind and similar-looking species as it matures. It must be kept in groups of at least 6 fish to avoid harrassment of subdominant specimens, or else it should be kept singly.&nbsp;Aggression can be kept to a minimum in a larger tank with plenty of territory and cover for each fish.<\\/div><div><div><strong>What We Like About This Fish:<\\/strong><\\/div><div><ul><li>Voracious algae eater<\\/li><li>Will not eat ornamental plants<\\/li><li>Generally peaceful disposition with fish and peaceful larger invertebrates<\\/li><li>Very active and noticeable fish in any aquarium<\\/li><li>Very hardy<\\/li><\\/ul><\\/div><div>&nbsp;<\\/div><div>&nbsp;<\\/div><div><strong>RECOMMENDED TANK PARAMETERS:<\\/strong><\\/div><div><ul><li>Temperature:&nbsp; 72\\u00b0 - 79\\u00b0 F (22\\u00b0 - 26\\u00b0 C)<\\/li><li>pH:&nbsp; 6.5 - 7.5<\\/li><li>KH:&nbsp; 4 - 15 dKH<\\/li><li><p>Minimum tank size:&nbsp; 50 gallons<\\/p><div><strong>CARE GUIDELINES:<\\/strong><\\/div><div><ul><li>Diet:&nbsp; Omnivorous. Will easily accept high quality dry and frozen foods as well as fresh vegetables. Should be fed mostly vegetable matter.<\\/li><li>Social behavior:&nbsp; Generally peaceful, schooling\\/shoaling as a juvenile. Can be somewhat territoral with its own kind or similar fish as an adult<\\/li><\\/ul><\\/div><\\/li><\\/ul><\\/div><\\/div>\",\"content\":null,\"images\":[null,\"siamese-algae-eater-min-300x300.jpg\"],\"product_type\":\"physical\",\"sale_type\":\"0\",\"sku\":null,\"price\":\"50\",\"sale_price\":null,\"start_date\":null,\"end_date\":null,\"cost_per_item\":\"0\",\"product_id\":\"439\",\"barcode\":null,\"with_storehouse_management\":\"0\",\"quantity\":\"0\",\"allow_checkout_when_out_of_stock\":\"0\",\"stock_status\":\"in_stock\",\"weight\":\"0\",\"length\":\"0\",\"wide\":\"0\",\"height\":\"0\",\"is_added_attributes\":\"0\",\"has_product_options\":\"1\",\"related_products\":null,\"faq_schema_config\":[[{\"key\":\"question\",\"value\":null},{\"key\":\"answer\",\"value\":null}]],\"seo_meta\":{\"seo_title\":null,\"seo_description\":null,\"index\":\"index\"},\"seo_meta_image\":null,\"language\":\"en_US\",\"layout\":null,\"is_popular\":\"0\",\"status\":\"published\",\"store_id\":null,\"is_featured\":\"0\",\"categories\":[\"45\"],\"brand_id\":null,\"image\":\"siamese-algae-eater-min-300x300.jpg\",\"minimum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"maximum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"tag\":null,\"submitter\":\"save\"}', 'updated', 'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/130.0.0.0 Safari/537.36', '2405:201:800e:d0d0:ad7b:3351:47bb:df30', 3, 439, 'SIAMESE ALGAE EATER', 'primary', '2024-11-05 16:21:04', '2024-11-05 16:21:04'),
