(2667, 3, 'product', '{\"name\":\"OTOCINCLUS\",\"model\":\"Botble\\\\Ecommerce\\\\Models\\\\Product\",\"slug\":\"otocinclus\",\"slug_id\":\"474\",\"is_slug_editable\":\"1\",\"description\":\"<p><strong>The Otocinclus Catfish is one of THE most peaceful fish for the nano, community, or planted aquarium. It is also an effective algae eater and scavenger!<\\/strong><\\/p><p>&nbsp;<\\/p><p>Whether or not you have an algae problem in your tank, Otocinclus Catfish make a great addition to any aquarium community.&nbsp; Also known as Otto Cats, otos, or dwarf suckermouth catfish, these fish use their sucker-mouths to attack algae on the aquarium glass, plants, and decorations.&nbsp; In fact, they are widely considered one of the best algae-eating fish in the world, and groups of them form quite the cleanup crew with their voracious appetite for algae.<strong>&nbsp; <\\/strong>They come from fast-moving rivers in South America, so they do best in aquariums with strong currents (which can be achieved with good water filters or powerheads), good filtration, and plenty of aeration.<\\/p><p>Otocinclus Catfish are recognizable by the rows of armor-like plating along their bodies.&nbsp; They often have a variety of neutral colors on their bodies (such as browns, grays, and black) that form attractive patterns.&nbsp; We sell these fish in schools of 3 and 5 because they are known to do best in groups of 3 or more.&nbsp; These are small catfish, growing up to a maximum of 2 inches in length. &nbsp;They have very social personalities and are quite peaceful, making them completely safe to keep with other non-aggressive fish, shrimp, snails, and live plants.<\\/p><p>If algae is not present in your aquarium, the Otocinclus\' diets can be supplemented with algae wafers or vegetable-based flake food.<\\/p><p><strong>What We Like About This Fish:<\\/strong><\\/p><ul><li>Widely considered the best algae-eating fish in the freshwater aquarium hobby<\\/li><li>Very social personalities<\\/li><li>Safe with plants<\\/li><li>Completely peaceful<\\/li><\\/ul><p>&nbsp;<\\/p><p><strong>RECOMMENDED TANK PARAMETERS:&nbsp;<\\/strong><\\/p><ul><li><u>Temperature<\\/u>:&nbsp; 74\\u00b0 - 79\\u00b0 F (23\\u00b0 - 26\\u00b0 C)<\\/li><li><u>pH<\\/u>:&nbsp; 6.8 - 7.5<\\/li><li><u>KH<\\/u>:&nbsp; 2 - 10 dKH<\\/li><li><u>Minimum tank size<\\/u>:&nbsp; 10 gallons<\\/li><\\/ul><p>&nbsp;<\\/p><p><strong>CARE GUIDELINES:<\\/strong><\\/p><ul><li><u>Diet<\\/u>:&nbsp; Can mostly sustain themselves on algae.&nbsp; If algae is not present in your aquarium, their diets can be supplemented with algae wafers or vegetable-based flake foods.<\\/li><\\/ul><p><u>Social behavior<\\/u>:&nbsp; Peaceful, schooling\\/shoaling.<\\/p>\",\"content\":null,\"images\":[null,\"otocinclus-300x300.jpg\"],\"product_type\":\"physical\",\"sale_type\":\"0\",\"sku\":null,\"price\":\"150\",\"sale_price\":null,\"start_date\":null,\"end_date\":null,\"cost_per_item\":\"0\",\"product_id\":\"438\",\"barcode\":null,\"with_storehouse_management\":\"0\",\"quantity\":\"0\",\"allow_checkout_when_out_of_stock\":\"0\",\"stock_status\":\"in_stock\",\"weight\":\"0\",\"length\":\"0\",\"wide\":\"0\",\"height\":\"0\",\"is_added_attributes\":\"0\",\"has_product_options\":\"1\",\"related_products\":null,\"faq_schema_config\":[[{\"key\":\"question\",\"value\":null},{\"key\":\"answer\",\"value\":null}]],\"seo_meta\":{\"seo_title\":null,\"seo_description\":null,\"index\":\"index\"},\"seo_meta_image\":null,\"language\":\"en_US\",\"layout\":null,\"is_popular\":\"0\",\"status\":\"published\",\"store_id\":null,\"is_featured\":\"0\",\"categories\":[\"45\"],\"brand_id\":null,\"image\":\"otocinclus-300x300.jpg\",\"minimum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"maximum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"tag\":null,\"submitter\":\"save\"}', 'updated', 'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/130.0.0.0 Safari/537.36', '2405:201:800e:d0d0:ad7b:3351:47bb:df30', 3, 438, 'OTOCINCLUS', 'primary', '2024-11-05 16:21:42', '2024-11-05 16:21:42'),
(2668, 3, 'product', '{\"name\":\"MOUNTAIN MINNOW\",\"model\":\"Botble\\\\Ecommerce\\\\Models\\\\Product\",\"slug\":\"mountain-minnow\",\"slug_id\":\"472\",\"is_slug_editable\":\"1\",\"description\":\"<p><strong>Overview<\\/strong>: Mountain Minnow is popular with so many names like Canton danio, Chinese danio, and just white cloud. The scientific name of this beautiful aquarium fish is Tanichthys micagemmae. Small, pretty, colorful, and extremely attractive, Mountain Minnow is a perfect aquarium fish for both beginners and experts. Since they resemble neon tetras but are inexpensive than them, they are called as \\u2018the working man\\u2019s neon.\\u2019 Although there are many other identified genus of the same species, only one is suitable for aquariums viz., Tanichthys micagemmae (Vietnamese white cloud).<\\/p><p><strong>Distribution and Habitat<\\/strong>: It is believed that Mountain Minnow is a native of China and Vietnam where due to unsuitable and drastic changes in habitat, they disappeared. Later, they were found dwelling in the coastal province of Guangdong and Hainan Island in China. Today, mountain minnows are common in the aquarium trade and widely found in the different parts of the world.<\\/p><p><strong>Temperature<\\/strong>: The perfect range of temperature for mountain minnow varies between 15 and 20 degrees centigrade. The fish remain hardy and survive well when they are provided with the right temperature. Although minnow are not a demanding fish, when it comes to water conditions, the right range will help to live them longer. Also, when the temperature goes above 22 degrees, it becomes hard for them to survive.<\\/p><p><strong>Water Conditions<\\/strong>: An aquarium with good vegetation, some driftwood, and a darker ambiance is suitable for the mountain minnows. The ideal pH ranges between 6.0 and 8.0, and the hardiness needs to be between 5 and 19 dGH. Make sure these two critical parameters do not reach extreme; however, a little fluctuation is tolerable. The minnows are sensitive to copper; therefore, ensure using medication free from copper in the water.<\\/p><p><strong>Feeding<\\/strong>: Minnows are avid insect-eaters when in the wild. When they are in a tank, you can feed them a variety of food like frozen and flake food, live food, daphnia, shrimp, larvae, etc. they relish all types of food.<\\/p><p><strong>Breeding<\\/strong>: If you are breeding fish for the first-time, mountain minnow will be the best choice as they can breed all around the year. You can take a small tank of size 10 gallons and add some colorful mates for spawning. Make sure the females are twice as males in the tank. The right pH of water for spawning should remain between 6.5 and 7.5 while the right temperature should be 68 to 72 degrees Fahrenheit.<\\/p><p><strong>Lifespan<\\/strong>: when provided with the right temperature, water conditions, and enough food, the mountain minnow live for 4 to 5 years healthily.<\\/p>\",\"content\":null,\"images\":[null,\"mountain-minnow-min-300x300.jpg\"],\"product_type\":\"physical\",\"sale_type\":\"0\",\"sku\":null,\"price\":\"45\",\"sale_price\":null,\"start_date\":null,\"end_date\":null,\"cost_per_item\":\"0\",\"product_id\":\"436\",\"barcode\":null,\"with_storehouse_management\":\"0\",\"quantity\":\"0\",\"allow_checkout_when_out_of_stock\":\"0\",\"stock_status\":\"in_stock\",\"weight\":\"0\",\"length\":\"0\",\"wide\":\"0\",\"height\":\"0\",\"is_added_attributes\":\"0\",\"has_product_options\":\"1\",\"related_products\":null,\"faq_schema_config\":[[{\"key\":\"question\",\"value\":null},{\"key\":\"answer\",\"value\":null}]],\"seo_meta\":{\"seo_title\":null,\"seo_description\":null,\"index\":\"index\"},\"seo_meta_image\":null,\"language\":\"en_US\",\"layout\":null,\"is_popular\":\"0\",\"status\":\"published\",\"store_id\":null,\"is_featured\":\"0\",\"categories\":[\"45\"],\"brand_id\":null,\"image\":\"mountain-minnow-min-300x300.jpg\",\"minimum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"maximum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"tag\":null,\"submitter\":\"save\"}', 'updated', 'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/130.0.0.0 Safari/537.36', '2405:201:800e:d0d0:ad7b:3351:47bb:df30', 3, 436, 'MOUNTAIN MINNOW', 'primary', '2024-11-05 16:22:06', '2024-11-05 16:22:06'),
(2669, 3, 'product', '{\"name\":\"ENDLIER GUPPY\",\"model\":\"Botble\\\\Ecommerce\\\\Models\\\\Product\",\"slug\":\"endlier-guppy\",\"slug_id\":\"471\",\"is_slug_editable\":\"1\",\"description\":\"<p><strong>Overview<\\/strong>: Endler\\u2019s Guppy, also known as Endler\\u2019s livebearer or simply Endlers, belongs to the genus Poecilia. The scientific name of this guppy fish is Poecilia wingei. It is native to Paria Peninsula in Venezuela. Being a prolific breeder, Endlers often fascinates the aquarists who breed the fish for developing a hybrid. They are known to produce beautiful and attractive hybrids as they easily mate with the guppies. Also, they are undemanding in nature and very peaceful. Being small in size, they are perfect to have in small or nano aquariums. They are often found in beautiful neon blue, red\\/orange, and black coloration.<\\/p><p><strong>Distribution and Habitat<\\/strong>: Endler\\u2019s Guppy is very similar to fancy guppy as it embarks striking colors that make it unique. Also, the small size makes it ideal for small tanks. It was first identified in Venezuela in the year 1937 and later rediscovered in 1975. With striking colors, easy breeding, and live-bearing features, aquarists start showing interest in Endlers, making it one of the popular additions in the guppy\\u2019s group. They are undemanding and live happily with similar size fish in the tank.<\\/p><p><strong>Temperature<\\/strong>: The ideal temperature range for Endler\\u2019s Guppy is 24 to 30 degrees centigrade. Although they can tolerate a wide range of temperatures, keeping them within the right range is essential. It is when the fish thrives well and swim happily in the tank.<\\/p><p><strong>Water conditions<\\/strong>: In order to maintain the perfect water conditions, we need to keep an eye on the pH and hardness of the water. For Endler\\u2019s guppy, the perfect pH ranges from 7.0 to 8.5. Likewise, the hardness should remain between 15 - 35 dKH. Always make sure that these two water parameters are in the correct range for the best health of the fish.<\\/p><p><strong>Breeding<\\/strong>: Endler\\u2019s guppies are prolific breeders. Their striking colors, small size, and live-bearing nature make them ideal for the breeders. They can easily generate their new generation, which in general, comprises attractive colorations. So, if you are a breeder and looking for an easy to breed fish, Endler\\u2019s guppy could be a great choice.<\\/p><p><strong>Feeding<\\/strong>: In general, Endler\\u2019s Guppy prefers remaining in the top level of the tank. However, when fed, they move to the middle and bottom-most parts as well to eat the food. They are not a picky eater. You can give them a variety of food, whether they are live, frozen, or dried. Being omnivorous and unfussy in nature, they again add to their value for an aquarist. Pellets, blood worms, Freeze-dried tubifex are some of the favorite food of this fish.<\\/p><p><strong>Lifespan<\\/strong>: Endler\\u2019s Guppy can live for 1.5 to 2 years when they are well-fed and provided with the right water conditions. Since they are top dwellers and do not hesitate to jump, make sure you keep the lid of the tank closed or lower the water level.<\\/p>\",\"content\":null,\"images\":[null,\"endlier-guppy-min-300x300.jpg\"],\"product_type\":\"physical\",\"sale_type\":\"0\",\"sku\":null,\"price\":\"60\",\"sale_price\":null,\"start_date\":null,\"end_date\":null,\"cost_per_item\":\"0\",\"product_id\":\"435\",\"barcode\":null,\"with_storehouse_management\":\"0\",\"quantity\":\"0\",\"allow_checkout_when_out_of_stock\":\"0\",\"stock_status\":\"in_stock\",\"weight\":\"0\",\"length\":\"0\",\"wide\":\"0\",\"height\":\"0\",\"is_added_attributes\":\"0\",\"has_product_options\":\"1\",\"related_products\":null,\"faq_schema_config\":[[{\"key\":\"question\",\"value\":null},{\"key\":\"answer\",\"value\":null}]],\"seo_meta\":{\"seo_title\":null,\"seo_description\":null,\"index\":\"index\"},\"seo_meta_image\":null,\"language\":\"en_US\",\"layout\":null,\"is_popular\":\"0\",\"status\":\"published\",\"store_id\":null,\"is_featured\":\"0\",\"categories\":[\"45\"],\"brand_id\":null,\"image\":\"endlier-guppy-min-300x300.jpg\",\"minimum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"maximum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"tag\":null}', 'updated', 'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/130.0.0.0 Safari/537.36', '2405:201:800e:d0d0:ad7b:3351:47bb:df30', 3, 435, 'ENDLIER GUPPY', 'primary', '2024-11-05 16:22:27', '2024-11-05 16:22:27'),
