(2674, 3, 'product', '{\"name\":\"RED BADIS\",\"model\":\"Botble\\\\Ecommerce\\\\Models\\\\Product\",\"slug\":\"red-badis\",\"slug_id\":\"467\",\"is_slug_editable\":\"1\",\"description\":\"<p>Red Badis: One of our favorite nano fishes that you may find is the scarlet badi, a very popular freshwater fish.<\\/p><p>Red Badis are quite entertaining to watch because of their beauty, degree of energy, and behaviour. Additionally, they don\\u2019t need much effort to be healthy!<\\/p><p>Having said that, there are several essential aspects of caring for Scarlet Badis that you should be aware of if you want them to prosper and lead a full, stress-free existence.<\\/p><p>These tiny fish will do well in constrained situations. The males will grow to a length of 0.8 inches. The females are much more little, growing to only 0.5 inches in length.<\\/p><p>They are known as micro fish because they may be kept in tanks as tiny as 10 gallons.<\\/p><p>The bodies of the males are alternately striped in red and turquoise. Despite their diminutive size, they are really attractive.<\\/p><p>It is simple to see why Scarlet Badis are also referred to as Gem Badis. Although the ladies are less vibrant, they are nonetheless stunning.<\\/p><p>Additionally, the female draws attention to the male\\u2019s vivid colours when they are swimming together.<\\/p><p><i><strong>II. You would love the fish because\\u2026<\\/strong><\\/i><\\/p><p>Red Badis is a little fish called the Scarlet Badis.<\\/p><p>Males are considerably smaller than females and rarely grow to a length of 1 inch.<\\/p><p>Additionally, the hues of men and females differ. Sexual dimorphism is the term for this distinction.<\\/p><p>Male adults are vivid red or rusty orange in colour. They have seven bands that extend from their flanks to their fins.<\\/p><p>Eight lines of silvery blue alternate with these stripes, and both lines extend along the fins.<\\/p><p>The ventral fins are typically bluish-white in hue with a white outline.<\\/p><p>One of the tiniest fish species is the scarlet badi, which belongs to the percoid superfamily, which also includes well-known species like the yellow perch<\\/p><p>(a gamefish native to North America) and the marine basslets.<\\/p><p>Small streams in India with modest water movement are their natural habitat. Specifically, the Brahmaputra River\\u2019s tributaries and tributaries.<\\/p><p>The Scarlet Badis may also be referred to as Badis bengalensis, an earlier name that has since been supplanted by Dario dario, depending on how ancient your sources are.<\\/p><p>It was previously placed in the genus alongside the larger, more similar-looking Blue Badis, Badis badis.<\\/p><p><i><strong>III. Is this fish species peaceful or hostile?<\\/strong><\\/i><\\/p><p>Is a peaceful fish.<\\/p><p><i><strong>IV. Species compatibility<\\/strong><\\/i><\\/p><p>Pearl danios (Peaceful temperament and small)&nbsp;Neon &amp; Small Tetras (Peaceful temperament and small)<\\/p><p><i><strong>V. How to feed this species?<\\/strong><\\/i><\\/p><p>Include fresh vegetables like spinach, cooked peas, and lettuce in a varied diet for optimal health.When preparing fish for breeding, live foods like blackworms, brine shrimp, and glass worms should be used as treats.<\\/p>\",\"content\":null,\"images\":[null,\"red-badis-min-300x300.jpg\"],\"product_type\":\"physical\",\"sale_type\":\"0\",\"sku\":null,\"price\":\"25\",\"sale_price\":null,\"start_date\":null,\"end_date\":null,\"cost_per_item\":\"0\",\"product_id\":\"431\",\"barcode\":null,\"with_storehouse_management\":\"0\",\"quantity\":\"0\",\"allow_checkout_when_out_of_stock\":\"0\",\"stock_status\":\"out_of_stock\",\"weight\":\"0\",\"length\":\"0\",\"wide\":\"0\",\"height\":\"0\",\"is_added_attributes\":\"0\",\"has_product_options\":\"1\",\"related_products\":null,\"faq_schema_config\":[[{\"key\":\"question\",\"value\":null},{\"key\":\"answer\",\"value\":null}]],\"seo_meta\":{\"seo_title\":null,\"seo_description\":null,\"index\":\"index\"},\"seo_meta_image\":null,\"language\":\"en_US\",\"layout\":null,\"is_popular\":\"0\",\"status\":\"draft\",\"store_id\":null,\"is_featured\":\"0\",\"categories\":[\"45\"],\"brand_id\":null,\"image\":\"red-badis-min-300x300.jpg\",\"minimum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"maximum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"tag\":null}', 'updated', 'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/130.0.0.0 Safari/537.36', '2405:201:800e:d0d0:ad7b:3351:47bb:df30', 3, 431, 'RED BADIS', 'primary', '2024-11-05 16:24:19', '2024-11-05 16:24:19'),
(2675, 3, 'product', '{\"name\":\"RED BADIS\",\"model\":\"Botble\\\\Ecommerce\\\\Models\\\\Product\",\"slug\":\"red-badis\",\"slug_id\":\"467\",\"is_slug_editable\":\"1\",\"description\":\"<p>Red Badis: One of our favorite nano fishes that you may find is the scarlet badi, a very popular freshwater fish.<\\/p><p>Red Badis are quite entertaining to watch because of their beauty, degree of energy, and behaviour. Additionally, they don\\u2019t need much effort to be healthy!<\\/p><p>Having said that, there are several essential aspects of caring for Scarlet Badis that you should be aware of if you want them to prosper and lead a full, stress-free existence.<\\/p><p>These tiny fish will do well in constrained situations. The males will grow to a length of 0.8 inches. The females are much more little, growing to only 0.5 inches in length.<\\/p><p>They are known as micro fish because they may be kept in tanks as tiny as 10 gallons.<\\/p><p>The bodies of the males are alternately striped in red and turquoise. Despite their diminutive size, they are really attractive.<\\/p><p>It is simple to see why Scarlet Badis are also referred to as Gem Badis. Although the ladies are less vibrant, they are nonetheless stunning.<\\/p><p>Additionally, the female draws attention to the male\\u2019s vivid colours when they are swimming together.<\\/p><p><i><strong>II. You would love the fish because\\u2026<\\/strong><\\/i><\\/p><p>Red Badis is a little fish called the Scarlet Badis.<\\/p><p>Males are considerably smaller than females and rarely grow to a length of 1 inch.<\\/p><p>Additionally, the hues of men and females differ. Sexual dimorphism is the term for this distinction.<\\/p><p>Male adults are vivid red or rusty orange in colour. They have seven bands that extend from their flanks to their fins.<\\/p><p>Eight lines of silvery blue alternate with these stripes, and both lines extend along the fins.<\\/p><p>The ventral fins are typically bluish-white in hue with a white outline.<\\/p><p>One of the tiniest fish species is the scarlet badi, which belongs to the percoid superfamily, which also includes well-known species like the yellow perch<\\/p><p>(a gamefish native to North America) and the marine basslets.<\\/p><p>Small streams in India with modest water movement are their natural habitat. Specifically, the Brahmaputra River\\u2019s tributaries and tributaries.<\\/p><p>The Scarlet Badis may also be referred to as Badis bengalensis, an earlier name that has since been supplanted by Dario dario, depending on how ancient your sources are.<\\/p><p>It was previously placed in the genus alongside the larger, more similar-looking Blue Badis, Badis badis.<\\/p><p><i><strong>III. Is this fish species peaceful or hostile?<\\/strong><\\/i><\\/p><p>Is a peaceful fish.<\\/p><p><i><strong>IV. Species compatibility<\\/strong><\\/i><\\/p><p>Pearl danios (Peaceful temperament and small)&nbsp;Neon &amp; Small Tetras (Peaceful temperament and small)<\\/p><p><i><strong>V. How to feed this species?<\\/strong><\\/i><\\/p><p>Include fresh vegetables like spinach, cooked peas, and lettuce in a varied diet for optimal health.When preparing fish for breeding, live foods like blackworms, brine shrimp, and glass worms should be used as treats.<\\/p>\",\"content\":null,\"images\":[null,\"red-badis-min-300x300.jpg\"],\"product_type\":\"physical\",\"sale_type\":\"0\",\"sku\":null,\"price\":\"25\",\"sale_price\":null,\"start_date\":null,\"end_date\":null,\"cost_per_item\":\"0\",\"product_id\":\"431\",\"barcode\":null,\"with_storehouse_management\":\"0\",\"quantity\":\"0\",\"allow_checkout_when_out_of_stock\":\"0\",\"stock_status\":\"out_of_stock\",\"weight\":\"0\",\"length\":\"0\",\"wide\":\"0\",\"height\":\"0\",\"is_added_attributes\":\"0\",\"has_product_options\":\"1\",\"related_products\":null,\"faq_schema_config\":[[{\"key\":\"question\",\"value\":null},{\"key\":\"answer\",\"value\":null}]],\"seo_meta\":{\"seo_title\":null,\"seo_description\":null,\"index\":\"index\"},\"seo_meta_image\":null,\"language\":\"en_US\",\"layout\":null,\"is_popular\":\"0\",\"status\":\"draft\",\"store_id\":null,\"is_featured\":\"0\",\"categories\":[\"45\"],\"brand_id\":null,\"image\":\"red-badis-min-300x300.jpg\",\"minimum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"maximum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"tag\":null,\"submitter\":\"save\"}', 'updated', 'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/130.0.0.0 Safari/537.36', '2405:201:800e:d0d0:ad7b:3351:47bb:df30', 3, 431, 'RED BADIS', 'primary', '2024-11-05 16:24:29', '2024-11-05 16:24:29'),
(2676, 3, 'product', '{\"name\":\"NBLUE BADIS\",\"model\":\"Botble\\\\Ecommerce\\\\Models\\\\Product\",\"slug\":\"nblue-badis\",\"slug_id\":\"466\",\"is_slug_editable\":\"1\",\"description\":\"<p>The Blue Badis (<i>Badis badis<\\/i>), also commonly known as the Chameleon Fish, is a nano-sized member of the perch family indigenous to the Ganges River system of India.&nbsp; The \\u201cchameleon fish\\u201d name refers to the unique ability of this fish, particularly adult males, to dramatically change colors during breeding and territorial behavior.&nbsp; The initial color in juveniles is mottled brown, tan, and red vertical striping.&nbsp; As the Blue Badis reaches maturity, males will often display more intense red and iridescent blue coloration on its fins.<\\/p><p>The Blue Badis is a micropredator requiring a diet of meaty foods.&nbsp; Many specimens will not accept dry flake and pellet foods, so live and frozen foods should be regularly offered.&nbsp; In nature, this fish eats various small worms, small crustaceans, insects and insect larvae.&nbsp; In the aquarium, glassworms, enriched Artemia, and Daphnia will make an excellent staple diet.&nbsp; Bloodworms and Tubifex worms can be fed on occasion, but should not be fed as a regular diet since they can lead to obesity problems with this species.<\\/p><p>The aquarium of the Blue Badis should include plenty of rockwork and driftwood.&nbsp; This fish is a cave spawner, so it is also a good idea to shape some d\\u00e9cor into cave-like structures.&nbsp; During spawning, the male will guard the eggs and newly-hatched fry, but any adults should be removed thereafter if you want to avoid cannibalism of the fry by the parents.<\\/p><p>The Blue Badis will thrive in a planted aquarium with relatively mild to moderate water flow and is generally peaceful with other species of fish.&nbsp; Though it is a predator, its small size makes it safe with all but the very tiniest fish.&nbsp; It can be housed with some invertebrates such as snails and larger shrimp, but it may eat most&nbsp;<i>Caridina<\\/i>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<i>Neocaridina<\\/i>&nbsp;shrimp. It may hybridize with other Badis species, although it is unlikely to do so with the Scarlet Badis (<i>Dario dario<\\/i>) due to the size difference.<\\/p><p><strong>What We Like About This Fish:<\\/strong><\\/p><ul><li>Iridescent blue and red coloration in males during courtship and territorial behavior<\\/li><li>Peaceful disposition with most fish<\\/li><li>Hardy and adaptable<\\/li><li>Very active in middle and lower levels of the aquarium<\\/li><\\/ul><p><strong>&nbsp;<\\/strong><\\/p><p><strong>RECOMMENDED TANK PARAMETERS:<\\/strong><\\/p><ul><li><u>Temperature<\\/u>:&nbsp; 59\\u00b0 - 77\\u00b0 F (15\\u00b0 - 25\\u00b0 C)<\\/li><li><u>pH<\\/u>:&nbsp; 6.0 - 7.5<\\/li><li><u>KH<\\/u>:&nbsp; 10 - 15 dKH<\\/li><li><u>Minimum tank size<\\/u>:&nbsp; 20 gallons<\\/li><\\/ul><p><strong>&nbsp;<\\/strong><\\/p><p><strong>CARE GUIDELINES:&nbsp;<\\/strong><\\/p><ul><li><u>Diet<\\/u>:&nbsp; Meaty foods, especially frozen foods such as Daphnia and Artemia, Bloodworms and Tubifex worms on occasion only. &nbsp;Dry foods will often be ignored.<\\/li><li><u>Social behavior<\\/u>:&nbsp; Mostly peaceful, loosely schooling\\/shoaling in small groups. Adult males can be territorial with other males.<\\/li><\\/ul>\",\"content\":null,\"images\":[null,\"nblue-badis-min-300x300.jpg\"],\"product_type\":\"physical\",\"sale_type\":\"0\",\"sku\":null,\"price\":\"25\",\"sale_price\":null,\"start_date\":null,\"end_date\":null,\"cost_per_item\":\"0\",\"product_id\":\"430\",\"barcode\":null,\"with_storehouse_management\":\"0\",\"quantity\":\"0\",\"allow_checkout_when_out_of_stock\":\"0\",\"stock_status\":\"in_stock\",\"weight\":\"0\",\"length\":\"0\",\"wide\":\"0\",\"height\":\"0\",\"is_added_attributes\":\"0\",\"has_product_options\":\"1\",\"related_products\":null,\"faq_schema_config\":[[{\"key\":\"question\",\"value\":null},{\"key\":\"answer\",\"value\":null}]],\"seo_meta\":{\"seo_title\":null,\"seo_description\":null,\"index\":\"index\"},\"seo_meta_image\":null,\"language\":\"en_US\",\"layout\":null,\"is_popular\":\"0\",\"status\":\"published\",\"store_id\":null,\"is_featured\":\"0\",\"categories\":[\"45\"],\"brand_id\":null,\"image\":\"nblue-badis-min-300x300.jpg\",\"minimum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"maximum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"tag\":null,\"submitter\":\"save\"}', 'updated', 'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/130.0.0.0 Safari/537.36', '2405:201:800e:d0d0:ad7b:3351:47bb:df30', 3, 430, 'NBLUE BADIS', 'primary', '2024-11-05 16:26:05', '2024-11-05 16:26:05'),
(2677, 3, 'product', '{\"name\":\"ASSAMISE BADIS\",\"model\":\"Botble\\\\Ecommerce\\\\Models\\\\Product\",\"slug\":\"assamise-badis\",\"slug_id\":\"465\",\"is_slug_editable\":\"1\",\"description\":\"<p>The Badis assamensis, commonly known as the Assam Badis, is a captivating freshwater fish species native to parts of India and Bangladesh. Specifically found in the Brahmaputra River basin, they inhabit slow-moving waters, including streams and swamps.<\\/p><p>Physically, the Assam Badis is characterized by its elongated body and vibrant coloration. Males typically display more intense colors, featuring shades of red, blue, and green, especially during courtship and spawning. They typically grow to a size of about 2 to 3 inches (5-7.5 cm).<\\/p><p>In their natural habitat, Assam Badis thrive in densely planted aquariums with areas for swimming and hiding spots provided by plants and small caves. They prefer soft to slightly hard water conditions, and maintaining a stable and clean environment with proper filtration contributes to their overall well-being.<\\/p><p>Known for their territorial behavior, Assam Badis are best kept in a species-only tank or with very small, peaceful tankmates. They are not suitable for community aquariums due to their territorial nature. A well-balanced diet, including live or frozen foods like small insects and microorganisms, meets their nutritional needs.<\\/p><p>Maintaining water conditions within the range of 72-79\\u00b0F (22-26\\u00b0C) and a pH level between 6.0 to 7.5 is advisable. Regular water changes and proper filtration contribute to their health and vitality.<\\/p><p>Breeding Assam Badis in captivity is possible but can be challenging due to their specific requirements. Creating a breeding tank with soft, acidic water and providing hiding spots with dense vegetation encourage successful spawning. Males intensify their colors during courtship.<\\/p><p>In summary, the Assam Badis is a captivating and colorful addition to aquariums, appreciated for its vibrant hues and unique behaviors. Recreating their natural habitat from the Brahmaputra River basin and adhering to proper care conditions contribute to their well-being in captivity.<\\/p>\",\"content\":null,\"images\":[null,\"assamise-badis-min-300x300.jpg\"],\"product_type\":\"physical\",\"sale_type\":\"0\",\"sku\":null,\"price\":\"25\",\"sale_price\":null,\"start_date\":null,\"end_date\":null,\"cost_per_item\":\"0\",\"product_id\":\"429\",\"barcode\":null,\"with_storehouse_management\":\"0\",\"quantity\":\"0\",\"allow_checkout_when_out_of_stock\":\"0\",\"stock_status\":\"in_stock\",\"weight\":\"0\",\"length\":\"0\",\"wide\":\"0\",\"height\":\"0\",\"is_added_attributes\":\"0\",\"has_product_options\":\"1\",\"related_products\":null,\"faq_schema_config\":[[{\"key\":\"question\",\"value\":null},{\"key\":\"answer\",\"value\":null}]],\"seo_meta\":{\"seo_title\":null,\"seo_description\":null,\"index\":\"index\"},\"seo_meta_image\":null,\"language\":\"en_US\",\"layout\":null,\"is_popular\":\"0\",\"status\":\"published\",\"store_id\":null,\"is_featured\":\"0\",\"categories\":[\"45\"],\"brand_id\":null,\"image\":\"assamise-badis-min-300x300.jpg\",\"minimum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"maximum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"tag\":null,\"submitter\":\"save\"}', 'updated', 'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/130.0.0.0 Safari/537.36', '2405:201:800e:d0d0:ad7b:3351:47bb:df30', 3, 429, 'ASSAMISE BADIS', 'primary', '2024-11-05 16:26:35', '2024-11-05 16:26:35'),
(2678, 3, 'product', '{\"name\":\"ASSAMISE BADIS\",\"model\":\"Botble\\\\Ecommerce\\\\Models\\\\Product\",\"slug\":\"assamise-badis\",\"slug_id\":\"465\",\"is_slug_editable\":\"1\",\"description\":\"<p>The Badis assamensis, commonly known as the Assam Badis, is a captivating freshwater fish species native to parts of India and Bangladesh. Specifically found in the Brahmaputra River basin, they inhabit slow-moving waters, including streams and swamps.<\\/p><p>Physically, the Assam Badis is characterized by its elongated body and vibrant coloration. Males typically display more intense colors, featuring shades of red, blue, and green, especially during courtship and spawning. They typically grow to a size of about 2 to 3 inches (5-7.5 cm).<\\/p><p>In their natural habitat, Assam Badis thrive in densely planted aquariums with areas for swimming and hiding spots provided by plants and small caves. They prefer soft to slightly hard water conditions, and maintaining a stable and clean environment with proper filtration contributes to their overall well-being.<\\/p><p>Known for their territorial behavior, Assam Badis are best kept in a species-only tank or with very small, peaceful tankmates. They are not suitable for community aquariums due to their territorial nature. A well-balanced diet, including live or frozen foods like small insects and microorganisms, meets their nutritional needs.<\\/p><p>Maintaining water conditions within the range of 72-79\\u00b0F (22-26\\u00b0C) and a pH level between 6.0 to 7.5 is advisable. Regular water changes and proper filtration contribute to their health and vitality.<\\/p><p>Breeding Assam Badis in captivity is possible but can be challenging due to their specific requirements. Creating a breeding tank with soft, acidic water and providing hiding spots with dense vegetation encourage successful spawning. Males intensify their colors during courtship.<\\/p><p>In summary, the Assam Badis is a captivating and colorful addition to aquariums, appreciated for its vibrant hues and unique behaviors. Recreating their natural habitat from the Brahmaputra River basin and adhering to proper care conditions contribute to their well-being in captivity.<\\/p>\",\"content\":null,\"images\":[null,\"assamise-badis-min-300x300.jpg\"],\"product_type\":\"physical\",\"sale_type\":\"0\",\"sku\":null,\"price\":\"25\",\"sale_price\":null,\"start_date\":null,\"end_date\":null,\"cost_per_item\":\"0\",\"product_id\":\"429\",\"barcode\":null,\"with_storehouse_management\":\"0\",\"quantity\":\"0\",\"allow_checkout_when_out_of_stock\":\"0\",\"stock_status\":\"in_stock\",\"weight\":\"0\",\"length\":\"0\",\"wide\":\"0\",\"height\":\"0\",\"is_added_attributes\":\"0\",\"has_product_options\":\"1\",\"related_products\":null,\"faq_schema_config\":[[{\"key\":\"question\",\"value\":null},{\"key\":\"answer\",\"value\":null}]],\"seo_meta\":{\"seo_title\":null,\"seo_description\":null,\"index\":\"index\"},\"seo_meta_image\":null,\"submitter\":\"save\",\"language\":\"en_US\",\"layout\":null,\"is_popular\":\"0\",\"status\":\"published\",\"store_id\":null,\"is_featured\":\"0\",\"categories\":[\"45\"],\"brand_id\":null,\"image\":\"assamise-badis-min-300x300.jpg\",\"minimum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"maximum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"tag\":null}', 'updated', 'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/130.0.0.0 Safari/537.36', '2405:201:800e:d0d0:ad7b:3351:47bb:df30', 3, 429, 'ASSAMISE BADIS', 'primary', '2024-11-05 16:27:15', '2024-11-05 16:27:15'),
(2679, 3, 'product', '{\"name\":\"TROCOLOUR ORANDA\",\"model\":\"Botble\\\\Ecommerce\\\\Models\\\\Product\",\"slug\":\"trocolour-oranda\",\"slug_id\":\"464\",\"is_slug_editable\":\"1\",\"description\":\"<p>The Tri-Color Oranda is a distinctive and visually striking variety of the Oranda Goldfish (Carassius auratus). Oranda Goldfish are known for their unique appearance, characterized by a prominent growth on the head called a \\u201cwen\\u201d or \\u201chood,\\u201d which can cover their entire head. The Tri-Color Oranda, as the name suggests, is recognized for its tri-coloration and impressive wen growth. Here are some key features and information about the Tri-Color Oranda:<\\/p><p>Tri-Color Orandas have a tri-colored pattern, typically consisting of red, white, and black markings. The red coloration can appear on the body, while the white and black colors are often on the fins, tail, and head. The exact distribution of colors may vary among individual fish.<\\/p><p>One of the standout features of the Tri-Color Oranda is the growth of the wen or hood. The wen covers the head and can develop into a substantial and fleshy mass, giving the fish a unique and charming appearance. The wen\\u2019s coloration may vary but often matches the body color.<\\/p><p>Oranda Goldfish, including the Tri-Color variety, can grow relatively large. They can reach lengths of up to 8 to 12 inches (20 to 30 centimeters) or even more in well-maintained aquariums or ponds.<\\/p><p>Tri-Color Orandas require a spacious aquarium with ample room to swim, as well as good water quality. They are hardy fish, but their wen growth requires careful attention. The wen is sensitive and prone to injury, so it\\u2019s essential to maintain excellent water conditions to prevent infections or injuries.<\\/p><p>Provide your Tri-Color Oranda with a well-planted aquarium with hiding places and open swimming areas. Ensure that the tank has a suitable filtration system to maintain water quality.<\\/p><p>Oranda Goldfish are generally peaceful and sociable. They are known for their curious and friendly nature, making them enjoyable to observe in a community tank.<\\/p><p>Tri-Color Orandas are beloved by fish enthusiasts for their unique and eye-catching appearance. Their striking coloration, distinctive wen growth, and friendly disposition make them a popular choice for aquarium keepers who are looking to add a touch of elegance to their aquatic displays. Proper care and attention to water quality are essential to ensure the health and well-being of these remarkable fish.<\\/p><p><span><strong>III. Is this fish species peaceful or hostile?<\\/strong><\\/span><\\/p><p><span>Extremely peaceful fish.<\\/span><\\/p><p><i><span><strong>IV. Species compatibility<\\/strong><\\/span><\\/i><\\/p><p>When keeping Tri-Color Orandas, choose tank mates that are peaceful and won\\u2019t nip at their long fins or disturb their wen growth. Other goldfish varieties, such as other Orandas or fancy goldfish, can make suitable companions.<\\/p><p>Avoid keeping them with aggressive or fin-nipping fish, as their delicate fins can be easily damaged.<\\/p><p><i><span><strong>V. How to feed this species?<\\/strong><\\/span><\\/i><\\/p><p>These goldfish are omnivorous and enjoy a varied diet. You can feed them high-quality pellets or flakes formulated for goldfish, as well as occasional treats such as live or frozen foods like brine shrimp, bloodworms, and vegetables like peas.<\\/p>\",\"content\":null,\"images\":[null,\"trocolour-oranda-min-300x300.jpg\"],\"product_type\":\"physical\",\"botble-ecommerce-tables-product-variation-table-428_length\":\"10\",\"has_product_options\":\"1\",\"related_products\":null,\"faq_schema_config\":[[{\"key\":\"question\",\"value\":null},{\"key\":\"answer\",\"value\":null}]],\"seo_meta\":{\"seo_title\":null,\"seo_description\":null,\"index\":\"index\"},\"seo_meta_image\":null,\"language\":\"en_US\",\"layout\":null,\"is_popular\":\"0\",\"status\":\"published\",\"store_id\":null,\"is_featured\":\"0\",\"categories\":[\"45\"],\"brand_id\":null,\"sku\":null,\"image\":\"trocolour-oranda-min-300x300.jpg\",\"product_labels\":[\"2\"],\"minimum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"maximum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"tag\":null,\"submitter\":\"save\"}', 'updated', 'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/130.0.0.0 Safari/537.36', '2405:201:800e:d0d0:ad7b:3351:47bb:df30', 3, 428, 'TROCOLOUR ORANDA', 'primary', '2024-11-05 16:32:35', '2024-11-05 16:32:35'),
(2680, 3, 'product', '{\"name\":\"CALICO ORANDA\",\"model\":\"Botble\\\\Ecommerce\\\\Models\\\\Product\",\"slug\":\"calico-oranda\",\"slug_id\":\"463\",\"is_slug_editable\":\"1\",\"description\":\"<p>The Calico Oranda features a festive, confetti-like blend of reds, oranges, white, and black. This coloration gives the Calico Oranda wonderful character and adds instant visual interest. The Calico Oranda closely resembles Veil Tail goldfish varieties in the shape and length of the tail, and is one of many varieties of what is collectively known as ornamental or fancy goldfish;&nbsp;<i>Carassius auratus auratus<\\/i>. Originally from parts of Asia, Japan, and China, Fancy Goldfish enjoy worldwide distribution due to controlled breeding programs.<\\/p><p>As a member of the carp family, the Calico Oranda is generally quite hardy. They will do well in 30 gallon aquariums or larger, as well as backyard garden ponds of 180 gallons or more. In addition to a fine gravel bottom or well-rounded river rocks, the Calico Oranda will appreciate hardy, cold water plants. Keep in mind that goldfish are diggers and will scatter the fine sand onto leaves, injuring thin and less hardy plants.<\\/p><p>There appears to be a definite courtship ritual when goldfish breed. Breeding often results in up to 1,000 eggs, with fry hatching in five to six days. They should be fed small pieces of live or prepared foods designed for egg-laying fish.<\\/p><p>Goldfish are omnivorous and will eat all types of dried and live foods. However, limit protein intake to 30% of the diet. Goldfish flake or pellet food will provide these fish with the proper nutrition.<\\/p>\",\"content\":null,\"images\":[null,\"calico-oranda-min-300x300.jpg\"],\"product_type\":\"physical\",\"sale_type\":\"0\",\"sku\":null,\"price\":\"600\",\"sale_price\":null,\"start_date\":null,\"end_date\":null,\"cost_per_item\":\"0\",\"product_id\":\"427\",\"barcode\":null,\"with_storehouse_management\":\"0\",\"quantity\":\"0\",\"allow_checkout_when_out_of_stock\":\"0\",\"stock_status\":\"out_of_stock\",\"weight\":\"0\",\"length\":\"0\",\"wide\":\"0\",\"height\":\"0\",\"is_added_attributes\":\"0\",\"has_product_options\":\"1\",\"related_products\":null,\"faq_schema_config\":[[{\"key\":\"question\",\"value\":null},{\"key\":\"answer\",\"value\":null}]],\"seo_meta\":{\"seo_title\":null,\"seo_description\":null,\"index\":\"index\"},\"seo_meta_image\":null,\"language\":\"en_US\",\"layout\":null,\"is_popular\":\"0\",\"status\":\"draft\",\"store_id\":null,\"is_featured\":\"0\",\"categories\":[\"45\"],\"brand_id\":null,\"image\":\"calico-oranda-min-300x300.jpg\",\"minimum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"maximum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"tag\":null,\"submitter\":\"save\"}', 'updated', 'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/130.0.0.0 Safari/537.36', '2405:201:800e:d0d0:ad7b:3351:47bb:df30', 3, 427, 'CALICO ORANDA', 'primary', '2024-11-05 16:33:32', '2024-11-05 16:33:32'),
(2681, 3, 'product', '{\"name\":\"GREEN TIGER BARB\",\"model\":\"Botble\\\\Ecommerce\\\\Models\\\\Product\",\"slug\":\"green-tiger-barb\",\"slug_id\":\"462\",\"is_slug_editable\":\"1\",\"description\":\"<p>The Green Tiger Barb (<i>Pethia nigrofasciata<\\/i>) is a very&nbsp;peaceful species that is an excellent fish for the community planted aquarium. It is known for its small size and black striping, but is most desired for the brilliant ruby coloration that males develop during spawning behaviour. This fish is also rather versatile regarding water conditions.<\\/p><p>The Green Tiger Barb typically occupies the top and middle level of the water column, although it can often be seen swimming and feeding in the middle and bottom levels as well. It is safe with other peaceful, small fish. It may prey on smaller dwarf shrimp and their fry. Larger, peaceful invertebrates can make good tank mates. The Green Tiger Barb must be kept in groups of 6 or more, although larger groups are more ideal so that subdominant specimens are not bullied by dominant individuals during breeding behaviour. Its natural habitat is tropical rainforest areas that typically have clear water. It requires clean water to thrive and it will display optimal coloration and health in a planted aquarium with dark substrate.<\\/p><p>&nbsp;<\\/p><p>While not a picky eater, The Green Tiger Barb will thrive and remain very colourful on a varied diet of&nbsp;omnivorous foods. High-quality flake food, pellets, and live, frozen, or freeze-dried&nbsp;<i>Artemia<\\/i>, microworms,&nbsp;<i>Tubifex<\\/i>, and finely chopped bloodworms will all be readily accepted. Some vegetable matter, especially dry food high in vegetable content, is essential for optimal health and coloration.<\\/p><div class=\\\"rte sm:text-start text-start js-product-description\\\"><p>What We Like About This Fish:<\\/p><ul><li>Males develop beautiful green coloration with maturity<\\/li><li>Peaceful disposition with fish and peaceful invertebrates too large to be considered prey<\\/li><li>Very active and noticeable fish in any aquarium<\\/li><li>Ideal for planted aquariums<\\/li><\\/ul><p>&nbsp;<\\/p><p><strong>RECOMMENDED TANK PARAMETERS:<\\/strong><\\/p><p>&nbsp;<\\/p><ul><li>Temperature: 68 - 81\\u00b0 F (20\\u00b0-27\\u00b0 C)<\\/li><li>pH:&nbsp;5.5 - 7.5<\\/li><li>KH: 3 - 12 dKH<\\/li><li>Minimum Tank Size: 20 gallons for a group of 6 \\u2013 8<\\/li><\\/ul><p>&nbsp;<\\/p><p><strong>CARE INFORMATION:<\\/strong><\\/p><ul><li>Diet: Omnivore\\/Micropredator. Will easily accept high quality dry and frozen foods of appropriate size. Requires a varied diet, including vegetable matter, for optimal health and coloration.<\\/li><li><u>Social Behaviour:<\\/u>&nbsp;Peaceful, schooling\\/shoaling.<\\/li><\\/ul><\\/div><div class=\\\"dbtfy-back-in-stock-container\\\"><div class=\\\"dbtfy-back-in-stock\\\">&nbsp;<\\/div><\\/div>\",\"content\":null,\"images\":[null,\"green-tiger-barb-min-300x300.jpg\"],\"product_type\":\"physical\",\"sale_type\":\"0\",\"sku\":null,\"price\":\"50\",\"sale_price\":null,\"start_date\":null,\"end_date\":null,\"cost_per_item\":\"0\",\"product_id\":\"426\",\"barcode\":null,\"with_storehouse_management\":\"0\",\"quantity\":\"0\",\"allow_checkout_when_out_of_stock\":\"0\",\"stock_status\":\"in_stock\",\"weight\":\"0\",\"length\":\"0\",\"wide\":\"0\",\"height\":\"0\",\"is_added_attributes\":\"0\",\"has_product_options\":\"1\",\"related_products\":null,\"faq_schema_config\":[[{\"key\":\"question\",\"value\":null},{\"key\":\"answer\",\"value\":null}]],\"seo_meta\":{\"seo_title\":null,\"seo_description\":null,\"index\":\"index\"},\"seo_meta_image\":null,\"language\":\"en_US\",\"layout\":null,\"is_popular\":\"0\",\"status\":\"published\",\"store_id\":null,\"is_featured\":\"0\",\"categories\":[\"45\"],\"brand_id\":null,\"image\":\"green-tiger-barb-min-300x300.jpg\",\"minimum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"maximum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"tag\":null,\"submitter\":\"save\"}', 'updated', 'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/130.0.0.0 Safari/537.36', '2405:201:800e:d0d0:ad7b:3351:47bb:df30', 3, 426, 'GREEN TIGER BARB', 'primary', '2024-11-05 16:34:52', '2024-11-05 16:34:52'),
(2682, 3, 'product', '{\"name\":\"RED TIGER BARB\",\"model\":\"Botble\\\\Ecommerce\\\\Models\\\\Product\",\"slug\":\"red-tiger-barb\",\"slug_id\":\"461\",\"is_slug_editable\":\"1\",\"description\":\"<p>GloFish fluorescent fish are wonderful fish that add brilliant color and excitement to any aquarium. They are born with their harmless, life-long color (they\\u2019re not dyed, injected, or painted). They require the same care as other freshwater tropical fish. The Long-Fin Barbs swim slower than normal barbs and can be a great addition to a community tank.<\\/p><p>Please note that this purchase includes only the fish, so you will need to have an aquarium available for them when they arrive.<\\/p><p><strong>Care Note:<\\/strong>&nbsp;GloFish Fin Barbs should be kept in groups of five or more, as they can become aggressive toward other fish when they are in smaller groups.<\\/p>\",\"content\":null,\"images\":[null,\"untitled-design-min-300x300.jpg\"],\"product_type\":\"physical\",\"sale_type\":\"0\",\"sku\":null,\"price\":\"50\",\"sale_price\":null,\"start_date\":null,\"end_date\":null,\"cost_per_item\":\"0\",\"product_id\":\"425\",\"barcode\":null,\"with_storehouse_management\":\"0\",\"quantity\":\"0\",\"allow_checkout_when_out_of_stock\":\"0\",\"stock_status\":\"in_stock\",\"weight\":\"0\",\"length\":\"0\",\"wide\":\"0\",\"height\":\"0\",\"is_added_attributes\":\"0\",\"has_product_options\":\"1\",\"related_products\":null,\"faq_schema_config\":[[{\"key\":\"question\",\"value\":null},{\"key\":\"answer\",\"value\":null}]],\"seo_meta\":{\"seo_title\":null,\"seo_description\":null,\"index\":\"index\"},\"seo_meta_image\":null,\"language\":\"en_US\",\"layout\":null,\"is_popular\":\"0\",\"status\":\"published\",\"store_id\":null,\"is_featured\":\"0\",\"categories\":[\"45\"],\"brand_id\":null,\"image\":\"untitled-design-min-300x300.jpg\",\"minimum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"maximum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"tag\":null,\"submitter\":\"save\"}', 'updated', 'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/130.0.0.0 Safari/537.36', '2405:201:800e:d0d0:ad7b:3351:47bb:df30', 3, 425, 'RED TIGER BARB', 'primary', '2024-11-05 16:35:11', '2024-11-05 16:35:11'),
(2683, 3, 'product', '{\"name\":\"RED BALLON PLATY\",\"model\":\"Botble\\\\Ecommerce\\\\Models\\\\Product\",\"slug\":\"red-ballon-platy\",\"slug_id\":\"460\",\"is_slug_editable\":\"1\",\"description\":\"<p>The Balloon Red Platy Fish is a delightful addition to any freshwater aquarium, known for its vibrant red color and unique balloon-like body shape. This livebearer fish is not only visually appealing but also easy to care for, making it an ideal choice for both beginner and experienced aquarists.<\\/p><p><strong>Features:<\\/strong><\\/p><ul><li><strong>Scientific Name:<\\/strong>&nbsp;Xiphophorus maculatus<\\/li><li><strong>Common Names:<\\/strong>&nbsp;Balloon Platy, Red Balloon Platy<\\/li><li><strong>Size:<\\/strong>&nbsp;Up to 2.5 inches (6 cm)<\\/li><li><strong>Lifespan:<\\/strong>&nbsp;2-3 years<\\/li><li><strong>Temperament:<\\/strong>&nbsp;Peaceful<\\/li><li><strong>Diet:<\\/strong>&nbsp;Omnivorous<\\/li><li><strong>Optimal Water Conditions:<\\/strong><ul><li><strong>Temperature:<\\/strong>&nbsp;70-82\\u00b0F (21-28\\u00b0C)<\\/li><li><strong>pH Level:<\\/strong>&nbsp;7.0-8.2<\\/li><li><strong>Hardness:<\\/strong>&nbsp;10-25 dGH<\\/li><\\/ul><\\/li><\\/ul><p><strong>Care Instructions:<\\/strong><\\/p><ol><li><strong>Tank Setup:<\\/strong><ul><li><strong>Tank Size:<\\/strong>&nbsp;Minimum 10 gallons (40 liters) for a small group.<\\/li><li><strong>Substrate:<\\/strong>&nbsp;Fine gravel or sand.<\\/li><li><strong>Plants:<\\/strong>&nbsp;Include plenty of live plants such as Java Fern, Anubias, and Hornwort to provide hiding spots and enhance the natural environment.<\\/li><li><strong>Decorations:<\\/strong>&nbsp;Add driftwood and rocks for additional hiding places and to create a stimulating environment.<\\/li><\\/ul><\\/li><li><strong>Water Quality:<\\/strong><ul><li>Perform regular water changes (25-30% weekly) to maintain high water quality.<\\/li><li>Use a reliable filter to keep the water clean and well-oxygenated.<\\/li><\\/ul><\\/li><li><strong>Feeding:<\\/strong><ul><li>Feed a varied diet consisting of high-quality flake food, frozen or live brine shrimp, daphnia, and bloodworms.<\\/li><li>Supplement with vegetable matter such as blanched spinach or spirulina flakes.<\\/li><\\/ul><\\/li><li><strong>Compatibility:<\\/strong><ul><li>Balloon Red Platy Fish are peaceful and can be kept with other non-aggressive fish such as Tetras, Guppies, Mollies, and Corydoras.<\\/li><li>Avoid keeping them with large or aggressive fish that may harm them.<\\/li><\\/ul><\\/li><li><strong>Breeding:<\\/strong><ul><li>Balloon Platies are livebearers, meaning they give birth to free-swimming fry.<\\/li><li>Provide plenty of plants or breeding boxes to protect the fry from being eaten by adult fish.<\\/li><li>Separate pregnant females into a breeding tank to ensure the safety of the fry.<\\/li><\\/ul><\\/li><\\/ol><p>You will get a pair (Male and Female) of Balloon Red platy fish. The packet is fully sealed with pure oxygen and it is safe to travel long distances for 5-7 days. Buying Balloon Red platy fishes online from aquastore is totally safe, we are delivering you with 100% satisfaction.<\\/p>\",\"content\":null,\"images\":[null,\"red-ballon-platy-min-300x300.jpg\"],\"product_type\":\"physical\",\"sale_type\":\"0\",\"sku\":null,\"price\":\"40\",\"sale_price\":null,\"start_date\":null,\"end_date\":null,\"cost_per_item\":\"0\",\"product_id\":\"424\",\"barcode\":null,\"with_storehouse_management\":\"0\",\"quantity\":\"0\",\"allow_checkout_when_out_of_stock\":\"0\",\"stock_status\":\"in_stock\",\"weight\":\"0\",\"length\":\"0\",\"wide\":\"0\",\"height\":\"0\",\"is_added_attributes\":\"0\",\"has_product_options\":\"1\",\"related_products\":null,\"faq_schema_config\":[[{\"key\":\"question\",\"value\":null},{\"key\":\"answer\",\"value\":null}]],\"seo_meta\":{\"seo_title\":null,\"seo_description\":null,\"index\":\"index\"},\"seo_meta_image\":null,\"language\":\"en_US\",\"layout\":null,\"is_popular\":\"0\",\"status\":\"published\",\"store_id\":null,\"is_featured\":\"0\",\"categories\":[\"45\"],\"brand_id\":null,\"image\":\"red-ballon-platy-min-300x300.jpg\",\"minimum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"maximum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"tag\":null,\"submitter\":\"save\"}', 'updated', 'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/130.0.0.0 Safari/537.36', '2405:201:800e:d0d0:ad7b:3351:47bb:df30', 3, 424, 'RED BALLON PLATY', 'primary', '2024-11-05 16:35:30', '2024-11-05 16:35:30'),
(2684, 3, 'product', '{\"name\":\"BALLON MOLLY\",\"model\":\"Botble\\\\Ecommerce\\\\Models\\\\Product\",\"slug\":\"ballon-molly\",\"slug_id\":\"459\",\"is_slug_editable\":\"1\",\"description\":\"<p>The Baloon Molly (<i>Poecilia latipinna\\/velifera<\\/i>) is one of the most celebrated and beautiful livebearers in the aquarium world, boasting a variety of stunning colour forms.&nbsp; It is affectionately known and named for the large, impressive dorsal fin displayed by males.&nbsp; This species has been bred extensively for decades and has been developed into nearly endless colour varieties including black, green, dalmatian, golden, harlequin\\/calico, chocolate, albino, creamsicle, and many others.&nbsp; While this fish originated from fresh, brackish, and saltwater habitats in southern North America, the tank-raised specimens available are almost exclusively raised and thrive in alkaline freshwater.&nbsp; This fish could be considered a larger fish in the world of small community fish because it grows to an size of 4 to 5 inches as an adult.&nbsp; Despite its large size, it has a generally peaceful yet outgoing disposition, and it makes a great addition to many mixed-species aquariums.<\\/p><p>The Baloon Molly compatible with most other peaceful aquarium species in a relatively spacious &nbsp;aquarium.&nbsp; It is an omnivore, so it will potentially prey on smaller dwarf shrimp and their fry, but it is otherwise safe to keep with peaceful invertebrates as well.&nbsp; This fish is not a picky eater and it will accept a variety of high quality dry foods, but these should be supplemented with a variety of frozen foods as well.&nbsp; It will mostly occupy the middle and upper regions of the aquarium, and it does have the ability to jump out of the water, especially while in the early stages of acclimating to a new aquarium.&nbsp; As a result, a secure lid is highly recommended to ensure that this fish does not jump out of the tank.<\\/p><p>Plants are not absolutely necessary for the Baloon Molly, but they will certainly be appreciated.&nbsp; All hardy stem plants, rooted plants, Marimo Moss Balls, and mosses are generally safe to keep with this fish as long as the Baloon Molly well fed.&nbsp; The Baloon Molly is an excellent fish for beginners as well as experts!<\\/p><p><strong>What We Like About This Fish:<\\/strong><\\/p><ul><li>Hardy and adaptable<\\/li><li>Beautiful variety of colours<\\/li><li>Excellent for medium and larger planted aquariums<\\/li><li>Peaceful disposition<\\/li><\\/ul><p>&nbsp;<\\/p><p><strong>RECOMMENDED TANK PARAMETERS:&nbsp;<\\/strong><\\/p><ul><li><u>Temperature<\\/u>:&nbsp; 72\\u00b0 - 80\\u00b0 F (22\\u00b0 - 26.7\\u00b0 C)<\\/li><li><u>pH<\\/u>:&nbsp;&nbsp;7.0 - 8.5, though 7.5 or higher is ideal<\\/li><li><u>KH<\\/u>:&nbsp; 15 - 35 dKH<\\/li><li><u>Minimum tank size<\\/u>:&nbsp; 10 gallons for a single specimen, 30+ gallons for a group<\\/li><\\/ul><p>&nbsp;<\\/p><p><strong>CARE GUIDELINES:<\\/strong><\\/p><ul><li><u>Diet<\\/u>:&nbsp; High quality flake foods and frozen foods, especially those high in plant matter.<\\/li><li><u>Social behaviour<\\/u>:&nbsp; Shoaling, peaceful with most species.<\\/li><\\/ul>\",\"content\":null,\"images\":[null,\"ballon-molly-min-300x300.jpg\"],\"product_type\":\"physical\",\"sale_type\":\"0\",\"sku\":null,\"price\":\"40\",\"sale_price\":null,\"start_date\":null,\"end_date\":null,\"cost_per_item\":\"0\",\"product_id\":\"423\",\"barcode\":null,\"with_storehouse_management\":\"1\",\"quantity\":\"5\",\"allow_checkout_when_out_of_stock\":\"1\",\"stock_status\":\"in_stock\",\"weight\":\"0\",\"length\":\"0\",\"wide\":\"0\",\"height\":\"0\",\"is_added_attributes\":\"0\",\"has_product_options\":\"1\",\"related_products\":null,\"faq_schema_config\":[[{\"key\":\"question\",\"value\":null},{\"key\":\"answer\",\"value\":null}]],\"seo_meta\":{\"seo_title\":null,\"seo_description\":null,\"index\":\"index\"},\"seo_meta_image\":null,\"language\":\"en_US\",\"layout\":null,\"is_popular\":\"0\",\"status\":\"published\",\"store_id\":null,\"is_featured\":\"0\",\"categories\":[\"45\"],\"brand_id\":null,\"image\":\"ballon-molly-min-300x300.jpg\",\"minimum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"maximum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"tag\":null,\"submitter\":\"save\"}', 'updated', 'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/130.0.0.0 Safari/537.36', '2405:201:800e:d0d0:ad7b:3351:47bb:df30', 3, 423, 'BALLON MOLLY', 'primary', '2024-11-05 16:36:27', '2024-11-05 16:36:27'),
(2685, 3, 'product', '{\"name\":\"YELLOW SNAIL\",\"model\":\"Botble\\\\Ecommerce\\\\Models\\\\Product\",\"slug\":\"yellow-snail\",\"slug_id\":\"458\",\"is_slug_editable\":\"1\",\"description\":\"<p>Pomacea canaliculata, commonly known as the golden apple snail or the channeled apple snail, is a species of large freshwater snail with gills and an operculum, an aquatic gastropod mollusc in the family Ampullariidae, the apple snails.<\\/p>\",\"content\":null,\"images\":[null,\"yellow-snail-min-300x300.jpg\"],\"product_type\":\"physical\",\"sale_type\":\"0\",\"sku\":null,\"price\":\"30\",\"sale_price\":null,\"start_date\":null,\"end_date\":null,\"cost_per_item\":\"0\",\"product_id\":\"422\",\"barcode\":null,\"with_storehouse_management\":\"0\",\"quantity\":\"0\",\"allow_checkout_when_out_of_stock\":\"0\",\"stock_status\":\"in_stock\",\"weight\":\"0\",\"length\":\"0\",\"wide\":\"0\",\"height\":\"0\",\"is_added_attributes\":\"0\",\"has_product_options\":\"1\",\"related_products\":null,\"faq_schema_config\":[[{\"key\":\"question\",\"value\":null},{\"key\":\"answer\",\"value\":null}]],\"seo_meta\":{\"seo_title\":null,\"seo_description\":null,\"index\":\"index\"},\"seo_meta_image\":null,\"language\":\"en_US\",\"layout\":null,\"is_popular\":\"0\",\"status\":\"published\",\"store_id\":null,\"is_featured\":\"0\",\"categories\":[\"45\"],\"brand_id\":null,\"image\":\"yellow-snail-min-300x300.jpg\",\"minimum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"maximum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"tag\":null,\"submitter\":\"save\"}', 'updated', 'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/130.0.0.0 Safari/537.36', '2405:201:800e:d0d0:ad7b:3351:47bb:df30', 3, 422, 'YELLOW SNAIL', 'primary', '2024-11-05 16:36:43', '2024-11-05 16:36:43');
INSERT INTO `audit_histories` (`id`, `user_id`, `module`, `request`, `action`, `user_agent`, `ip_address`, `reference_user`, `reference_id`, `reference_name`, `type`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
(2686, 3, 'product', '{\"name\":\"GERMAN RAMIREZI\",\"model\":\"Botble\\\\Ecommerce\\\\Models\\\\Product\",\"slug\":\"german-ramirezi\",\"slug_id\":\"456\",\"is_slug_editable\":\"1\",\"description\":\"<div>German Blue Ram Cichlids are known throughout the aquarium hobby not only for their fantastically iridescent colors, but also for their charming and playful personalities.&nbsp; These little beauties feature yellow-green bodies dotted with stunning electric blue markings.&nbsp; These fish also have a dark stripe that runs vertically through their blood red eyes, which is sometimes accompanied by more vertical stripes across the body.&nbsp; Some specimens also have shimmering pink bellies.&nbsp; Their large, spiky fins are trimmed in red and black, which may make these friendly fish appear much more intimidating than they actually are.&nbsp; German Blue Ram Cichlids range from 1 to 2 inches in length.<\\/div><div>&nbsp;<\\/div><div>These cichlids hail from the river basins of Venezuela and Colombia, so their natural environment consists of warm and slow-moving waters.&nbsp; When keeping these fish, it is very important to maintain high quality of water in your tank and to keep it within the recommended water parameters.&nbsp; Like most fish, they do best in tanks that have live plants, rocks, or driftwood that provides them with cover.&nbsp; Under ideal conditions, German Blue Ram Cichlids may mate with each other and will try to lay their eggs in a secure hiding place, such as a cave.&nbsp; If no hiding places are provided, they may become aggressive toward other aquarium inhabitants in order to protect their eggs.<\\/div><div>&nbsp;<\\/div><p>Otherwise, German Blue Ram Cichlids are very peaceful and totally safe to keep with larger species of shrimp, snails, live plants, and other non-aggressive fish.&nbsp; We sell these fish in groups because they are known to do best in groups of 3 or more.&nbsp; These fish are omnivores, but they may be finicky about food upon being introduced to a new tank.&nbsp; It\'s a good idea to start them on foods like brine shrimp, bloodworms, and frozen or live mosquito larvae.&nbsp; Then you can gradually introduce them to easier foods like fish flakes or pellets.<\\/p><div><div><strong>What We Like About This Fish:<\\/strong><\\/div><div><ul><li>Remarkable and exotic colors and patterns<\\/li><li>Charming and playful personality<\\/li><li>Safe with plants<\\/li><li>Completely peaceful<\\/li><\\/ul><div><strong>&nbsp;<\\/strong><\\/div><div><strong>RECOMMENDED TANK PARAMETERS:&nbsp;<\\/strong><\\/div><div><ul><li>Temperature:&nbsp;&nbsp;78.8\\u00b0 - 86\\u00b0 F (26\\u00b0 - 30\\u00b0 C), although 82\\u00b0+ F (28\\u00b0+ C) is optimal<\\/li><li>pH:&nbsp; 5.5 - 7.0<\\/li><li>KH:&nbsp; 2 - 10 dKH<\\/li><li>Minimum tank size:&nbsp; 10 gallons per fish (30 gallons for 3)<\\/li><\\/ul><\\/div><\\/div><div><strong>&nbsp;<\\/strong><\\/div><div><strong>CARE GUIDELINES:<\\/strong><\\/div><div><ul><li>Diet:&nbsp; Omnivorous.&nbsp; More likely to accept brine shrimp, bloodworms, and frozen or live mosquito larvae, and most will eventually eat fish flakes or pellets as well.<\\/li><li>Social behavior:&nbsp; Peaceful, schooling\\/shoaling.<\\/li><li>Origin:&nbsp; Tank-bred, but indigenous to rivers in Venezuela and Columbia<\\/li><li>Average adult size:&nbsp; 1 - 2 inches (2.5 - 5 cm)<\\/li><li>Average purchase size:&nbsp; .75 - 1.5 inches (1.9 - 3.8 cm)<\\/li><\\/ul><\\/div><\\/div>\",\"content\":null,\"images\":[null,\"german-ramirosey-min-300x300.jpg\"],\"product_type\":\"physical\",\"sale_type\":\"0\",\"sku\":null,\"price\":\"90\",\"sale_price\":null,\"start_date\":null,\"end_date\":null,\"cost_per_item\":\"0\",\"product_id\":\"420\",\"barcode\":null,\"with_storehouse_management\":\"0\",\"quantity\":\"0\",\"allow_checkout_when_out_of_stock\":\"0\",\"stock_status\":\"in_stock\",\"weight\":\"0\",\"length\":\"0\",\"wide\":\"0\",\"height\":\"0\",\"is_added_attributes\":\"0\",\"has_product_options\":\"1\",\"related_products\":null,\"faq_schema_config\":[[{\"key\":\"question\",\"value\":null},{\"key\":\"answer\",\"value\":null}]],\"seo_meta\":{\"seo_title\":null,\"seo_description\":null,\"index\":\"index\"},\"seo_meta_image\":null,\"language\":\"en_US\",\"layout\":null,\"is_popular\":\"0\",\"status\":\"published\",\"store_id\":null,\"is_featured\":\"0\",\"categories\":[\"45\"],\"brand_id\":null,\"image\":\"german-ramirosey-min-300x300.jpg\",\"minimum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"maximum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"tag\":null,\"submitter\":\"save\"}', 'updated', 'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/130.0.0.0 Safari/537.36', '2405:201:800e:d0d0:ad7b:3351:47bb:df30', 3, 420, 'GERMAN RAMIREZI', 'primary', '2024-11-05 16:37:15', '2024-11-05 16:37:15'),
(2687, 3, 'product', '{\"name\":\"THAISILK RAMIREZI\",\"model\":\"Botble\\\\Ecommerce\\\\Models\\\\Product\",\"slug\":\"thaisilk-ramirezi\",\"slug_id\":\"457\",\"is_slug_editable\":\"1\",\"description\":\"<p><strong>Appearance:<\\/strong>&nbsp;The Thai Silk Blue Ramirezi Fish is a breathtaking variant of the Ramirezi Dwarf Cichlid known for its vibrant and iridescent blue coloration. These fish have a sleek, elongated body with a shimmering, metallic blue hue that covers their entire body, giving them a striking and eye-catching appearance. Their large, expressive eyes and delicate finnage add to their overall allure, making them a favorite among aquarists.<\\/p><p>&nbsp;<\\/p><p><strong>Body Shape:<\\/strong>&nbsp;Thai Silk Blue Ramirezi Fish have a compact, oval-shaped body with a slightly pointed head. Their dorsal and anal fins are elongated and flow gracefully, enhancing their elegant look. The caudal fin is fan-shaped, adding to their visual appeal when they swim.<\\/p><p>&nbsp;<\\/p><p><strong>Temperament:<\\/strong>&nbsp;Known for their peaceful and calm demeanor, Thai Silk Blue Ramirezi Fish are excellent community fish. They get along well with other non-aggressive tank mates and can be kept in pairs or small groups. While they are generally peaceful, they may exhibit some territorial behavior, especially during breeding.<\\/p><p>&nbsp;<\\/p><p><strong>Tank Requirements:<\\/strong>&nbsp;To ensure the well-being of Thai Silk Blue Ramirezi Fish, an aquarium with a minimum capacity of 20 gallons is recommended. They thrive in well-maintained tanks with stable water conditions. The ideal water temperature for these fish ranges from 78\\u00b0F to 85\\u00b0F (25\\u00b0C to 29\\u00b0C), with a slightly acidic to neutral pH level (6.0 to 7.5). Providing plenty of plants, hiding spots, and soft substrate will help create a comfortable and enriching environment.<\\/p><p>&nbsp;<\\/p><p><strong>Diet:<\\/strong>&nbsp;Thai Silk Blue Ramirezi Fish are omnivorous and have a varied diet. A high-quality flake or pellet food should form the basis of their diet, supplemented with live or frozen foods such as brine shrimp, daphnia, and bloodworms. They also enjoy blanched vegetables like spinach and zucchini, which provide essential nutrients and variety.<\\/p><p>&nbsp;<\\/p><p><strong>Care:<\\/strong>&nbsp;Caring for Thai Silk Blue Ramirezi Fish involves maintaining pristine water quality through regular water changes and monitoring of water parameters. They are sensitive to poor water conditions, so consistent tank maintenance is crucial. Providing a balanced diet and a stress-free environment with plenty of hiding spots will ensure their health and happiness.<\\/p>\",\"content\":null,\"images\":[null,\"thaisilk-remirosey-300x300.jpg\"],\"product_type\":\"physical\",\"sale_type\":\"0\",\"sku\":null,\"price\":\"90\",\"sale_price\":null,\"start_date\":null,\"end_date\":null,\"cost_per_item\":\"0\",\"product_id\":\"421\",\"barcode\":null,\"with_storehouse_management\":\"0\",\"quantity\":\"0\",\"allow_checkout_when_out_of_stock\":\"0\",\"stock_status\":\"in_stock\",\"weight\":\"0\",\"length\":\"0\",\"wide\":\"0\",\"height\":\"0\",\"is_added_attributes\":\"0\",\"has_product_options\":\"1\",\"related_products\":null,\"faq_schema_config\":[[{\"key\":\"question\",\"value\":null},{\"key\":\"answer\",\"value\":null}]],\"seo_meta\":{\"seo_title\":null,\"seo_description\":null,\"index\":\"index\"},\"seo_meta_image\":null,\"language\":\"en_US\",\"layout\":null,\"is_popular\":\"0\",\"status\":\"published\",\"store_id\":null,\"is_featured\":\"0\",\"categories\":[\"45\"],\"brand_id\":null,\"image\":\"thaisilk-remirosey-300x300.jpg\",\"minimum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"maximum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"tag\":null,\"submitter\":\"save\"}', 'updated', 'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/130.0.0.0 Safari/537.36', '2405:201:800e:d0d0:ad7b:3351:47bb:df30', 3, 421, 'THAISILK RAMIREZI', 'primary', '2024-11-05 16:38:07', '2024-11-05 16:38:07'),
(2688, 3, 'product', '{\"name\":\"YELLOW DANIO\",\"model\":\"Botble\\\\Ecommerce\\\\Models\\\\Product\",\"slug\":\"yellow-danio\",\"slug_id\":\"455\",\"is_slug_editable\":\"1\",\"description\":\"<p><span>Zebra danio \\u2013 Yellow is a freshwater fish of the danio family, Cyprinidae. Zebra danios have thin bodies with zebra-like horizontal black and white stripes.<\\/span><\\/p><p><span>Because of their gregarious, placid demeanor, the fish are popular among aquarists, yet they can be aggressive if housed in a crowded tank.<\\/span><\\/p><p><span>The Zebra danios come in various colors, including a neon-colored, genetically modified variant known as the GloFish\\u00ae danio.<\\/span><\\/p><p><span>Zebra danio \\u2013 Yellow are popular among freshwater fish hobbyists. They are also prolific breeders and the most easily bred type of egglayer. These fish are easily identified by their nicely striped, black and white zebra-patterned bodies.<\\/span><\\/p><p><span>Zebrafish are extremely tough and can survive various water temperatures and conditions. They are often good without a water heater because they are comfortable in temperatures as low as the low 60s F. Unlike most fish species, they are lifelong partners and breeding partners.<\\/span><\\/p><p><span>Tropical and subtropical seas in India, Bhutan, and Bangladesh are home to zebra danios. The native habitat of the zebra danio changes with the seasons.<\\/span><\\/p><p><span>Water temperatures can reach 82\\u00b0F in the summer and dip to roughly 60\\u00b0F in the winter, depending on the location.<\\/span><\\/p><p><span>Zebra danios can be found in various environments, including slow-flowing streams and rivers, flooded ponds, and rice paddies. The fish have adapted to a variety of water parameters, as well as varying quantities of vegetation and light.<\\/span><\\/p><p><span>The bodies of zebra danios are thin and torpedo-shaped, with striking horizontal stripes running from head to tail. Zebra danios are lively, peaceful, and playful fish that do not cause problems when housed with appropriate species.<\\/span><\\/p><p><span>Zebra danios are tiny fish with zebra-like stripes on their bodies. The fish are silvery-gold in color with blue stripes in the wild. Males are more golden in hue than females, who are silvery-white.<\\/span><\\/p><p><span>The small, rounded fins and rounded tail of the common zebra danio.&nbsp;<\\/span><\\/p><p><span>The longfin zebra danio is a captive-bred aquarium fish with long, flowing fins and a long tail that is approximately three times the length of the fins and tail of the common zebra danio.<\\/span><\\/p><p><i><strong>I. Size<\\/strong><\\/i><\\/p><ul><li>Average Adult Size: 4 cm [1.5 inches]<\\/li><li>Maximum Adult Size: 1.5 inches<\\/li><li>Swimming Level: &nbsp;surface oriented<\\/li><\\/ul><p><i><span><strong>II. You would love the fish because\\u2026<\\/strong><\\/span><\\/i><\\/p><p><span>Zebra danio \\u2013 Yellow is available in a variety of hues in the aquarium market, including silvery-green, pink, blue, and purple bodies. All zebra danios have white stripes with black borders and varied colored stripes \\u2014 such as blue \\u2014 between these stripes.<\\/span><\\/p><p><span>GloFish danios, neon counterparts of the zebra danio, are also available in a variety of colors, including Sunburst Orange, Galactic Purple, Starfire Red, Electric Green, and Cosmic Blue.<\\/span><\\/p><p><span>White-gold bodies and crimson eyes distinguish albino zebra danios. These fish are uncommon in the wild due to their bright coloring, but they are rather popular in the fish trade.<\\/span><\\/p><p><span>Zebra danios lose their coloring when stressed. Male and female zebra danios have brighter, bolder stripes when trying to impress their mates during the breeding season.<\\/span><\\/p><p><span>Zebra danios are active, playful fish that get on well with most fish in a community tank. The zebra danios swim quickly around the upper and middle sections of the tank, and are diurnal, meaning they\\u2019re more active during the day than at night.<\\/span><\\/p><p><span>As shoaling fish, zebra danios are bravest in groups of five or more. Getting the balance right is important \\u2014 too few zebra danios can cause stress, while too many zebra danios can cause hyperactivity and territorial behavior<\\/span><\\/p><p><i><strong>III. Is this fish species peaceful or hostile?<\\/strong><\\/i><\\/p><ul><li>Recommended: 6 and more<\\/li><li>Recommended Male\\/Female \\u2013 1:1<\\/li><li>Overall hostility: Peaceful<\\/li><li class=\\\"TrT0Xe\\\">Hostility towards own species: Peaceful<\\/li><li class=\\\"TrT0Xe\\\">Hostility towards other Species: Peaceful<\\/li><\\/ul><p>.However they nibble the fins of certain species. Angelfish, bettas, and guppies, as well as any fish with long-flowing fins, are potential prey for the energetic zebra danio.<\\/p><p><i><span><strong>IV. Species compatibility<\\/strong><\\/span><\\/i><\\/p><p><span>Ember tetras<\\/span><\\/p><p><span>guppies<\\/span><\\/p><p><span>plecos,<\\/span><\\/p><p><span>Tetras<\\/span><\\/p><p><span>Zebra danios can pretty much live happily with most other types of fish, as long as they have plenty of space.<\\/span><\\/p><p><i><span><strong>V. How to feed this species?<\\/strong><\\/span><\\/i><\\/p><p><span>The majority of danios are omnivorous and thrive on Aqueon Tropical Flakes, Color Flakes, Tropical Granules, and Shrimp Pellets. Frozen and live foods can also be given as treats or to aid in the induction of spawning. To achieve the greatest results, rotate their diet regularly and feed them only what they can take in under 2 minutes once or twice a day.<\\/span><\\/p><p><i>Recommended food<\\/i><\\/p><ul><li><p class=\\\"oxy-product-title product_title entry-title oxy-woo-element\\\"><span>Aqueon Tropical Flakes<\\/span><\\/p><\\/li><li><p class=\\\"a-size-large a-spacing-none\\\" id=\\\"title\\\"><span class=\\\"a-size-large product-title-word-break\\\" id=\\\"productTitle\\\">WA Cichlid Vital Pellets<\\/span><\\/p><\\/li><\\/ul>\",\"content\":null,\"images\":[null,\"yellow-danio-min-300x300.jpg\"],\"product_type\":\"physical\",\"sale_type\":\"0\",\"sku\":null,\"price\":\"25\",\"sale_price\":null,\"start_date\":null,\"end_date\":null,\"cost_per_item\":\"0\",\"product_id\":\"419\",\"barcode\":null,\"with_storehouse_management\":\"0\",\"quantity\":\"0\",\"allow_checkout_when_out_of_stock\":\"0\",\"stock_status\":\"in_stock\",\"weight\":\"0\",\"length\":\"0\",\"wide\":\"0\",\"height\":\"0\",\"is_added_attributes\":\"0\",\"has_product_options\":\"1\",\"related_products\":null,\"faq_schema_config\":[[{\"key\":\"question\",\"value\":null},{\"key\":\"answer\",\"value\":null}]],\"seo_meta\":{\"seo_title\":null,\"seo_description\":null,\"index\":\"index\"},\"seo_meta_image\":null,\"language\":\"en_US\",\"layout\":null,\"is_popular\":\"0\",\"status\":\"published\",\"store_id\":null,\"is_featured\":\"0\",\"categories\":[\"45\"],\"brand_id\":null,\"image\":\"yellow-danio-min-300x300.jpg\",\"minimum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"maximum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"tag\":null,\"submitter\":\"save\"}', 'updated', 'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/130.0.0.0 Safari/537.36', '2405:201:800e:d0d0:ad7b:3351:47bb:df30', 3, 419, 'YELLOW DANIO', 'primary', '2024-11-05 16:38:45', '2024-11-05 16:38:45'),
