uickly around the upper and middle sections of the tank, and are diurnal, meaning they\\u2019re more active during the day than at night.<\\/span><\\/p><p><span>As shoaling fish, zebra danios are bravest in groups of five or more. Getting the balance right is important \\u2014 too few zebra danios can cause stress, while too many zebra danios can cause hyperactivity and territorial behavior<\\/span><\\/p><p><i><strong>III. Is this fish species peaceful or hostile?<\\/strong><\\/i><\\/p><ul><li>Recommended: 6 and more<\\/li><li>Recommended Male\\/Female \\u2013 1:1<\\/li><li>Overall hostility: Peaceful<\\/li><li class=\\\"TrT0Xe\\\">Hostility towards own species: Peaceful<\\/li><li class=\\\"TrT0Xe\\\">Hostility towards other Species: Peaceful<\\/li><\\/ul><p><i><span><strong>IV. Species compatibility<\\/strong><\\/span><\\/i><\\/p><ul><li><span>Ember tetras<\\/span><\\/li><li><span>Guppies<\\/span><\\/li><li><span>Plecos<\\/span><\\/li><li><span>Tetras<\\/span><\\/li><li><span>Zebra danios&nbsp;<\\/span><\\/li><\\/ul><p><span>However they nibble the fins of certain species. Angelfish, bettas, and guppies, as well as any fish with long-flowing fins, are potential prey for the energetic zebra danio.<\\/span><\\/p><p><i><span><strong>V. How to feed this species?<\\/strong><\\/span><\\/i><\\/p><p><span>The majority of danios are omnivorous and thrive on Aqueon Tropical Flakes, Color Flakes, Tropical Granules, and Shrimp Pellets. Frozen and live foods can also be given as treats or to aid in the induction of spawning. To achieve the greatest results, rotate their diet regularly and feed them only what they can take in under 2 minutes once or twice a day.<\\/span><\\/p><p><i>Recommended food<\\/i><\\/p><ul><li><p class=\\\"oxy-product-title product_title entry-title oxy-woo-element\\\"><span>Aqueon Tropical Flakes<\\/span><\\/p><\\/li><li><p class=\\\"a-size-large a-spacing-none\\\" id=\\\"title\\\"><span class=\\\"a-size-large product-title-word-break\\\" id=\\\"productTitle\\\">WA Cichlid Vital Pellets<\\/span><\\/p><\\/li><\\/ul>\",\"content\":null,\"images\":[null,\"pink-danio-min-300x300.jpg\"],\"product_type\":\"physical\",\"sale_type\":\"0\",\"sku\":null,\"price\":\"25\",\"sale_price\":null,\"start_date\":null,\"end_date\":null,\"cost_per_item\":\"0\",\"product_id\":\"418\",\"barcode\":null,\"with_storehouse_management\":\"0\",\"quantity\":\"0\",\"allow_checkout_when_out_of_stock\":\"0\",\"stock_status\":\"in_stock\",\"weight\":\"0\",\"length\":\"0\",\"wide\":\"0\",\"height\":\"0\",\"is_added_attributes\":\"0\",\"has_product_options\":\"1\",\"related_products\":null,\"faq_schema_config\":[[{\"key\":\"question\",\"value\":null},{\"key\":\"answer\",\"value\":null}]],\"seo_meta\":{\"seo_title\":null,\"seo_description\":null,\"index\":\"index\"},\"seo_meta_image\":null,\"language\":\"en_US\",\"layout\":null,\"is_popular\":\"0\",\"status\":\"published\",\"store_id\":null,\"is_featured\":\"0\",\"categories\":[\"45\"],\"brand_id\":null,\"image\":\"pink-danio-min-300x300.jpg\",\"minimum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"maximum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"tag\":null,\"submitter\":\"save\"}', 'updated', 'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/130.0.0.0 Safari/537.36', '2405:201:800e:d0d0:ad7b:3351:47bb:df30', 3, 418, 'PINK DANIO', 'primary', '2024-11-05 16:38:59', '2024-11-05 16:38:59'),
(2690, 3, 'product', '{\"name\":\"BLUE DANIO\",\"model\":\"Botble\\\\Ecommerce\\\\Models\\\\Product\",\"slug\":\"blue-danio\",\"slug_id\":\"453\",\"is_slug_editable\":\"1\",\"description\":\"<p>The zebrafish is a freshwater fish belonging to the minnow family of the order Cypriniformes. Native to South Asia, it is a popular aquarium fish, frequently sold under the trade name zebra danio. It is also found in private ponds<\\/p><div class=\\\"NJo7tc Z26q7c uUuwM\\\"><div class=\\\"VwiC3b yXK7lf MUxGbd yDYNvb lyLwlc\\\"><i>Zebra danios<\\/i>&nbsp;are a favorite of freshwater fish hobbyists because of their ease of care. They are also prolific breeders and the easiest type&nbsp;...<\\/div><\\/div><div class=\\\"NJo7tc Z26q7c uUuwM\\\"><div class=\\\"IThcWe\\\"><div class=\\\"YgpRwf\\\"><div class=\\\"wFMWsc JCsJK OSrXXb\\\"><div class=\\\"rEYMH OSrXXb\\\"><span class=\\\"YrbPuc WGKbId BBwThe\\\">Breeding:&nbsp;<\\/span> <span class=\\\"wHYlTd z8gr9e\\\">Egglayer<\\/span><\\/div><\\/div><div class=\\\"wFMWsc OSrXXb\\\"><div class=\\\"rEYMH OSrXXb\\\"><span class=\\\"YrbPuc WGKbId BBwThe\\\">Tank Level:&nbsp;<\\/span> <span class=\\\"wHYlTd z8gr9e\\\">All levels<\\/span><\\/div><\\/div><\\/div><div class=\\\"YgpRwf\\\"><div class=\\\"wFMWsc JCsJK OSrXXb\\\"><div class=\\\"rEYMH OSrXXb\\\"><span class=\\\"YrbPuc WGKbId BBwThe\\\">Minimum Tank Size:&nbsp;<\\/span> <span class=\\\"wHYlTd z8gr9e\\\">10 gallon<\\/span><\\/div><\\/div><div class=\\\"wFMWsc OSrXXb\\\"><div class=\\\"rEYMH OSrXXb\\\"><span class=\\\"YrbPuc WGKbId BBwThe\\\">Temperature:&nbsp;<\\/span> <span class=\\\"wHYlTd z8gr9e\\\">64 to 74 F (18 to 24 C)<\\/span> The&nbsp;<i>Zebra Danio<\\/i>&nbsp;(Danio rerio) is small and eye-catching freshwater fish that have long captivated fish enthusiasts<\\/div><\\/div><\\/div><\\/div><\\/div>\",\"content\":null,\"images\":[null,\"blue-danio-min-300x300.jpg\"],\"product_type\":\"physical\",\"sale_type\":\"0\",\"sku\":null,\"price\":\"25\",\"sale_price\":null,\"start_date\":null,\"end_date\":null,\"cost_per_item\":\"0\",\"product_id\":\"417\",\"barcode\":null,\"with_storehouse_management\":\"0\",\"quantity\":\"0\",\"allow_checkout_when_out_of_stock\":\"0\",\"stock_status\":\"in_stock\",\"weight\":\"0\",\"length\":\"0\",\"wide\":\"0\",\"height\":\"0\",\"is_added_attributes\":\"0\",\"has_product_options\":\"1\",\"related_products\":null,\"faq_schema_config\":[[{\"key\":\"question\",\"value\":null},{\"key\":\"answer\",\"value\":null}]],\"seo_meta\":{\"seo_title\":null,\"seo_description\":null,\"index\":\"index\"},\"seo_meta_image\":null,\"language\":\"en_US\",\"layout\":null,\"is_popular\":\"0\",\"status\":\"published\",\"store_id\":null,\"is_featured\":\"0\",\"categories\":[\"45\"],\"brand_id\":null,\"image\":\"blue-danio-min-300x300.jpg\",\"minimum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"maximum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"tag\":null,\"submitter\":\"save\"}', 'updated', 'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/130.0.0.0 Safari/537.36', '2405:201:800e:d0d0:ad7b:3351:47bb:df30', 3, 417, 'BLUE DANIO', 'primary', '2024-11-05 16:39:40', '2024-11-05 16:39:40'),
(2691, 3, 'product', '{\"name\":\"Blood red parrot\",\"model\":\"Botble\\\\Ecommerce\\\\Models\\\\Product\",\"slug\":\"blood-red-parrot\",\"slug_id\":\"452\",\"is_slug_editable\":\"1\",\"description\":\"<p>Blood parrots are often bright orange in coloration, but there are other colors that they can have naturally, such as red, yellow or gray. Other colors may be produced by <a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/en.wikipedia.org\\/wiki\\/Painted_fish\\\" title=\\\"Painted fish\\\">dyeing<\\/a> the fish, which can shorten <a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/en.wikipedia.org\\/wiki\\/Life_expectancy\\\" title=\\\"Life expectancy\\\">life expectancy<\\/a>. Some fish have been injected with a colored dye by the breeder. Another modification, generally considered inhumane by enthusiasts, involves cutting the tail while small which causes the fish to grow into a heart shape; these are usually sold under the name of \\\"heart parrots\\\". As the press has brought this practice to light, the majority of fish stockists will no longer sell these modified fish. Adult fish can grow to a length of 8 inches (20 centimeters) and reach an age of 10 to 15 years.<a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/en.wikipedia.org\\/wiki\\/Blood_parrot_cichlid#cite_note-aquafriend-2\\\"><span class=\\\"cite-bracket\\\"><sup class=\\\"reference\\\" id=\\\"cite_ref-aquafriend_2-1\\\">[<\\/sup><\\/span> <sup class=\\\"reference\\\">2<\\/sup><span class=\\\"cite-bracket\\\"><sup class=\\\"reference\\\">]<\\/sup><\\/span> <\\/a>Various breeds of blood parrots have been developed, such as the \\\"King Kong parrot\\\", which typically vary in color from red to yellow. They have fully functioning mouths with less of a nuchal deformity and grow larger. They are usually considered more valuable than the traditional blood parrots. Blood parrots are <a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/en.wikipedia.org\\/wiki\\/Hardiness_(plants)\\\" title=\\\"Hardiness (plants)\\\">hardy<\\/a> and may be housed singly, in <a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/en.wikipedia.org\\/wiki\\/Shoaling_and_schooling\\\" title=\\\"Shoaling and schooling\\\">schools<\\/a>, or with complementary species under a variety of conditions. Sufficient lighting can be provided by a variety of <a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/en.wikipedia.org\\/wiki\\/Compact_fluorescent_lamp\\\" title=\\\"Compact fluorescent lamp\\\">compact fluorescent lamps<\\/a> without the use of T5 or <a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/en.wikipedia.org\\/wiki\\/Halide\\\" title=\\\"Halide\\\">halide<\\/a> fixtures. The fish are voracious eaters and generate significant uneaten debris during feeding. High volume <a class=\\\"mw-redirect\\\" href=\\\"https:\\/\\/en.wikipedia.org\\/wiki\\/Filter_(aquarium)\\\" title=\\\"Filter (aquarium)\\\">filtration<\\/a> and frequent <a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/en.wikipedia.org\\/wiki\\/Substrate_(aquarium)\\\" title=\\\"Substrate (aquarium)\\\">substrate<\\/a> suctioning is recommended to minimize <a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/en.wikipedia.org\\/wiki\\/Nitrate\\\" title=\\\"Nitrate\\\">nitrates<\\/a>.<\\/p>\",\"content\":null,\"images\":[null,\"untitled-design263-min-300x300.png\"],\"product_type\":\"physical\",\"sale_type\":\"0\",\"sku\":null,\"price\":\"350\",\"sale_price\":null,\"start_date\":null,\"end_date\":null,\"cost_per_item\":\"0\",\"product_id\":\"416\",\"barcode\":null,\"with_storehouse_management\":\"0\",\"quantity\":\"0\",\"allow_checkout_when_out_of_stock\":\"0\",\"stock_status\":\"in_stock\",\"weight\":\"0\",\"length\":\"0\",\"wide\":\"0\",\"height\":\"0\",\"is_added_attributes\":\"0\",\"has_product_options\":\"1\",\"related_products\":null,\"faq_schema_config\":[[{\"key\":\"question\",\"value\":null},{\"key\":\"answer\",\"value\":null}]],\"seo_meta\":{\"seo_title\":null,\"seo_description\":null,\"index\":\"index\"},\"seo_meta_image\":null,\"language\":\"en_US\",\"layout\":null,\"is_popular\":\"0\",\"status\":\"published\",\"store_id\":null,\"is_featured\":\"0\",\"categories\":[\"45\"],\"brand_id\":null,\"image\":\"untitled-design263-min-300x300.png\",\"minimum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"maximum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"tag\":null,\"submitter\":\"save\"}', 'updated', 'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/130.0.0.0 Safari/537.36', '2405:201:800e:d0d0:ad7b:3351:47bb:df30', 3, 416, 'Blood red parrot', 'primary', '2024-11-05 16:39:59', '2024-11-05 16:39:59'),
(2692, 3, 'product', '{\"name\":\"yellow parrot\",\"model\":\"Botble\\\\Ecommerce\\\\Models\\\\Product\",\"slug\":\"yellow-parrot\",\"slug_id\":\"451\",\"is_slug_editable\":\"1\",\"description\":\"<p><span class=\\\"BxUVEf ILfuVd hgKElc\\\" lang=\\\"en\\\">Yellow Parrot: This fish\'s distinctive appearance\\u2014<strong>round body, beak-like head, and huge eyes<\\/strong>\\u2014along with its ability to cohabit with various species in a communal habitat have made it quite popular among some aficionados. Yellow parrots are yellow, but they can also be orange, red, or grey.<\\/span><\\/p><div class=\\\"product__description rte quick-add-hidden\\\"><p>The&nbsp; parrot cichlid, or parrot cichlid, is a hybrid species of fish in the family Cichlid. The fish was first bred in Taiwan around 1986. Blood parrots should not be confused with other parrot cichlids or salt water parrotfish.<\\/p><div class=\\\"NJo7tc Z26q7c uUuwM\\\"><div class=\\\"VwiC3b yXK7lf MUxGbd yDYNvb lyLwlc\\\"><span class=\\\"MUxGbd wuQ4Ob WZ8Tjf\\\">&nbsp;<\\/span> The&nbsp;<i>blood parrot cichlid<\\/i>&nbsp;is a hybrid produced by breeding the midas and the redhead cichlid. The fish was first created in Taiwan around 1986.<\\/div><\\/div><div class=\\\"NJo7tc Z26q7c uUuwM\\\"><div class=\\\"IThcWe\\\"><div class=\\\"YgpRwf\\\"><div class=\\\"wFMWsc JCsJK OSrXXb\\\"><div class=\\\"rEYMH OSrXXb\\\"><span class=\\\"YrbPuc WGKbId BBwThe\\\">Minimum tank size:&nbsp;<\\/span> <span class=\\\"wHYlTd z8gr9e\\\">30 gallons for single fish; 10 ...<\\/span><\\/div><\\/div><div class=\\\"wFMWsc OSrXXb\\\"><div class=\\\"rEYMH OSrXXb\\\"><span class=\\\"YrbPuc WGKbId BBwThe\\\">Breeding:&nbsp;<\\/span> <span class=\\\"wHYlTd z8gr9e\\\">Males are sterile, but females somet...<\\/span><\\/div><\\/div><\\/div><div class=\\\"YgpRwf\\\"><div class=\\\"wFMWsc JCsJK OSrXXb\\\"><div class=\\\"rEYMH OSrXXb\\\"><span class=\\\"YrbPuc WGKbId BBwThe\\\">Tank level:&nbsp;<\\/span> <span class=\\\"wHYlTd z8gr9e\\\">Mid- and bottom-level<\\/span><\\/div><\\/div><div class=\\\"wFMWsc OSrXXb\\\"><div class=\\\"rEYMH OSrXXb\\\"><span class=\\\"YrbPuc WGKbId BBwThe\\\">Temperature:&nbsp;<\\/span> <span class=\\\"wHYlTd z8gr9e\\\">76 F to 80 F<\\/span><\\/div><\\/div><\\/div><\\/div><\\/div><\\/div>\",\"content\":null,\"images\":[null,\"untitled-design264-min-300x300.png\"],\"product_type\":\"physical\",\"sale_type\":\"0\",\"sku\":null,\"price\":\"400\",\"sale_price\":null,\"start_date\":null,\"end_date\":null,\"cost_per_item\":\"0\",\"product_id\":\"415\",\"barcode\":null,\"with_storehouse_management\":\"0\",\"quantity\":\"0\",\"allow_checkout_when_out_of_stock\":\"0\",\"stock_status\":\"in_stock\",\"weight\":\"0\",\"length\":\"0\",\"wide\":\"0\",\"height\":\"0\",\"is_added_attributes\":\"0\",\"has_product_options\":\"1\",\"related_products\":null,\"faq_schema_config\":[[{\"key\":\"question\",\"value\":null},{\"key\":\"answer\",\"value\":null}]],\"seo_meta\":{\"seo_title\":null,\"seo_description\":null,\"index\":\"index\"},\"seo_meta_image\":null,\"language\":\"en_US\",\"layout\":null,\"is_popular\":\"0\",\"status\":\"published\",\"store_id\":null,\"is_featured\":\"0\",\"categories\":[\"45\"],\"brand_id\":null,\"image\":\"untitled-design264-min-300x300.png\",\"minimum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"maximum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"tag\":null,\"submitter\":\"save\"}', 'updated', 'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/130.0.0.0 Safari/537.36', '2405:201:800e:d0d0:ad7b:3351:47bb:df30', 3, 415, 'yellow parrot', 'primary', '2024-11-05 16:42:08', '2024-11-05 16:42:08'),
(2693, 3, 'product', '{\"name\":\"ALBINO CORY CAT\",\"model\":\"Botble\\\\Ecommerce\\\\Models\\\\Product\",\"slug\":\"bronze-cory-cat\",\"slug_id\":\"450\",\"is_slug_editable\":\"1\",\"description\":\"<p style=\\\"text-align:left;\\\">The Albino Aeneus Cory Catfish (<i>Corydoras aeneus<\\/i>) is a variant of the classic Bronze Cory&nbsp;that is native to several countries in South America. It is one of the most popular bottom-dwellers in the aquarium hobby and&nbsp;is a very animated, distinctively marked schooling fish that is perfect for the nano, community, and planted aquarium.<\\/p><div style=\\\"text-align:left;\\\">The Albino Aeneus Cory Catfish is a very peaceful schooling fish that is compatible with most nano aquarium animals, including dwarf cichlids and angelfish. It might prey on small dwarf shrimp, but is safe with larger shrimp and most other peaceful ornamental invertebrates. It is a classic scavenger and will inhabit and feed at the aquarium floor, which should be comprised of sand or smooth gravel. Very coarse substrate can damage its delicate barbels and underbelly, so it should be kept in an aquarium with sand or very smooth gravel substrate. This fish is otherwise undemanding as it will accept most dry ,frozen, and live foods. It is adaptable to most tropical freshwater conditions as long as standard regular maintenance is performed and sudden changes are avoided.<\\/div>\",\"content\":null,\"images\":[null,\"albino-cory-cat-300x300.jpg\"],\"product_type\":\"physical\",\"sale_type\":\"0\",\"sku\":null,\"price\":\"40\",\"sale_price\":null,\"start_date\":null,\"end_date\":null,\"cost_per_item\":\"0\",\"product_id\":\"414\",\"barcode\":null,\"with_storehouse_management\":\"0\",\"quantity\":\"0\",\"allow_checkout_when_out_of_stock\":\"0\",\"stock_status\":\"in_stock\",\"weight\":\"0\",\"length\":\"0\",\"wide\":\"0\",\"height\":\"0\",\"is_added_attributes\":\"0\",\"has_product_options\":\"1\",\"related_products\":null,\"faq_schema_config\":[[{\"key\":\"question\",\"value\":null},{\"key\":\"answer\",\"value\":null}]],\"seo_meta\":{\"seo_title\":null,\"seo_description\":null,\"index\":\"index\"},\"seo_meta_image\":null,\"language\":\"en_US\",\"layout\":null,\"is_popular\":\"0\",\"status\":\"published\",\"store_id\":null,\"is_featured\":\"0\",\"categories\":[\"45\"],\"brand_id\":null,\"image\":\"albino-cory-cat-300x300.jpg\",\"minimum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"maximum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"tag\":null,\"submitter\":\"save\"}', 'updated', 'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/130.0.0.0 Safari/537.36', '2405:201:800e:d0d0:ad7b:3351:47bb:df30', 3, 414, 'ALBINO CORY CAT', 'primary', '2024-11-05 16:42:43', '2024-11-05 16:42:43'),
(2694, 3, 'product', '{\"name\":\"Red chili oscar\",\"model\":\"Botble\\\\Ecommerce\\\\Models\\\\Product\",\"slug\":\"red-chili-oscar\",\"slug_id\":\"449\",\"is_slug_editable\":\"1\",\"description\":\"<p><strong>Descriptions:<\\/strong><\\/p><ul><li>Chili Red&nbsp;Oscars come from Brazil, Columbia, Ecuador, French Guiana and Peru. They can be found along the Amazon River and its surrounding areas, which is one of the most bio diverse environments in the world.<\\/li><li>This is a species full of personality. A few different varieties have been bred which offer some different colours and patterns.<\\/li><li>Oscars are territorial, so adding them to your tank can be risky.<\\/li><li>They aren\\u2019t afraid to attack other fish and will do so if a fish encroaches on their territory. Mating and feeding times can also fuel their aggression.<\\/li><li>Most of their time will be spent swimming in the mid-levels of the tank, though they\\u2019ll often head down to the substrate in search of food. You might see them uproot plants and decorations during this search, so everything in the aquarium should be secured down.<\\/li><li>The good news is that if the tank is setup correctly and you choose the right tank mates, their aggression can be controlled.<\\/li><\\/ul><p><strong>Ratios:<\\/strong><\\/p><ul><li>Most Oscar varieties grow to be large, reaching up to 30cm. They reach this size quite quickly in their lifetime.<\\/li><li>Oscars can be kept together, and this is usually the safest option. Their need for territory can cause them to attack tank mates. Make sure they have lots of space as this reduces territory disputes.<\\/li><li>1 Oscar per 40L<\\/li><\\/ul><p><strong><u>Feeding Directions:<\\/u><\\/strong><\\/p><ul><li>In an aquarium, the simplest option is to use flake\\/pellet foods. These have been designed to contain all the nutrition your fish need. Hikari Gold, Sinking Gold or Hikari Staple.<\\/li><li>Live\\/frozen foods (which are full of protein). These include bloodworms, brine shrimp and daphnia. Live foods encourage Oscars to catch their food which brings out their natural hunting instincts.<\\/li><\\/ul><p><strong><u>Care Guidlines<\\/u><\\/strong>:<\\/p><ul><li>Oscars require more care than most other species. Their size and large appetite means that they produce a lot of mess. This makes regular cleaning very important, or conditions will deteriorate quickly. Perform 20-30% water changes at least once a week, ideally twice.<\\/li><li>These cichlids are hardier than most fish, so they don\\u2019t get sick often, but they can get ill like all species.<\\/li><\\/ul><p>&nbsp;<\\/p>\",\"content\":null,\"images\":[null,\"untitled-design265-min-300x300-1.png\"],\"product_type\":\"physical\",\"sale_type\":\"0\",\"sku\":null,\"price\":\"250\",\"sale_price\":null,\"start_date\":null,\"end_date\":null,\"cost_per_item\":\"0\",\"product_id\":\"413\",\"barcode\":null,\"with_storehouse_management\":\"0\",\"quantity\":\"0\",\"allow_checkout_when_out_of_stock\":\"0\",\"stock_status\":\"in_stock\",\"weight\":\"0\",\"length\":\"0\",\"wide\":\"0\",\"height\":\"0\",\"is_added_attributes\":\"0\",\"has_product_options\":\"1\",\"related_products\":null,\"faq_schema_config\":[[{\"key\":\"question\",\"value\":null},{\"key\":\"answer\",\"value\":null}]],\"seo_meta\":{\"seo_title\":null,\"seo_description\":null,\"index\":\"index\"},\"seo_meta_image\":null,\"language\":\"en_US\",\"layout\":null,\"is_popular\":\"0\",\"status\":\"published\",\"store_id\":null,\"is_featured\":\"0\",\"categories\":[\"45\"],\"brand_id\":null,\"image\":\"untitled-design265-min-300x300-1.png\",\"minimum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"maximum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"tag\":null,\"submitter\":\"save\"}', 'updated', 'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/130.0.0.0 Safari/537.36', '2405:201:800e:d0d0:ad7b:3351:47bb:df30', 3, 413, 'Red chili oscar', 'primary', '2024-11-05 16:43:23', '2024-11-05 16:43:23'),
(2695, 3, 'product', '{\"name\":\"LEMON OSCAR\",\"model\":\"Botble\\\\Ecommerce\\\\Models\\\\Product\",\"slug\":\"lemon-oscar\",\"slug_id\":\"448\",\"is_slug_editable\":\"1\",\"description\":\"<p>The Lemon Oscar is a stunning color variety of the extremely popular Oscar cichlid. Vibrant lemon yellow coloring over an opaque, cream-white body makes for a brilliant appearance. The eye-catching Lemon Oscar is so visually dissimilar to the normally dark colored Tiger Oscar that it instantly becomes the center of attention and a topic of conversation.<\\/p><p>The Lemon Oscar requires a large, well-filtered aquarium of at least 70 gallons with a deep sand bottom and a few large rocks. It will dig up plants so any that are in the tank should be potted with the root surfaces covered with rocks. Using floating plants is a good alternative. The Lemon Oscar is not as territorial as most other cichlids when full grown but will consume anything they can fit into their mouth. Though this hardy and easy-to-care-for cichlid is generally mild-mannered in nature, the Lemon Oscar is best kept in a species tanks or with similar-size tank mates.<\\/p><p>A large tank should be used for breeding, if possible, as large as 100 gallons. The Lemon Oscar will spawn in soft or hard water as long as it is clean and clear and has a temperature between 79-86\\u00b0F. The Lemon Oscar will pair to form a nuclear family. The female will then lay between 1,000-2,000 eggs on rocks that have been carefully cleaned. The eggs are opaque at first, turning transparent in 24 hours. The brood will be carefully guarded and cared for and the fry will be kept in pits and may even be covered. When they are free-swimming, the fry should be fed Cyclops. Sometimes the fry will cling to their parents. The male and female are difficult to differentiate but during spawning the genital papilla of the female becomes noticeable.<\\/p><p>The Lemon Oscar is a predatory carnivore with a hearty appetite. Oscars will eat a variety of meaty foods, including small fish and earthworms, Cichlid pellets, larger flake food, ocean plankton, Bloodworms, Mysis Shrimp and Tubifex Worms.<\\/p><p><strong>Approximate Purchase Size:<\\/strong> 2-1\\/4\\\" to 2-3\\/4\\\"<\\/p>\",\"content\":null,\"images\":[null,\"untitled-design266-min-300x300.png\"],\"product_type\":\"physical\",\"sale_type\":\"0\",\"sku\":null,\"price\":\"250\",\"sale_price\":null,\"start_date\":null,\"end_date\":null,\"cost_per_item\":\"0\",\"product_id\":\"412\",\"barcode\":null,\"with_storehouse_management\":\"0\",\"quantity\":\"0\",\"allow_checkout_when_out_of_stock\":\"0\",\"stock_status\":\"out_of_stock\",\"weight\":\"0\",\"length\":\"0\",\"wide\":\"0\",\"height\":\"0\",\"is_added_attributes\":\"0\",\"has_product_options\":\"1\",\"related_products\":null,\"faq_schema_config\":[[{\"key\":\"question\",\"value\":null},{\"key\":\"answer\",\"value\":null}]],\"seo_meta\":{\"seo_title\":null,\"seo_description\":null,\"index\":\"index\"},\"seo_meta_image\":null,\"language\":\"en_US\",\"layout\":null,\"is_popular\":\"0\",\"status\":\"draft\",\"store_id\":null,\"is_featured\":\"0\",\"categories\":[\"45\"],\"brand_id\":null,\"image\":\"untitled-design266-min-300x300.png\",\"minimum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"maximum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"tag\":null,\"submitter\":\"save\"}', 'updated', 'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/130.0.0.0 Safari/537.36', '2405:201:800e:d0d0:ad7b:3351:47bb:df30', 3, 412, 'LEMON OSCAR', 'primary', '2024-11-05 16:43:58', '2024-11-05 16:43:58'),
(2696, 3, 'product', '{\"name\":\"STONE CAT\",\"model\":\"Botble\\\\Ecommerce\\\\Models\\\\Product\",\"slug\":\"stone-cat\",\"slug_id\":\"447\",\"is_slug_editable\":\"1\",\"description\":\"<p>Inhabits slow-moving streams and small rivers. It\\u2019s preferred habitats are characterised by soft substrates.<\\/p><p>Provide as many hiding places as possible, along with a soft, sandy substrates. The addition of some dried beech or oak leaves and pieces of driftwood would simulate the natural habitat of the fish nicely. The water must be kept clean, relatively cool and well-oxygenated or the fish will suffer as its natural waters are high in dissolved oxygen.<\\/p><p>It will accept most small foods, including dried pellets, but should be offered a diet composed mainly of live and frozen varieties, such as bloodworm, daphnia etc. It\\u2019s strictly a noctunal feeder so add food after lights out to ensure it gets its share.<\\/p>\",\"content\":null,\"images\":[null,\"stone-cat-min-300x300.jpg\"],\"product_type\":\"physical\",\"sale_type\":\"0\",\"sku\":null,\"price\":\"25\",\"sale_price\":null,\"start_date\":null,\"end_date\":null,\"cost_per_item\":\"0\",\"product_id\":\"411\",\"barcode\":null,\"with_storehouse_management\":\"0\",\"quantity\":\"0\",\"allow_checkout_when_out_of_stock\":\"0\",\"stock_status\":\"in_stock\",\"weight\":\"0\",\"length\":\"0\",\"wide\":\"0\",\"height\":\"0\",\"is_added_attributes\":\"0\",\"has_product_options\":\"1\",\"related_products\":null,\"faq_schema_config\":[[{\"key\":\"question\",\"value\":null},{\"key\":\"answer\",\"value\":null}]],\"seo_meta\":{\"seo_title\":null,\"seo_description\":null,\"index\":\"index\"},\"seo_meta_image\":null,\"language\":\"en_US\",\"layout\":null,\"is_popular\":\"0\",\"status\":\"published\",\"store_id\":null,\"is_featured\":\"0\",\"categories\":[\"45\"],\"brand_id\":null,\"image\":\"stone-cat-min-300x300.jpg\",\"minimum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"maximum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"tag\":null,\"submitter\":\"save\"}', 'updated', 'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/130.0.0.0 Safari/537.36', '2405:201:800e:d0d0:ad7b:3351:47bb:df30', 3, 411, 'STONE CAT', 'primary', '2024-11-05 16:44:44', '2024-11-05 16:44:44');
INSERT INTO `audit_histories` (`id`, `user_id`, `module`, `request`, `action`, `user_agent`, `ip_address`, `reference_user`, `reference_id`, `reference_name`, `type`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
(2697, 3, 'product', '{\"name\":\"FIREMOUTH CICHLID\",\"model\":\"Botble\\\\Ecommerce\\\\Models\\\\Product\",\"slug\":\"firemouth-cichlid\",\"slug_id\":\"446\",\"is_slug_editable\":\"1\",\"description\":\"<p>The <strong>firemouth cichlid<\\/strong> (<i>Thorichthys meeki<\\/i>) is a species of <a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/en.wikipedia.org\\/wiki\\/Cichlid\\\" title=\\\"Cichlid\\\">cichlid<\\/a> fish native to <a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/en.wikipedia.org\\/wiki\\/Central_America\\\" title=\\\"Central America\\\">Central America<\\/a>. They occur in rivers of the <a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/en.wikipedia.org\\/wiki\\/Yucat%C3%A1n_Peninsula\\\" title=\\\"Yucat\\u00e1n Peninsula\\\">Yucat\\u00e1n Peninsula<\\/a>, <a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/en.wikipedia.org\\/wiki\\/Mexico\\\" title=\\\"Mexico\\\">Mexico<\\/a>, south through <a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/en.wikipedia.org\\/wiki\\/Belize\\\" title=\\\"Belize\\\">Belize<\\/a> and into northern <a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/en.wikipedia.org\\/wiki\\/Guatemala\\\" title=\\\"Guatemala\\\">Guatemala<\\/a>.<\\/p><p>Their natural habitat is typically shallow, slow-moving, often <a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/en.wikipedia.org\\/wiki\\/Turbidity\\\" title=\\\"Turbidity\\\">turbid<\\/a>, water with a <a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/en.wikipedia.org\\/wiki\\/PH\\\" title=\\\"PH\\\">pH<\\/a> of 6.5 - 8.0. It has also been reported to live in cave systems. As fish with a tropical distribution, firemouth cichlids live in warm water with a temperature range of 23\\u201330&nbsp;\\u00b0C (73\\u201386&nbsp;\\u00b0F). The common name \\\"firemouth\\\" is derived from the bright orange-red colouration on the underside of the jaw, while the <a class=\\\"mw-redirect\\\" href=\\\"https:\\/\\/en.wikipedia.org\\/wiki\\/Specific_epithet\\\" title=\\\"Specific epithet\\\">specific epithet<\\/a> <i>meeki<\\/i> honors American ichthyologist <a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/en.wikipedia.org\\/wiki\\/Seth_Eugene_Meek\\\" title=\\\"Seth Eugene Meek\\\">Seth Eugene Meek<\\/a>. Males in particular flare out their gills, exposing their red throats, in a threat display designed to ward off male rivals from their territory.<\\/p><p>Like most cichlids, <a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/en.wikipedia.org\\/wiki\\/Offspring\\\" title=\\\"Offspring\\\">brood<\\/a> care is highly developed; this species is an egg-layer. Firemouth cichlids form <a class=\\\"mw-redirect\\\" href=\\\"https:\\/\\/en.wikipedia.org\\/wiki\\/Monogamous\\\" title=\\\"Monogamous\\\">monogamous<\\/a> pairs and spawn on flattened surfaces of rocks, leaves or submerged wood. Breeding males are primarily responsible for territorial defense, while females are more intensively involved in raising the fry, though both parents lead the fry in search of food. Firemouth cichlids are omnivorous and opportunistic in their feeding strategies. Their ability to protrude their jaw 6% standard length limits their diet to about 6% evasive prey.<a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/en.wikipedia.org\\/wiki\\/Firemouth_cichlid#cite_note-2\\\"><span class=\\\"cite-bracket\\\"><sup class=\\\"reference\\\" id=\\\"cite_ref-2\\\">[<\\/sup><\\/span> <sup class=\\\"reference\\\">2<\\/sup><span class=\\\"cite-bracket\\\"><sup class=\\\"reference\\\">]<\\/sup><\\/span> <\\/a>Sexual dimorphism is present, though limited in this species. Males are generally larger than females (up to 15&nbsp;cm (5.9&nbsp;in)), with brighter and more red colouration around the throat. They also have more pointed dorsal and anal fins. Firemouths are suitable for community aquaria, though they may become extremely aggressive to other members of its species and other community fish during spawning.<\\/p><div class=\\\"mw-heading mw-heading2\\\"><h2 id=\\\"See_also\\\">&nbsp;<\\/h2><\\/div>\",\"content\":null,\"images\":[null,\"untitled-design267-min-300x300.png\"],\"product_type\":\"physical\",\"sale_type\":\"0\",\"sku\":null,\"price\":\"150\",\"sale_price\":null,\"start_date\":null,\"end_date\":null,\"cost_per_item\":\"0\",\"product_id\":\"410\",\"barcode\":null,\"with_storehouse_management\":\"0\",\"quantity\":\"0\",\"allow_checkout_when_out_of_stock\":\"0\",\"stock_status\":\"out_of_stock\",\"weight\":\"0\",\"length\":\"0\",\"wide\":\"0\",\"height\":\"0\",\"is_added_attributes\":\"0\",\"has_product_options\":\"1\",\"related_products\":null,\"faq_schema_config\":[[{\"key\":\"question\",\"value\":null},{\"key\":\"answer\",\"value\":null}]],\"seo_meta\":{\"seo_title\":null,\"seo_description\":null,\"index\":\"index\"},\"seo_meta_image\":null,\"language\":\"en_US\",\"layout\":null,\"is_popular\":\"0\",\"status\":\"draft\",\"store_id\":null,\"is_featured\":\"0\",\"categories\":[\"45\"],\"brand_id\":null,\"image\":\"untitled-design267-min-300x300.png\",\"minimum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"maximum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"tag\":null,\"submitter\":\"save\"}', 'updated', 'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/130.0.0.0 Safari/537.36', '2405:201:800e:d0d0:ad7b:3351:47bb:df30', 3, 410, 'FIREMOUTH CICHLID', 'primary', '2024-11-05 16:45:14', '2024-11-05 16:45:14'),
(2698, 3, 'product', '{\"name\":\"RED SAKE SKIN ONSCAR\",\"model\":\"Botble\\\\Ecommerce\\\\Models\\\\Product\",\"slug\":\"red-sake-skin-onscar\",\"slug_id\":\"445\",\"is_slug_editable\":\"1\",\"description\":\"<p>The RED SAKE SKIN ONSCAR, also known as the Marble Cichlid or Velvet Cichlid, is a large South American cichlid species that needs little to no introduction. It is one of the most popular and beloved fish in the entire aquarium hobby, and with good reason. It has beautiful markings, is extremely hardy and unfussy in every way, and is easily a centerpiece fish in any large aquarium. It grows to a substantial, but manageable size and is one of the most interactive fish when it comes to paying attention to its keeper.<\\/p><p>&nbsp;<\\/p><p>The RED SAKE SKIN ONSCAR&nbsp;will thrive in a large aquarium with a sand or gravel substrate and sturdy decor as well as plenty of open swimming space. It does consume some plant matter, so artificial plants are a better choice for decor than live plants (if plants are used at all). Like many cichlids, this species is known to sometimes rearrange decor to its liking, so it is necessary to avoid \\\"avalanches\\\" of decorative stones and driftwood. The RED SAKE SKIN ONSCAR is considerably less aggressive than most other medium and large cichlids, but it does have a voracious appetite and will eat any fish or invertebrate that will fit (or nearly fit) in its mouth. Territoriality is typically at its peak during spawning. Due to the eventual adult size of the RED SAKE SKIN ONSCAR, it should not be kept with ornamental invertebrates. If spawning is desired, tankmates of other species should be avoided altogether. It should also be noted that the RED SAKE SKIN ONSCAR is typically most peaceful with tankmates when it is grown up with them from juvenile age rather than introduced as an adult. Powerful filtration and regular water changes are necessarry for this large species.&nbsp;<strong>This fish grows to an impressive size rather quickly, so a large aquarium is necessary at an early stage, even when starting with a juvenile.<\\/strong><\\/p><p>&nbsp;<\\/p><p>Feeding is simple for the unfussy RED SAKE SKIN ONSCAR. High-quality dry, frozen, and live meaty foods will all be readily accepted, but&nbsp;some vegetable matter is also necessary&nbsp;and can easily be provided in the form of spirulina-rich dry foods. Quality and variety are the keys to a diet that will ensure that this fish maintains optimal health and coloration.&nbsp;<strong>Meat from mammals (such as beefheart) or birds is extremely unhealthy for Oscars and most other fish and should never make up part of the diet.<\\/strong><\\/p>\",\"content\":null,\"images\":[null,\"red-snake-skin-oscar-300x300-1.jpg\"],\"product_type\":\"physical\",\"sale_type\":\"0\",\"sku\":null,\"price\":\"250\",\"sale_price\":null,\"start_date\":null,\"end_date\":null,\"cost_per_item\":\"0\",\"product_id\":\"409\",\"barcode\":null,\"with_storehouse_management\":\"0\",\"quantity\":\"0\",\"allow_checkout_when_out_of_stock\":\"0\",\"stock_status\":\"in_stock\",\"weight\":\"0\",\"length\":\"0\",\"wide\":\"0\",\"height\":\"0\",\"is_added_attributes\":\"0\",\"has_product_options\":\"1\",\"related_products\":null,\"faq_schema_config\":[[{\"key\":\"question\",\"value\":null},{\"key\":\"answer\",\"value\":null}]],\"seo_meta\":{\"seo_title\":null,\"seo_description\":null,\"index\":\"index\"},\"seo_meta_image\":null,\"language\":\"en_US\",\"layout\":null,\"is_popular\":\"0\",\"status\":\"published\",\"store_id\":null,\"is_featured\":\"0\",\"categories\":[\"45\"],\"brand_id\":null,\"image\":\"red-snake-skin-oscar-300x300-1.jpg\",\"minimum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"maximum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"tag\":null,\"submitter\":\"save\"}', 'updated', 'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/130.0.0.0 Safari/537.36', '2405:201:800e:d0d0:ad7b:3351:47bb:df30', 3, 409, 'RED SAKE SKIN ONSCAR', 'primary', '2024-11-05 16:46:14', '2024-11-05 16:46:14'),
(2699, 3, 'product', '{\"name\":\"BANDED TALKING CAT\",\"model\":\"Botble\\\\Ecommerce\\\\Models\\\\Product\",\"slug\":\"banded-talking-cat\",\"slug_id\":\"444\",\"is_slug_editable\":\"1\",\"description\":\"<p style=\\\"text-align:left;\\\">The Striped Raphael Catfish (<i>Platydoras armatulus<\\/i>, formerly&nbsp;<i>P. costatus<\\/i>) is a medium sized catfish species from the Orinico and Amazon River basins as well as many other waterways throughout much of South America. It has been a very popular aquarium fish for many years due to its hardiness, generally peaceful nature, and attractive markings. It grows too large for the nano aquarium, but is an excellent candidate for the medium or large aquarium, especially Amazon-type setups with cichlids or tetras. This species is also known as the Striped Talking Catfish due to its ability to \\\"croak\\\" when removed from the water. It is a doradid (family Doradidae) catfish whose closest relatives are Wood and Banjo catfish families.<\\/p><p style=\\\"text-align:left;\\\">The Striped Raphael&nbsp;Catfish is a somewhat gregarious species, although it is also fine as a single specimen in an aquarium. It is somewhat reclusive and definitely requires ample hiding places in the form of driftwood, pipes, or other crevices. Multiple specimens will sometimes wedge into the same refuge. This fish is not particularly territorial or aggressive, but like most catfish, it will prey on anything small enough to fit in its mouth, such as tiny fish, dwarf shrimp, and fry. It will not bother plants. It is not particularly sensitive, but it prefers fairly calm to moderate water flow. Like many scaleless fish, it will deteriorate from poor water quality and maintenance.<\\/p><p style=\\\"text-align:left;\\\">Feeding is very simple for the Striped Raphael&nbsp;Catfish. In the wild, it mainly feeds on small crustaceans and other invertebrates. In the aquarium, it will accept most live, frozen, and dry meaty foods, although some vegetable matter (such as spirulina-rich dry foods) is recommended as well. It is a voracious eater, so care should be taken not to overfeed. Inserting food near the fish\'s hiding place is very effective, although it will typically learn to come out of hiding with enthusiasm when food is available.<\\/p>\",\"content\":null,\"images\":[null,\"banded-talking-cat-min-300x300.jpg\"],\"product_type\":\"physical\",\"sale_type\":\"0\",\"sku\":null,\"price\":\"450\",\"sale_price\":null,\"start_date\":null,\"end_date\":null,\"cost_per_item\":\"0\",\"product_id\":\"408\",\"barcode\":null,\"with_storehouse_management\":\"0\",\"quantity\":\"0\",\"allow_checkout_when_out_of_stock\":\"0\",\"stock_status\":\"in_stock\",\"weight\":\"0\",\"length\":\"0\",\"wide\":\"0\",\"height\":\"0\",\"is_added_attributes\":\"0\",\"has_product_options\":\"1\",\"related_products\":null,\"faq_schema_config\":[[{\"key\":\"question\",\"value\":null},{\"key\":\"answer\",\"value\":null}]],\"seo_meta\":{\"seo_title\":null,\"seo_description\":null,\"index\":\"index\"},\"seo_meta_image\":null,\"language\":\"en_US\",\"layout\":null,\"is_popular\":\"0\",\"status\":\"published\",\"store_id\":null,\"is_featured\":\"0\",\"categories\":[\"45\"],\"brand_id\":null,\"image\":\"banded-talking-cat-min-300x300.jpg\",\"minimum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"maximum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"tag\":null,\"submitter\":\"save\"}', 'updated', 'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/130.0.0.0 Safari/537.36', '2405:201:800e:d0d0:ad7b:3351:47bb:df30', 3, 408, 'BANDED TALKING CAT', 'primary', '2024-11-05 16:46:35', '2024-11-05 16:46:35'),
(2700, 3, 'product', '{\"name\":\"SOVELNOSE CAT\",\"model\":\"Botble\\\\Ecommerce\\\\Models\\\\Product\",\"slug\":\"sovelnose-cat\",\"slug_id\":\"443\",\"is_slug_editable\":\"1\",\"description\":\"<p>A fascinating freshwater fish, the&nbsp;<strong>Tiger Shovelnose Catfish<\\/strong>,<strong>Pseudoplatystoma fasciatum<\\/strong>, has captured the attention of aquarists for many years. However, because of their unique appearance, they have become one of the most popular large fish to keep.<\\/p>\",\"content\":null,\"images\":[null,\"sovelnose-cat-min-300x300.jpg\"],\"product_type\":\"physical\",\"sale_type\":\"0\",\"sku\":null,\"price\":\"450\",\"sale_price\":null,\"start_date\":null,\"end_date\":null,\"cost_per_item\":\"0\",\"product_id\":\"407\",\"barcode\":null,\"with_storehouse_management\":\"0\",\"quantity\":\"0\",\"allow_checkout_when_out_of_stock\":\"0\",\"stock_status\":\"in_stock\",\"weight\":\"0\",\"length\":\"0\",\"wide\":\"0\",\"height\":\"0\",\"is_added_attributes\":\"0\",\"has_product_options\":\"1\",\"related_products\":null,\"faq_schema_config\":[[{\"key\":\"question\",\"value\":null},{\"key\":\"answer\",\"value\":null}]],\"seo_meta\":{\"seo_title\":null,\"seo_description\":null,\"index\":\"index\"},\"seo_meta_image\":null,\"language\":\"en_US\",\"layout\":null,\"is_popular\":\"0\",\"status\":\"published\",\"store_id\":null,\"is_featured\":\"0\",\"categories\":[\"45\"],\"brand_id\":null,\"image\":\"sovelnose-cat-min-300x300.jpg\",\"minimum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"maximum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"tag\":null,\"submitter\":\"save\"}', 'updated', 'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/130.0.0.0 Safari/537.36', '2405:201:800e:d0d0:ad7b:3351:47bb:df30', 3, 407, 'SOVELNOSE CAT', 'primary', '2024-11-05 16:46:56', '2024-11-05 16:46:56'),
(2701, 3, 'product', '{\"name\":\"TIGER LOACH\",\"model\":\"Botble\\\\Ecommerce\\\\Models\\\\Product\",\"slug\":\"tiger-loach\",\"slug_id\":\"442\",\"is_slug_editable\":\"1\",\"description\":\"<p>The Redfin Peppered Tiger Loach is known from swiftly-flowing, clear, highly-oxygenated rivers and streams. During the rainy season, when water depth\\/flow increases and the water temperature drops, they migrate into flooded areas to spawn, usually staying close to submerged trees, logs, and roots. The waterways are usually lined with riparian vegetation, and the substrate is comprised of sand, bedrock, driftwood, and small boulders, creating an endless labyrinth of effective hiding places. In some areas there will be fast current as water is forced past haphazard rockwork. As with all botiids, these loaches must only be added to aquariums that are biologically mature.<\\/p><p>&nbsp;<\\/p><p>However, unlike their close relatives, the&nbsp;<i>Botia<\\/i>&nbsp;spp., the pointy-faced&nbsp;<i>Syncrossus<\\/i>&nbsp;genus of loaches grow larger and are exceptionally aggressive and territorial. It is essential that a spacious aquarium is provided, and numerous hiding spots and \\\"\\u02dcvisual barriers\\\"\\u2122 created with driftwood, smooth rounded rocks, cobbles, and pebbles of varying sizes. Ensure that the substrate has no sharp edges as these loaches will enjoy digging around the bottom of the tank in their search for titbits of food, and it is important that nothing damages their delicate sensory barbels. Dim lighting is preferable, and a well-covered tank is a must as these loaches are expert jumpers and can escape through the smallest of openings. Powerful filtration (ideally provided by external canister\\/s) and a decent level of oxygenation are requisite, as are frequent partial water changes.<\\/p><p>&nbsp;<\\/p><p>Like other fish from riverine habitats, these loaches are intolerant of a build up of organic pollutants, so ensure that a regular partial water change schedule is in place. As mentioned above, Redfin Peppered Tiger Loaches are extremely hostile towards other fish, and in the confines of the home aquarium, this can include their own kind. However, despite the hostility, they do form fascinating highly complex social structures within a group, and their physical health will suffer if they don\\\"\\u2122t have contact with more of their own species. To this end, they should always be maintained in large groups of 8 or more. This will not only meet their social needs but it will help spread any aggression amongst the shoal, so that no one fish bears the continual brunt of the antagonistic behaviour. It is also why adequate space and visual barriers are so important.<\\/p><p>&nbsp;<\\/p><p>Tankmates, if desired, must be chosen with much care - only large, robust, fast-swimming species that can hold their own should be considered (large but placid species, even if larger than the loaches, will be mercilessly bullied). Some aquarists like to keep more than one species of&nbsp;<i>Syncrossus<\\/i>&nbsp;loach together; this usually works well, but do make sure there are several of each species and not just single specimens. In addition to the tiger loaches, some of the&nbsp;<i>Yasuhikotakia<\\/i>&nbsp;species of loach also cohabit well with&nbsp;<i>Syncrossus<\\/i>&nbsp;due to their similar belligerent behaviour and environmental needs. Several different geographical variants are sometimes available, the colour and intensity of pattern depending on collection location and maturity. May also be seen on sale as Berdmore\'s Loach, Blyth\'s Loach, Burmese Peppered Firetail Botia, or Redfin Tiger Loach.<\\/p>\",\"content\":null,\"images\":[null,\"tiger-loach-min-300x300.jpg\"],\"product_type\":\"physical\",\"sale_type\":\"0\",\"sku\":null,\"price\":\"50\",\"sale_price\":null,\"start_date\":null,\"end_date\":null,\"cost_per_item\":\"0\",\"product_id\":\"406\",\"barcode\":null,\"with_storehouse_management\":\"0\",\"quantity\":\"0\",\"allow_checkout_when_out_of_stock\":\"0\",\"stock_status\":\"in_stock\",\"weight\":\"0\",\"length\":\"0\",\"wide\":\"0\",\"height\":\"0\",\"is_added_attributes\":\"0\",\"has_product_options\":\"1\",\"related_products\":null,\"faq_schema_config\":[[{\"key\":\"question\",\"value\":null},{\"key\":\"answer\",\"value\":null}]],\"seo_meta\":{\"seo_title\":null,\"seo_description\":null,\"index\":\"index\"},\"seo_meta_image\":null,\"language\":\"en_US\",\"layout\":null,\"is_popular\":\"0\",\"status\":\"published\",\"store_id\":null,\"is_featured\":\"0\",\"categories\":[\"45\"],\"brand_id\":null,\"image\":\"tiger-loach-min-300x300.jpg\",\"minimum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"maximum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"tag\":null,\"submitter\":\"save\"}', 'updated', 'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/130.0.0.0 Safari/537.36', '2405:201:800e:d0d0:ad7b:3351:47bb:df30', 3, 406, 'TIGER LOACH', 'primary', '2024-11-05 16:50:59', '2024-11-05 16:50:59'),
(2702, 3, 'product', '{\"name\":\"RANI LOACH\",\"model\":\"Botble\\\\Ecommerce\\\\Models\\\\Product\",\"slug\":\"rani-loach\",\"slug_id\":\"441\",\"is_slug_editable\":\"1\",\"description\":\"<p><i><strong>Botia dario<\\/strong><\\/i>&nbsp;(<strong>Bengal loach<\\/strong>&nbsp;or&nbsp;<strong>queen loach<\\/strong>) is a species of fish in the loach family Botiidae found in the Brahmaputra and Ganges basins in Bangladesh, Bhutan and northern India. The species is overall widespread.<\\/p><p><i>Botia dario<\\/i> is a good fish to have in tropical aquariums, quickly taking care of pest snail populations and less shy than B. striata. They get as long as 6 inches (150 mm) and are commonly kept in groups of 4 or more. They are omnivores and are fed sinking pellets as well as algae wafers. They also enjoy fresh vegetables, such as cucumber, zucchini, and frozen foods like bloodworms and brine shrimp.<\\/p>\",\"content\":null,\"images\":[null,\"rani-loach-min-300x300.jpg\"],\"product_type\":\"physical\",\"sale_type\":\"0\",\"sku\":null,\"price\":\"100\",\"sale_price\":null,\"start_date\":null,\"end_date\":null,\"cost_per_item\":\"0\",\"product_id\":\"405\",\"barcode\":null,\"with_storehouse_management\":\"0\",\"quantity\":\"0\",\"allow_checkout_when_out_of_stock\":\"0\",\"stock_status\":\"in_stock\",\"weight\":\"0\",\"length\":\"0\",\"wide\":\"0\",\"height\":\"0\",\"is_added_attributes\":\"0\",\"has_product_options\":\"1\",\"related_products\":null,\"faq_schema_config\":[[{\"key\":\"question\",\"value\":null},{\"key\":\"answer\",\"value\":null}]],\"seo_meta\":{\"seo_title\":null,\"seo_description\":null,\"index\":\"index\"},\"seo_meta_image\":null,\"submitter\":\"save\",\"language\":\"en_US\",\"layout\":null,\"is_popular\":\"0\",\"status\":\"published\",\"store_id\":null,\"is_featured\":\"0\",\"brand_id\":null,\"image\":\"rani-loach-min-300x300.jpg\",\"minimum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"maximum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"tag\":null}', 'updated', 'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/130.0.0.0 Safari/537.36', '2405:201:800e:d0d0:ad7b:3351:47bb:df30', 3, 405, 'RANI LOACH', 'primary', '2024-11-05 16:53:03', '2024-11-05 16:53:03'),
(2703, 3, 'product', '{\"name\":\"OB PEACOCK\",\"model\":\"Botble\\\\Ecommerce\\\\Models\\\\Product\",\"slug\":\"ob-peacock\",\"slug_id\":\"440\",\"is_slug_editable\":\"1\",\"description\":\"<p>The designation \\\"OB\\\" refers to distinctive Malawi Cichlids sporting captivating spotted patterns. This moniker came about through the crossbreeding of a male Aulonocara and a female Mbuna. While the OB gene is a natural feature of Mbunas, it has been artfully integrated into Peacocks and Haps through meticulous selective breeding.<\\/p><p>Within the realm of Cichlid enthusiasts, fervent discussions abound regarding the merits of these hybrids. Yet, despite the debate, we find ourselves captivated by the remarkable beauty and individuality inherent in these hybrids. In fact, we\'ve embarked on a journey to craft strains that are exclusively our own, setting the stage for unprecedented aquatic wonders.<\\/p><p>Consider an O.B. peacock cichlid. This fish results from a hybridization involving male Aulonocara cichlids and female mbuna cichlids. Both these cichlid species originated in Lake Malawi in Africa and, as such, generally prefer a freshwater tank.<\\/p><p>Peacock cichlids come in several colors, often featuring blue, red, yellow, orange, black, and white scales. This species is dimorphic, with males developing a mixed and spotted coloration, while females keep a black and silver coloring (while developing a spotted morph).<\\/p><p>Expect to maintain a minimum 55-gallon tank for peacock cichlids, with some adults requiring 100 gallons or more to flourish. We don\\u2019t consider peacock cichlids either plant or reef compatible. They thrive with a low level of care and may produce eggs if you keep a male and female together.<\\/p><p>O.B. peacock cichlids may live up to 15 years. Aquarium experts consider the species very hardy and rate them as semi-aggressive to aggressive with other aquatic animals.<\\/p><h2>&nbsp;<\\/h2>\",\"content\":null,\"images\":[null,\"ob-peacock-min-300x300.jpg\"],\"product_type\":\"physical\",\"sale_type\":\"0\",\"sku\":null,\"price\":\"250\",\"sale_price\":null,\"start_date\":null,\"end_date\":null,\"cost_per_item\":\"0\",\"product_id\":\"404\",\"barcode\":null,\"with_storehouse_management\":\"0\",\"quantity\":\"0\",\"allow_checkout_when_out_of_stock\":\"0\",\"stock_status\":\"in_stock\",\"weight\":\"0\",\"length\":\"0\",\"wide\":\"0\",\"height\":\"0\",\"is_added_attributes\":\"0\",\"has_product_options\":\"1\",\"related_products\":null,\"faq_schema_config\":[[{\"key\":\"question\",\"value\":null},{\"key\":\"answer\",\"value\":null}]],\"seo_meta\":{\"seo_title\":null,\"seo_description\":null,\"index\":\"index\"},\"seo_meta_image\":null,\"language\":\"en_US\",\"layout\":null,\"is_popular\":\"0\",\"status\":\"published\",\"store_id\":null,\"is_featured\":\"0\",\"categories\":[\"45\"],\"brand_id\":null,\"image\":\"ob-peacock-min-300x300.jpg\",\"product_labels\":[\"2\"],\"minimum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"maximum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"tag\":null,\"submitter\":\"save\"}', 'updated', 'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/130.0.0.0 Safari/537.36', '2405:201:800e:d0d0:ad7b:3351:47bb:df30', 3, 404, 'OB PEACOCK', 'primary', '2024-11-05 16:54:09', '2024-11-05 16:54:09'),
(2704, 3, 'product', '{\"name\":\"DRAGON BLOOD\",\"model\":\"Botble\\\\Ecommerce\\\\Models\\\\Product\",\"slug\":\"dragon-blood\",\"slug_id\":\"439\",\"is_slug_editable\":\"1\",\"description\":\"<p>Dragon Blood Peacock African Cichlids are stunning freshwater fish known for their vibrant colors and captivating appearance. These fish belong to the Cichlidae family and are native to the rocky shores of Lake Malawi in East Africa. With their striking red and orange hues, Dragon Blood Peacock African Cichlids are highly sought after by aquarium enthusiasts.<\\/p><p>&nbsp;<\\/p><p>These cichlids grow to an average length of about 4 to 6 inches, making them suitable for medium-sized aquariums. They have a peaceful temperament, which makes them a great addition to community tanks. However, it\'s important to note that they can display aggression towards other fish of the same species or similar coloration.<\\/p><p>&nbsp;<\\/p><p>One of the unique features of Dragon Blood Peacock African Cichlids is their ability to change color based on their mood or breeding behavior. During courtship, males intensify their bright red and orange colors to attract females. This mesmerizing display creates a visual spectacle in any aquarium.<\\/p><p>&nbsp;<\\/p><p>To keep these magnificent fish healthy and vibrant, it is crucial to provide them with a well-maintained aquarium environment. A spacious tank with plenty of hiding places, such as caves or rocks, mimics their natural habitat. A balanced diet consisting of high-quality cichlid pellets, supplemented with occasional live or frozen foods, will help support their optimal growth and coloration.<\\/p><p>&nbsp;<\\/p><p>Dragon Blood Peacock African Cichlids are undoubtedly a prized addition to any aquarium, offering both beauty and intrigue. Their captivating colors and peaceful nature make them a delightful choice for hobbyists seeking an eye-catching centerpiece fish.<\\/p><h2>Behavior<\\/h2><p>Dragon Blood Peacock African Cichlids are known for their intriguing behavior, making them a fascinating species to observe in an aquarium setting. These vibrant freshwater fish, native to Lake Malawi in East Africa, exhibit distinct social dynamics and unique courtship rituals.<\\/p><p>&nbsp;<\\/p><p>In a community tank, Dragon Blood Peacock African Cichlids are generally peaceful and can coexist with other African Cichlids of similar aggression levels. However, it\'s important to note that they can display territorial behavior, especially towards other fish of the same species or similar coloration. Providing sufficient hiding places and territories, such as caves or rocks, can help mitigate aggression and promote a harmonious environment.<\\/p><p>&nbsp;<\\/p><p>During breeding season, the behavior of these cichlids becomes even more captivating. Males showcase their dominance by intensifying their bright red and orange colors while engaging in intricate courtship displays. They dance and swim in a zigzag pattern, attracting the attention of females. Once a female shows interest, the male leads her to a chosen spot where she lays her eggs, while the male fertilizes them.<\\/p><p>&nbsp;<\\/p><p>Dragon Blood Peacock African Cichlids are attentive parents, with the female guarding the eggs and the male patrolling the area to ward off potential threats. After hatching, the fry are closely guarded and protected until they are independent enough to venture out on their own.<\\/p><p>&nbsp;<\\/p><p>Observing the behavior of Dragon Blood Peacock African Cichlids offers an engaging glimpse into the natural instincts and social interactions of these captivating fish. Whether it\'s their territorial tendencies or their elaborate courtship rituals, these cichlids never fail to captivate aquarium enthusiasts.<\\/p><p>&nbsp;<\\/p><h2>Lifespan<\\/h2><p>The lifespan of Dragon Blood Peacock African Cichlids can vary depending on various factors such as water quality, diet, and overall care provided. On average, these vibrant freshwater fish have a lifespan of 5 to 8 years when kept in optimal conditions.<\\/p><p>&nbsp;<\\/p><p>Maintaining a healthy and stable aquarium environment is crucial for promoting longevity in Dragon Blood Peacock African Cichlids. Consistently monitoring and maintaining appropriate water parameters, such as temperature and pH levels, helps ensure their well-being. Regular water changes and filtration are essential for keeping the water clean and free from toxins.<\\/p><p>&nbsp;<\\/p><p>A balanced and nutritious diet is also vital for the longevity of these cichlids. Offering a variety of high-quality cichlid pellets, supplemented with occasional live or frozen foods, helps provide the necessary nutrients they require to thrive. It\'s important to avoid overfeeding, as excess food can lead to obesity and related health issues.<\\/p><p>&nbsp;<\\/p><p>Genetics can also play a role in the lifespan of Dragon Blood Peacock African Cichlids. Breeding from healthy and robust individuals with a good genetic lineage can potentially contribute to longer lifespans in subsequent generations.<\\/p><p>&nbsp;<\\/p><p>By providing a well-maintained aquarium environment, a nutritious diet, and suitable genetic lineage, hobbyists can help ensure that Dragon Blood Peacock African Cichlids live a long and fulfilling life in captivity.<\\/p><h2>Tank Requirements<\\/h2><p>Creating the ideal tank environment for Dragon Blood Peacock African Cichlids is essential to promote their health and well-being. These striking freshwater fish, native to Lake Malawi in East Africa, have specific tank requirements that should be met to ensure their optimal growth and vibrant coloration.<\\/p><p>&nbsp;<\\/p><p>First and foremost, Dragon Blood Peacock African Cichlids require a spacious aquarium due to their territorial nature. A tank size of at least 75 gallons is recommended to accommodate their active swimming habits and provide ample room for multiple individuals if kept in a community setup. Additionally, the tank should have a secure lid to prevent any potential escapes.<\\/p><p>&nbsp;<\\/p><p>To mimic their natural habitat, it is important to create a rocky environment within the tank. Adding plenty of caves, rocks, and hiding places not only serves as territories for these cichlids but also helps reduce aggression by providing areas for retreat. The tank should have a sandy substrate to replicate the sandy lake bottom, as this allows the cichlids to exhibit their natural digging behavior.<\\/p><p>&nbsp;<\\/p><p>Maintaining water quality is paramount for the well-being of Dragon Blood Peacock African Cichlids. The water temperature should be maintained between 75\\u00b0F and 82\\u00b0F (24\\u00b0C and 28\\u00b0C), with a pH level ranging from 7.8 to 8.6. Regular water changes and effective filtration are necessary to keep the water clean and stable.<\\/p><p>&nbsp;<\\/p><p>In conclusion, providing a spacious tank with ample hiding places, a sandy substrate, and maintaining appropriate water parameters are key factors in creating a suitable habitat for Dragon Blood Peacock African Cichlids. Meeting these tank requirements will help these captivating fish thrive and showcase their vibrant colors in an aquarium setting.<\\/p>\",\"content\":null,\"images\":[null,\"dragon-blood-min-300x300.jpg\"],\"product_type\":\"physical\",\"sale_type\":\"0\",\"sku\":null,\"price\":\"250\",\"sale_price\":null,\"start_date\":null,\"end_date\":null,\"cost_per_item\":\"0\",\"product_id\":\"403\",\"barcode\":null,\"with_storehouse_management\":\"0\",\"quantity\":\"0\",\"allow_checkout_when_out_of_stock\":\"0\",\"stock_status\":\"in_stock\",\"weight\":\"0\",\"length\":\"0\",\"wide\":\"0\",\"height\":\"0\",\"is_added_attributes\":\"0\",\"has_product_options\":\"1\",\"related_products\":null,\"faq_schema_config\":[[{\"key\":\"question\",\"value\":null},{\"key\":\"answer\",\"value\":null}]],\"seo_meta\":{\"seo_title\":null,\"seo_description\":null,\"index\":\"index\"},\"seo_meta_image\":null,\"language\":\"en_US\",\"layout\":null,\"is_popular\":\"0\",\"status\":\"published\",\"store_id\":null,\"is_featured\":\"0\",\"categories\":[\"45\"],\"brand_id\":null,\"image\":\"dragon-blood-min-300x300.jpg\",\"product_labels\":[\"2\"],\"minimum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"maximum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"tag\":null,\"submitter\":\"save\"}', 'updated', 'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/130.0.0.0 Safari/537.36', '2405:201:800e:d0d0:ad7b:3351:47bb:df30', 3, 403, 'DRAGON BLOOD', 'primary', '2024-11-05 16:54:49', '2024-11-05 16:54:49'),
(2705, 3, 'product', '{\"name\":\"BANANA CICHLID\",\"model\":\"Botble\\\\Ecommerce\\\\Models\\\\Product\",\"slug\":\"banana-cichlid\",\"slug_id\":\"438\",\"is_slug_editable\":\"1\",\"description\":\"<p>The electric yellow&nbsp;<i>cichlid<\\/i>&nbsp;is set apart from other African&nbsp;<i>cichlids<\\/i>&nbsp;by its striking electric yellow coloration.<\\/p>\",\"content\":null,\"images\":[null,\"banana-cichlid-min-300x300.jpg\"],\"product_type\":\"physical\",\"sale_type\":\"0\",\"sku\":null,\"price\":\"150\",\"sale_price\":null,\"start_date\":null,\"end_date\":null,\"cost_per_item\":\"0\",\"product_id\":\"402\",\"barcode\":null,\"with_storehouse_management\":\"0\",\"quantity\":\"0\",\"allow_checkout_when_out_of_stock\":\"0\",\"stock_status\":\"in_stock\",\"weight\":\"0\",\"length\":\"0\",\"wide\":\"0\",\"height\":\"0\",\"is_added_attributes\":\"0\",\"has_product_options\":\"1\",\"related_products\":null,\"faq_schema_config\":[[{\"key\":\"question\",\"value\":null},{\"key\":\"answer\",\"value\":null}]],\"seo_meta\":{\"seo_title\":null,\"seo_description\":null,\"index\":\"index\"},\"seo_meta_image\":null,\"language\":\"en_US\",\"layout\":null,\"is_popular\":\"0\",\"status\":\"published\",\"store_id\":null,\"is_featured\":\"0\",\"categories\":[\"45\"],\"brand_id\":null,\"image\":\"banana-cichlid-min-300x300.jpg\",\"product_labels\":[\"2\"],\"minimum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"maximum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"tag\":null,\"submitter\":\"save\"}', 'updated', 'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/130.0.0.0 Safari/537.36', '2405:201:800e:d0d0:ad7b:3351:47bb:df30', 3, 402, 'BANANA CICHLID', 'primary', '2024-11-05 16:55:17', '2024-11-05 16:55:17'),
(2706, 3, 'product', '{\"name\":\"ICE BLUE\",\"model\":\"Botble\\\\Ecommerce\\\\Models\\\\Product\",\"slug\":\"ice-blue\",\"slug_id\":\"437\",\"is_slug_editable\":\"1\",\"description\":\"<p>The Pseudotropheus Ice Blue fish, also known as the \\u201cIce Blue Zebra Cichlid,\\u201d is a species of freshwater fish that originates from Lake Malawi in Africa. As their name suggests, these fish have a striking blue coloration, with a metallic shimmer that makes them appear as if they are covered in ice.<\\/p><p>The William\\u2019s Mbuna, also known as the Red Top Ice Blue Zebra, is a fish that belongs to the Mbuna genus. Since these fish love rocky surroundings, any setup should have plenty of places for them to construct nests and territories. Although not particularly aggressive, it will not accept other fish with similar colours or even males of the same species. Given that Mbuna have similar behaviour and food requirements, it is best maintained with other Mbuna. The male becomes extremely gorgeous when its dorsal fin turns orange and its body turns icy blue. Females have more pronounced vertical stripes and a brownish colour.<\\/p>\",\"content\":null,\"images\":[null,\"ice-blue-min-300x300.jpg\"],\"product_type\":\"physical\",\"sale_type\":\"0\",\"sku\":null,\"price\":\"150\",\"sale_price\":null,\"start_date\":null,\"end_date\":null,\"cost_per_item\":\"0\",\"product_id\":\"401\",\"barcode\":null,\"with_storehouse_management\":\"0\",\"quantity\":\"0\",\"allow_checkout_when_out_of_stock\":\"0\",\"stock_status\":\"in_stock\",\"weight\":\"0\",\"length\":\"0\",\"wide\":\"0\",\"height\":\"0\",\"is_added_attributes\":\"0\",\"has_product_options\":\"1\",\"related_products\":null,\"faq_schema_config\":[[{\"key\":\"question\",\"value\":null},{\"key\":\"answer\",\"value\":null}]],\"seo_meta\":{\"seo_title\":null,\"seo_description\":null,\"index\":\"index\"},\"seo_meta_image\":null,\"language\":\"en_US\",\"layout\":null,\"is_popular\":\"0\",\"status\":\"published\",\"store_id\":null,\"is_featured\":\"0\",\"categories\":[\"45\"],\"brand_id\":null,\"image\":\"ice-blue-min-300x300.jpg\",\"product_labels\":[\"2\"],\"minimum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"maximum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"tag\":null,\"submitter\":\"save\"}', 'updated', 'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/130.0.0.0 Safari/537.36', '2405:201:800e:d0d0:ad7b:3351:47bb:df30', 3, 401, 'ICE BLUE', 'primary', '2024-11-05 16:55:40', '2024-11-05 16:55:40'),
(2707, 3, 'product', '{\"name\":\"ALBINO HECKELI GEOPHEGUS\",\"model\":\"Botble\\\\Ecommerce\\\\Models\\\\Product\",\"slug\":\"albino-heckeli-geophegus\",\"slug_id\":\"436\",\"is_slug_editable\":\"1\",\"description\":\"<p>The ALBINO HECKELI GEOPHEGUS is a beautiful \\u201cearth-eater\\u201d from Brasil.<br>The reason it is called an earth eater (also earth mover) is due to the fact that they will constantly pick up and move rocks along the bottom of your aquarium creating piles and pits throughout your substrate.<\\/p>\",\"content\":null,\"images\":[null,\"albino-heckeli-geophegus-min-300x300-1.jpg\"],\"product_type\":\"physical\",\"sale_type\":\"0\",\"sku\":null,\"price\":\"750\",\"sale_price\":null,\"start_date\":null,\"end_date\":null,\"cost_per_item\":\"0\",\"product_id\":\"400\",\"barcode\":null,\"with_storehouse_management\":\"0\",\"quantity\":\"0\",\"allow_checkout_when_out_of_stock\":\"0\",\"stock_status\":\"in_stock\",\"weight\":\"0\",\"length\":\"0\",\"wide\":\"0\",\"height\":\"0\",\"is_added_attributes\":\"0\",\"has_product_options\":\"1\",\"related_products\":null,\"faq_schema_config\":[[{\"key\":\"question\",\"value\":null},{\"key\":\"answer\",\"value\":null}]],\"seo_meta\":{\"seo_title\":null,\"seo_description\":null,\"index\":\"index\"},\"seo_meta_image\":null,\"language\":\"en_US\",\"layout\":null,\"is_popular\":\"0\",\"status\":\"published\",\"store_id\":null,\"is_featured\":\"0\",\"categories\":[\"45\"],\"brand_id\":null,\"image\":\"albino-heckeli-geophegus-min-300x300-1.jpg\",\"product_labels\":[\"2\"],\"minimum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"maximum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"tag\":null,\"submitter\":\"save\"}', 'updated', 'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/130.0.0.0 Safari/537.36', '2405:201:800e:d0d0:ad7b:3351:47bb:df30', 3, 400, 'ALBINO HECKELI GEOPHEGUS', 'primary', '2024-11-05 16:55:59', '2024-11-05 16:55:59'),
(2708, 3, 'product', '{\"name\":\"UARU CICHLID\",\"model\":\"Botble\\\\Ecommerce\\\\Models\\\\Product\",\"slug\":\"uaru-cichlid\",\"slug_id\":\"431\",\"is_slug_editable\":\"1\",\"description\":\"<p>A fish with real character which needs a large, well-filtered, softwater aquarium and frequent partial water changes to remain in good health.Best kept in groups with non-aggressive tankmates.<\\/p><h2 id=\\\"section_care\\\">Care<\\/h2><p>Uaru are gentle giants which congregate in small social groups within their natural blackwater habitat. The water is warm, and very soft and acidic, and these conditions must be recreated in the home aquarium (peat filtration highly recommended) in order for this species to do well. In the wild, these majestic fish prefer the safety of shady areas amongst vegetation and fallen trees, so this should be replicated in the home aquarium as best as possible. The tank must be at least 48\\\" long and should incorporate dark substrate and decor. Lighting should be dim. The aquarium should be aquascaped with plenty of bogwood and robust plants such as&nbsp;<i>Microsorum pteropus<\\/i>, or plastic\\/silk varieties. Uaru very much enjoy eating fine-leaved or soft-leaved plants; indeed their faces will almost appear to \\\"light up\\\" if you present them with some&nbsp;<i>Cabomba caroliniana<\\/i>&nbsp;from time to time, a particular favourite! Uaru are peaceful fish and can be kept alongside other medium-large sized peaceable species. They should not be housed with aggressive or boisterous fish. The only time they are likely to become confrontational is if two of the fish pair off, at which time they should be separated from the rest of the group. Uaru are very susceptible to poor water conditions, so good filtration and frequent partial water changes are a must. Ideally they will only be added to mature aquaria. Not recommended for beginners. Young specimens show a \\\"spotted\\\" pattern and undergo a dramatic transformation into their adult form. May also be seen on sale as Triangle Cichlid.<\\/p><h2 id=\\\"section_feeding\\\">Feeding<\\/h2><p>It is important that Uaru receive a varied diet, incorporating a good amount of vegetable matter. They can sometimes be a little picky, but will generally feed on: flake, green flake, slow-sinking pellets\\/granular foods, lettuce, spinach, kale, cucumber, soft-leaved aquatic plants (such as&nbsp;<i>Cabomba caroliniana<\\/i>), frozen foods such as mosquito larvae, Mysis shrimp, Krill, chopped prawns (salad shrimp) etc.<\\/p>\",\"content\":null,\"images\":[null,\"uaru-cichlid-min-300x300.jpg\"],\"product_type\":\"physical\",\"sale_type\":\"0\",\"sku\":null,\"price\":\"1500\",\"sale_price\":null,\"start_date\":null,\"end_date\":null,\"cost_per_item\":\"0\",\"product_id\":\"399\",\"barcode\":null,\"with_storehouse_management\":\"0\",\"quantity\":\"0\",\"allow_checkout_when_out_of_stock\":\"0\",\"stock_status\":\"in_stock\",\"weight\":\"0\",\"length\":\"0\",\"wide\":\"0\",\"height\":\"0\",\"is_added_attributes\":\"0\",\"has_product_options\":\"1\",\"related_products\":null,\"faq_schema_config\":[[{\"key\":\"question\",\"value\":null},{\"key\":\"answer\",\"value\":null}]],\"seo_meta\":{\"seo_title\":null,\"seo_description\":null,\"index\":\"index\"},\"seo_meta_image\":null,\"submitter\":\"save\",\"language\":\"en_US\",\"layout\":null,\"is_popular\":\"0\",\"status\":\"published\",\"store_id\":null,\"is_featured\":\"0\",\"brand_id\":null,\"image\":\"uaru-cichlid-min-300x300.jpg\",\"product_labels\":[\"2\"],\"minimum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"maximum_order_quantity\":\"0\",\"tag\":null}', 'updated', 'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/130.0.0.0 Safari/537.36', '2405:201:800e:d0d0:ad7b:3351:47bb:df30', 3, 399, 'UARU CICHLID', 'primary', '2024-11-05 16:56:25', '2024-11-05 16:56:25'),
