(126, 'Alternanthera Reineckii Mini Growow Tc', '<p>Description: Alternanthera reineckii ‘Mini’ is a diminutive and captivating aquatic plant that adds a touch of vibrant color to aquariums. As a cultivar of the popular Alternanthera reineckii, this mini variant offers alluring foliage in a compact size, making it an excellent choice for aquascaping. Originating from South America, this plant belongs to the amaranth family (Amaranthaceae) and is cherished for its rich red and pink hues.</p><p>The ‘Mini’ variant maintains the signature lance-shaped leaves of its parent species but on a smaller scale. The leaves exhibit a spectrum of colors, ranging from green to deep red or pink, depending on the aquarium conditions. Its compact growth and vivid colors make ‘Mini’ a versatile plant suitable for foregrounds, borders, or small spaces within the aquascape.</p><p>Plant Information:</p><p>Scientific Name: Alternanthera reineckii ‘Mini’<br>Common Names: Mini Alternanthera, AR ‘Mini’<br>Family: Amaranthaceae<br>Origin: South America<br>Difficulty Level: Moderate<br>Lighting Requirements: Medium to High<br>CO2 Requirement: Beneficial for enhanced growth<br>Temperature Range: 72-82°F (22-28°C)<br>pH Range: 6.0-7.0<br>Propagation: Cuttings, side shoots</p>', '', 'published', '[\"alternanthera-reineckii-mini-growow-tc-min-1.jpg\"]', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, 0, 0, 300, 250, NULL, NULL, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0, 7, '2024-09-09 15:11:39', '2024-10-05 16:24:41', 'in_stock', 3, 'Botble\\ACL\\Models\\User', 'alternanthera-reineckii-mini-growow-tc-min-1.jpg', 'physical', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 0),
