(132, 'Alternanthera Reineckii Rosenervig Growow Tc', '<p>Description: Alternanthera reineckii “Rosanervig” is a captivating and vibrant aquatic plant known for its distinctive pink and red hues. Belonging to the amaranth family (Amaranthaceae), this cultivar is a variation of the popular Alternanthera reineckii. Originating from South America, “Rosanervig” stands out with its striking coloration, making it a sought-after choice for aquascaping enthusiasts.</p><p>The plant’s leaves are lance-shaped and exhibit a unique blend of green and intense pink or red pigmentation. The undersides of the leaves often feature a contrasting pinkish color, creating a visually appealing effect. Under optimal conditions, the plant can develop a lush and bushy appearance, making it an excellent choice for adding depth and contrast to aquarium layouts.</p><p>Plant Information:</p><p>Scientific Name: Alternanthera reineckii “Rosanervig”<br>Common Names: Pink Alternanthera, AR “Rosanervig”<br>Family: Amaranthaceae<br>Origin: South America<br>Difficulty Level: Moderate to Advanced<br>Lighting Requirements: Medium to High<br>CO2 Requirement: Beneficial for enhanced growth<br>Temperature Range: 72-82°F (22-28°C)<br>pH Range: 6.0-7.0<br>Propagation: Cuttings, side shoots</p>', '', 'published', '[\"alternanthera-reineckii-rosenervig-min-1.jpg\"]', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, 0, 0, 300, 250, NULL, NULL, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0, 6, '2024-09-09 15:24:12', '2024-10-05 16:25:11', 'in_stock', 3, 'Botble\\ACL\\Models\\User', 'alternanthera-reineckii-rosenervig-min-1.jpg', 'physical', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 0),
