(152, 'WA RED MELANO FISH FEED 45G', '<ul><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">WA RED MELANO FISH FEED</strong></li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Protein – 45%</strong></li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Fat – 5%</strong></li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Fibre – 4%</strong></li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Moisture – 9%</strong></li></ul>', NULL, 'published', '[\"wa-red-melano-fish-feed.png\"]', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 260, 220, NULL, NULL, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0, 3, '2024-09-09 17:38:23', '2024-09-09 17:38:23', 'in_stock', 3, 'Botble\\ACL\\Models\\User', NULL, 'physical', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, 0, 0),
(153, 'Bacopa Monierri', '<p>Common name: Small bacopa Use : Background plant CO2 : Low Light: Low (price per stem) (•Plant Pictures shown are of Submersed Grown Plants in Aquariums under Optimum Plant Growing Conditions. •Plants Sent are grown in Farms in Emmersed or Submersed Conditions depending on variety. Hence, Plant/Leaf Structures may vary from that shown in pictures. When they are grown submersed in aquariums under Optimum Growing Conditions as required by the Plant they will get the appearance as shown in pictures)</p>', '', 'published', '[\"bacopa-monierri-min.jpg\"]', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, 0, 0, 140, 110, NULL, NULL, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0, 4, '2024-09-09 17:39:28', '2024-10-03 13:21:02', 'in_stock', 3, 'Botble\\ACL\\Models\\User', 'bacopa-monierri-min.jpg', 'physical', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 0),
(154, 'Bacopa Monierri Platinum Growow Tc Plant', '<p>Description: Bacopa Monnieri, commonly known as Water Hyssop or Brahmi, is an aquatic plant renowned for its delicate appearance and therapeutic history. As a member of the Plantaginaceae family, this herbaceous perennial is native to wetlands in Asia, North and South America, and Australia. Its emersed growth showcases pairs of opposite, succulent leaves along the stems, while its submersed form features finer, dissected leaves. Bacopa Monnieri’s overall appearance is a testament to simplicity, making it a popular choice for both aquarium enthusiasts and herbalists alike.</p><p>Beyond its ornamental value in aquascaping, Bacopa Monnieri is recognized for its use in traditional medicine, particularly in Ayurveda, where it is believed to offer cognitive and adaptogenic benefits.</p>', '', 'published', '[\"bacopa-monierri-platinum-growow-tc-plant-min.jpg\"]', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, 0, 0, 300, 250, NULL, NULL, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0, 4, '2024-09-09 17:42:04', '2024-10-05 16:26:04', 'in_stock', 3, 'Botble\\ACL\\Models\\User', 'bacopa-monierri-platinum-growow-tc-plant-min.jpg', 'physical', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 0),
(155, 'Bacopa Salzmani Growow Tc Plant', '<p>Description: Bacopa Salzmanii SG, often referred to simply as Bacopa Salzmannii, stands as a captivating aquatic plant cherished for its unique appearance and graceful growth. As a member of the Plantaginaceae family, this species hails from South America, bringing a touch of elegance to freshwater aquariums. Bacopa Salzmanii SG is characterized by its slender stems and pairs of opposite, lance-shaped leaves that can display varying shades of green. The leaves often feature a subtle ripple effect, contributing to the plant’s overall aesthetic appeal.</p><p>This plant’s charming features make it a popular choice for aquascapers aiming to add a touch of sophistication to their underwater landscapes.</p><p>Plant Information:</p><p>Scientific Name: Bacopa Salzmanii SG<br>Family: Plantaginaceae<br>Origin: South America<br>Difficulty Level: Moderate<br>Lighting Requirements: Medium to High<br>CO2 Requirement: Low to Medium<br>Temperature Range: 64-78°F (18-26°C)<br>pH Range: 6.0-7.5<br>Propagation: Cuttings</p>', '', 'published', '[\"bacopa-salzmani-growow-tc-plant-min.jpg\"]', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, 0, 0, 300, 250, NULL, NULL, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0, 1, '2024-09-09 17:43:10', '2024-10-05 16:39:42', 'in_stock', 3, 'Botble\\ACL\\Models\\User', 'bacopa-salzmani-growow-tc-plant-min.jpg', 'physical', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 0),
(156, 'Cryptocoryne Axelrodii Growow Tc Plant', '<p>Common Name: Cryptocoryne Axelrodi</p><p>Crypt Axelrodi is a rarer Cryptocoryne species that features narrow leaves, hardy nature and a greenish-brown color. It works great for mid ground plant coverage in planted tanks and is easy to care for. However, we’d recommend that it is not moved like most crypts as this can potentially trigger Crypt melt.</p><p>Like other crypts, Cryptocoryne Axelrodi is great for beginner hobbyists due to its ease in keeping and low care requirements. If grown in good aquarium substrate such as Ultum Nature System Controsoil, the plant can feed through the roots and grow quickly without the need for high light, CO2 or fertilizer dosing. However, the addition of CO2 and good lighting will result in healthier, more robust growth.</p><p>Crypts can be grown emersed or submerged. Propagate by splitting the rhizome or cutting off new growth and replanting</p><p>Notes:</p><p>Cryptocoryne prefer not to be moved once planted. If possible, do not move them!<br>Do not make drastic changes to the aquarium. Unstable parameters will result in melt and rotting of the aquarium plant.<br>Please be sure to remove this plant from its pot. Remove the cotton surrounding the roots and plant into a quality substrate.<br>CO2 injection and quality aquarium soil will yield better growth.<br>Please research according to ensure the plant receives proper care.Family Name: AraceaeEndemic To: BorneoLeaves: 2-3+”<br>Height: 10-15″</p><p>pH: 6-7.5</p><p>Care: Easy</p><p>Light: Low to Medium</p><p>Co2: Not necessary but recommended</p><p>Propagation: Cut by rhizome</p><p>Growth rate: Slow</p>', '', 'published', '[\"cryptocoryne-axelrodii-growow-tc-plant-min.jpg\"]', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, 0, 0, 300, 250, NULL, NULL, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0, 4, '2024-09-09 17:52:47', '2024-10-05 16:40:42', 'in_stock', 3, 'Botble\\ACL\\Models\\User', 'cryptocoryne-axelrodii-growow-tc-plant-min.jpg', 'physical', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 0),
(157, '2Hr Aquarist APT Jazz', '<p><strong style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255);color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:bolder;word-spacing:0px;\">The best root fertiliser for planted tanks.</strong><br><span style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255);color:rgb(105,105,105);font-size:16px;\"><span>Thicker, fuller growth forms with superior algae control. </span> </span><br><span style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255);color:rgb(105,105,105);font-size:16px;\"><span>Nitrate Limitation made easy. APT j/Jazz from 2HR Aquarist are root fertiliser capsules for planted aquariums. They consist of round baked clay pellets mixed with a blend of inorganic mineral salts and provide the plants with nutrients for 2 months. </span> </span><br><span style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255);color:rgb(105,105,105);font-size:16px;\"><span>Potassium, phosphate, nitrogen salts and chelated trace elements are integrated into the clay matrix and slowly diffuse out of the clay when immersed in water, acting directly on the roots. </span> </span></p>', '', 'published', '[\"2hr-aquarist-apt-jazz.png\"]', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 13, 0, 0, 1140, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0, 0, '2024-09-09 17:55:24', '2024-10-05 14:51:01', 'in_stock', 3, 'Botble\\ACL\\Models\\User', '2hr-aquarist-apt-jazz.png', 'physical', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 0),
(158, 'Cryptocoryne Becketii Growow Tc Plant', '<p>Cryptocoryne beckettii ‘Petchii’ is a small variety of Cryptocoryne beckettii from Sri Lanka, which has beautiful, slightly fluted leaf margins, 10-15 cm long. Leaves become dark olive-brown with violet underside. Like many other Cryptocorynes, the leaf colour and shape depends largely on environmental conditions in the aquarium.</p>', '', 'published', '[\"cryptocoryne-becketii-growow-tc-plant-min.jpg\"]', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, 0, 0, 300, 250, NULL, NULL, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0, 4, '2024-09-09 17:55:40', '2024-10-05 16:41:47', 'in_stock', 3, 'Botble\\ACL\\Models\\User', 'cryptocoryne-becketii-growow-tc-plant-min.jpg', 'physical', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 0),
(159, 'Cryptocoryne Becketii Growow Tc Plant', NULL, NULL, 'published', '[\"cryptocoryne-becketii-growow-tc-plant-min.jpg\"]', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 300, 250, NULL, NULL, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, NULL, 0, '2024-09-09 17:55:40', '2024-10-05 16:41:47', 'in_stock', 3, 'Botble\\ACL\\Models\\User', NULL, 'physical', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 0),
(160, 'API Life Aayu Bio Media 1ltr/500gm', '<p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">API Life Aayu Bio Media is a mixture of porous filtration media specially designed for recreating the water purification system of the nature.</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">Porous natural stone has a high permeability and provides an ideal environment for filtration bacteria to colonize.</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">It also helps to remove organic substances, which become a cause of water pollution and degrade quickly through the work of microorganisms.</p>', NULL, 'published', '[\"happy-raksha-bandhan-instagram-post8.png\"]', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 990, 890, NULL, NULL, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0, 0, '2024-09-09 18:01:33', '2024-09-09 18:01:33', 'in_stock', 3, 'Botble\\ACL\\Models\\User', NULL, 'physical', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, 0, 0),
(161, 'API Life Aayuh Bio Media 0.5 Ltr / 250gm', '<p style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\">API Life Aayuh Bio Media is a mixture of porous filtration media specially designed for recreating the water purification system of the nature.</p><p style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\">Porous natural stone has a high permeability and provides an ideal environment for filtration bacteria to colonize.</p><p style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\">It also helps to remove organic substances, which become a cause of water pollution and degrade quickly through the work of microorganisms.</p>', '', 'published', '[\"happy-raksha-bandhan-instagram-post8.png\"]', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 590, 531, NULL, NULL, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0, 6, '2024-09-09 18:18:25', '2024-10-04 17:01:49', 'out_of_stock', 3, 'Botble\\ACL\\Models\\User', 'happy-raksha-bandhan-instagram-post8.png', 'physical', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 0),
(162, 'API Life Aayuh Bio Media 2ltr/1kg', '<p style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\">API Life Aayu Bio Media is a mixture of porous filtration media specially designed for recreating the water purification system of the nature.</p><p style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\">Porous natural stone has a high permeability and provides an ideal environment for filtration bacteria to colonize.</p><p style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\">It also helps to remove organic substances, which become a cause of water pollution and degrade quickly through the work of microorganisms.</p>', '', 'published', '[\"happy-raksha-bandhan-instagram-post7-1.png\"]', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1590, 1430, NULL, NULL, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0, 2, '2024-09-09 18:20:10', '2024-10-04 17:01:08', 'in_stock', 3, 'Botble\\ACL\\Models\\User', 'happy-raksha-bandhan-instagram-post7-1.png', 'physical', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 0),
(163, 'Cryptocoryne Brown Growow Tc Plant', '<p style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Description: </strong>Cryptocoryne ‘Brown’ admired for its rich and deep brown coloration that adds a warm and earthy tone to freshwater aquariums. As a member of the Cryptocoryne genus within the family Araceae, this plant hails from Sri Lanka. The ‘Brown’ variety is characterized by its broad and slightly ruffled leaves, creating a visually striking contrast in planted tank setups. Known for its adaptability and aesthetic appeal, Cryptocoryne ‘Brown’ is a popular choice for aquarists seeking a distinctive and colorful addition to their aquatic landscapes.</p><p style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Plant Information:</strong></p><ul><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Scientific Name:</strong> Cryptocoryne ‘Brown’</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Family:</strong> Araceae</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Origin:</strong> Sri Lanka</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Difficulty Level:</strong> Easy</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Lighting Requirements:</strong> Low to Medium</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">CO2 Requirement:</strong> Low to Medium</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Temperature Range:</strong> 72-82°F (22-28°C)</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">pH Range:</strong> 6.0-7.5</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Propagation:</strong> Runner, division</li></ul>', '', 'published', '[\"cryptocoryne-brown-growow-tc-plant-min.jpg\"]', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, 0, 0, 300, 250, NULL, NULL, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0, 3, '2024-09-09 18:35:02', '2024-10-05 16:42:34', 'in_stock', 3, 'Botble\\ACL\\Models\\User', 'cryptocoryne-brown-growow-tc-plant-min.jpg', 'physical', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 0),
(164, 'Cryptocoryne Gecko Growow Tc Plant', '<p>Cryptocoryne Gecko Growow Tc Plant<br> </p>', '', 'published', '[\"cryptocoryne-gecko-growow-tc-plant-min-600x600.jpg\"]', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, 0, 0, 300, 250, NULL, NULL, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0, 3, '2024-09-09 18:36:10', '2024-10-05 16:43:31', 'in_stock', 3, 'Botble\\ACL\\Models\\User', 'cryptocoryne-gecko-growow-tc-plant-min-600x600.jpg', 'physical', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 0),
(165, 'Cryptocoryne Green Growow Tc Plant', '<p style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Description:</strong> Cryptocoryne ‘Green’ is celebrated for its lush green foliage that brings a refreshing and vibrant aesthetic to freshwater aquariums. As a member of the Cryptocoryne genus within the family Araceae, this plant originates from Sri Lanka. The ‘Green’ variety is characterized by its broad and slightly ruffled leaves, creating an inviting and natural look in planted tank setups. Known for its versatility and ease of care, Cryptocoryne ‘Green’ is a popular choice for aquarists seeking a classic and visually appealing addition to their aquatic landscapes.</p><p style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Plant Information:</strong></p><ul><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Scientific Name:</strong> Cryptocoryne ‘Green’</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Family:</strong> Araceae</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Origin:</strong> Sri Lanka</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Difficulty Level:</strong> Easy</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Lighting Requirements:</strong> Low to Medium</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">CO2 Requirement:</strong> Low to Medium</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Temperature Range:</strong> 72-82°F (22-28°C)</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">pH Range:</strong> 6.0-7.5</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Propagation:</strong> Runner, division</li></ul>', '', 'published', '[\"cryptocoryne-green-growow-tc-plant-min.jpg\"]', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, 0, 0, 300, 250, NULL, NULL, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0, 2, '2024-09-09 18:40:42', '2024-10-05 16:44:05', 'in_stock', 3, 'Botble\\ACL\\Models\