(166, 'Cryptocoryne Lucens Growow Tc Plant', '<p style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Description:</strong> Cryptocoryne lucens, often referred to as Lucens Crypt, is a popular aquatic plant celebrated for its lush green foliage and versatility in planted aquariums. As a member of the Cryptocoryne genus within the family Araceae, this plant is native to Sri Lanka and other parts of Southeast Asia. It features elongated, lance-shaped leaves that form dense clusters, creating a vibrant and verdant tapestry in aquariums. Cryptocoryne lucens is known for its adaptability and ease of care, making it an excellent choice for both beginners and experienced aquarists.</p><p style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\">This Cryptocoryne species adds a touch of natural beauty and a sense of tranquility to freshwater tanks, making it a favored component of aquascapes.</p><p style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Plant Information:</strong></p><ul><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Scientific Name:</strong> Cryptocoryne lucens</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Family:</strong> Araceae</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Origin:</strong> Sri Lanka, Southeast Asia</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Difficulty Level:</strong> Easy</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Lighting Requirements:</strong> Low to Medium</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">CO2 Requirement:</strong> Low to Medium</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Temperature Range:</strong> 72-82°F (22-28°C)</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">pH Range:</strong> 6.0-7.5</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Propagation:</strong> Rhizome division</li></ul>', '', 'published', '[\"cryptocoryne-lucens-growow-tc-plant-min.jpg\"]', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, 0, 0, 300, 250, NULL, NULL, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0, 3, '2024-09-09 18:47:04', '2024-10-05 16:44:39', 'in_stock', 3, 'Botble\\ACL\\Models\\User', 'cryptocoryne-lucens-growow-tc-plant-min.jpg', 'physical', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 0),
(167, 'Cryptocoryne Nurii Growow Tc Plant', '<p style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\">This beautiful variation of Cryptocoryne nurii was found growing in the wild in Malaysia around 1970. In the aquarium hobby it became popular under the name ‘Rose Maiden’.</p><p style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\">The plant is as easy to grow as Cryptocoryne wendtii and has the same size and leaf shape. It will, given the time, produce runners under the bottom layer, often showing up quite far from the mother plant.</p><p style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\">Intensity of colour and patterns in leaves is dependant on light and nutrition.</p><div class=\"description\" style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\"><p>This beautiful variation of Cryptocoryne nurii was found growing in the wild in Malaysia around 1970. In the aquarium hobby it became popular under the name ‘Rose Maiden’.</p><p>The plant is as easy to grow as Cryptocoryne wendtii and has the same size and leaf shape. It will, given the time, produce runners under the bottom layer, often showing up quite far from the mother plant.</p><p>Intensity of colour and patterns in leaves is dependant on light and nutrition.</p></div>', '', 'published', '[\"cryptocoryne-nurii-growow-tc-plant-min.jpg\"]', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, 0, 0, 300, 250, NULL, NULL, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0, 3, '2024-09-09 18:49:28', '2024-10-05 16:45:18', 'in_stock', 3, 'Botble\\ACL\\Models\\User', 'cryptocoryne-nurii-growow-tc-plant-min.jpg', 'physical', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 0),
(168, 'Cryptocoryne Perva', '<p>Cryptocoryne parva fromac Sri Lanka is the smallest of all Cryptocorynes (only 3-6 cm tall and a roset less than 5-8 cm wide). It is one of the few species that does not significantly change its leaf shape and colour depending on cultivation conditions. It needs more light than most other Cryptocorynes because it almost loses its leaf plate under water. So, it must never be overshadowed by other plants.</p><p>Known for its slow growth, but Nutrition Capsules in the bottom layer will enhance the development. Individual plants should be planted a few centimetres apart, and after about six months they will form a cohesive low group of plants.</p><p>Very recommendable foreground plant.</p>', '', 'published', '[\"cryptocoryne-perva-min.jpg\"]', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, 0, 0, 140, 110, NULL, NULL, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0, 6, '2024-09-09 18:50:25', '2024-10-03 14:57:40', 'in_stock', 3, 'Botble\\ACL\\Models\\User', 'cryptocoryne-perva-min.jpg', 'physical', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 0),
(169, 'Cryptocoryne Perva Growow Tc Plant', '<p style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Description:</strong> Cryptocoryne parva, often known simply as Parva Crypt, is a diminutive yet charming aquatic plant prized for its petite size and delicate appearance. As a member of the Cryptocoryne genus within the family Araceae, this plant is native to Sri Lanka. Cryptocoryne parva is characterized by narrow, lance-shaped leaves that form compact rosettes, creating a carpet-like effect when planted in groups. Despite its small stature, this Cryptocoryne species adds a touch of elegance to aquariums, making it a popular choice for aquascaping and foreground planting.</p><p style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\">Cryptocoryne parva’s ability to create lush carpets and its undemanding nature contribute to its appeal among both beginners and experienced aquarists.</p><p style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Plant Information:</strong></p><ul><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Scientific Name:</strong> Cryptocoryne parva</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Family:</strong> Araceae</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Origin:</strong> Sri Lanka</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Difficulty Level:</strong> Easy</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Lighting Requirements:</strong> Low to Medium</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">CO2 Requirement:</strong> Low to Medium</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Temperature Range:</strong> 72-82°F (22-28°C)</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">pH Range:</strong> 6.0-7.5</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Propagation:</strong> Runner, division</li></ul>', '', 'published', '[\"cryptocoryne-perva-min-1.jpg\"]', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, 0, 0, 300, 250, NULL, NULL, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0, 3, '2024-09-10 11:26:09', '2024-10-05 16:45:49', 'in_stock', 3, 'Botble\\ACL\\Models\\User', 'cryptocoryne-perva-min-1.jpg', 'physical', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 0),
(170, 'Cryptocoryne Pigmy Growow Tc Plant', '<p>The Cryptocoryne pygmy Tissue Culture (TC) Cup is a convenient and easy way to add this beautiful aquatic plant to your aquarium. This tissue culture cup contains a small, compact variety of Cryptocoryne that is perfect for creating a lush, green carpet in your tank. The plant is grown in a sterile environment, free</p>', '', 'published', '[\"cryptocoryne-pigmy-growow-tc-plant-min.jpg\"]', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, 0, 0, 300, 250, NULL, NULL, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0, 0, '2024-09-10 11:32:27', '2024-10-05 16:46:19', 'in_stock', 3, 'Botble\\ACL\\Models\\User', 'cryptocoryne-pigmy-growow-tc-plant-min.jpg', 'physical', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 0),
(171, 'Cryptocoryne Ponterdifolia Growow Tc Plant', '<p style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Description:</strong> Cryptocoryne pontederiifolia, commonly known as Pontederiifolia Crypt, is a captivating aquatic plant admired for its unique and decorative leaves. As a member of the Cryptocoryne genus within the family Araceae, this plant is native to Southeast Asia, including regions in India and Sri Lanka. Cryptocoryne pontederiifolia is characterized by its elongated and lance-shaped leaves that feature a prominent midrib and undulating edges. The leaves may exhibit various shades of green, contributing to its aesthetic appeal. This Cryptocoryne species adds a touch of elegance to freshwater aquariums, making it a popular choice among aquarists engaged in planted tank setups.</p><p style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\">Known for its hardiness and adaptability, Cryptocoryne pontederiifolia is suitable for both novice and experienced aquarium enthusiasts.</p><p style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Plant Information:</strong></p><ul><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Scientific Name:</strong> Cryptocoryne pontederiifolia</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Family:</strong> Araceae</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Origin:</strong> Southeast Asia (India, Sri Lanka)</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Difficulty Level:</strong> Easy to Moderate</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Lighting Requirements:</strong> Low to Medium</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">CO2 Requirement:</strong> Low to Medium</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Temperature Range:</strong> 72-82°F (22-28°C)</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">pH Range:</strong> 6.0-7.5</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Propagation:</strong> Runner, division</li></ul>', '', 'published', '[\"cryptocoryne-ponterdifolia-growow-tc-plant-min.jpeg\"]', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, 0, 0, 300, 250, NULL, NULL, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0, 3, '2024-09-10 11:33:32', '2024-10-05 16:46:50', 'in_stock', 3, 'Botble\\ACL\\Models\\User', 'cryptocoryne-ponterdifolia-growow-tc-plant-min.jpeg', 'physical', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 0),
(172, 'Cryptocoryne Sindoor Growow Tc Plant', '<p style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Common Name:</strong> Cryptocoryne Sindoor, Water Trumpet, Wendtii Sreepadma Sindoor</p><p style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\">Cryptocoryne Wendtii Sindoor is a new variation of Cryptocoryne available to the aquarium community. This particular Crypt was created from Wendtii Brown and developed in lab to ensure a stable mutation. Its name refers to the rich maroon to pink tones the plant produces when grown in suitable conditions for Cryptocoryne species. Because this variety is relatively new, it can be assumed that care is similar to other forms of Cryptocoryne plants.</p><p style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\">Cryptocoryne do best when provided with a nutrient-dense aquarium soil and stability. Cryptocoryne plants require time to establish strong root systems and frequent moving or parameter changes will slow growth and impact overall health.</p><p class=\"p1\" style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\"><b style=\"font-weight:bolder;\"><strong>Key Features &amp; Important Notes:</strong></b></p><ul><li class=\"ul1\">Tissue culture plants are grown in-vitro from state of the art laboratories that specialize in propagating aquatic plants. They provide the best option for those who want to ensure that absolutely zero unwanted pests are introduced into the aquarium.</li><li class=\"ul1\">Remove tissue culture gel before planting. Simply wash the gel away or soak the plant in water and squeeze the gel off gently with your fingers.</li><li class=\"ul1\">Cryptocoryne prefer not to be moved once planted. If possible, do not move them.</li><li class=\"ul1\">For instructions on how to properly plant tissue culture aquarium plants, click <a style=\"background-color:transparent;text-decoration:none;\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=FJLHDmTxBl0\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">here</a>.</li><li class=\"ul1\">Refrain from making drastic or sudden changes to the aquarium. Unstable parameters contribute to melt and rotting of Cryptocoryne plants.</li><li class=\"ul1\">Please research appropriately to ensure your plant thrives.</li><li class=\"ul1\"><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Species Information:Family Name:</strong> Araceae<br><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Origin:</strong> South East Asia<br><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Height:</strong> 3-6″<br><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">pH:</strong> 5.5-7.5<br><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Care:</strong> Medium<br><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Light:</strong> Moderate<br><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Co2:</strong> Recommended<br><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Propagation:</strong> Separate plantlets<br><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Growth rate: </strong>Slow</li></ul>', '', 'published', '[\"cryptocoryne-sindoor-growow-tc-plant-min.jpg\"]', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, 0, 0, 800, 600, NULL, NULL, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0, 3, '2024-09-10 11:34:55', '2024-10-05 16:49:12', 'in_stock', 3, 'Botble\\ACL\\Models\\User', 'cryptocoryne-sindoor-growow-tc-plant-min.jpg', 'physical', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 0),
(173, 'Cryptocoryne Spiralis Green', '<p>This plant requires nutrient rich substrate. Regular pruning will keep it looking its best.</p><p>Plant Difficulty : Easy</p><p>Light Requirement : Low</p><p>Plant Type : Rhizome</p>', '', 'published', '[\"cryptocoryne-spiralis-green-min-600x600.jpg\"]', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, 0, 0, 140, 110, NULL, NULL, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0, 2, '2024-09-10 11:35:50', '2024-10-03 15:00:23', 'in_stock', 3, 'Botble\\ACL\\Models\\User', 'cryptocoryne-spiralis-green-min-600x600.jpg', 'physical', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 0),
(174, 'Cryptocoryne Spiralis Jwala Growow Tc Plant', '<p style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Overview:</strong> Coming from the family Araceae, Cryptocoryne spiralis is a beautiful aquatic plant. It is one of the best plants for the beginners as it is the least demanding and easy to maintain. When C. spiralis is grown solitarily, it gives a good and aesthetic view to the aquarium. However, when grown in clusters it creates a bushy facade to the underwater ambiance. The plant is native to India and can be seen growing between the rice fields. When the plant is maintained with regular pruning and cutting it gives the best look to the aquarium.</p><p style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Appearance:</strong> C. spiralis is a perfect plant to add height and visual drama to your tank. The growth form of the plant is rosette. The green leaves become lengthy and slender and sway underwater. The emergent leaves in the other hand are small in size and have wide blades. The long leaves make the plant an excellent option to ponder as a background plant. Generally, it is advised to plant it in a planned fashion like small plants in the foreground and larger ones at the back. It doesn’t give a forest-like appearance to the aquarium and grace it beautifully. It is hard to achieve the variations when planted randomly.</p><p style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Hard/soft Plant:</strong> It is a very hardy plant</p><p style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Ideal water temperature:</strong> The temperature requirement of the plant is between 75° and 82°F.</p><p style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Lightening conditions:</strong> The light requirement of the plant is medium to high. Using full spectrum bulbs of at least 2 watts per gallon will fulfill the needs of the plant to flourish well.</p><p style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Ideal pH level:</strong> Water conditions need to be stable for better plant growth to prevent stems and roots from rotting away. pH within the range of 6.5 to 7.5 is considered best for C. spiralis.</p><p style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Do you know:</strong> C. spiralis can be propagated by using multiple runners or rhizome divisions.</p>', '', 'published', '[\"cryptocoryne-spiralis-jwala-growow-tc-plant-min.jpg\"]', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, 0, 0, 300, 250, NULL, NULL, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0, 0, '2024-09-10 11:39:37', '2024-10-05 16:50:26', 'in_stock', 3, 'Botble\\ACL\\Models\\User', 'cryptocoryne-spiralis-jwala-growow-tc-plant-min.jpg', 'physical', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 0),
(175, 'Cryptocoryne Spiralis red', '<p style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\">This plant requires nutrient rich substrate. Regular pruning will keep it looking its best.</p><p style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Plant Difficulty</strong> : Medium</p><p style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Light Requirement</strong> : Medium</p><p style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Plant Type</strong> : Rhizome</p>', '', 'published', '[\"cryptocoryne-spiralis-red-min.jpg\"]', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, 0, 0, 140, 110, NULL, NULL, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0, 5, '2024-09-10 13:05:18', '2024-10-03 15:01:07', 'in_stock', 3, 'Botble\\ACL\\Models\\User', 'cryptocoryne-spiralis-red-min.jpg', 'physical', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 0),
(176, 'Cryptocoryne Tropica Growow Tc Plant', '<p>This beautiful variety with the dark, hammered leaves is named after ‘Tropica’. When grown in an open space the leaves will virtually lie on the bottom. It is suitable for small aquariums with leaves from 10-20 cm, and a rosette from 10-20 cm wide. Like most other Sri Lanka Cryptocorynes, it also grows well in hard water.</p>', '', 'published', '[\"cryptocoryne-tropica-growow-tc-plant-min.jpg\"]', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, 0, 0, 300, 250, NULL, NULL, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0, 1, '2024-09-10 13:09:49', '2024-10-05 16:50:56', 'in_stock', 3, 'Botble\\ACL\\Models\\User', 'cryptocoryne-tropica-growow-tc-plant-min.jpg', 'physical', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 0),
(177, 'Cryptocoryne Wendetii', '<p style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\">This easy to grow plant can be kept in groups and can be grown under various conditions.</p><p style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Plant Difficulty</strong> : Easy</p><p style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Light Requirement</strong> : Medium</p><p style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Plant Type</strong> : Rhizome</p>', '', 'published', '[\"cryptocoryne-wendetii-min.jpg\"]', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, 0, 0, 140, 110, NULL, NULL, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0, 5, '2024-09-10 13:11:25', '2024-10-03 15:01:58', 'in_stock', 3, 'Botble\\ACL\\Models\\User', 'cryptocoryne-wendetii-min.jpg', 'physical', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 0),
(178, 'Cryptocoryne Wendetii Long Growow Tc Plants', '<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-9022ba2 elementor-widget elementor-widget-woocommerce-product-title elementor-page-title elementor-widget-heading\" style=\"background-color:rgb(242,246,249);color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;width:512px;word-spacing:0px;\"><div class=\"elementor-widget-container\"><h4 class=\"product_title entry-title elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default\" style=\"font-family:\'Sans-serif\';\">Cryptocoryne Wendetii Long Growow Tc Plants</h4></div></div><div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-69c042e6 elementor-widget elementor-widget-woocommerce-product-price\" style=\"background-color:rgb(242,246,249);color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;width:512px;word-spacing:0px;\"><div class=\"elementor-widget-container\"><br> </div></div>', '', 'published', '[\"cryptocoryne-wendetii-long-growow-tc-plants-min.jpg\"]', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, 0, 0, 300, 250, NULL, NULL, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0, 3, '2024-09-10 13:13:10', '2024-10-05 16:51:33', 'in_stock', 3, 'Botble\\ACL\\Models\\User', 'cryptocoryne-wendetii-long-growow-tc-plants-min.jpg', 'physical', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 0),
(179, 'Cryptocoryne Wendetii Pink Growow Tc Plant', '<p style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Description:</strong> Cryptocoryne wendtii ‘Pink’ is a captivating variant of the Wendtii Crypt, cherished for its delicate and subtle pink hues that bring a touch of elegance to freshwater aquariums. As a member of the Cryptocoryne genus within the family Araceae, this plant originates from Sri Lanka. The ‘Pink’ variety is characterized by its broad and slightly ruffled leaves, displaying a rosy tint that adds a unique and charming dimension to planted tank setups. Known for its adaptability and aesthetic appeal, Cryptocoryne wendtii ‘Pink’ is a sought-after choice for aquarists looking to infuse a gentle burst of color into their aquatic landscapes.</p><p style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Plant Information:</strong></p><ul><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Scientific Name:</strong> Cryptocoryne wendtii ‘Pink’</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Family:</strong> Araceae</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Origin:</strong> Sri Lanka</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Difficulty Level:</strong> Easy</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Lighting Requirements:</strong> Low to Medium</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">CO2 Requirement:</strong> Low to Medium</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Temperature Range:</strong> 72-82°F (22-28°C)</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">pH Range:</strong> 6.0-7.5</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Propagation:</strong> Runner, division</li></ul>', '', 'published', '[\"cryptocoryne-wendetii-pink-growow-tc-plant-min-600x600.jpg\"]', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, 0, 0, 300, 250, NULL, NULL, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0, 1, '2024-09-10 13:14:26', '2024-10-05 16:52:01', 'in_stock', 3, 'Botble\\ACL\\Models\\User', 'cryptocoryne-wendetii-pink-growow-tc-plant-min-600x600.jpg', 'physical', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 0),
(180, 'Cryptocoryne Wendetii Tropica', '<p style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\">This low growing plant can be used as foreground or midground plant. Grows fast and bushy.</p><p style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Plant Difficulty</strong> : Easy</p><p style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Light Requirement</strong> : Medium</p><p style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Plant Type</strong> : Rhizome</p>', '', 'published', '[\"cryptocoryne-wendetii-tropica-min.jpg\"]', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, 0, 0, 140, 110, NULL, NULL, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0, 1, '2024-09-10 13:15:26', '2024-10-03 15:02:23', 'in_stock', 3, 'Botble\\ACL\\Models\\User', 'cryptocoryne-wendetii-tropica-min.jpg', 'physical', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 0),
(181, 'Cyeprus helferi', '<p style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\">Requires CO2, adequate fertilization and nutrient rich substrate. Does well in slightly cooler temperature.</p><p style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Plant Difficulty</strong> : Medium</p><p style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Light Requirement</strong> : Very Bright</p><p style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Plant Type</strong> :  Rhizome</p>', '', 'published', '[\"cyeprus-helferimin.jpg\"]', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, 0, 0, 140, 110, NULL, NULL, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0, 1, '2024-09-10 13:16:28', '2024-10-03 15:17:27', 'in_stock', 3, 'Botble\\ACL\\Models\\User', 'cyeprus-helferimin.jpg', 'physical', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 0),
(182, 'Didipilis Diandra', '<p style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\">Common Name: Peplis Diandra</p><p style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\">Didiplis diandra is a stem plant which can be found growing in lakes and streams throughout the states. Its a beautiful addition to an aquarium thanks to the thin, needle like leaves that can exhibit bright red tips when grown under high light with fertilization and CO2. In order to achieve the desired bushy effect, this plant is best  grown in groups or bunches.</p><p style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\">Propagation is simple and straightforward like other stem plants. Simply cut anywhere along the stem and replant the cuttings.  In order to keep this plant low growing and spread laterally runners, trim frequently and grow it under high light.</p><p style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\">Family Name: Lythraceae</p><p style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\">Origin: USA</p><p style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\">Height: 4-12”</p><p style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\">pH: 6.0-7.5</p><p style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\">Care: Easy</p><p style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\">Light: Moderate to High</p><p style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\">Co2: Not necessary</p><p style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\">Propagation: Cuttings</p><p style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\">Growth rate: Slow</p>', '', 'published', '[\"didipilis-diandra-min.jpg\"]', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, 0, 0, 140, 110, NULL, NULL, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0, 2, '2024-09-10 13:17:33', '2024-10-03 15:19:12', 'in_stock', 3, 'Botble\\ACL\\Models\\User', 'didipilis-diandra-min.jpg', 'physical', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 0),
(183, 'Drosera Spatulata Growow Tc Plant', '<p style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\">Drosera spatulata, also known as the Spoon-leaved Sundew, is a carnivorous plant that is native to Southeast Asia and Australia. It is a small, herbaceous perennial that grows in a rosette shape and produces long, thin stems with small, spoon-shaped leaves.</p><p style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\">Like all sundews, Drosera spatulata captures its prey by using sticky hairs on its leaves that trap insects. When an insect lands on the leaf, the hairs bend inward, bringing the insect closer to the center of the leaf, where it becomes stuck in the sticky secretion. The leaf then curls around the insect, enclosing it in a sticky prison, and the plant secretes digestive enzymes to break down the insect and extract its nutrients.</p><p style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\">Drosera spatulata is relatively easy to care for and is a popular choice for home gardeners who want to try growing carnivorous plants. It prefers bright, indirect light and well-draining soil that is kept consistently moist. The plant also requires high humidity levels, which can be achieved by placing the pot on a tray of pebbles filled with water. In terms of feeding, Drosera spatulata can be fed small insects, such as fruit flies or gnats, once or twice a month, but it can survive without being fed if it is placed in a location where it can catch insects on its own.</p><p style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Care Tips</strong></p><ul><li>Light: Drosera spatulata prefers bright, indirect light. A sunny windowsill or a grow light that provides 12-14 hours of light per day is ideal.</li><li>Soil: Drosera spatulata prefers a soilless growing medium that is made up of peat moss, perlite, and sand. The soil should be kept consistently moist but not waterlogged.</li><li>Water: Water Drosera spatulata with distilled or rainwater. Avoid using tap water, which can contain minerals and other chemicals that are harmful to carnivorous plants. Water the plant from the bottom by placing the pot in a tray of water and allowing the soil to soak up the water from the bottom</li></ul>', '', 'published', '[\"drosera-spatulata-min.jpeg\"]', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, 0, 0, 300, 250, NULL, NULL, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0, 26, '2024-09-10 13:18:39', '2024-10-05 16:52:29', 'in_stock', 3, 'Botble\\ACL\\Models\\User', 'drosera-spatulata-min.jpeg', 'physical', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 0),
(184, 'Echindorus Argentenesis', '<p>Description: Echinodorus Argentinensis, commonly known as the Argentine Sword Plant, is a charming and graceful aquatic species appreciated for its decorative presence in freshwater aquariums. As a member of the Echinodorus genus within the Alismataceae family, this plant is native to South America. Echinodorus Argentinensis is recognized for its broad, lanceolate leaves that form an attractive rosette. With its versatile nature and striking appearance, it is often used by aquarists to create lush and visually appealing aquascapes.</p>', '', 'published', '[\"echindorus-argentenesis-min.jpg\"]', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, 0, 0, 140, 110, NULL, NULL, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0, 3, '2024-09-10 13:19:54', '2024-10-03 15:20:08', 'in_stock', 3, 'Botble\\ACL\\Models\\User', 'echindorus-argentenesis-min.jpg', 'physical', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 0),
(185, 'Echindorus Fancy Curl', '<p><strong style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255);color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:bolder;word-spacing:0px;\">Description:</strong><span style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255);color:rgb(105,105,105);font-size:16px;\"><span> Echinodorus ‘Fancy Curl’ is an enchanting and distinctive variant of the Sword Plant, appreciated for its unique and ornate leaf structure. As a member of the Echinodorus genus within the Alismataceae family, this aquatic plant is known for its lush and decorative appearance. ‘Fancy Curl’ stands out with its leaves that exhibit an elegant curling pattern, adding a touch of sophistication to freshwater aquariums. Its vibrant green color and captivating form make it a sought-after choice for aquarists aiming to introduce a visually appealing centerpiece to their aquatic landscapes. </span> </span></p>', '', 'published', '[\"echindorus-fancy-curl-min.jpg\"]', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, 0, 0, 140, 110, NULL, NULL, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0, 3, '2024-09-10 13:20:58', '2024-10-03 15:20:44', 'in_stock', 3, 'Botble\\ACL\\Models\\User', 'echindorus-fancy-curl-min.jpg', 'physical', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 0),
(186, 'Echindorus Marble queen yelow', '<p><strong style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255);color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:bolder;word-spacing:0px;\">Description:</strong><span style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255);color:rgb(105,105,105);font-size:16px;\"><span> Echinodorus Cordifolius “Marble Queen Yellow” is a captivating aquatic plant celebrated for its vibrant yellow variegation and graceful presence. As a member of the Echinodorus genus within the Alismataceae family, this plant hails from South America. The “Marble Queen Yellow” variety is distinguished by its heart-shaped leaves adorned with striking patterns of yellow and green. With its unique coloration and elegant form, it serves as a focal point, adding warmth and visual appeal to freshwater aquariums. Aquarists appreciate its adaptability and ability to thrive in various tank conditions. </span>  </span></p>', '', 'published', '[\"echindorus-marble-queen-yelow-min.jpg\"]', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, 0, 0, 140, 110, NULL, NULL, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0, 3, '2024-09-10 13:22:03', '2024-10-03 15:22:02', 'in_stock', 3, 'Botble\\ACL\\Models\\User', 'echindorus-marble-queen-yelow-min.jpg', 'physical', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 0),
(187, 'Echindorus Ozelot', '<p style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Description:</strong> Echinodorus sp. “Ozelot,” commonly known as Ozelot Sword, is a visually striking aquatic plant celebrated for its unique leopard-like spotted pattern on its leaves. As a member of the Echinodorus genus within the Alismataceae family, this plant adds a touch of the exotic to freshwater aquariums. The distinctive red and green markings on its leaves make it a captivating choice for aquarists looking to introduce a bold and eye-catching element to their aquascapes.</p><p style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Plant Information:</strong></p><ul><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Scientific Name:</strong> Echinodorus sp. “Ozelot”</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Family:</strong> Alismataceae</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Origin:</strong> Cultivar (exact origin may vary)</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Difficulty Level:</strong> Easy to Moderate</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Lighting Requirements:</strong> Moderate to High</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">CO2 Requirement:</strong> Low to Medium</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Temperature Range:</strong> 72-82°F (22-28°C)</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">pH Range:</strong> 6.0-7.5</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Propagation:</strong> Adventitious plantlets, division</li></ul>', '', 'published', '[\"echindorus-ozelot-min-600x600.jpg\"]', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, 0, 0, 140, 110, NULL, NULL, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0, 5, '2024-09-10 13:24:02', '2024-10-03 15:23:03', 'in_stock', 3, 'Botble\\ACL\\Models\\User', 'echindorus-ozelot-min-600x600.jpg', 'physical', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 0),
(188, 'Echindorus Rose', '<p style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Description:</strong> Echinodorus Rose, often known as the Rose Sword, is an exquisite aquatic plant cherished for its unique rosette of pink and green-hued leaves. As a member of the Echinodorus genus within the Alismataceae family, this plant hails from South America. The Echinodorus Rose stands out with its captivating coloration, bringing a touch of elegance to freshwater aquariums. With its distinctive appearance and relatively undemanding care requirements, it serves as a beautiful centerpiece in aquascapes.</p><p style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Plant Information:</strong></p><ul><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Scientific Name:</strong> Echinodorus Rose</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Family:</strong> Alismataceae</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Origin:</strong> South America</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Difficulty Level:</strong> Easy</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Lighting Requirements:</strong> Low to Medium</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">CO2 Requirement:</strong> Low</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Temperature Range:</strong> 72-82°F (22-28°C)</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">pH Range:</strong> 6.0-7.5</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Propagation:</strong> Adventitious plantlets, division</li></ul>', '', 'published', '[\"echindorus-rose-min-300x300.png\"]', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, 0, 0, 140, 110, NULL, NULL, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0, 2, '2024-09-10 13:26:46', '2024-10-03 15:26:55', 'in_stock', 3, 'Botble\\ACL\\Models\\User', 'echindorus-rose-min-300x300.png', 'physical', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0