(193, 'Echinodorus Marble queen green', '<p style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Description:</strong> Echinodorus Cordifolius “Marble Queen Green,” often referred to as the Marble Queen Sword or Radican Marble Queen, is a striking aquatic plant known for its unique variegated leaves and graceful appearance. As a member of the Echinodorus genus within the Alismataceae family, this plant originates from South America. The “Marble Queen Green” variety is characterized by its heart-shaped leaves featuring marbled patterns of green and cream. With its distinctive foliage, it adds a touch of elegance and visual interest to freshwater aquariums, making it a favored choice among aquarists.</p><p style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Plant Information:</strong></p><ul><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Scientific Name:</strong> Echinodorus Cordifolius “Marble Queen Green”</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Family:</strong> Alismataceae</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Origin:</strong> South America</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Difficulty Level:</strong> Easy to Moderate</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Lighting Requirements:</strong> Low to Medium</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">CO2 Requirement:</strong> Low</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Temperature Range:</strong> 68-82°F (20-28°C)</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">pH Range:</strong> 6.0-7.5</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Propagation:</strong> Adventitious plantlets, division</li></ul>', '', 'published', '[\"echinodorus-marble-queen-green.jpg\"]', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, 0, 0, 140, 110, NULL, NULL, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0, 3, '2024-09-1