(272, 'Limnophila Sp Dwarf Growow Tc Plant', '<p style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Description:</strong> Limnophila Aquatica sp. “Dwarf” is a charming and diminutive aquatic plant that adds a touch of elegance to freshwater aquariums. Belonging to the Scrophulariaceae family, this “Dwarf” variant is a compact version of the traditional Limnophila Aquatica. Native to Southeast Asia, it is admired for its delicate, feathery leaves and adaptability to various aquarium setups. The petite size makes it an excellent choice for aquarists looking to create intricate aquascapes or foreground accents in planted tanks.</p><p style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\"> </p><p style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Plant Information:</strong></p><ul><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Scientific Name:</strong> Limnophila Aquatica sp. “Dwarf”</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Family:</strong> Scrophulariaceae</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Origin:</strong> Southeast Asia</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Difficulty Level:</strong> Easy to Moderate</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Lighting Requirements:</strong> Low to Medium</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">CO2 Requirement:</strong> Low</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Temperature Range:</strong> 68-82°F (20-28°C)</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">pH Range:</strong> 6.0-7.5</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Propagation:</strong> Cuttings</li></ul>', '', 'published', '[\"limnophila-sp-dwarf-min.jpg\"]', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, 0, 0, 300, 250, NULL, NULL, 0.00, 0.00, 