(299, 'Pogostemon Eructus Growow Tc Plant', '<p style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Description:</strong> Pogostemon Erectus is a captivating aquarium plant known for its upright and elegant growth pattern. Belonging to the Lamiaceae family, this species hails from Asia, particularly regions like India and Southeast Asia. Its striking appearance and ease of care make it a popular choice among aquarists who seek to add vertical interest and lush greenery to their aquatic environments. The plant’s slender stems, closely packed leaves, and vibrant green coloration contribute to its overall appeal.</p><p style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Plant Information:</strong></p><ul><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Scientific Name:</strong> Pogostemon Erectus</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Family:</strong> Lamiaceae</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Origin:</strong> Asia (India, Southeast Asia)</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Difficulty Level:</strong> Moderate</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Lighting Requirements:</strong> Medium to High</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">CO2 Requirement:</strong> Medium to High</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Temperature Range:</strong> 68-82°F (20-28°C)</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">pH Range:</strong> 6.0-7.5</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Propagation:</strong> Cuttings, Side Shoots</li></ul>', '', 'published', '[\"pogostemon-eructus-growow-tc-plant-min.jpg\"]', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, 0, 0, 300, 250, NULL, NULL, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0, 1, '2024-09-11 16:19:28', '2024-10-06 13:37:35', 'in_stock', 3, 'Botble\\ACL\\Models\\User', 'pogostemon-eructus-growow-tc-plant-min.jpg', 'physical', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 0),
(300, 'AQUATIC REMEDIES PARACIDOL-FW220ml', '<ul><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">A broad spectrum anti parasitic copper based remedy for fresh water fish, effective against external free- swimming parasites such as Lernea sp (anchor worm), argulus sp (Fish lice), Ichthyophthiruius multifillis (White spot / Ich), Gill flukes, Costia, cloudy eye and other disease causing external parasites.</strong></li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Paracidol FW successfully tested against koi sleeping syndrome and all other external parasites.</strong></li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">One Remedy For: Koi Sleeping Disease | White Spot (Itch) | Anchor Worm | Fish Lice | Gill Flukes | Costia Parasite | Arowana Parasites | Flower Horn Diseases | Discus Discoloration | Discus External Parasites | Gold Fish Parasites and other external parasites.</strong></li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Dosage: 5ml / 25 liter.</strong></li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Note: To be used in Freshwater systems only and not to be used with invertebrates and scaleless fish.</strong></li></ul>', '', 'published', '[\"addasubheading-29-600x600.png\"]', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 14, 0, 0, 420, 290, NULL, NULL, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0, 7, '2024-09-11 16:19:42', '2024-10-07 12:34:43', 'in_stock', 3, 'Botble\\ACL\\Models\\User', 'addasubheading-29-600x600.png', 'physical', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 0),
(301, 'Pogostemon helferi Growow Tc Plant', '<p style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\">Pogostemon helferi forms a dense carpet in the fore ground of the aquarium. It needs high light. Optimum temperature is 20-25’C. Growth is best in medium hard water with a neutral to alkaline Ph-value.</p><h2 style=\"font-family:\'Sans-serif\';font-style:normal;word-spacing:0px;\">Description</h2><p style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Genus: Pogostemon                                                                           Family: Lamiaceae</strong></p><p style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Pogostemon</strong> is a large genus from the family<strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\"> Lamiaceae</strong> and many of them can grow in submerged conditions. The are generally found in warmer parts of Asia. <strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">P. erectus</strong>, <strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">P. helferi</strong> and <strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">P. stellatus</strong> <strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">‘Dassen’</strong> are quite popular in the trade.</p><p style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\"> </strong></p><p style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Pogostemon helferi</strong></p><p style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\">Pogostemon helferi forms a dense carpet in the fore ground of the aquarium. It needs high light. Optimum temperature is 20-25’C. Growth is best in medium hard water with a neutral to alkaline Ph-value.</p>', '', 'published', '[\"pogostemon-helferi-min.jpg\"]', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, 0, 0, 300, 250, NULL, NULL, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0, 7, '2024-09-11 16:20:28', '2024-10-06 13:38:22', 'in_stock', 3, 'Botble\\ACL\\Models\\User', 'pogostemon-helferi-min.jpg', 'physical', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 0),
(302, 'Aquatic Remedies pH Reducer, 120ML', '<h2 style=\"font-family:\'Sans-serif\';font-style:normal;word-spacing:0px;\">About The Product</h2><div class=\"product__description rte\" style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\"><p><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Reduces and stabilizes the pH.</strong></p><p>pH Reduces is an advanced formula for the safe decrease of pH. Maintains pH low and stable for longer time.</p><p><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Why pH reducer?</strong></p><p>Most of the tropical fish from amazon habitat need low pH to survival and reproduction (for example: discus, tetra, angel fish and aquatic plants). pH Reducer can be used to reduce the pH for this type of fish.</p><p><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">INSTRUCTION:</strong></p><p>Mix required amount of pH Reducer in a cup of aquarium water and disperse evenly in the aquarium water. Do not increase the pH value more than 0.2 in a single dose. Use a pH test kit to monitor the correct level of pH.</p><h4 style=\"font-family:\'Sans-serif\';\">DOSAGE:</h4><p>10 ml / 50 liter</p></div>', '', 'published', '[\"untitled-design255-min.png\"]', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 14, 0, 0, 220, 155, NULL, NULL, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0, 7, '2024-09-11 16:20:59', '2024-10-07 12:35:12', 'in_stock', 3, 'Botble\\ACL\\Models\\User', 'untitled-design255-min.png', 'physical', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 0),
(303, 'Pogostemon helferi white Growow Tc Plant', '<p style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\">The pogostemon helferi is a compact distinctive foreground plant with unique ruffled leaves and texture. This plant is found in Thailand and is also called “Downoi”, which means little stars in Thai.  It can be used as a foreground or midground plant.</p><p style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\">This new variant has white color on the leaf edges.</p><p class=\"style1\" style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">INSTRUCTION:</strong></p><p class=\"style1\" style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\"> </p><ul><li>Type: Stem</li><li>Origin: Asia</li><li>Growth Rate: Medium</li><li>Height: 15-30+ cm</li><li>Light Demand: Medium</li><li>CO2: Medium</li></ul>', '', 'published', '[\"pogostemon-helferi-white-min-600x600.jpg\"]', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, 0, 0, 300, 250, NULL, NULL, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0, 6, '2024-09-11 16:22:03', '2024-10-06 13:38:46', 'in_stock', 3, 'Botble\\ACL\\Models\\User', 'pogostemon-helferi-white-min-600x600.jpg', 'physical', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 0),
(304, 'AQUATIC REMEDIES PHYTOCARB 250ML', '<p class=\"uppercase\" style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">AQUATIC REMEDIES PHYTO CARB CO2 PLUS</strong><br> </p><p style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\">AQUATIC REMEDIES Phyto CARB is a source of bioavailable organic carbon. All plants require a source of carbon. This is typically obtained from CO2, but, may also be derived from simple organic compounds.</p><p style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\">One can derive a substantial benefit with the use of Phyto CARB either alone or in conjunction with CO2. The combination is particularly ideal for situations when continuing to add CO2 could result in dangerously low pH levels.</p><p style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\">This <a style=\"background-color:transparent;text-decoration:none;\" href=\"https://www.aquariumsindia.com/product-category/plant-supplies/fertilisers/\">fertilisers</a> increases the efficiency of iron assimilation by plants.<br>Can be used for algae problems also.</p><p style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\">Use in with combination with <strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Plant Food</strong> + <strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Plant Health Formula</strong> and <strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">K++</strong> for best result and optimum plant growth.</p><p style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Dosing:</strong><br>3ml per 100 litre daily or every alternate day.</p>', '', 'published', '[\"aquatic-remedies-phytocarb.png\"]', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 14, 0, 0, 520, 400, NULL, NULL, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0, 11, '2024-09-11 16:22:10', '2024-10-07 12:43:26', 'in_stock', 3, 'Botble\\ACL\\Models\\User', 'aquatic-remedies-phytocarb.png', 'physical', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 0),
(305, 'Pogostemon Octopus', '<p style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Description:</strong> Pogostemon Stellatus “Octopus” is a captivating aquatic plant known for its distinctive and unusual leaf structure. Belonging to the Lamiaceae family, this species is native to Asia, particularly regions like India and Southeast Asia. The name “Octopus” is derived from the plant’s elongated and curled leaves, resembling the tentacles of an octopus. With its striking appearance, Pogostemon Stellatus “Octopus” is a popular choice among aquarists looking to add a touch of uniqueness to their planted aquariums.</p><p style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Plant Information:</strong></p><ul><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Scientific Name:</strong> Pogostemon Stellatus “Octopus”</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Family:</strong> Lamiaceae</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Origin:</strong> Asia (India, Southeast Asia)</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Difficulty Level:</strong> Moderate to Advanced</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Lighting Requirements:</strong> Medium to High</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">CO2 Requirement:</strong> Medium to High</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Temperature Range:</strong> 68-82°F (20-28°C)</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">pH Range:</strong> 6.0-7.5</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Propagation:</strong> Cuttings, Side Shoots</li></ul>', '', 'published', '[\"pogostemon-octopus-min-600x600.jpg\"]', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, 0, 0, 140, 110, NULL, NULL, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0, 5, '2024-09-11 16:23:01', '2024-10-04 18:19:48', 'in_stock', 3, 'Botble\\ACL\\Models\\User', 'pogostemon-octopus-min-600x600.jpg', 'physical', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 0),
(306, 'Aquatic Remedies Stress Heal Water Conditioner, 200 ml', '<p><span style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255);color:rgb(105,105,105);font-size:16px;\"><span class=\"a-list-item\">Wound healer, stress remover, transport aid, slime coat, ammonia controller, chlorine remover, water conditioner;Dosage – 10 ml / 100 litre;Quickly removes chlorine in tap water and binds toxic compounds, reduces ammonia toxicity in water, rapidly reduces stress and mortality;An active ingredient, aloe vera acts as natural wound healer and greater immune stimulant, reduces fish stress</span><span>.</span></span></p>', NULL, 'published', '[\"untitled-design253-min-1.png\"]', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 550, 390, NULL, NULL, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0, 3, '2024-09-11 16:23:14', '2024-09-11 16:23:14', 'in_stock', 3, 'Botble\\ACL\\Models\\User', NULL, 'physical', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, 0, 0),
(307, 'Pogostemon Stellatus Dassen', '<p style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Description:</strong> Pogostemon Stellatus “Dassen” is a distinctive variation of the well-known Pogostemon Stellatus, prized for its unique leaf structure and graceful appearance. Belonging to the Lamiaceae family, this aquatic plant is native to Asia, with origins in regions such as India and Southeast Asia. Characterized by its slender stems and finely textured leaves, Pogostemon Stellatus “Dassen” adds an element of elegance and visual interest to freshwater aquariums.</p><p style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Plant Information:</strong></p><ul><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Scientific Name:</strong> Pogostemon Stellatus “Dassen”</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Family:</strong> Lamiaceae</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Origin:</strong> Asia (India, Southeast Asia)</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Difficulty Level:</strong> Moderate to Advanced</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Lighting Requirements:</strong> Medium to High</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">CO2 Requirement:</strong> Medium to High</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Temperature Range:</strong> 68-82°F (20-28°C)</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">pH Range:</strong> 6.0-7.5</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Propagation:</strong> Cuttings, Side Shoots</li></ul>', '', 'published', '[\"pogostemon-stellatus-dassen-min-600x600.jpg\"]', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, 0, 0, 140, 110, NULL, NULL, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0, 0, '2024-09-11 16:24:03', '2024-10-04 18:20:44', 'in_stock', 3, 'Botble\\ACL\\Models\\User', 'pogostemon-stellatus-dassen-min-600x600.jpg', 'physical', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 0),
(308, 'Pogostemon Stellatus dassen Growow Tc Plant', '<p style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Description:</strong> Pogostemon Stellatus “Dassen” is a distinctive variation of the well-known Pogostemon Stellatus, prized for its unique leaf structure and graceful appearance. Belonging to the Lamiaceae family, this aquatic plant is native to Asia, with origins in regions such as India and Southeast Asia. Characterized by its slender stems and finely textured leaves, Pogostemon Stellatus “Dassen” adds an element of elegance and visual interest to freshwater aquariums.</p><p style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Plant Information:</strong></p><ul><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Scientific Name:</strong> Pogostemon Stellatus “Dassen”</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Family:</strong> Lamiaceae</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Origin:</strong> Asia (India, Southeast Asia)</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Difficulty Level:</strong> Moderate to Advanced</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Lighting Requirements:</strong> Medium to High</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">CO2 Requirement:</strong> Medium to High</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Temperature Range:</strong> 68-82°F (20-28°C)</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">pH Range:</strong> 6.0-7.5</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Propagation:</strong> Cuttings, Side Shoots</li></ul>', '', 'published', '[\"pogostemon-stellatus-dassen-min.jpg\"]', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, 0, 0, 300, 110, NULL, NULL, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0, 4, '2024-09-11 16:24:54', '2024-10-06 13:39:09', 'in_stock', 3, 'Botble\\ACL\\Models\\User', 'pogostemon-stellatus-dassen-min.jpg', 'physical', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 0),
(309, 'Proserpinaca palustris Growow Tc Plant', '<p style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Description:</strong> Proserpinaca Palustris, commonly known as Mermaid Weed, is an aquatic plant cherished for its delicate and whorled foliage, adding a touch of elegance to freshwater aquariums. Belonging to the watermilfoil family (Haloragaceae), this species is characterized by its intricately arranged leaves that resemble a graceful underwater dance. The plant’s vibrant green coloration and unique leaf structure make it a captivating choice for aquascaping enthusiasts seeking to create visually appealing aquatic landscapes.</p><p style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Plant Information:</strong></p><ul><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Scientific Name:</strong> Proserpinaca Palustris</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Family:</strong> Haloragaceae</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Origin:</strong> North America</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Difficulty Level:</strong> Moderate</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Lighting Requirements:</strong> Medium to High</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">CO2 Requirement:</strong> Low to Medium</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Temperature Range:</strong> 68-82°F (20-28°C)</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">pH Range:</strong> 6.5-7.5</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Propagation:</strong> Stem Cuttings</li></ul>', '', 'published', '[\"proserpinaca-palustris-min.jpg\"]', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, 0, 0, 300, 250, NULL, NULL, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0, 2, '2024-09-11 16:25:54', '2024-10-06 13:39:33', 'in_stock', 3, 'Botble\\ACL\\Models\\User', 'proserpinaca-palustris-min.jpg', 'physical', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 0),
(310, 'Aquatic Remedies Water Conditioner Blackwater Concentrate 120ml', '<ul><li>Prepared from natural year old extracts of foliage and peat</li><li>Contains natural rain forest essence and minerals</li><li>Stimulates fish spawning.<b style=\"font-weight:bolder;\"><strong>AQUATIC REMEDIES Blackwater Concentrate</strong></b></li></ul><p>AQUATIC REMEDIES Blackwater Concentrate creates natural rainforest water</p><ul><li>Black water concentrate prepared from natural year old extracts of foliage and peat.</li><li>This <a style=\"background-color:transparent;text-decoration:none;\" href=\"https://www.aquariumsindia.com/product-category/water-conditioners/shrimp-tank-water-conditioners/\">shrimp conditioners</a> contains organic acids, plant hormones, minerals and natural rain forest essence.</li><li>It creates natural environment which stimulates fish spawning and feel like its natural biotope.</li><li>This product is best choice for Discus, Angelfish, Tetra, Killifish, Rainbow fish, Shrimps and etc.</li></ul>', '', 'published', '[\"untitled-design254-min.png\"]', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 14, 0, 0, 320, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0, 5, '2024-09-11 16:28:09', '2024-10-07 12:44:27', 'in_stock', 3, 'Botble\\ACL\\Models\\User', 'untitled-design254-min.png', 'physical', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 0),
(311, 'AQUATIC VENTUREZ Algaecide | 120ml', '<p style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\">Removes and prevents algae growth.</p><p class=\"uppercase\" style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">AQUATIC VENTUREZ Algaecide</strong></p><p style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\">It effectively removes and prevents algae growth such as hair algae, beard algae, brown algae, blue-green algae, black brush algae and harmless to aquatic plant and fishes if used according to the directions. It is important to note that during application, the aquarium must be supplied with enough oxygen.</p><p style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">USAGE INSTRUCTIONS:</strong><br>2 ml daily for 10 litres for 7 days. Change 50% water next day and repeat the dose.<br><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Note:</strong> Not to be used with invertebrates.Cap-full is 6 ml.</p>', '', 'published', '[\"untitled-design285-min.png\"]', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 15, 0, 0, 250, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0, 6, '2024-09-11 16:39:57', '2024-10-07 12:58:45', 'in_stock', 3, 'Botble\\ACL\\Models\\User', 'untitled-design285-min.png', 'physical', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 0),
(312, 'Aquarium Products India Water Test Strips 6 in 1-60 tests', '<h2 style=\"font-family:\'Sans-serif\';font-style:normal;word-spacing:0px;\">Description</h2><ul><li class=\"a-unordered-list a-vertical a-spacing-mini\"><span class=\"a-list-item\">API Water Test Strips 6 in 1</span></li><li class=\"a-unordered-list a-vertical a-spacing-mini\"><span class=\"a-list-item\">Nitrate + Nitrite + Chlorine + GH + KH + pH</span></li><li class=\"a-unordered-list a-vertical a-spacing-mini\"><span class=\"a-list-item\">60 tests – Test Color Chart Inside</span></li><li class=\"a-unordered-list a-vertical a-spacing-mini\"><span class=\"a-list-item\">ONLY for Fresh Water</span></li><li class=\"a-unordered-list a-vertical a-spacing-mini\"><span class=\"a-list-item\">Must have test kit for daily use</span></li></ul>', '', 'published', '[\"untitled-design262-min.png\"]', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 290, 260, NULL, NULL, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0, 4, '2024-09-11 16:43:55', '2024-10-07 12:17:47', 'in_stock', 3, 'Botble\\ACL\\Models\\User', 'untitled-design262-min.png', 'physical', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 0),
(313, 'AQUATIC VENTUREZ Air Plant Mist | 120ml', '<h2 style=\"font-family:\'Sans-serif\';font-style:normal;word-spacing:0px;\">Description</h2><div class=\"large-2 col pb-0 mb-0\" style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\"><h5 class=\"uppercase mt\" style=\"font-family:\'Sans-serif\';\">Description</h5></div><div class=\"large-10 col pb-0 mb-0\" style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\"><div class=\"panel entry-content\"><p class=\"uppercase\"><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">AQUATIC VENTUREZ Air Plant Mist</strong><br> </p><p>Want your AIR PLANTS to grow faster? Feed your air plants with our air plant food! This fertilizer has been specially formulated to help your air plants thrive, and <strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">DOES NOT REPLACE</strong> regular waterings or proper air plant care.</p><p>Fertilizing your air plants, once a week, while giving them bright light and abundant water is the best way to encourage growth, color, blooms and blushing. It is also the best way to promote pups or new plant buds.</p><p><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">FEATURES</strong></p><ul><li>Innovative fertilizer for air plants &amp; succulents</li><li>Enhances growth, color &amp; blooms</li><li>Contains important nutrients</li></ul><p><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">USAGE</strong><br>Spray 1-2 times over the plant leaves adequately once a week according to plant size.</p></div></div>', '', 'published', '[\"aquatic-venturez-air-plant-mist-120ml-min.jpg\"]', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 15, 0, 0, 500, 450, NULL, NULL, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0, 2, '2024-09-11 16:47:21', '2024-10-07 12:57:14', 'in_stock', 3, 'Botble\\ACL\\Models\\User', 'aquatic-venturez-air-plant-mist-120ml-min.jpg', 'physical', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 0),
(314, 'AQUATIC VENTUREZ Extreme Tannins | 120ml', '<h2 style=\"font-family:\'Sans-serif\';font-style:normal;word-spacing:0px;\">Description</h2><div class=\"large-2 col pb-0 mb-0\" style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\"><h5 class=\"uppercase mt\" style=\"font-family:\'Sans-serif\';\">Description</h5></div><div class=\"large-10 col pb-0 mb-0\" style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\"><div class=\"panel entry-content\"><p class=\"uppercase\"><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">AQUATIC VENTUREZ Extreme Tannins</strong><br> </p><p>Contains essential black water extracts from peat, tropical roots, bark and wood originated from tropical rainforests which helps to stimulate the natural color, improves breeding and spawning rate. It also helps in creating slightly acidic water which effectively restores soft water environment found in the wild.</p><p><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">USAGE INSTRUCTIONS:</strong><br>2ml for 10 liters when setting up an aquarium, adding or changing water.<br>Cap-full is 6 ml.</p></div></div>', '', 'published', '[\"aquatic-venturez-extreme-tannins-120ml-min.jpg\"]', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 15, 0, 0, 300, 250, NULL, NULL, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0, 3, '2024-09-11 16:52:15', '2024-10-07 13:03:48', 'in_stock', 3, 'Botble\\ACL\\Models\\User', 'aquatic-venturez-extreme-tannins-120ml-min.jpg', 'physical', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 0),
(315, 'AQUATIC VENTUREZ Aqua Salt | 250g', '<p style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255);color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong class=\"uppercase\" style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">AQUATIC VENTUREZ Aqua Salt</strong></p><p style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255);color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\">This is 100% pure and organic Himalayan rock salt and is a must-have conditioner for freshwater aquariums. It promotes fish health by improving gill function, making it easier for fish to breathe. It also provides essential electrolytes that fish need to reach peak coloration and vitality. These electrolytes may be lost each time you perform a partial water change, and will need to be replenished.</p><p style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255);color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">USAGE INSTRUCTIONS:</strong></p><p style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255);color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\">Use when starting a new aquarium or any time you perform a water change. Care should be taken when using salt in aquariums with live plants, as some plants may be sensitive. It can also be use to hatch brine shrimp eggs.</p><p style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255);color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\">Dose 1 scoop for every 10 liters of water. Measuring scoop inside.</p><p style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255);color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">NOTE</strong></p><p style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255);color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\">This product contains 100% natural Himalayan Pink Salt in grinded form, and hence the salt color0 may vary from batch to batch without losing its effectiveness.</p><p style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255);color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">STORAGE &amp; CAUTION</strong></p><p style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255);color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\">Store in a cool, dry place and keep out of reach of children. Not for human consumption.</p>', '', 'published', '[\"aquatic-venturez-aqua-salt-250g-min.jpg\"]', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 15, 0, 0, 300, 250, NULL, NULL, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0, 5, '2024-09-11 16:52:19', '2024-10-07 12:59:23', 'in_stock', 3, 'Botble\\ACL\\Models\\User', 'aquatic-venturez-aqua-salt-250g-min.jpg', 'physical', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 0),
(316, 'Ranaculus inandatus Growow Tc Plant', '<p style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Description:</strong> Ranunculus Inundatus, commonly known as Water Crowfoot, is an aquatic plant renowned for its delicate and frilly foliage, adding a touch of elegance to freshwater aquariums. Belonging to the buttercup family (Ranunculaceae), this species is recognized for its finely dissected leaves that create a feathery and intricate appearance underwater. The plant’s bright green coloration and unique leaf structure make it a sought-after choice for aquascaping enthusiasts looking to introduce a graceful element to their aquatic landscapes.</p><p style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Plant Information:</strong></p><ul><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Scientific Name:</strong> Ranunculus Inundatus</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Family:</strong> Ranunculaceae</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Origin:</strong> Native to Australia and New Zealand</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Difficulty Level:</strong> Moderate to Difficult</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Lighting Requirements:</strong> Medium to High</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">CO2 Requirement:</strong> Medium to High</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Temperature Range:</strong> 59-77°F (15-25°C)</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">pH Range:</strong> 6.5-7.5</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Propagation:</strong> Runners, Division</li></ul>', '', 'published', '[\"ranaculus-inandatus-min-600x600.jpg\"]', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, 0, 0, 300, 250, NULL, NULL, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0, 8, '2024-09-11 16:52:28', '2024-10-06 13:40:06', 'in_stock', 3, 'Botble\\ACL\\Models\\User', 'ranaculus-inandatus-min-600x600.jpg', 'physical', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 0),
(317, 'AQUATIC VENTUREZ Betta Complete | 120ml', '<ul><li>Formulated for fighter fishes</li><li>Provides optimum water condition</li><li>Boost fish color, growth and health.</li></ul><div class=\"large-10 col pb-0 mb-0\"><div class=\"panel entry-content\"><p class=\"uppercase\"><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">AQUATIC VENTUREZ betta complete</strong><br> </p><p>This complete multi-purpose water conditioner instantly makes tap water safe for BETTA fish by removing Chlorine, Chloramines, and Heavy metals. In addition, it also contains STRESS relieving agents along with natural TANNINS and MINERALS which promotes activeness, healing, vigor and induce SPAWNING.</p><p><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">USAGE INSTRUCTIONS:</strong><br>2 ml per 1 litre when setting up an aquarium, adding or changing water.<br>Cap-full is 6 ml.</p></div></div>', '', 'published', '[\"untitled-design290-min.png\"]', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, 0, 0, 200, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0, 5, '2024-09-11 16:53:27', '2024-10-07 01:55:15', 'in_stock', 3, 'Botble\\ACL\\Models\\User', 'untitled-design290-min.png', 'physical', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 0),
(318, 'AQUATIC VENTUREZ One Fertilizer | 120ml', '<h2 style=\"font-family:\'Sans-serif\';font-style:normal;word-spacing:0px;\">Description</h2><div class=\"large-2 col pb-0 mb-0\" style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\"><h5 class=\"uppercase mt\" style=\"font-family:\'Sans-serif\';\">Description</h5></div><div class=\"large-10 col pb-0 mb-0\" style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\"><div class=\"panel entry-content\"><p class=\"uppercase\"><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">AQUATIC VENTUREZ ONE FERTILIZER</strong><br> </p><p>Fertilizer dosing is a complex topic within the aquarium hobby, but this <strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">ALL IN ONE</strong> fertilizer has been developed to make it simple for <strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">beginners</strong>. It contains all the essential nutrients &amp; traces your plants need to thrive and grow.<strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\"> Ideal for LOW to MEDIUM light aquariums</strong>. For optimum result, use it along with CARBO BOOST.</p><p><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">USAGE INSTRUCTIONS:</strong><br>1 ml daily for 50 litres LOW LIGHT planted aquarium.<br>2 ml daily for 50 litres MEDIUM LIGHT planted aquarium.<br>Avoid dosing on water changing day.<br>Cap-full is 6 ml.</p></div></div>', '', 'published', '[\"aquatic-venturez-one-fertilizer-120ml-min.jpg\"]', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 15, 0, 0, 350, 300, NULL, NULL, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0, 7, '2024-09-11 16:54:41', '2024-10-07 13:04:11', 'in_stock', 3, 'Botble\\ACL\\Models\\User', 'aquatic-venturez-one-fertilizer-120ml-min.jpg', 'physical', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 0),
(319, 'Riccia Fluitans Growow Tc Plant', '<p style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\">The crystalwort, Riccia fluitans, is known as a floating plant since the early days of the aquarium hobby. Especially Takashi Amano has inspired many aquarists to keep Riccia also submerged as a ground cover, tied with a line to stones. However certain types from the Riccia fluitans species group are more suitable for that than others. The form that is nowadays most commonly available does not easily float up to the surface and forms large cushions of long, thin thallus branches under water in a short time. Another form with similarly long but wider branches is sold by us as Riccia fluitans “Broad”.</p><p style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\">Submerged Riccia fluitans grows best with rather intense lighting, CO<sub style=\"font-size:12px;line-height:0;\">2</sub> addition and good nutrient supply via the water column. Under good conditions, oxygen bubbles will form on the branch tips. This liverwort can be tied with a line (e.g. ADA Riccia Line) to hardscape material such as stones (e.g. ADA Riccia Stone) or driftwood. Ceramic moss pads with stainless steel grid are another easy way to lay a Riccia lawn. Every snippet will sprout. The crystalwort often settles between other ground-covering plants and mosses. The Riccia cushions need to be trimmed with scissors from time to time.</p><p style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\">A light green Riccia lawn full of silvery oxygen bubbles gives a spectacular sight in the aquarium. Used as a floating plant, Riccia fluitans also provides a great protection for fish fry.</p><p style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\">Riccia fluitans aka crystalwort is a floating plant found in all the world. It was scientifically described and catalogised as early as 1753 by Linnaeus, however, Takashi Amano from Japan was the first to keep it submersed in his nature aquaria, using it as an epiphyte by tying it to wood and rocks with a thin fishing line. Thus, Riccia became one of the most favourite plants of plant aquaristis. Meanwhile it has found its way into most plant dealers’ product catalogues. There are four different varieties (originating from Japan, Europe, Thailand and Singapore), however, only the variety from Japan is suitable for submersed cultivation.</p>', '', 'published', '[\"riccia-fluitans-min.jpg\"]', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, 0, 0, 300, 250, NULL, NULL, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0, 17, '2024-09-11 16:56:21', '2024-10-06 13:40:35', 'in_stock', 3, 'Botble\\ACL\\Models\\User', 'riccia-fluitans-min.jpg', 'physical', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 0),
(320, 'AQUATIC VENTUREZ Root Sticks', '<h2 style=\"font-family:\'Sans-serif\';font-style:normal;word-spacing:0px;\">Description</h2><div class=\"product-short-description\" style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\"><p class=\"uppercase\"><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Aquarium plant fertilizer</strong><br> </p><div><ul><li>Supply key nutrients</li><li>Help plants grow and keep flourishing</li><li>Can be used in conjunction with liquid fertilizer.</li></ul><div> </div><div class=\"large-10 col pb-0 mb-0\"><div class=\"panel entry-content\"><p class=\"uppercase\"><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">AQUATIC VENTUREZ Root Sticks</strong><br> </p><p>This nutrient rich Root Sticks promotes lush growth of aquatic plants with ingredients such as iron, potassium, and other nutrients that help develop strong roots.</p><p>These sticks are safe for use with tropical fish and can be used in conjunction with any liquid fertilizer for optimal aquatic plant growth. The nutrients within the sticks are consumed over the time in the aquarium and is replenished every 2 months.</p><p><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">USAGE INSTRUCTIONS:</strong><br>Insert 1 stick for every 4 square inches of substrate.<br>Push midway into substrate with the help of plant tweezer.</p></div></div></div></div>', '', 'published', '[\"untitled-design280-min.png\"]', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 15, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0, 9, '2024-09-11 16:56:36', '2024-10-07 13:06:07', 'in_stock', 3, 'Botble\\ACL\\Models\\User', 'untitled-design280-min.png', 'physical', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 0),
(321, 'AQUATIC VENTUREZ Terrarium Fertz | 120ml', '<p class=\"uppercase\" style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255);color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">AQUATIC VENTUREZ Terrarium Fertz</strong><br> </p><p style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255);color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\">This easy to use complete Terrarium Fertilizers has been specially developed for new-age TERRA-SCAPERS which contains all the essential and required nutrients for optimum plant growth and color.</p><p style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255);color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">FEATURES</strong></p><ul><li>Innovative fertilizer for vivariums &amp; terrariums</li><li>Contains important nutrients</li><li>Enhances leaves color</li></ul><p style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255);color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">USAGE</strong><br>3-5 sprays according to plant volume/density on 15 x 15 cm plant area daily.</p>', '', 'published', '[\"aquatic-venturez-terrarium-fertz-120ml-min.jpg\"]', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 15, 0, 0, 500, 450, NULL, NULL, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0, 5, '2024-09-11 16:59:07', '2024-10-07 13:07:35', 'in_stock', 3, 'Botble\\ACL\\Models\\User', 'aquatic-venturez-terrarium-fertz-120ml-min.jpg', 'physical', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 0),
(322, 'AQUATIC VENTUREZ Dewormer | 120ml', '<p class=\"uppercase\" style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255);color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Aquarium FISH MEDICINE</strong><br> </p><div style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255);color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\"><ul><li>Outstanding deworming formula</li><li>Cures and clears Gastro Intestinal Worms</li><li>Effective in treating white-poop</li></ul><div class=\"large-10 col pb-0 mb-0\"><div class=\"panel entry-content\"><p class=\"uppercase\"><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">AQUATIC VENTUREZ dewormer</strong><br> </p><p>This outstanding deworming formula effectively cures and clears Gastro Intestinal Worms in fish’s stomach and liver, such as Tape Worm, Flat Worm, Nematode, Threadworms etc.</p><p>It is also effective in treating white-poop of FlowerHorn, Discus and other fishes.</p><p><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">USAGE INSTRUCTIONS:</strong><br><i>Option 1 (Recommended)</i> – Soak 1 table-spoon of dried feed into 2 ml of this solution for 1 minutes and feed your fish for 3-5 days. Cap-full is 6 ml.<br><i>Option 2</i> – Can also be used directly in aquarium as water application, use 2 ml per 10 litres for 7 days.<br>Cap-full is 6 ml.</p></div></div></div>', '', 'published', '[\"untitled-design284-min.png\"]', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 15, 0, 0, 200, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0, 5, '2024-09-11 17:30:10', '2024-10-07 13:02:52', 'in_stock', 3, 'Botble\\ACL\\Models\\User', 'untitled-design284-min.png', 'physical', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 0),
(323, 'AQUATIC VENTUREZ Extreme Tannins | 120ml', '<p class=\"uppercase\" style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255);color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">AQUATIC VENTUREZ Extreme Tannins</strong><br> </p><p style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255);color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\">Contains essential black water extracts from peat, tropical roots, bark and wood originated from tropical rainforests which helps to stimulate the natural color, improves breeding and spawning rate. It also helps in creating slightly acidic water which effectively restores soft water environment found in the wild.</p><p style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255);color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">USAGE INSTRUCTIONS:</strong><br>2ml for 10 liters when setting up an aquarium, adding or changing water.<br>Cap-full is 6 ml.</p>', '', 'published', '[\"aquatic-venturez-extreme-tannins-120ml-min-1.jpg\"]', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 15, 0, 0, 300, 250, NULL, NULL, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0, 6, '2024-09-11 17:31:47', '2024-10-07 13:03:14', 'in_stock', 3, 'Botble\\ACL\\Models\\User', 'aquatic-venturez-extreme-tannins-120ml-min-1.jpg', 'physical', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 0),
(324, 'AQUATIC VENTUREZ pH Test', '<ul><li>Easy to use</li><li>Accurate and quick results</li><li>Performs 40 tests</li></ul><div class=\"large-10 col pb-0 mb-0\"><div class=\"panel entry-content\"><p class=\"uppercase\"><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">AQUATIC VENTUREZ pH Test</strong></p><p>This pH Test Kit offers a simple to use, reliable reading for testing your aquarium water pH levels. Each kit enables 40 tests to be completed.</p><p><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Usage Instructions:</strong></p><ol><li>Add 3ml of tank water in the test tube (given inside).</li><li>Add 2 drops of indicator solution in the test tube and mix well.</li><li>Match the color with the given color chart to interpret the result for taking further action.</li></ol></div></div>', '', 'published', '[\"untitled-design279-min1.png\"]', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 15, 0, 0, 200, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0, 5, '2024-09-11 17:34:25', '2024-10-07 13:04:50', 'in_stock', 3, 'Botble\\ACL\\Models\\User', 'untitled-design279-min1.png', 'physical', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 0),
(325, 'AQUATIC VENTUREZ Planaria Killer | 120ml', '<p style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\">Effectively kills PLANARIA.</p><div class=\"large-10 col pb-0 mb-0\" style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\"><div class=\"panel entry-content\"><p class=\"uppercase\"><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">AQUATIC VENTUREZ Planaria Killer</strong></p><p>This outstanding formula effectively kills PLANARIA in shrimp aquarium without harming shrimps and shrimplets.</p><p><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">USAGE INSTRUCTIONS:</strong><br>Day 1: Use 2 ml for 10 litres.<br>Day 2 to 5: Perform 25% water change and dose again.<br>Cap-full is 6 ml.</p><p><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Note:</strong> Stop dosing when there are no visible planaria and perform water change.</p></div></div>', '', 'published', '[\"untitled-design289-min.png\"]', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 15, 0, 0, 250, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0, 3, '2024-09-11 17:51:50', '2024-10-07 13:05:36', 'in_stock', 3, 'Botble\\ACL\\Models\\User', 'untitled-design289-min.png', 'physical', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 0);
