(347, 'Rotala Sp. Mini Gold', '<p style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Description:</strong> Rotala sp. Mini “Gold” is a captivating aquatic plant prized for its unique golden-yellow coloration and intricate, compact growth pattern. Hailing from the Lythraceae family, this miniature Rotala variant is a sought-after choice for aquascaping due to its ability to add a touch of warmth and brilliance to freshwater aquariums. Its delicate foliage and bushy structure make it a standout feature in planted tanks.</p><p style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Plant Information:</strong></p><ul><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Scientific Name:</strong> Rotala sp. Mini “Gold”</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Family:</strong> Lythraceae</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Origin:</strong> Cultivated variant, likely from Southeast Asia</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Difficulty Level:</strong> Moderate</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Lighting Requirements:</strong> Medium to High</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">CO2 Requirement:</strong> Medium to High</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Temperature Range:</strong> 68-82°F (20-28°C)</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">pH Range:</strong> 6.0-7.5</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Propagation:</strong> Cuttings</li></ul>', '', 'published', '[\"rotala-sp-mini-gold-min.jpg\"]', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, 0, 0, 140, 110, NULL, NULL, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0, 7, '2024-09-11 18:15:35', '2024-10-04 18:39:00', 'in_stock', 3, 'Botble\\ACL\\Models\\User', 'rotala-sp-mini-gold-min.jpg', 'physical', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 0),
(348, 'Rotala Spikey', '<p style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Description:</strong> Rotala sp. Spikey is an elegant aquatic plant known for its distinct appearance and delicate, feathery foliage. Belonging to the Lythraceae family, this Rotala variant is appreciated by aquarium enthusiasts for its fine, needle-like leaves and its ability to add a graceful touch to freshwater setups. The plant’s unique structure and vibrant green coloration make it a sought-after choice for aquascaping, providing an eye-catching element in planted tanks.</p><p style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Plant Information:</strong></p><ul><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Scientific Name:</strong> Rotala sp. Spikey</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Family:</strong> Lythraceae</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Origin:</strong> Cultivated variant, likely from Southeast Asia</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Difficulty Level:</strong> Moderate</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Lighting Requirements:</strong> Medium to High</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">CO2 Requirement:</strong> Medium to High</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Temperature Range:</strong> 68-82°F (20-28°C)</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">pH Range:</strong> 6.0-7.5</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Propagation:</strong> Cuttings</li></ul>', '', 'published', '[\"rotala-spikey-min.jpg\"]', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, 0, 0, 140, 110, NULL, NULL, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0, 8, '2024-09-11 18:19:15', '2024-10-04 18:39:17', 'in_stock', 3, 'Botble\\ACL\\Models\\User', 'rotala-spikey-min.jpg', 'physical', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 0),
(349, 'Rotala Twilight', '<p style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Description:</strong> Rotala Rotundifolia ‘Twilight’ is a captivating aquatic plant known for its unique coloration that transitions from vibrant green to shades of pink and orange. This stunning gradient effect adds a touch of serenity and elegance to freshwater aquariums, making it a popular choice among aquascaping enthusiasts. ‘Twilight’ combines beauty with ease of care, making it suitable for both beginners and experienced aquarists looking to create a visually striking underwater landscape.</p><p style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Plant Information:</strong></p><ul><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Scientific Name:</strong> Rotala Rotundifolia ‘Twilight’</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Family:</strong> Lythraceae</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Origin:</strong> Cultivated variant, likely from Southeast Asia</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Difficulty Level:</strong> Easy to Moderate</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Lighting Requirements:</strong> Low to Medium</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">CO2 Requirement:</strong> Low to Medium</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Temperature Range:</strong> 68-82°F (20-28°C)</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">pH Range:</strong> 6.0-7.5</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Propagation:</strong> Cuttings</li></ul>', '', 'published', '[\"rotala-twilight-min-600x600.jpg\"]', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, 0, 0, 140, 110, NULL, NULL, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0, 10, '2024-09-11 18:20:10', '2024-10-04 18:39:50', 'in_stock', 3, 'Botble\\ACL\\Models\\User', 'rotala-twilight-min-600x600.jpg', 'physical', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 0),
(350, 'Rotala Wallichi Red', '<p style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\">aquatic plant known for its delicate appearance and vibrant coloration. This species belongs to the Lythraceae family and is native to Southeast Asia. With its fine, feathery leaves arranged in whorls along the stem, Rotala Wallichii adds a touch of elegance to freshwater aquariums. The plant’s hues can range from green to pinkish-red, depending on the tank conditions.</p><p style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Plant Information:</strong></p><ul><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Scientific Name:</strong> Rotala Wallichii</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Family:</strong> Lythraceae</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Origin:</strong> Southeast Asia</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Difficulty Level:</strong> Moderate to High</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Lighting Requirements:</strong> High</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">CO2 Requirement:</strong> High</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Temperature Range:</strong> 72-82°F (22-28°C)</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">pH Range:</strong> 5.5-7.5</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Propagation:</strong> Cuttings</li></ul>', '', 'published', '[\"rotala-wallichi-red-min-600x600.jpg\"]', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, 0, 0, 140, 110, NULL, NULL, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0, 9, '2024-09-11 18:21:22', '2024-10-04 18:40:12', 'in_stock', 3, 'Botble\\ACL\\Models\\User', 'rotala-wallichi-red-min-600x600.jpg', 'physical', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 0),
(351, 'Sturogyne Porto Velho', '<p style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Description:</strong> Staurogyne sp. Porto Velho is an aquatic plant renowned for its vibrant and distinctive foliage, making it a sought-after choice for aquascaping enthusiasts. Belonging to the Acanthaceae family, this species adds a touch of elegance to freshwater aquariums with its unique leaf structure and eye-catching coloration. Originating from the freshwater habitats of Porto Velho in Brazil, this plant has gained popularity for its ornamental qualities and suitability for planted tank setups.</p><p style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Plant Information:</strong></p><ul><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Scientific Name:</strong> Staurogyne sp. Porto Velho</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Common Name:</strong> Porto Velho Staurogyne</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Origin:</strong> Freshwater habitats of Porto Velho, Brazil</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Difficulty Level:</strong> Moderate</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Lighting Requirements:</strong> Moderate to High</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">CO2 Requirement:</strong> Moderate</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Temperature Range:</strong> 68-82°F (20-28°C)</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">pH Range:</strong> 6.0-7.5</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Propagation:</strong> Cuttings, side shoots</li></ul>', '', 'published', '[\"sturogyne-porto-velho-min.jpg\"]', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, 0, 0, 140, 110, NULL, NULL, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0, 8, '2024-09-11 18:22:14', '2024-10-04 18:40:52', 'in_stock', 3, 'Botble\\ACL\\Models\\User', 'sturogyne-porto-velho-min.jpg', 'physical', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 0),
(352, 'Tonina belem', '<p style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Description:</strong> Tonina sp. Belem, a diminutive yet captivating aquatic plant, is celebrated for its delicate appearance and vibrant green coloration. Hailing from the Eriocaulaceae family, this species is cherished by aquascapers for its intricate structure and ability to add finesse to the foreground of freshwater aquariums. Despite its small size, Tonina sp. Belem commands attention with its graceful presence.</p><p style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Plant Information:</strong></p><ul><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Scientific Name:</strong> Tonina sp. Belem</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Common Name:</strong> Belem Tonina</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Origin:</strong> South America</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Difficulty Level:</strong> Advanced</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Lighting Requirements:</strong> High</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">CO2 Requirement:</strong> High</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Temperature Range:</strong> 72-82°F (22-28°C)</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">pH Range:</strong> 6.0-7.5</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Propagation:</strong> Cuttings</li></ul>', '', 'published', '[\"tonina-belem-min-600x600.jpg\"]', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, 0, 0, 140, 110, NULL, NULL, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0, 17, '2024-09-11 18:22:55', '2024-10-04 18:41:09', 'in_stock', 3, 'Botble\\ACL\\Models\\User', 'tonina-belem-min-600x600.jpg', 'physical', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 0),
(353, 'Wrinkled', '<p style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Description:</strong> Microsorum Pteropus “Wrinkled Leaf,” also known as Wrinkled Leaf Java Fern, is a distinctive variant of the classic Java Fern celebrated for its textured and crinkled foliage. Belonging to the Polypodiaceae family, this fern originates from Southeast Asia and has gained popularity among aquarists for its unique leaf structure. The leaves, characterized by their wrinkled appearance, add a touch of individuality and aquatic elegance to aquarium landscapes.</p><p style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Plant Information:</strong></p><ul><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Scientific Name:</strong> Microsorum Pteropus “Wrinkled Leaf”</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Family:</strong> Polypodiaceae</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Origin:</strong> Southeast Asia</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Difficulty Level:</strong> Easy</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Lighting Requirements:</strong> Low to Medium</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">CO2 Requirement:</strong> Low</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Temperature Range:</strong> 68-82°F (20-28°C)</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">pH Range:</strong> 6.0-7.5</li><li><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Propagation:</strong> Rhizome Division, Adventitious Plantlets</li></ul>', '', 'published', '[\"wrinkled-min.jpg\"]', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, 0, 0, 250, 150, NULL, NULL, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0, 18, '2024-09-11 18:23:42', '2024-10-04 17:35:51', 'in_stock', 3, 'Botble\\ACL\\Models\\User', 'wrinkled-min.jpg', 'physical', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 0),
(354, 'Sunken Garden Anti Chlorine 200Ml + 30Ml', '<p style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\">solution for making aquarium water safe. It effectively removes harmful chlorine, chloramine, and heavy metals. Beyond this, this product is enriched with 15 strains of beneficial bacteria, each selected for their role in establishing and maintaining a healthy, balanced, and thriving ecosystem within your aquarium.</p><p class=\"Body\" style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;line-height:19.2px;word-spacing:0px;\"><span lang=\"en-us\"> Benefits:</span></p><p class=\"Body\" style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;line-height:19.2px;word-spacing:0px;\"><span lang=\"en-us\">– Rapidly Removes Harmful Chemicals: Instantly neutralises chlorine and chloramine, making tap water safe for your aquatic life.</span></p><p class=\"Body\" style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;line-height:19.2px;word-spacing:0px;\"><span lang=\"en-us\">– Detoxifies Heavy Metals: Actively binds and neutralises heavy metals that can be toxic to fish and plants.</span></p><p class=\"Body\" style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;line-height:19.2px;word-spacing:0px;\"><span lang=\"en-us\">– Promotes Healthy Ecosystem: Introduces a diverse range of beneficial bacteria to establish and support a balanced aquatic environment.</span></p><p class=\"Body\" style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;line-height:19.2px;word-spacing:0px;\"><span lang=\"en-us\">– Enhances Water Quality: Aids in breaking down organic waste and reducing ammonia levels, ensuring clearer and healthier water.</span></p><p class=\"Body\" style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;line-height:19.2px;word-spacing:0px;\"><span lang=\"en-us\">Directions for Use:</span></p><p class=\"Body\" style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;line-height:19.2px;word-spacing:0px;\"><span lang=\"en-us\">Shake well before use.</span></p><p class=\"Body\" style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;line-height:19.2px;word-spacing:0px;\"><span lang=\"en-us\">Add 1ml of Sunken Garden Anti Chlorine for every 10 liters of aquarium water when setting up a new tank or performing water changes.</span></p><p class=\"Body\" style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;line-height:19.2px;word-spacing:0px;\"><span lang=\"en-us\">Distribute evenly around the aquarium for best results.</span></p><p class=\"Body\" style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;line-height:19.2px;word-spacing:0px;\"><span lang=\"en-us\">Do not overdose.</span></p><p class=\"Body\" style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;line-height:19.2px;word-spacing:0px;\"><span lang=\"en-us\">For aquarium use only.</span></p><ul><li><b style=\"font-weight:bolder;\"><strong>Best Before : 2 Years from the Mfd Date </strong></b></li></ul>', '', 'published', '[\"sunken-garden-anti-chlorine-200ml-30ml-min-1.jpg\"]', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 9, 0, 0, 490, 441, NULL, NULL, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0, 11, '2024-09-12 01:42:11', '2024-10-04 17:49:18', 'in_stock', 3, 'Botble\\ACL\\Models\\User', 'sunken-garden-anti-chlorine-200ml-30ml-min-1.jpg', 'physical', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 0),
(355, 'Sunken Garden Arowana Fish Water Conditioner 100Ml', '<p style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\">Delve into the world of majestic Arowana fish with Sunken Garden Arowana Conditioner, meticulously crafted to cater to the unique needs of these regal aquatic giants. This conditioner recreates their natural habitat, ensuring their health, vibrancy, and the impressive beauty that Arowana’s are known for.</p><p style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Benefits:</strong></p><ol><li>pH Reducer: Sunken Garden Arowana Conditioner expertly lowers and stabilises pH levels, replicating the slightly acidic and soft water conditions favoured by Arowanas. Transform your aquarium into an authentic representation of their native environment.</li><li>Chlorine Neutraliser: Instantly neutralises harmful chlorine and chloramines from tap water, safeguarding your Arowanas from stress and potential health issues. Create a safe and serene aquatic haven for your majestic Arowanas.</li><li>Beneficial Bacteria Booster: Enriched with specialised strains of beneficial bacteria, this conditioner supports a healthy nitrogen cycle in your aquarium. These microorganisms actively reduce ammonia and nitrite levels, promoting a balanced and thriving ecosystem.</li><li>Stress Relief: Sunken Garden Arowana Conditioner is thoughtfully formulated to keep your Arowanas stress-free and content. By reducing stress, it enhances overall well-being and vitality, allowing your Arowanas to thrive in their natural-inspired environment.</li><li>Bloat Prevention: Protect your Arowanas from common digestive issues, such as bloat. Our conditioner creates a protective shield, ensuring a healthy and secure aquatic environment.</li></ol><p style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\">Elevate your Arowana’s aquatic experience with Sunken Garden Arowana Conditioner – where science    blends harmoniously with nature, dedicated to replicating the perfect habitat for these magnificent      fish. Your Arowanas deserve nothing but the best. Immerse yourself in a world of vibrant, thriving aquatic life today!</p><p style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"font-weight:bolder;\">Directions for use:</strong></p><ul><li>Shake well before use.</li><li>Add 1ml for every 5 litres of water.</li><li>Overdosing does not affect aquatic life.</li><li>Store in a cool, dry place</li></ul>', '', 'published', '[\"untitled-design211-min.png\"]', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 9, 0, 0, 290, 261, NULL, NULL, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, 0, 6, '2024-09-12 01:44:55', '2024-10-04 17:48:57', 'in_stock', 3, 'Botble\\ACL\\Models\\User', 'untitled-design211-min.png', 'physical', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 0),
