x-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Ingredients</strong></h4><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">Fish meal, Wheat flour, Fish hydrolysate, Krill-meal, Shrimp meal, Soy lecithin, Fish oil, Inositol, Astaxanthine, Phycocyanin, Beta-Carotene, Spirulina, Yeast powder, Vitamin A, D, E , K &amp; C, Vitamin B complex, trace minerals (Cu, Na, Fe, I, Mn, Co, Zn &amp; Se) amino acids (18 types), and essential fatty acids.</p><h4 style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:var( --e-global-color-secondary );font-family:var( --e-global-typography-83682a1-font-family ), Sans-serif;font-size:var( --e-global-typography-83682a1-font-size );font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:var( --e-global-typography-83682a1-font-weight );letter-spacing:normal;line-height:var( --e-global-typography-83682a1-line-height );margin-block:0.5rem 1rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Instruction</strong></h4><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">Feed twice a day. Remove uneaten feed. Not for human consumption. Keep out of reach of children. Keep at room temperature</p><h4 style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:var( --e-global-color-secondary );font-family:var( --e-global-typography-83682a1-font-family ), Sans-serif;font-size:var( --e-global-typography-83682a1-font-size );font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:var( --e-global-typography-83682a1-font-weight );letter-spacing:normal;line-height:var( --e-global-typography-83682a1-line-height );margin-block:0.5rem 1rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Nutritional Fact</strong></h4><ul><li>Protein – 34%</li><li>Fat – 5%</li><li>Fiber – 4%</li><li>Moisture – 9%</li></ul>', NULL),
('bn_BD', 152, 'WA RED MELANO FISH FEED 45G', '<ul><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">WA RED MELANO FISH FEED</strong></li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Protein – 45%</strong></li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Fat – 5%</strong></li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Fibre – 4%</strong></li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Moisture – 9%</strong></li></ul>', NULL),
('bn_BD', 153, 'Bacopa Monierri', '<p>Common name: Small bacopa Use : Background plant CO2 : Low Light: Low (price per stem) (•Plant Pictures shown are of Submersed Grown Plants in Aquariums under Optimum Plant Growing Conditions. •Plants Sent are grown in Farms in Emmersed or Submersed Conditions depending on variety. Hence, Plant/Leaf Structures may vary from that shown in pictures. When they are grown submersed in aquariums under Optimum Growing Conditions as required by the Plant they will get the appearance as shown in pictures)</p>', NULL),
('bn_BD', 154, 'Bacopa Monierri Platinum Growow Tc Plant', '<p>Description: Bacopa Monnieri, commonly known as Water Hyssop or Brahmi, is an aquatic plant renowned for its delicate appearance and therapeutic history. As a member of the Plantaginaceae family, this herbaceous perennial is native to wetlands in Asia, North and South America, and Australia. Its emersed growth showcases pairs of opposite, succulent leaves along the stems, while its submersed form features finer, dissected leaves. Bacopa Monnieri’s overall appearance is a testament to simplicity, making it a popular choice for both aquarium enthusiasts and herbalists alike.</p><p>Beyond its ornamental value in aquascaping, Bacopa Monnieri is recognized for its use in traditional medicine, particularly in Ayurveda, where it is believed to offer cognitive and adaptogenic benefits.</p>', NULL),
('bn_BD', 155, 'Bacopa Salzmani Growow Tc Plant', '<p>Description: Bacopa Salzmanii SG, often referred to simply as Bacopa Salzmannii, stands as a captivating aquatic plant cherished for its unique appearance and graceful growth. As a member of the Plantaginaceae family, this species hails from South America, bringing a touch of elegance to freshwater aquariums. Bacopa Salzmanii SG is characterized by its slender stems and pairs of opposite, lance-shaped leaves that can display varying shades of green. The leaves often feature a subtle ripple effect, contributing to the plant’s overall aesthetic appeal.</p><p>This plant’s charming features make it a popular choice for aquascapers aiming to add a touch of sophistication to their underwater landscapes.</p><p>Plant Information:</p><p>Scientific Name: Bacopa Salzmanii SG<br>Family: Plantaginaceae<br>Origin: South America<br>Difficulty Level: Moderate<br>Lighting Requirements: Medium to High<br>CO2 Requirement: Low to Medium<br>Temperature Range: 64-78°F (18-26°C)<br>pH Range: 6.0-7.5<br>Propagation: Cuttings</p>', NULL),
('bn_BD', 156, 'Cryptocoryne Axelrodii Growow Tc Plant', '<p>Common Name: Cryptocoryne Axelrodi</p><p>Crypt Axelrodi is a rarer Cryptocoryne species that features narrow leaves, hardy nature and a greenish-brown color. It works great for mid ground plant coverage in planted tanks and is easy to care for. However, we’d recommend that it is not moved like most crypts as this can potentially trigger Crypt melt.</p><p>Like other crypts, Cryptocoryne Axelrodi is great for beginner hobbyists due to its ease in keeping and low care requirements. If grown in good aquarium substrate such as Ultum Nature System Controsoil, the plant can feed through the roots and grow quickly without the need for high light, CO2 or fertilizer dosing. However, the addition of CO2 and good lighting will result in healthier, more robust growth.</p><p>Crypts can be grown emersed or submerged. Propagate by splitting the rhizome or cutting off new growth and replanting</p><p>Notes:</p><p>Cryptocoryne prefer not to be moved once planted. If possible, do not move them!<br>Do not make drastic changes to the aquarium. Unstable parameters will result in melt and rotting of the aquarium plant.<br>Please be sure to remove this plant from its pot. Remove the cotton surrounding the roots and plant into a quality substrate.<br>CO2 injection and quality aquarium soil will yield better growth.<br>Please research according to ensure the plant receives proper care.Family Name: AraceaeEndemic To: BorneoLeaves: 2-3+”<br>Height: 10-15″</p><p>pH: 6-7.5</p><p>Care: Easy</p><p>Light: Low to Medium</p><p>Co2: Not necessary but recommended</p><p>Propagation: Cut by rhizome</p><p>Growth rate: Slow</p>', NULL),
('bn_BD', 157, '2Hr Aquarist APT Jazz', '<p><strong style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255);color:rgb(105,105,105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:bolder;word-spacing:0px;\">The best root fertiliser for planted tanks.</strong><br><span style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255);color:rgb(105,105,105);font-size:16px;\"><span>Thicker, fuller growth forms with superior algae control.&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></span><br><span style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255);color:rgb(105,105,105);font-size:16px;\"><span>Nitrate Limitation made easy.&nbsp;APT j/Jazz from 2HR Aquarist are root fertiliser capsules for planted aquariums. They consist of round baked clay pellets mixed with a blend of inorganic mineral salts and provide the plants with nutrients for 2 months.&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></span><br><span style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255);color:rgb(105,105,105);font-size:16px;\"><span>Potassium, phosphate, nitrogen salts and chelated trace elements are integrated into the clay matrix and slowly diffuse out of the clay when immersed in water, acting directly on the roots.&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></span></p>', NULL);
INSERT INTO `ec_products_translations` (`lang_code`, `ec_products_id`, `name`, `description`, `content`) VALUES
('bn_BD', 158, 'Cryptocoryne Becketii Growow Tc Plant', '<p>Cryptocoryne beckettii ‘Petchii’ is a small variety of Cryptocoryne beckettii from Sri Lanka, which has beautiful, slightly fluted leaf margins, 10-15 cm long. Leaves become dark olive-brown with violet underside. Like many other Cryptocorynes, the leaf colour and shape depends largely on environmental conditions in the aquarium.</p>', NULL),
('bn_BD', 159, 'Cryptocoryne Becketii Growow Tc Plant', '<p>Cryptocoryne beckettii ‘Petchii’ is a small variety of Cryptocoryne beckettii from Sri Lanka, which has beautiful, slightly fluted leaf margins, 10-15 cm long. Leaves become dark olive-brown with violet underside. Like many other Cryptocorynes, the leaf colour and shape depends largely on environmental conditions in the aquarium.</p>', NULL),
('bn_BD', 160, 'API Life Aayu Bio Media 1ltr/500gm', '<p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">API Life Aayu Bio Media is a mixture of porous filtration media specially designed for recreating the water purification system of the nature.</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">Porous natural stone has a high permeability and provides an ideal environment for filtration bacteria to colonize.</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">It also helps to remove organic substances, which become a cause of water pollution and degrade quickly through the work of microorganisms.</p>', NULL),
('bn_BD', 161, 'API Life Aayuh Bio Media 0.5 Ltr / 250gm', '<p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">API Life Aayuh Bio Media is a mixture of porous filtration media specially designed for recreating the water purification system of the nature.</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">Porous natural stone has a high permeability and provides an ideal environment for filtration bacteria to colonize.</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">It also helps to remove organic substances, which become a cause of water pollution and degrade quickly through the work of microorganisms.</p>', NULL),
('bn_BD', 162, 'API Life Aayuh Bio Media 2ltr/1kg', '<p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">API Life Aayu Bio Media is a mixture of porous filtration media specially designed for recreating the water purification system of the nature.</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">Porous natural stone has a high permeability and provides an ideal environment for filtration bacteria to colonize.</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">It also helps to remove organic substances, which become a cause of water pollution and degrade quickly through the work of microorganisms.</p>', NULL),
('bn_BD', 163, 'Cryptocoryne Brown Growow Tc Plant', '<p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Description:&nbsp;</strong>Cryptocoryne ‘Brown’ admired for its rich and deep brown coloration that adds a warm and earthy tone to freshwater aquariums. As a member of the Cryptocoryne genus within the family Araceae, this plant hails from Sri Lanka. The ‘Brown’ variety is characterized by its broad and slightly ruffled leaves, creating a visually striking contrast in planted tank setups. Known for its adaptability and aesthetic appeal, Cryptocoryne ‘Brown’ is a popular choice for aquarists seeking a distinctive and colorful addition to their aquatic landscapes.</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Plant Information:</strong></p><ul><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Scientific Name:</strong> Cryptocoryne ‘Brown’</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Family:</strong>&nbsp;Araceae</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Origin:</strong>&nbsp;Sri Lanka</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Difficulty Level:</strong>&nbsp;Easy</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Lighting Requirements:</strong>&nbsp;Low to Medium</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">CO2 Requirement:</strong>&nbsp;Low to Medium</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Temperature Range:</strong>&nbsp;72-82°F (22-28°C)</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">pH Range:</strong>&nbsp;6.0-7.5</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Propagation:</strong>&nbsp;Runner, division</li></ul>', NULL),
('bn_BD', 164, 'Cryptocoryne Gecko Growow Tc Plant', '<p>Cryptocoryne Gecko Growow Tc Plant<br>&nbsp;</p>', NULL),
('bn_BD', 165, 'Cryptocoryne Green Growow Tc Plant', '<p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Description:</strong> Cryptocoryne ‘Green’ is celebrated for its lush green foliage that brings a refreshing and vibrant aesthetic to freshwater aquariums. As a member of the Cryptocoryne genus within the family Araceae, this plant originates from Sri Lanka. The ‘Green’ variety is characterized by its broad and slightly ruffled leaves, creating an inviting and natural look in planted tank setups. Known for its versatility and ease of care, Cryptocoryne ‘Green’ is a popular choice for aquarists seeking a classic and visually appealing addition to their aquatic landscapes.</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Plant Information:</strong></p><ul><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Scientific Name:</strong> Cryptocoryne ‘Green’</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Family:</strong>&nbsp;Araceae</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Origin:</strong>&nbsp;Sri Lanka</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Difficulty Level:</strong>&nbsp;Easy</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Lighting Requirements:</strong>&nbsp;Low to Medium</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">CO2 Requirement:</strong>&nbsp;Low to Medium</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Temperature Range:</strong>&nbsp;72-82°F (22-28°C)</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">pH Range:</strong>&nbsp;6.0-7.5</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Propagation:</strong>&nbsp;Runner, division</li></ul>', NULL),
('bn_BD', 166, 'Cryptocoryne Lucens Growow Tc Plant', '<p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Description:</strong>&nbsp;Cryptocoryne lucens, often referred to as Lucens Crypt, is a popular aquatic plant celebrated for its lush green foliage and versatility in planted aquariums. As a member of the Cryptocoryne genus within the family Araceae, this plant is native to Sri Lanka and other parts of Southeast Asia. It features elongated, lance-shaped leaves that form dense clusters, creating a vibrant and verdant tapestry in aquariums. Cryptocoryne lucens is known for its adaptability and ease of care, making it an excellent choice for both beginners and experienced aquarists.</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">This Cryptocoryne species adds a touch of natural beauty and a sense of tranquility to freshwater tanks, making it a favored component of aquascapes.</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Plant Information:</strong></p><ul><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Scientific Name:</strong>&nbsp;Cryptocoryne lucens</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Family:</strong>&nbsp;Araceae</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Origin:</strong>&nbsp;Sri Lanka, Southeast Asia</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Difficulty Level:</strong>&nbsp;Easy</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Lighting Requirements:</strong>&nbsp;Low to Medium</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">CO2 Requirement:</strong>&nbsp;Low to Medium</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Temperature Range:</strong>&nbsp;72-82°F (22-28°C)</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">pH Range:</strong>&nbsp;6.0-7.5</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Propagation:</strong>&nbsp;Rhizome division</li></ul>', NULL),
('bn_BD', 167, 'Cryptocoryne Nurii Growow Tc Plant', '<p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">This beautiful variation of Cryptocoryne nurii was found growing in the wild in Malaysia around 1970. In the aquarium hobby it became popular under the name ‘Rose Maiden’.</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">The plant is as easy to grow as Cryptocoryne wendtii and has the same size and leaf shape. It will, given the time, produce runners under the bottom layer, often showing up quite far from the mother plant.</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">Intensity of colour and patterns in leaves is dependant on light and nutrition.</p><div class=\"description\" style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><p style=\"box-sizing:border-box;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;\">This beautiful variation of Cryptocoryne nurii was found growing in the wild in Malaysia around 1970. In the aquarium hobby it became popular under the name ‘Rose Maiden’.</p><p style=\"box-sizing:border-box;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;\">The plant is as easy to grow as Cryptocoryne wendtii and has the same size and leaf shape. It will, given the time, produce runners under the bottom layer, often showing up quite far from the mother plant.</p><p style=\"box-sizing:border-box;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;\">Intensity of colour and patterns in leaves is dependant on light and nutrition.</p></div>', NULL),
('bn_BD', 168, 'Cryptocoryne Perva', '<p>Cryptocoryne parva fromac Sri Lanka is the smallest of all Cryptocorynes (only 3-6 cm tall and a roset less than 5-8 cm wide). It is one of the few species that does not significantly change its leaf shape and colour depending on cultivation conditions. It needs more light than most other Cryptocorynes because it almost loses its leaf plate under water. So, it must never be overshadowed by other plants.</p><p>Known for its slow growth, but Nutrition Capsules in the bottom layer will enhance the development. Individual plants should be planted a few centimetres apart, and after about six months they will form a cohesive low group of plants.</p><p>Very recommendable foreground plant.</p>', NULL),
('bn_BD', 169, 'Cryptocoryne Perva Growow Tc Plant', '<p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Description:</strong>&nbsp;Cryptocoryne parva, often known simply as Parva Crypt, is a diminutive yet charming aquatic plant prized for its petite size and delicate appearance. As a member of the Cryptocoryne genus within the family Araceae, this plant is native to Sri Lanka. Cryptocoryne parva is characterized by narrow, lance-shaped leaves that form compact rosettes, creating a carpet-like effect when planted in groups. Despite its small stature, this Cryptocoryne species adds a touch of elegance to aquariums, making it a popular choice for aquascaping and foreground planting.</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">Cryptocoryne parva’s ability to create lush carpets and its undemanding nature contribute to its appeal among both beginners and experienced aquarists.</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Plant Information:</strong></p><ul><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Scientific Name:</strong>&nbsp;Cryptocoryne parva</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Family:</strong>&nbsp;Araceae</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Origin:</strong>&nbsp;Sri Lanka</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Difficulty Level:</strong>&nbsp;Easy</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Lighting Requirements:</strong>&nbsp;Low to Medium</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">CO2 Requirement:</strong>&nbsp;Low to Medium</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Temperature Range:</strong>&nbsp;72-82°F (22-28°C)</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">pH Range:</strong>&nbsp;6.0-7.5</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Propagation:</strong>&nbsp;Runner, division</li></ul>', NULL),
('bn_BD', 170, 'Cryptocoryne Pigmy Growow Tc Plant', '<p>The Cryptocoryne pygmy Tissue Culture (TC) Cup is a convenient and easy way to add this beautiful aquatic plant to your aquarium. This tissue culture cup contains a small, compact variety of Cryptocoryne that is perfect for creating a lush, green carpet in your tank. The plant is grown in a sterile environment, free</p>', NULL),
('bn_BD', 171, 'Cryptocoryne Ponterdifolia Growow Tc Plant', '<p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Description:</strong>&nbsp;Cryptocoryne pontederiifolia, commonly known as Pontederiifolia Crypt, is a captivating aquatic plant admired for its unique and decorative leaves. As a member of the Cryptocoryne genus within the family Araceae, this plant is native to Southeast Asia, including regions in India and Sri Lanka. Cryptocoryne pontederiifolia is characterized by its elongated and lance-shaped leaves that feature a prominent midrib and undulating edges. The leaves may exhibit various shades of green, contributing to its aesthetic appeal. This Cryptocoryne species adds a touch of elegance to freshwater aquariums, making it a popular choice among aquarists engaged in planted tank setups.</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">Known for its hardiness and adaptability, Cryptocoryne pontederiifolia is suitable for both novice and experienced aquarium enthusiasts.</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Plant Information:</strong></p><ul><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Scientific Name:</strong>&nbsp;Cryptocoryne pontederiifolia</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Family:</strong>&nbsp;Araceae</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Origin:</strong>&nbsp;Southeast Asia (India, Sri Lanka)</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Difficulty Level:</strong>&nbsp;Easy to Moderate</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Lighting Requirements:</strong>&nbsp;Low to Medium</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">CO2 Requirement:</strong>&nbsp;Low to Medium</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Temperature Range:</strong>&nbsp;72-82°F (22-28°C)</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">pH Range:</strong>&nbsp;6.0-7.5</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Propagation:</strong>&nbsp;Runner, division</li></ul>', NULL),
('bn_BD', 172, 'Cryptocoryne Sindoor Growow Tc Plant', '<p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Common Name:</strong> Cryptocoryne Sindoor, Water Trumpet, Wendtii Sreepadma Sindoor</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">Cryptocoryne Wendtii Sindoor is a new variation of Cryptocoryne available to the aquarium community. This particular Crypt was created from Wendtii Brown and developed in lab to ensure a stable mutation. Its name refers to the rich maroon to pink tones the plant produces when grown in suitable conditions for Cryptocoryne species.&nbsp;Because this variety is relatively new, it can be assumed that care is similar to other forms of Cryptocoryne plants.</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">Cryptocoryne do best when provided with a nutrient-dense aquarium soil and stability. Cryptocoryne plants require time to establish strong root systems and frequent moving or parameter changes will slow growth and impact overall health.</p><p class=\"p1\" style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><b style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\"><strong>Key Features &amp; Important Notes:</strong></b></p><ul><li class=\"ul1\">Tissue culture plants are grown in-vitro from state of the art laboratories that specialize in propagating aquatic plants. They provide the best option for those who want to ensure that absolutely zero unwanted pests are introduced into the aquarium.</li><li class=\"ul1\">Remove tissue culture gel before planting. Simply wash the gel away or soak the plant in water and squeeze the gel off gently with your fingers.</li><li class=\"ul1\">Cryptocoryne prefer not to be moved once planted. If possible, do not move them.</li><li class=\"ul1\">For instructions on how to properly plant&nbsp;tissue culture aquarium plants, click&nbsp;<a style=\"background-color:transparent;box-shadow:none;box-sizing:border-box;color:var( --e-global-color-primary );text-decoration:none;\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=FJLHDmTxBl0\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"How to: prep tissue culture aquarium plants\">here</a>.</li><li class=\"ul1\">Refrain from making drastic or sudden changes to the aquarium. Unstable parameters contribute to melt and rotting of Cryptocoryne plants.</li><li class=\"ul1\">Please research appropriately to ensure your plant thrives.</li><li class=\"ul1\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Species Information:Family Name:</strong>&nbsp;Araceae<br><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Origin:</strong>&nbsp;South East Asia<br><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Height:</strong>&nbsp;3-6″<br><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">pH:</strong>&nbsp;5.5-7.5<br><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Care:</strong>&nbsp;Medium<br><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Light:</strong>&nbsp;Moderate<br><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Co2:</strong>&nbsp;Recommended<br><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Propagation:</strong>&nbsp;Separate plantlets<br><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Growth rate:&nbsp;</strong>Slow</li></ul>', NULL),
('bn_BD', 173, 'Cryptocoryne Spiralis Green', '<p>This plant requires nutrient rich substrate. Regular pruning will keep it looking its best.</p><p>Plant Difficulty : Easy</p><p>Light Requirement : Low</p><p>Plant Type : Rhizome</p>', NULL),
('bn_BD', 174, 'Cryptocoryne Spiralis Jwala Growow Tc Plant', '<p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Overview:</strong>&nbsp;Coming from the family Araceae, Cryptocoryne spiralis is a beautiful aquatic plant. It is one of the best plants for the beginners as it is the least demanding and easy to maintain. When C. spiralis is grown solitarily, it gives a good and aesthetic view to the aquarium. However, when grown in clusters it creates a bushy facade to the underwater ambiance. The plant is native to India and can be seen growing between the rice fields. When the plant is maintained with regular pruning and cutting it gives the best look to the aquarium.</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Appearance:</strong>&nbsp;C. spiralis is a perfect plant to add height and visual drama to your tank. The growth form of the plant is rosette. The green leaves become lengthy and slender and sway underwater. The emergent leaves in the other hand are small in size and have wide blades. The long leaves make the plant an excellent option to ponder as a background plant. Generally, it is advised to plant it in a planned fashion like small plants in the foreground and larger ones at the back. It doesn’t give a forest-like appearance to the aquarium and grace it beautifully. It is hard to achieve the variations when planted randomly.</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Hard/soft Plant:</strong>&nbsp;It is a very hardy plant</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Ideal water temperature:</strong>&nbsp;The temperature requirement of the plant is between 75° and 82°F.</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Lightening conditions:</strong>&nbsp;The light requirement of the plant is medium to high. Using full spectrum bulbs of at least 2 watts per gallon will fulfill the needs of the plant to flourish well.</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Ideal pH level:</strong>&nbsp;Water conditions need to be stable for better plant growth to prevent stems and roots from rotting away. pH within the range of 6.5 to 7.5 is considered best for C. spiralis.</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Do you know:</strong>&nbsp;C. spiralis can be propagated by using multiple runners or rhizome divisions.</p>', NULL),
('bn_BD', 175, 'Cryptocoryne Spiralis red', '<p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">This plant requires nutrient rich substrate. Regular pruning will keep it looking its best.</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Plant Difficulty</strong> : Medium</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Light Requirement</strong>&nbsp;: Medium</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Plant Type</strong> : Rhizome</p>', NULL),
('bn_BD', 176, 'Cryptocoryne Tropica Growow Tc Plant', '<p>This beautiful variety with the dark, hammered leaves is named after ‘Tropica’. When grown in an open space the leaves will virtually lie on the bottom. It is suitable for small aquariums with leaves from 10-20 cm, and a rosette from 10-20 cm wide. Like most other Sri Lanka Cryptocorynes, it also grows well in hard water.</p>', NULL),
('bn_BD', 177, 'Cryptocoryne Wendetii', '<p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">This easy to grow plant can be kept in groups and can be grown under various conditions.</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Plant Difficulty</strong> : Easy</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Light Requirement</strong> : Medium</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Plant Type</strong> : Rhizome</p>', NULL),
('bn_BD', 178, 'Cryptocoryne Wendetii Long Growow Tc Plants', '<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-9022ba2 elementor-widget elementor-widget-woocommerce-product-title elementor-page-title elementor-widget-heading\" style=\"--align-content:initial;--align-items:initial;--align-self:initial;--flex-basis:initial;--flex-direction:initial;--flex-grow:initial;--flex-shrink:initial;--flex-wrap:initial;--gap:initial;--justify-content:initial;--order:initial;--swiper-navigation-size:44px;--swiper-pagination-bullet-horizontal-gap:6px;--swiper-pagination-bullet-size:6px;--swiper-theme-color:#000;--widgets-spacing:20px 20px;-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;align-content:var(--align-content);align-items:var(--align-items);align-self:var(--align-self);background-color:rgb(242, 246, 249);box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);display:var(--page-title-display);flex-basis:var(--flex-basis);flex-direction:var(--flex-direction);flex-grow:var(--flex-grow);flex-shrink:var(--flex-shrink);flex-wrap:var(--flex-wrap);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;gap:var(--gap);justify-content:var(--justify-content);letter-spacing:normal;margin-block-end:20px;margin-bottom:20px;order:var(--order);orphans:2;position:relative;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;width:512px;word-spacing:0px;\" data-widget_type=\"woocommerce-product-title.default\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-id=\"9022ba2\"><div class=\"elementor-widget-container\" style=\"box-sizing:border-box;transition:background .3s,border .3s,border-radius .3s,box-shadow .3s,transform var(--e-transform-transition-duration,.4s);\"><h4 class=\"product_title entry-title elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default\" style=\"box-sizing:border-box;clear:none;color:var( --e-global-color-secondary );font-family:var( --e-global-typography-83682a1-font-family ), Sans-serif;font-size:var( --e-global-typography-83682a1-font-size );font-style:var( --e-global-typography-83682a1-font-style );font-weight:var( --e-global-typography-83682a1-font-weight );letter-spacing:var( --e-global-typography-83682a1-letter-spacing );line-height:var( --e-global-typography-83682a1-line-height );margin-block:0.5rem 1rem;margin:0px;padding:0px;text-transform:var( --e-global-typography-83682a1-text-transform );word-spacing:var( --e-global-typography-83682a1-word-spacing );\">Cryptocoryne Wendetii Long Growow Tc Plants</h4></div></div><div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-69c042e6 elementor-widget elementor-widget-woocommerce-product-price\" style=\"--align-content:initial;--align-items:initial;--align-self:initial;--flex-basis:initial;--flex-direction:initial;--flex-grow:initial;--flex-shrink:initial;--flex-wrap:initial;--gap:initial;--justify-content:initial;--order:initial;--swiper-navigation-size:44px;--swiper-pagination-bullet-horizontal-gap:6px;--swiper-pagination-bullet-size:6px;--swiper-theme-color:#000;--widgets-spacing:20px 20px;-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;align-content:var(--align-content);align-items:var(--align-items);align-self:var(--align-self);background-color:rgb(242, 246, 249);box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);flex-basis:var(--flex-basis);flex-direction:var(--flex-direction);flex-grow:var(--flex-grow);flex-shrink:var(--flex-shrink);flex-wrap:var(--flex-wrap);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;gap:var(--gap);justify-content:var(--justify-content);letter-spacing:normal;margin-block-end:20px;margin-bottom:20px;order:var(--order);orphans:2;position:relative;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;width:512px;word-spacing:0px;\" data-widget_type=\"woocommerce-product-price.default\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-id=\"69c042e6\"><div class=\"elementor-widget-container\" style=\"box-sizing:border-box;transition:background .3s,border .3s,border-radius .3s,box-shadow .3s,transform var(--e-transform-transition-duration,.4s);\"><br>&nbsp;</div></div>', NULL),
('bn_BD', 179, 'Cryptocoryne Wendetii Pink Growow Tc Plant', '<p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Description:</strong>&nbsp;Cryptocoryne wendtii ‘Pink’ is a captivating variant of the Wendtii Crypt, cherished for its delicate and subtle pink hues that bring a touch of elegance to freshwater aquariums. As a member of the Cryptocoryne genus within the family Araceae, this plant originates from Sri Lanka. The ‘Pink’ variety is characterized by its broad and slightly ruffled leaves, displaying a rosy tint that adds a unique and charming dimension to planted tank setups. Known for its adaptability and aesthetic appeal, Cryptocoryne wendtii ‘Pink’ is a sought-after choice for aquarists looking to infuse a gentle burst of color into their aquatic landscapes.</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Plant Information:</strong></p><ul><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Scientific Name:</strong>&nbsp;Cryptocoryne wendtii ‘Pink’</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Family:</strong>&nbsp;Araceae</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Origin:</strong>&nbsp;Sri Lanka</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Difficulty Level:</strong>&nbsp;Easy</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Lighting Requirements:</strong>&nbsp;Low to Medium</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">CO2 Requirement:</strong>&nbsp;Low to Medium</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Temperature Range:</strong>&nbsp;72-82°F (22-28°C)</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">pH Range:</strong>&nbsp;6.0-7.5</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Propagation:</strong>&nbsp;Runner, division</li></ul>', NULL);
INSERT INTO `ec_products_translations` (`lang_code`, `ec_products_id`, `name`, `description`, `content`) VALUES
('bn_BD', 180, 'Cryptocoryne Wendetii Tropica', '<p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">This low growing plant can be used as foreground or midground plant. Grows fast and bushy.</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Plant Difficulty</strong> : Easy</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Light Requirement</strong> : Medium</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Plant Type</strong> : Rhizome</p>', NULL),
('bn_BD', 181, 'Cyeprus helferi', '<p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">Requires CO2, adequate fertilization and nutrient rich substrate. Does well in slightly cooler temperature.</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Plant Difficulty</strong> : Medium</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Light Requirement</strong> : Very Bright</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Plant Type</strong> : &nbsp;Rhizome</p>', NULL),
('bn_BD', 182, 'Didipilis Diandra', '<p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">Common Name:&nbsp;Peplis Diandra</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">Didiplis diandra is a stem plant which can be found growing in lakes and streams throughout the states. Its a beautiful addition to an aquarium thanks to the thin, needle like leaves that can exhibit bright red tips when grown under high light with fertilization and CO2. In order to achieve the desired bushy effect, this plant is best &nbsp;grown in groups or bunches.</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">Propagation is simple and straightforward like other stem plants. Simply cut anywhere along the stem and replant the cuttings. &nbsp;In order to keep this plant low growing and spread laterally runners, trim frequently and grow it under high light.</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">Family Name:&nbsp;Lythraceae</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">Origin:&nbsp;USA</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">Height: 4-12”</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">pH: 6.0-7.5</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">Care: Easy</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">Light:&nbsp;Moderate to High</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">Co2: Not necessary</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">Propagation: Cuttings</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">Growth rate: Slow</p>', NULL),
('bn_BD', 183, 'Drosera Spatulata Growow Tc Plant', '<p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">Drosera spatulata, also known as the Spoon-leaved Sundew, is a carnivorous plant that is native to Southeast Asia and Australia. It is a small, herbaceous perennial that grows in a rosette shape and produces long, thin stems with small, spoon-shaped leaves.</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">Like all sundews, Drosera spatulata captures its prey by using sticky hairs on its leaves that trap insects. When an insect lands on the leaf, the hairs bend inward, bringing the insect closer to the center of the leaf, where it becomes stuck in the sticky secretion. The leaf then curls around the insect, enclosing it in a sticky prison, and the plant secretes digestive enzymes to break down the insect and extract its nutrients.</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">Drosera spatulata is relatively easy to care for and is a popular choice for home gardeners who want to try growing carnivorous plants. It prefers bright, indirect light and well-draining soil that is kept consistently moist. The plant also requires high humidity levels, which can be achieved by placing the pot on a tray of pebbles filled with water. In terms of feeding, Drosera spatulata can be fed small insects, such as fruit flies or gnats, once or twice a month, but it can survive without being fed if it is placed in a location where it can catch insects on its own.</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Care Tips</strong></p><ul><li>Light: Drosera spatulata prefers bright, indirect light. A sunny windowsill or a grow light that provides 12-14 hours of light per day is ideal.</li><li>Soil: Drosera spatulata prefers a soilless growing medium that is made up of peat moss, perlite, and sand. The soil should be kept consistently moist but not waterlogged.</li><li>Water: Water Drosera spatulata with distilled or rainwater. Avoid using tap water, which can contain minerals and other chemicals that are harmful to carnivorous plants. Water the plant from the bottom by placing the pot in a tray of water and allowing the soil to soak up the water from the bottom</li></ul>', NULL),
('bn_BD', 184, 'Echindorus Argentenesis', '<p>Description: Echinodorus Argentinensis, commonly known as the Argentine Sword Plant, is a charming and graceful aquatic species appreciated for its decorative presence in freshwater aquariums. As a member of the Echinodorus genus within the Alismataceae family, this plant is native to South America. Echinodorus Argentinensis is recognized for its broad, lanceolate leaves that form an attractive rosette. With its versatile nature and striking appearance, it is often used by aquarists to create lush and visually appealing aquascapes.</p>', NULL),
('bn_BD', 185, 'Echindorus Fancy Curl', '<p><strong style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:bolder;letter-spacing:normal;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">Description:</strong><span style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255);color:rgb(105,105,105);font-size:16px;\"><span>&nbsp;Echinodorus ‘Fancy Curl’ is an enchanting and distinctive variant of the Sword Plant, appreciated for its unique and ornate leaf structure. As a member of the Echinodorus genus within the Alismataceae family, this aquatic plant is known for its lush and decorative appearance. ‘Fancy Curl’ stands out with its leaves that exhibit an elegant curling pattern, adding a touch of sophistication to freshwater aquariums. Its vibrant green color and captivating form make it a sought-after choice for aquarists aiming to introduce a visually appealing centerpiece to their aquatic landscapes.</span></span></p>', NULL),
('bn_BD', 186, 'Echindorus Marble queen yelow', '<p><strong style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:bolder;letter-spacing:normal;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">Description:</strong><span style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255);color:rgb(105,105,105);font-size:16px;\"><span>&nbsp;Echinodorus Cordifolius “Marble Queen Yellow” is a captivating aquatic plant celebrated for its vibrant yellow variegation and graceful presence. As a member of the Echinodorus genus within the Alismataceae family, this plant hails from South America. The “Marble Queen Yellow” variety is distinguished by its heart-shaped leaves adorned with striking patterns of yellow and green. With its unique coloration and elegant form, it serves as a focal point, adding warmth and visual appeal to freshwater aquariums. Aquarists appreciate its adaptability and ability to thrive in various tank conditions.</span></span></p>', NULL),
('bn_BD', 187, 'Echindorus Ozelot', '<p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Description:</strong>&nbsp;Echinodorus sp. “Ozelot,” commonly known as Ozelot Sword, is a visually striking aquatic plant celebrated for its unique leopard-like spotted pattern on its leaves. As a member of the Echinodorus genus within the Alismataceae family, this plant adds a touch of the exotic to freshwater aquariums. The distinctive red and green markings on its leaves make it a captivating choice for aquarists looking to introduce a bold and eye-catching element to their aquascapes.</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Plant Information:</strong></p><ul><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Scientific Name:</strong>&nbsp;Echinodorus sp. “Ozelot”</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Family:</strong>&nbsp;Alismataceae</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Origin:</strong>&nbsp;Cultivar (exact origin may vary)</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Difficulty Level:</strong>&nbsp;Easy to Moderate</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Lighting Requirements:</strong>&nbsp;Moderate to High</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">CO2 Requirement:</strong>&nbsp;Low to Medium</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Temperature Range:</strong>&nbsp;72-82°F (22-28°C)</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">pH Range:</strong>&nbsp;6.0-7.5</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Propagation:</strong>&nbsp;Adventitious plantlets, division</li></ul>', NULL),
('bn_BD', 188, 'Echindorus Rose', '<p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Description:</strong>&nbsp;Echinodorus Rose, often known as the Rose Sword, is an exquisite aquatic plant cherished for its unique rosette of pink and green-hued leaves. As a member of the Echinodorus genus within the Alismataceae family, this plant hails from South America. The Echinodorus Rose stands out with its captivating coloration, bringing a touch of elegance to freshwater aquariums. With its distinctive appearance and relatively undemanding care requirements, it serves as a beautiful centerpiece in aquascapes.</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Plant Information:</strong></p><ul><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Scientific Name:</strong>&nbsp;Echinodorus Rose</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Family:</strong>&nbsp;Alismataceae</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Origin:</strong>&nbsp;South America</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Difficulty Level:</strong>&nbsp;Easy</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Lighting Requirements:</strong>&nbsp;Low to Medium</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">CO2 Requirement:</strong>&nbsp;Low</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Temperature Range:</strong>&nbsp;72-82°F (22-28°C)</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">pH Range:</strong>&nbsp;6.0-7.5</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Propagation:</strong>&nbsp;Adventitious plantlets, division</li></ul>', NULL),
('bn_BD', 189, 'Echindorus Rubyn', '<p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Description:</strong>&nbsp;Echinodorus Rubin, commonly known as Rubin Sword or Red Melon Sword, is a stunning aquatic plant prized for its vibrant, jewel-toned leaves. As a member of the Echinodorus genus within the Alismataceae family, this plant originates from South America. Echinodorus Rubin stands out with its deep red to burgundy foliage, creating a striking contrast in freshwater aquariums. With its eye-catching coloration and relatively undemanding care requirements, it serves as a focal point, adding a touch of elegance to aquascapes.</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Plant Information:</strong></p><ul><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Scientific Name:</strong>&nbsp;Echinodorus Rubin</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Family:</strong>&nbsp;Alismataceae</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Origin:</strong>&nbsp;South America</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Difficulty Level:</strong>&nbsp;Easy to Moderate</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Lighting Requirements:</strong>&nbsp;Moderate to High</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">CO2 Requirement:</strong>&nbsp;Low to Medium</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Temperature Range:</strong>&nbsp;72-82°F (22-28°C)</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">pH Range:</strong>&nbsp;6.0-7.5</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Propagation:</strong>&nbsp;Adventitious plantlets, division</li></ul>', NULL),
('bn_BD', 190, 'Echindorus Tennelus Micro', '<p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Description:</strong>&nbsp;Echinodorus Tenellus ‘Micro,’ a delightful variant of the Pygmy Chain Sword, is a petite aquatic plant celebrated for its compact size and delicate appearance. As a member of the Echinodorus genus within the Alismataceae family, this miniature version is a charming addition to freshwater aquariums. Echinodorus Tenellus ‘Micro’ features slender, grass-like leaves that form a dense carpet, making it an excellent choice for aquarists looking to create intricate and visually appealing foregrounds in their aquascapes. With its diminutive size and undemanding care requirements, it brings a touch of elegance to aquarium landscapes.</p><ul><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Scientific Name:</strong>&nbsp;Echinodorus Tenellus ‘Micro’</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Family:</strong>&nbsp;Alismataceae</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Origin:</strong>&nbsp;Cultivar (bred for aquarium use)</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Difficulty Level:</strong>&nbsp;Easy</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Lighting Requirements:</strong>&nbsp;Medium to High</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">CO2 Requirement:</strong>&nbsp;Low to Medium</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Temperature Range:</strong>&nbsp;68-82°F (20-28°C)</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">pH Range:</strong>&nbsp;6.0-7.5</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Propagation:</strong>&nbsp;Runners, division</li></ul>', NULL),
('bn_BD', 191, 'Echinodorus Big Bear', '<p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">A rare type of Echinodorus sp with green leaves and red marking on leaves.</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Plant Difficulty</strong> : Easy</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Light Requirement</strong> : Low</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Plant Type</strong> : Rosette</p>', NULL),
('bn_BD', 192, 'Echinodorus Joyo Red', '<p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">An attractive hybrid variety with ruby red lanceolate leaves.</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Plant Difficulty</strong> : Easy</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Light Requirement </strong>: Low</p>', NULL),
('bn_BD', 193, 'Echinodorus Marble queen green', '<p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Description:</strong>&nbsp;Echinodorus Cordifolius “Marble Queen Green,” often referred to as the Marble Queen Sword or Radican Marble Queen, is a striking aquatic plant known for its unique variegated leaves and graceful appearance. As a member of the Echinodorus genus within the Alismataceae family, this plant originates from South America. The “Marble Queen Green” variety is characterized by its heart-shaped leaves featuring marbled patterns of green and cream. With its distinctive foliage, it adds a touch of elegance and visual interest to freshwater aquariums, making it a favored choice among aquarists.</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Plant Information:</strong></p><ul><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Scientific Name:</strong>&nbsp;Echinodorus Cordifolius “Marble Queen Green”</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Family:</strong>&nbsp;Alismataceae</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Origin:</strong>&nbsp;South America</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Difficulty Level:</strong>&nbsp;Easy to Moderate</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Lighting Requirements:</strong>&nbsp;Low to Medium</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">CO2 Requirement:</strong>&nbsp;Low</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Temperature Range:</strong>&nbsp;68-82°F (20-28°C)</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">pH Range:</strong>&nbsp;6.0-7.5</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Propagation:</strong>&nbsp;Adventitious plantlets, division</li></ul>', NULL),
('bn_BD', 194, 'Echinodorus Parviflorus Tropica', '<p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Description:</strong>&nbsp;Echinodorus Parviflorus “Tropica,” commonly known as Tropica Sword or Rosette Sword “Tropica,” is a refined aquatic plant appreciated for its delicate appearance and adaptability. As a member of the Echinodorus genus within the Alismataceae family, this plant is native to South America. “Tropica” is distinguished by its compact rosette of slender, elongated leaves, creating a subtle yet captivating presence in freshwater aquariums. With its versatility and graceful charm, it adds a touch of elegance to aquascapes.</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Plant Information:</strong></p><ul><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Scientific Name:</strong>&nbsp;Echinodorus Parviflorus “Tropica”</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Family:</strong>&nbsp;Alismataceae</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Origin:</strong>&nbsp;South America</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Difficulty Level:</strong>&nbsp;Easy</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Lighting Requirements:</strong>&nbsp;Low to Medium</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">CO2 Requirement:</strong>&nbsp;Low</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Temperature Range:</strong>&nbsp;72-82°F (22-28°C)</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">pH Range:</strong>&nbsp;6.0-7.5</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Propagation:</strong>&nbsp;Adventitious plantlets, division</li></ul>', NULL),
('bn_BD', 195, 'Echinodorus Tennelus Broad Leaf Growow Tc Plant', '<p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><em style=\"box-sizing:border-box;\"><i><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;\" data-preserver-spaces=\"true\">Echinodorus&nbsp;</span></i></em><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;\" data-preserver-spaces=\"true\">Tenellus, also known as&nbsp;</span><em style=\"box-sizing:border-box;\"><i><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;\" data-preserver-spaces=\"true\">Helanthium&nbsp;</span></i></em><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;\" data-preserver-spaces=\"true\">Tenellus, is a grassy foreground plant that looks like a cross between Micro Swords and Dwarf Hair Grass. This plant spreads and forms a carpet by sending runners horizontally from its roots.</span></p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;\" data-preserver-spaces=\"true\">Although high light and CO₂ injection are not essential to grow&nbsp;</span><em style=\"box-sizing:border-box;\"><i><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;\" data-preserver-spaces=\"true\">Echinodorus</span></i></em><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;\" data-preserver-spaces=\"true\">&nbsp;Tenellus, they are strongly suggested for faster and more complete growth. To plant, simply cut larger mats into small pieces and place each half into the substrate, an inch or so apart. Trimming will be required regularly once the plant has established itself.&nbsp;</span><em style=\"box-sizing:border-box;\"><i><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;\" data-preserver-spaces=\"true\">Echinodorus</span></i></em><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;\" data-preserver-spaces=\"true\">&nbsp;Tenellus is the common name for this plant.</span></p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;\" data-preserver-spaces=\"true\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Care Tips</strong></span></p><ul><li><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;\" data-preserver-spaces=\"true\">Larger mats should be divided into small sections and planted one inch or so apart midway into the substrate.</span></li><li><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;\" data-preserver-spaces=\"true\">CO₂ is strongly recommended for faster and more complete growth.</span></li></ul>', NULL),
('bn_BD', 196, 'Echinodorus Tennelus Micro Growow Tc Plant', '<p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Description:</strong>&nbsp;Echinodorus Tenellus ‘Micro,’ a delightful variant of the Pygmy Chain Sword, is a petite aquatic plant celebrated for its compact size and delicate appearance. As a member of the Echinodorus genus within the Alismataceae family, this miniature version is a charming addition to freshwater aquariums. Echinodorus Tenellus ‘Micro’ features slender, grass-like leaves that form a dense carpet, making it an excellent choice for aquarists looking to create intricate and visually appealing foregrounds in their aquascapes. With its diminutive size and undemanding care requirements, it brings a touch of elegance to aquarium landscapes.</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Plant Information:</strong></p><ul><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Scientific Name:</strong>&nbsp;Echinodorus Tenellus ‘Micro’</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Family:</strong>&nbsp;Alismataceae</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Origin:</strong>&nbsp;Cultivar (bred for aquarium use)</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Difficulty Level:</strong>&nbsp;Easy</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Lighting Requirements:</strong>&nbsp;Medium to High</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">CO2 Requirement:</strong>&nbsp;Low to Medium</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Temperature Range:</strong>&nbsp;68-82°F (20-28°C)</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">pH Range:</strong>&nbsp;6.0-7.5</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Propagation:</strong>&nbsp;Runners, division</li></ul>', NULL),
('bn_BD', 197, 'Elecharis vivipara Growow Tc Plant', '<p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Description:</strong>&nbsp;Eleocharis vivipara, commonly known as Tall Hairgrass or Giant Hairgrass, is an aquatic plant renowned for its tall and graceful appearance. As a member of the Cyperaceae family, this plant is native to various regions, including North and South America, Europe, and Asia. Characterized by its long, thin blades, Eleocharis vivipara creates an elegant and natural look in aquariums, particularly when planted as background vegetation.</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Plant Information:</strong></p><ul><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Scientific Name:</strong>&nbsp;Eleocharis vivipara</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Family:</strong>&nbsp;Cyperaceae</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Origin:</strong>&nbsp;North America, South America, Europe, Asia</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Difficulty Level:</strong>&nbsp;Moderate</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Lighting Requirements:</strong>&nbsp;Moderate to High</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">CO2 Requirement:</strong>&nbsp;Low to Medium</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Temperature Range:</strong>&nbsp;68-82°F (20-28°C)</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">pH Range:</strong>&nbsp;6.0-7.5</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Propagation:</strong>&nbsp;Runners, division</li></ul>', NULL);
INSERT INTO `ec_products_translations` (`lang_code`, `ec_products_id`, `name`, `description`, `content`) VALUES
('bn_BD', 198, 'Eleocharis accicularis Growow Tc Plant', '<p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><i style=\"box-sizing:border-box;\">Eleocharis&nbsp;</i>Accicularis, commonly known as Hair Grass, Japanese Hair Grass, and a variety of other names. This is a well-known aquarium plant that has been around for a long time!</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><i style=\"box-sizing:border-box;\">Eleocharis&nbsp;</i>acicularis’mini’, grows even slower than&nbsp;<em style=\"box-sizing:border-box;\"><i>Eleocharis</i></em>&nbsp;parvula, was given to Tropica by Thomas Barr of the United States.</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">Typically used as a foreground aquarium plant,&nbsp;<i style=\"box-sizing:border-box;\">Eleocharis&nbsp;</i>Accicularis is similar to its popular counterpart,&nbsp;<i style=\"box-sizing:border-box;\">Eleocharis&nbsp;</i>Parvula, but produces a slight curve giving off the appearance of the compact, low growth that is highly coveted when using any type of aquarium hair grass in a planted aquarium tank.</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">A dense carpet will be obtained in a short period. It requires light to work at its best, but it is one of the safest species for creating a carpet — and requires little upkeep because the leaves stay small (3-5 cm). While CO₂ injection is not essential, it will greatly boost&nbsp;<i style=\"box-sizing:border-box;\">Eleocharis&nbsp;</i>Accicularis growth rate and thickness, resulting in a lush carpet much faster!</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">For best conditions, choose a high-quality aquarium LED lighting unit and nutrient-dense aquarium soil in addition to CO₂ injection. To plant, just split this aquarium plant into small sections and place each portion an inch or so apart halfway into the aquarium substrate.&nbsp;<i style=\"box-sizing:border-box;\">Eleocharis&nbsp;</i>Accicularis will need to be trimmed regularly once it has established itself since it grows swiftly once it sends out runners.&nbsp;<i style=\"box-sizing:border-box;\">Eleocharis&nbsp;</i>Accicularis is less invasive than other species of Hair Grass and is, therefore, easier to contain if a specific location needs this aquatic plant!</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><b style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\"><strong>Care Tips</strong></b></p><ul><li>Trimming is necessary for every carpet plant, and&nbsp;<em style=\"box-sizing:border-box;\"><i>Eleocharis</i></em>&nbsp;acicularis is no exception.</li><li>Provide medium to high light to keep your&nbsp;<em style=\"box-sizing:border-box;\"><i>Eleocharis</i></em>&nbsp;acicularis looking its best.</li></ul>', NULL),
('bn_BD', 199, 'Eleocharis Montevendesis Growow Tc Plant', '<p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Overview</strong>: Eleocharis montevidensis is an amazing green grass stolon aquatic plant suitable for aquariums. It is also popular with names like Giant Hairgrass and Sand Spikerush. Being a low-maintenance plant, it is beginner friendly and is not very demanding. It grows densely, where the height of different straws may grow up to 20- 40 cm; therefore, using it as a background plant is the right choice.</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">Regarding thickness, it is only a few millimeters thick, growing openly. Due to its varied height and flashy green color, it is perfect for creating an attractive aquascape with different depths and hues. Since Eleocharis grows through runners, regular trimming is an essentiality.</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Advantages:</strong>&nbsp;Tissue culture aquarium plants are superior in quality compared to normal plants as they are developed in-vitro conditions. They are devoid of pests and infestations that can harm an already-established tank. Adding the tissue cultures version of Eleocharis montevidensis is safe and risk-free.</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Care:</strong>&nbsp;Eleocharis is a hardy plant, so it will survive unless you have provided it with nutrient-rich water. It will thrive well under the temperature range of 15 to 22 degrees Celsius. Under the right water parameters, this plant will flourish and may grow to a very impressive height, reaching the water’s surface. Since it is a tall grass plant, it is suitable for medium to large aquariums.</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">There is no need to supplement extra carbon dioxide to Eleocharis; however, providing it will hasten its growth, and you may see the grass getting taller than expected in a shorter time.</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Light requirements:</strong>&nbsp;Eleocharis requires moderate light conditions to develop flashy green color leaves.</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">pH requirement:</strong>&nbsp;It can range between 6 and 9.</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Other requirements:</strong>&nbsp;Eleocharis generally do not need any specific requirements as it is undemanding, but including nutrients and basic fertilizers will aid in its growth. Carbon dioxide supplementation will hasten the growth, making the plant attain good height and structure with bright green colors. With proper water conditions, Eleocharis will cover larger areas and provide enough hiding places.</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">Make sure to avoid extreme water parameters.</p>', NULL),
('bn_BD', 200, 'Eleocharis Parvula', '<p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">Forms a lush grassy carpet under very bright light, CO2 and adequate nutrients.</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Plant Difficulty</strong> : Easy</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Light Requirement</strong> : Bright</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Plant Type</strong> : Rhizome</p>', NULL),
('bn_BD', 201, 'Eleocharis parvula Growow Tc Plant', '<p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Description:</strong>&nbsp;Eleocharis parvula, commonly known as Dwarf Hairgrass, is a popular and versatile aquatic plant that is widely recognized for its fine, grass-like appearance and its ability to create lush carpeting in aquariums. This plant belongs to the Cyperaceae family and is native to North America. Its delicate and vibrant green blades make it a favorite among aquascapers and aquarium enthusiasts.</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Plant Information:</strong></p><ul><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Scientific Name:</strong>&nbsp;Eleocharis parvula</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Family:</strong>&nbsp;Cyperaceae</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Origin:</strong>&nbsp;North America</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Difficulty Level:</strong>&nbsp;Easy to Moderate</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Lighting Requirements:</strong>&nbsp;Moderate to High</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">CO2 Requirement:</strong>&nbsp;Low to Medium</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Temperature Range:</strong>&nbsp;68-82°F (20-28°C)</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">pH Range:</strong>&nbsp;6.0-7.5</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Propagation:</strong>&nbsp;Runners</li></ul>', NULL),
('bn_BD', 202, 'Eriocaulon Quinquangulare Growow Tc Plant', '<p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">Eriocaulon quinquangulare is a species of flowering plant in the family Eriocaulaceae. This family is commonly known as the pipewort family. Eriocaulon quinquangulare is commonly referred to as “Five-angled pipewort” or “Five-angled hatpins” due to the distinctive five-angled stems it possesses.</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">This plant species is typically found in wetlands, such as marshes, swamps, and other wet, low-lying areas. It prefers habitats with shallow water or moist soil.</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">Eriocaulon quinquangulare is characterized by its slender, erect stems that have five distinct angles, giving it a unique appearance. The stems can grow up to about 20-40 centimeters in height.</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">The leaves of Eriocaulon quinquangulare are typically basal and grass-like. They are usually linear or narrowly lanceolate in shape.</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">The tiny flowers of this species are typically clustered in dense, spherical heads or inflorescences. The flowers are often white or pale in color.Eriocaulon quinquangulare plays a role in providing habitat and food for various wildlife species. It also helps stabilize wetland soils and contributes to the overall health of these ecosystems.</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Care Tips</strong></p><ul><li>Eriocaulon quinquangulare thrives in consistently moist to wet conditions. Ensure that the plant’s soil remains consistently damp but not waterlogged.</li><li>Provide moderate to bright indirect light. In its natural habitat, this plant often grows in partial shade.</li></ul>', NULL),
('bn_BD', 203, 'Glossostigma Elatinoides Growow Tc Plant', '<p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Description:</strong>&nbsp;Glossostigma elatinoides, commonly known as Glosso, is a popular and versatile aquatic plant sought after for its ability to form dense and vibrant carpets in aquariums. This low-growing plant belongs to the family Phrymaceae and is native to Australia, New Zealand, and parts of Asia. Glosso is characterized by its small, bright green leaves and creeping growth habit, making it a favorite choice for aquascaping enthusiasts.</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Plant Information:</strong></p><ul><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Scientific Name:</strong>&nbsp;Glossostigma elatinoides</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Family:</strong>&nbsp;Phrymaceae</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Origin:</strong>&nbsp;Australia, New Zealand, Asia</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Difficulty Level:</strong>&nbsp;Moderate to Difficult</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Lighting Requirements:</strong>&nbsp;High</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">CO2 Requirement:</strong>&nbsp;High</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Temperature Range:</strong>&nbsp;68-82°F (20-28°C)</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">pH Range:</strong>&nbsp;5.8-7.2</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Propagation:</strong>&nbsp;Runners</li></ul>', NULL),
('bn_BD', 204, 'Glossostigma Elatinoides white Growow Tc Plant', '<p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Overview:</strong>&nbsp;Commonly known as Glosso, Glossostigma elatinoides, from the Phrymaceae family, is a beautiful low creeping green plant species. It is used in planted aquariums to aquascape the foreground. Although the plant is easy to keep, it is highly demanding; therefore, recommended mostly by experts. The use of Glosso in aquariums dates back to the 1980s when it was used majorly for Dutch-type aquascapes to make the foreground beautiful. There are six accepted species of Glosso, among which only Glossostigma elatinoides is used in aquascaping. It is native to Australia, New Zealand, and Tasmania, where it can be found completely or partially submerged in shallow water, bogs, marshes, and river banks. The stature of this plant is fairly small; however, it can easily attain high densities and form extensive mats on the substrate. Therefore, it is also popular as Mud Mat.</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Appearance:</strong>&nbsp;Glosso is one of the smallest aquarium plants that do not grow more than 5 to 6 cm, making it a perfect foreground cover plant. The leaves are typically small (6mm), bright green, and tongue-shaped. While the internodes are around 1 cm, they can reach up to 5 cm under high light intensity and facilitate rapid spreading. Glosso is a fast grower and can put out new leaves while spreading on the aquarium floor. It can form lush green mats when planted in a nutrient-rich substrate and provided with enough light, carbon dioxide, and nutrients.</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Hard/soft plant:</strong>&nbsp;It is a soft plant.</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Ideal water temperature:&nbsp;</strong>The optimal temperature is between 20 to 30 degrees Celsius. However, the plant is hard enough to easily survive in minor fluctuations in temperature. It can survive in both- soft and hard water.</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Lightening conditions:&nbsp;</strong>Glosso loves high light conditions. Intense lightning allows rapid proliferation of the plant and forms a thick mat on the surface. On the contrary, low light triggers upward growth of the shoots. A photoperiod of 8 to 10 hours is ideal for getting optimal growth of this plant.</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Ideal pH level:&nbsp;</strong>While the ideal pH range is between 6.5 to 7.5, Glosso can withstand slight acidic water conditions where the pH is around 5.0</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Propagation:&nbsp;</strong>Glosso propagates rapidly by sending off runners or lateral shoots, which start forming once the plants mature in the aquarium.</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Do you know:&nbsp;</strong>Once you achieve carpet, frequent trimming is essential to maintain a low and compact look. In the lack of regular trimming, the old foliage rots as the new foliage will smother them while growing. Trimming also encourages lateral growth.</p>', NULL),
('bn_BD', 205, 'Gratiola Viscidula Growow Tc Plant', '<div class=\"small-12 medium-8 columns leftpane\" style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><div class=\"row thumbs\" style=\"box-sizing:border-box;\"><div class=\"small-6 medium-3 columns\" style=\"box-sizing:border-box;\">Gratiola viscidula originates from Northern America and is relatively new to the aquatic hobby. The somewhat ‘thorny’ appearance of the submersed form makes it very distinct and easily recognizable.</div></div></div><div class=\"small-12 medium-4 columns rightpane\" style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><div class=\"description\" style=\"box-sizing:border-box;\"><p style=\"box-sizing:border-box;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;\">It is quite easy to grow and prefers good light. By regular trimming it can be kept very low, almost carpeting, but will also present itself well as a fore/mid-ground cushion-plant.</p><p style=\"box-sizing:border-box;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;\">Each stem is approximately 1-2 cm wide and can become 10+ cm tall. The stem willingly branches and spreads giving a very dense appearance to the plant.</p></div></div>', NULL),
('bn_BD', 206, 'H.c. Cuba Growow Tc Plant', '<p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Hemianthus callitrichoides ‘Cuba’: Creating a Miniature Aquatic Landscape</strong></p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Description:</strong>&nbsp;Hemianthus callitrichoides ‘Cuba,’ often referred to as HC Cuba, is a small and delicate aquatic plant known for its vibrant green color and carpeting growth habit. Originating from Cuba, this species belongs to the family Scrophulariaceae. Its miniature size and lush appearance make it a popular choice for aquascaping, especially in creating intricate foregrounds and captivating underwater landscapes.</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Plant Information:</strong></p><ul><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Scientific Name:</strong>&nbsp;Hemianthus callitrichoides ‘Cuba’</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Family:</strong>&nbsp;Scrophulariaceae</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Origin:</strong>&nbsp;Cuba</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Difficulty Level:</strong>&nbsp;Moderate to Difficult</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Lighting Requirements:</strong>&nbsp;High</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">CO2 Requirement:</strong>&nbsp;High</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Temperature Range:</strong>&nbsp;68-82°F (20-28°C)</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">pH Range:</strong>&nbsp;5.5-7.5</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Propagation:</strong>&nbsp;Runners</li></ul>', NULL),
('bn_BD', 207, 'Hellenthium Bollivianum Quadricostus Growow Tc Plant', '<p>Echinodorus ‘Quadricostatus’ from South America has characteristic light-green leaves 10-15 cm long which form a good contrast to the darker aquarium plants. It is most beautiful when planted in groups, each roset becoming 15-20 cm wide. In good conditions it produces runners which spread over the bottom. Very light leaves are a sign of a shortage of micro-nutrients. There is some confusion about the name of this plant, and it has been sold as Echinodorus bolivianus var. magdalenensis.</p><p>Previously known as Echinodorus ‘Quadricostatus’.</p>', NULL),
('bn_BD', 208, 'Hydrocotyle Tripartita Growow Tc Plant', '<p>Hydrocotyle sp.’Japan’ is the popular name of the plant in different plant forums. It is a variant of Hydrocotyle tripartita from South-East Asia. It is characterised by fast, compact growth and small, intense green leaves on vertical stems.<br>The plant is carpet-forming (5-10 cm tall) and its compact growth can be promoted by physically pressing the carpet with your hand when maintaining your aquarium (mechanical retardation). Carpet formation and compact growth do best in good light.</p>', NULL),
('bn_BD', 209, 'Hydrocotyle Tripartita Honda', '<p>Description: Hydrocotyle tripartita “Honda” is a delightful and compact aquatic plant known for its vibrant green leaves and intricate growth pattern. A variant of the popular Hydrocotyle tripartita, “Honda” is often used in aquascaping to create lush foregrounds or to add a touch of greenery to hardscapes. With its low and creeping habit, this plant brings a lively and dynamic element to freshwater aquariums.</p><p>Plant Information:</p><p>Scientific Name: Hydrocotyle tripartita “Honda”<br>Family: Apiaceae<br>Origin: Southeast Asia<br>Difficulty Level: Moderate<br>Lighting Requirements: Moderate to High<br>CO2 Requirement: Medium to High<br>Temperature Range: 68-82°F (20-28°C)<br>pH Range: 6.0-7.5<br>Propagation: Runners, Division</p>', NULL),
('bn_BD', 210, 'AQUATIC VENTUREZ Pipe Holder', '<p class=\"uppercase\" style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">AQUATIC VENTUREZ Pipe Holder</strong></p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">With the Aquatic Venturez Pipe Holder, managing the pipe during water change is very easy. It’s made of high-quality plastic, to be used to stabilize pipe on bucket and tank when cleaning or maintaining the aquarium. The adjustable clamping mechanism of the pipe holder is suitable for pipe of upto 12 mm thickness. The tube is guided over the edge in a gentle arc, which effectively prevents kinking.</p>', NULL),
('bn_BD', 211, 'C3 Power Filter, up to 50 US Gal (190 L)', '<ul><li>Designed for aquariums between 20 and 50 gallons</li><li>Two Mechanical stages trap large and fine debris – foams easily slide out for quick cleaning</li><li>Chemical stage with activated carbon effectively removes toxins</li><li>Biological stage features Bio-Screen pad – blocks debris and provides massive surface area for beneficial bacteria growth</li><li>Biological Trickle Chamber – super charged for fast and efficient nitrification when loaded with Fluval C-Nodes</li><li>Patented refiltration control system permits slower water output to protect delicate fish/plants and increase contact time with media</li><li>Independent filtration stage management – changes can be made at different times while maintaining continuous biological activity</li><li>Cleaning indicator notifies user when polyfoam needs rinsing</li><li>Made in Italy</li><li>For use in freshwater and saltwater aquariums</li></ul>', NULL),
('bn_BD', 212, 'C4 Power Filter, up to 70 US Gal (265 L)', '<ul><li>Designed for aquariums between 40 and 70 gallons</li><li>Two Mechanical stages trap large and fine debris – foams easily slide out for quick cleaning</li><li>Chemical stage with activated carbon effectively removes toxins</li><li>Biological stage features Bio-Screen pad – blocks debris and provides massive surface area for beneficial bacteria growth</li><li>Biological Trickle Chamber – super charged for fast and efficient nitrification when loaded with Fluval C-Nodes</li><li>Patented refiltration control system permits slower water output to protect delicate fish/plants and increase contact time with media</li><li>Independent filtration stage management – changes can be made at different times while maintaining continuous biological activity</li><li>Cleaning indicator notifies user when polyfoam needs rinsing</li><li>Made in Italy</li><li>For use in freshwater and saltwater aquariums</li></ul>', NULL),
('bn_BD', 213, 'FIREGLOW DUO 21W', '<p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">Fireglow DUO 21W :</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">●Super Flexible Stand<br>●Dual Round Panel LED with White and Blue<br>●ABS&nbsp; Body.<br>●Polycarbonate based Transparent Splash Guard.<br>●Support upto 12mm glass thickness</p>', NULL);
