('bn_BD', 328, 'Rotala Bangladesh Growow Tc Plant', '<p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">This is a new variant of Rotala with slender leaves that gives a stiff impression.&nbsp; The leaf color change from green to yellow depending on the growing enviornment.</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">“Bangladesh” is an easy to keep, vigorous Rotala mexicana form. It has larger, less curved leaves than R. mexicana ‘Araguaia’. It shows light green to light red tones and varies much depending on lighting and nutrient supply, so a stand of this stem plant looks quite colourful.</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">As well as other fine-leaved Rotala forms, Rotala mexicana “Bangladesh” prefers good lighting, CO<sub style=\"bottom:-0.25em;box-sizing:border-box;font-size:12px;line-height:0;position:relative;vertical-align:baseline;\">2</sub>&nbsp;and nutrient supply. Its fast growth makes regular trimming necessary.</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">Rotala mexicana “Bangladesh” looks most beautiful as a group in the midground to background of larger tanks</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">&nbsp;</p><figure class=\"image\"><img src=\"https://aqua.teminos.com/storage/image-1.png\"></figure>', NULL),
('bn_BD', 329, 'Rotala Big Bear', '<p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Description:</strong>&nbsp;Rotala sp. ‘Big Bear’ is a distinctive and vibrant aquatic plant that adds a bold touch to freshwater aquariums. Known for its eye-catching reddish-pink hues and unique leaf structure, ‘Big Bear’ stands out as an attractive and attention-grabbing element in aquascapes. This plant’s striking appearance makes it a popular choice among aquarium enthusiasts looking to create visually captivating underwater landscapes.</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Plant Information:</strong></p><ul><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Scientific Name:</strong>&nbsp;Rotala sp. ‘Big Bear’</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Family:</strong>&nbsp;Lythraceae</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Origin:</strong>&nbsp;Cultivated variant, likely from Southeast Asia</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Difficulty Level:</strong>&nbsp;Moderate</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Lighting Requirements:</strong>&nbsp;Medium to High</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">CO2 Requirement:</strong>&nbsp;Medium to High</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Temperature Range:</strong>&nbsp;68-82°F (20-28°C)</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">pH Range:</strong>&nbsp;6.0-7.5</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Propagation:</strong>&nbsp;Cuttings</li></ul>', NULL),
('bn_BD', 330, 'STRESS HEAL 100ml', '<ul><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Contains natural antibacterial compound</strong></li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Removes stress, chlorine in tap water and binds toxic compounds</strong></li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Suitable during transport, acclimatization and water exchange</strong></li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Reduces Ammonia toxicity in water</strong></li></ul>', NULL),
('bn_BD', 331, 'Rotala Big Bear Growow Tc Plant', '<p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Description:</strong>&nbsp;Rotala sp. ‘Big Bear’ is a distinctive and vibrant aquatic plant that adds a bold touch to freshwater aquariums. Known for its eye-catching reddish-pink hues and unique leaf structure, ‘Big Bear’ stands out as an attractive and attention-grabbing element in aquascapes. This plant’s striking appearance makes it a popular choice among aquarium enthusiasts looking to create visually captivating underwater landscapes.</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Plant Information:</strong></p><ul><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Scientific Name:</strong>&nbsp;Rotala sp. ‘Big Bear’</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Family:</strong>&nbsp;Lythraceae</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Origin:</strong>&nbsp;Cultivated variant, likely from Southeast Asia</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Difficulty Level:</strong>&nbsp;Moderate</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Lighting Requirements:</strong>&nbsp;Medium to High</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">CO2 Requirement:</strong>&nbsp;Medium to High</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Temperature Range:</strong>&nbsp;68-82°F (20-28°C)</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">pH Range:</strong>&nbsp;6.0-7.5</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Propagation:</strong>&nbsp;Cuttings</li></ul>', NULL),
('bn_BD', 332, 'Rotala Ceylon', '<p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Description:</strong>&nbsp;Rotala sp. ‘Ceylon’ is an exquisite and graceful aquatic plant that enhances the beauty of freshwater aquariums. Characterized by its slender stems and vibrant green foliage, ‘Ceylon’ adds a touch of elegance to aquascapes. This plant’s delicate appearance, combined with its ease of care, makes it a popular choice for both beginners and experienced aquarists looking to create lush and captivating underwater environments.</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Plant Information:</strong></p><ul><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Scientific Name:</strong>&nbsp;Rotala sp. ‘Ceylon’</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Family:</strong>&nbsp;Lythraceae</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Origin:</strong>&nbsp;Cultivated variant, likely from Southeast Asia</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Difficulty Level:</strong>&nbsp;Easy to Moderate</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Lighting Requirements:</strong>&nbsp;Low to Medium</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">CO2 Requirement:</strong>&nbsp;Low to Medium</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Temperature Range:</strong>&nbsp;68-82°F (20-28°C)</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">pH Range:</strong>&nbsp;6.0-7.5</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Propagation:</strong>&nbsp;Cuttings</li></ul>', NULL),
('bn_BD', 333, 'Rotala Green', '<p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Description:</strong>&nbsp;Rotala Rotundifolia “Green” is a vibrant and versatile aquatic plant that adds a refreshing touch of greenery to freshwater aquariums. Belonging to the family Lythraceae, this species is a variant of the well-known Rotala Rotundifolia. Its round, coin-shaped leaves and rich green coloration make it a popular choice among aquarists seeking a lush and visually appealing aquatic landscape. Originating from Southeast Asia, this plant is valued for its adaptability and ease of care.</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Plant Information:</strong></p><ul><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Scientific Name:</strong>&nbsp;Rotala Rotundifolia “Green”</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Family:</strong>&nbsp;Lythraceae</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Origin:</strong>&nbsp;Southeast Asia</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Difficulty Level:</strong>&nbsp;Easy to Moderate</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Lighting Requirements:</strong>&nbsp;Moderate to High</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">CO2 Requirement:</strong>&nbsp;Low to Medium</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Temperature Range:</strong>&nbsp;68-82°F (20-28°C)</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">pH Range:</strong>&nbsp;6.0-7.5</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Propagation:</strong>&nbsp;Cuttings</li></ul>', NULL),
('bn_BD', 334, 'STRESS HEAL 200ml', '<ul><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Contains natural antibacterial compound</strong></li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Removes stress, chlorine in tap water and binds toxic compounds</strong></li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Suitable during transport, acclimatization and water exchange</strong></li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Reduces Ammonia toxicity in water</strong></li></ul>', NULL),
('bn_BD', 335, 'Rotala Indica', '<p>Description: Rotala Indica, commonly known as Indian Toothcup, is a versatile and popular aquatic plant appreciated for its vibrant colors and feathery foliage. Belonging to the family Lythraceae, this species is native to Southeast Asia and has become a staple in freshwater aquariums. Rotala Indica is characterized by its slender stems, fine leaves, and the ability to display varying hues, ranging from green to shades of pink and orange under optimal conditions.</p><p>Plant Information:</p><p>Scientific Name: Rotala Indica<br>Family: Lythraceae<br>Origin: Southeast Asia<br>Difficulty Level: Easy to Moderate<br>Lighting Requirements: Medium to High<br>CO2 Requirement: Low to Medium<br>Temperature Range: 68-82°F (20-28°C)<br>pH Range: 6.0-7.5<br>Propagation: Cuttings, Side Shoots</p>', NULL),
('bn_BD', 336, 'Suken Garden Flowerhorn Fish Water Conditioner 200Ml + 30Ml Free', '<p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">Enter the world of magnificent Flower-horn cichlids with Sunken Garden Flower-horn Conditioner, meticulously designed to cater to the unique needs of these remarkable fish. This conditioner recreates their natural habitat, ensuring their health, vibrancy, and the stunning beauty that Flower-horns are known for.</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Benefits:</strong></p><ol><li>pH Reducer: Sunken Garden Flower-horn Conditioner expertly lowers and stabilizes pH levels, replicating the slightly acidic and soft water conditions favoured by Flower-horns. Transform your aquarium into an authentic representation of their native environment.</li><li start=\"2\">Chlorine Neutraliser: Instantly neutralises harmful chlorine and chloramines from tap water, safeguarding your Flower-horns from stress and potential health issues. Create a safe and serene aquatic haven for your prized Flower-horns.</li><li start=\"3\">Beneficial Bacteria Booster: Enriched with specialised strains of beneficial bacteria, this conditioner supports a healthy nitrogen cycle in your aquarium. These microorganisms actively reduce ammonia and nitrite levels, promoting a balanced and thriving ecosystem.</li><li start=\"4\">Stress Relief: Sunken Garden&nbsp;Flower-horn Conditioner is thoughtfully formulated to keep your Flower-horns stress-free and content. By reducing stress, it enhances overall well-being and vitality, allowing your Flower-horns to thrive in their natural-inspired environment.</li><li start=\"5\">Hexamita Prevention: Protect your Flower-horns from common aquatic diseases, including Hexamita. Our conditioner creates a protective shield, ensuring a disease-free and secure aquatic environment.</li></ol><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Directions for use:</strong></p><ul><li>Shake well before use.</li><li>Add 1ml for every 5 litres of water.</li><li>Overdosing does not affect aquatic life.</li><li>Store in a cool, dry place.</li></ul><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">&nbsp;</p>', NULL),
('bn_BD', 337, 'Rotala macrandra mini butterfly hi red', '<p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Description:</strong>&nbsp;Rotala Macrandra “Mini Butterfly” is a captivating and diminutive aquatic plant renowned for its striking colors and delicate appearance. Belonging to the Lythraceae family, this variant of Rotala Macrandra originates from Southeast Asia. The “Mini Butterfly” variety is characterized by its petite size, fine leaves, and a remarkable color palette that includes shades of red, pink, and orange under optimal conditions. The intricate and feathery foliage of this plant resembles a butterfly, adding a touch of elegance to freshwater aquariums.</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Plant Information:</strong></p><ul><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Scientific Name:</strong>&nbsp;Rotala Macrandra “Mini Butterfly”</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Family:</strong>&nbsp;Lythraceae</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Origin:</strong>&nbsp;Southeast Asia</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Difficulty Level:</strong>&nbsp;Moderate to Advanced</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Lighting Requirements:</strong>&nbsp;High</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">CO2 Requirement:</strong>&nbsp;Medium to High</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Temperature Range:</strong>&nbsp;72-82°F (22-28°C)</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">pH Range:</strong>&nbsp;5.5-7.0</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Propagation:</strong>&nbsp;Cuttings, Side Shoots</li></ul>', NULL),
('bn_BD', 338, 'Sunken Garden All In One Fancy Guppy Fish Water Conditioner 100Ml', '<p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">Dive into the world of colourful and vibrant guppies with Sunken Garden Guppy Conditioner. Expertly crafted to cater to the unique needs of these lively fish, this conditioner ensures their health, vibrancy, and the captivating beauty that guppy enthusiasts admire.</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">&nbsp;Benefits:</strong></p><ol><li>pH Reducer: Sunken Garden Guppy Conditioner expertly lowers and stabilises pH levels, creating a water environment ideal for guppies. Replicate the slightly acidic and soft water conditions preferred by guppies, reminiscent of their native habitats.</li><li start=\"2\">Chlorine Neutraliser: Instantly neutralises harmful chlorine and chloramines from tap water, safeguarding your guppies from stress and potential health issues. Create a safe and serene aquatic haven for your cherished guppies.</li><li start=\"3\">Beneficial Bacteria Booster: Enriched with specialised strains of beneficial bacteria, this conditioner supports a healthy nitrogen cycle in your aquarium. These microorganisms actively reduce ammonia and nitrite levels, promoting a balanced and thriving ecosystem.</li><li start=\"4\">Stress Relief: Sunken Garden Guppy Conditioner is thoughtfully formulated to keep your guppies stress-free and content. By reducing stress, it enhances overall well-being and vitality, allowing your guppies to thrive in their natural-inspired environment.</li><li start=\"5\">Ich Prevention: Protect your guppies from common aquatic diseases, including ich. Our conditioner creates a protective shield, ensuring a disease-free and secure aquatic environment.</li></ol><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">&nbsp; &nbsp; Directions for use:</strong></p><ul><li>Shake well before use.</li><li>Add 1ml for every 5 litres of water.</li><li>Overdosing does not affect aquatic life.</li><li>Store in a cool, dry place.</li></ul><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">&nbsp;</p>', NULL),
('bn_BD', 339, 'Rotala Macrandra narrow leaf', '<p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Description:</strong>&nbsp;Rotala Macrandra ‘Narrow Leaf’ is a captivating aquatic plant admired for its slender and finely textured leaves, adding a touch of elegance to freshwater aquariums. Belonging to the Lythraceae family, this species is native to Southeast Asia. The ‘Narrow Leaf’ variant is characterized by its delicate and elongated leaves that exhibit varying shades of red and pink under optimal conditions. This plant’s graceful appearance makes it a popular choice among aquarists seeking to introduce a visually striking and refined element to their aquascapes.</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Plant Information:</strong></p><ul><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Scientific Name:</strong>&nbsp;Rotala Macrandra ‘Narrow Leaf’</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Family:</strong>&nbsp;Lythraceae</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Origin:</strong>&nbsp;Southeast Asia</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Difficulty Level:</strong>&nbsp;Moderate to Advanced</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Lighting Requirements:</strong>&nbsp;High</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">CO2 Requirement:</strong>&nbsp;Medium to High</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Temperature Range:</strong>&nbsp;72-82°F (22-28°C)</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">pH Range:</strong>&nbsp;5.5-7.0</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Propagation:</strong>&nbsp;Cuttings, Side Shoots</li></ul>', NULL),
('bn_BD', 340, 'Rotala Nanjenshan', '<p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Description:</strong>&nbsp;Rotala Nanjenshan is an exquisite aquatic plant known for its delicate and intricate appearance, making it a favored choice among aquarists looking to enhance the visual appeal of their freshwater tanks. Belonging to the family Lythraceae, this species originates from the Nanjenshan region in Taiwan. Its fine foliage and vibrant colors add a touch of elegance to aquariums, creating a captivating underwater landscape.</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Plant Information:</strong></p><ul><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Scientific Name:</strong>&nbsp;Rotala Nanjenshan</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Family:</strong>&nbsp;Lythraceae</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Origin:</strong>&nbsp;Taiwan (Nanjenshan region)</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Difficulty Level:</strong>&nbsp;Moderate to Advanced</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Lighting Requirements:</strong>&nbsp;High</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">CO2 Requirement:</strong>&nbsp;Medium to High</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Temperature Range:</strong>&nbsp;72-82°F (22-28°C)</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">pH Range:</strong>&nbsp;5.5-7.0</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Propagation:</strong>&nbsp;Cuttings, Side Shoots</li></ul>', NULL);
INSERT INTO `ec_products_translations` (`lang_code`, `ec_products_id`, `name`, `description`, `content`) VALUES
('bn_BD', 341, 'Sunken Garden All In One Fancy Guppy Fish Water Conditioner 200Ml + 30Ml', '<p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">Dive into the world of colourful and vibrant guppies with Sunken Garden Guppy Conditioner. Expertly crafted to cater to the unique needs of these lively fish, this conditioner ensures their health, vibrancy, and the captivating beauty that guppy enthusiasts admire.</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">&nbsp;Benefits:</strong></p><ol><li>pH Reducer: Sunken Garden Guppy Conditioner expertly lowers and stabilises pH levels, creating a water environment ideal for guppies. Replicate the slightly acidic and soft water conditions preferred by guppies, reminiscent of their native habitats.</li><li start=\"2\">Chlorine Neutraliser: Instantly neutralises harmful chlorine and chloramines from tap water, safeguarding your guppies from stress and potential health issues. Create a safe and serene aquatic haven for your cherished guppies.</li><li start=\"3\">Beneficial Bacteria Booster: Enriched with specialised strains of beneficial bacteria, this conditioner supports a healthy nitrogen cycle in your aquarium. These microorganisms actively reduce ammonia and nitrite levels, promoting a balanced and thriving ecosystem.</li><li start=\"4\">Stress Relief: Sunken Garden Guppy Conditioner is thoughtfully formulated to keep your guppies stress-free and content. By reducing stress, it enhances overall well-being and vitality, allowing your guppies to thrive in their natural-inspired environment.</li><li start=\"5\">Ich Prevention: Protect your guppies from common aquatic diseases, including ich. Our conditioner creates a protective shield, ensuring a disease-free and secure aquatic environment.</li></ol><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">&nbsp; &nbsp; Directions for use:</strong></p><ul><li>Shake well before use.</li><li>Add 1ml for every 5 litres of water.</li><li>Overdosing does not affect aquatic life.</li><li>Store in a cool, dry place.</li></ul><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">&nbsp;</p>', NULL),
('bn_BD', 342, 'Rotala Orange', '<p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Description:</strong>&nbsp;Rotala Rotundifolia ‘Orange’ is a captivating and vibrant aquatic plant that adds a burst of citrus-inspired color to freshwater aquariums. This variant of Rotala Rotundifolia features striking orange hues, making it a sought-after choice among aquarists looking to infuse warmth and vibrancy into their underwater landscapes. With its attractive appearance and moderate care requirements, ‘Orange’ stands out as a beautiful and dynamic addition to planted aquariums.</p><ul><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Scientific Name:</strong>&nbsp;Rotala Rotundifolia ‘Orange’</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Family:</strong>&nbsp;Lythraceae</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Origin:</strong>&nbsp;Cultivated variant, likely from Southeast Asia</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Difficulty Level:</strong>&nbsp;Moderate</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Lighting Requirements:</strong>&nbsp;Medium to High</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">CO2 Requirement:</strong>&nbsp;Low to Medium</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Temperature Range:</strong>&nbsp;68-82°F (20-28°C)</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">pH Range:</strong>&nbsp;6.0-7.5</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Propagation:</strong>&nbsp;Cuttings</li></ul>', NULL),
('bn_BD', 343, 'Sunken Garden Amazon Fish Water Conditioner 200Ml + 30Ml', '<p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">Embark on a journey into the heart of the Amazon with Sunken Garden Amazon Water Conditioner, meticulously crafted to replicate the pristine waters of the tropical rainforest. Tailored to the unique needs of Amazonian fish such as angels and tetras, this conditioner transforms your aquarium into an authentic slice of the Amazon River, ensuring the well-being and vitality of your aquatic companions.</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Benefits:</strong></p><ol><li>pH Reducer: Sunken Garden Amazon Water Conditioner expertly lowers and stabilises pH levels, recreating the slightly acidic, soft water conditions found in the Amazon. Provide your tropical Amazon fish with a habitat that closely resembles their native environment.</li><li start=\"2\">Chlorine Neutraliser: Instantly neutralises harmful chlorine and chloramines from tap water, shielding your Amazonian fish from stress and potential health issues. Ensure a safe and serene aquatic haven.</li><li start=\"3\">Beneficial Bacteria Booster: Enriched with specialised strains of beneficial bacteria, this conditioner supports a healthy nitrogen cycle in your aquarium. These microorganisms actively reduce ammonia and nitrite levels, promoting a balanced and thriving ecosystem.</li><li start=\"4\">Stress Relief: Sunken Garden Amazon Water Conditioner is designed to keep your Amazonian fish stress-free and content. By reducing stress, it enhances overall well-being and vitality, allowing your fish to flourish in their natural-inspired environment.</li><li start=\"5\">Parasite Prevention: Protect your tropical Amazon fish from common aquatic pests, including parasites like ich. Our conditioner creates a protective shield, ensuring a pest-free and secure aquatic environment.</li></ol><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Directions for use:</strong></p><ul><li>Shake well before use.</li><li>Add 1ml for every 5 litres of water.</li><li>Overdosing does not affect aquatic life.</li><li>Store in a cool, dry place.</li></ul>', NULL),
('bn_BD', 344, 'Rotala rotundifolia “hi red”', '<p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Description:</strong>&nbsp;Rotala Rotundifolia ‘Hi Red’ is a captivating and vibrant aquatic plant that adds a fiery touch to freshwater aquariums. Known for its intense red hues, this variant of Rotala Rotundifolia belongs to the Lythraceae family. With its striking appearance and relative ease of care, ‘Hi Red’ has become a sought-after choice among aquarists looking to infuse bold colors into their underwater landscapes.</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Plant Information:</strong></p><ul><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Scientific Name:</strong>&nbsp;Rotala Rotundifolia ‘Hi Red’</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Family:</strong>&nbsp;Lythraceae</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Origin:</strong>&nbsp;Cultivated variant, likely from Southeast Asia</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Difficulty Level:</strong>&nbsp;Moderate</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Lighting Requirements:</strong>&nbsp;Medium to High</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">CO2 Requirement:</strong>&nbsp;Low to Medium</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Temperature Range:</strong>&nbsp;68-82°F (20-28°C)</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">pH Range:</strong>&nbsp;6.0-7.5</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Propagation:</strong>&nbsp;Cuttings</li></ul>', NULL),
('bn_BD', 345, 'Sunken Garden Anti Chlorine 200Ml + 30Ml', '<p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">solution for making aquarium water safe. It effectively removes harmful chlorine, chloramine, and heavy metals. Beyond this, this product is enriched with 15 strains of beneficial bacteria, each selected for their role in establishing and maintaining a healthy, balanced, and thriving ecosystem within your aquarium.</p><p class=\"Body\" style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:19.2px;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;\" lang=\"EN-US\">&nbsp;Benefits:</span></p><p class=\"Body\" style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:19.2px;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;\" lang=\"EN-US\">– Rapidly Removes Harmful Chemicals: Instantly neutralises chlorine and chloramine, making tap water safe for your aquatic life.</span></p><p class=\"Body\" style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:19.2px;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;\" lang=\"EN-US\">– Detoxifies Heavy Metals: Actively binds and neutralises heavy metals that can be toxic to fish and plants.</span></p><p class=\"Body\" style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:19.2px;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;\" lang=\"EN-US\">– Promotes Healthy Ecosystem: Introduces a diverse range of beneficial bacteria to establish and support a balanced aquatic environment.</span></p><p class=\"Body\" style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:19.2px;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;\" lang=\"EN-US\">– Enhances Water Quality: Aids in breaking down organic waste and reducing ammonia levels, ensuring clearer and healthier water.</span></p><p class=\"Body\" style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:19.2px;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;\" lang=\"EN-US\">Directions for Use:</span></p><p class=\"Body\" style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:19.2px;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;\" lang=\"EN-US\">Shake well before use.</span></p><p class=\"Body\" style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:19.2px;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;\" lang=\"EN-US\">Add 1ml of Sunken Garden Anti Chlorine for every 10 liters of aquarium water when setting up a new tank or performing water changes.</span></p><p class=\"Body\" style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:19.2px;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;\" lang=\"EN-US\">Distribute evenly around the aquarium for best results.</span></p><p class=\"Body\" style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:19.2px;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;\" lang=\"EN-US\">Do not overdose.</span></p><p class=\"Body\" style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:19.2px;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;\" lang=\"EN-US\">For aquarium use only.</span></p><ul><li><b style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\"><strong>Best Before : 2 Years from the Mfd Date&nbsp;</strong></b></li></ul>', NULL),
('bn_BD', 346, 'Rotala Rotundifolia Pink', '<p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Description:</strong>&nbsp;Rotala Rotundifolia “Pink” is a captivating and ornamental aquatic plant renowned for its delicate pink hues, which add a touch of elegance to freshwater aquariums. This plant belongs to the Lythraceae family and is a variant of the well-known Rotala Rotundifolia. Originating from Southeast Asia, Rotala Rotundifolia “Pink” is celebrated for its vibrant coloration and graceful appearance, making it a sought-after choice among aquarists aiming to create visually stunning aquatic landscapes.</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Plant Information:</strong></p><ul><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Scientific Name:</strong>&nbsp;Rotala Rotundifolia “Pink”</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Family:</strong>&nbsp;Lythraceae</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Origin:</strong>&nbsp;Southeast Asia</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Difficulty Level:</strong>&nbsp;Moderate</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Lighting Requirements:</strong>&nbsp;Moderate to High</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">CO2 Requirement:</strong>&nbsp;Low to Medium</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Temperature Range:</strong>&nbsp;68-82°F (20-28°C)</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">pH Range:</strong>&nbsp;6.0-7.5</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Propagation:</strong>&nbsp;Cuttings</li></ul>', NULL),
('bn_BD', 347, 'Rotala Sp. Mini Gold', '<p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Description:</strong>&nbsp;Rotala sp. Mini “Gold” is a captivating aquatic plant prized for its unique golden-yellow coloration and intricate, compact growth pattern. Hailing from the Lythraceae family, this miniature Rotala variant is a sought-after choice for aquascaping due to its ability to add a touch of warmth and brilliance to freshwater aquariums. Its delicate foliage and bushy structure make it a standout feature in planted tanks.</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Plant Information:</strong></p><ul><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Scientific Name:</strong>&nbsp;Rotala sp. Mini “Gold”</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Family:</strong>&nbsp;Lythraceae</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Origin:</strong>&nbsp;Cultivated variant, likely from Southeast Asia</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Difficulty Level:</strong>&nbsp;Moderate</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Lighting Requirements:</strong>&nbsp;Medium to High</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">CO2 Requirement:</strong>&nbsp;Medium to High</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Temperature Range:</strong>&nbsp;68-82°F (20-28°C)</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">pH Range:</strong>&nbsp;6.0-7.5</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Propagation:</strong>&nbsp;Cuttings</li></ul>', NULL),
('bn_BD', 348, 'Rotala Spikey', '<p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Description:</strong>&nbsp;Rotala sp. Spikey is an elegant aquatic plant known for its distinct appearance and delicate, feathery foliage. Belonging to the Lythraceae family, this Rotala variant is appreciated by aquarium enthusiasts for its fine, needle-like leaves and its ability to add a graceful touch to freshwater setups. The plant’s unique structure and vibrant green coloration make it a sought-after choice for aquascaping, providing an eye-catching element in planted tanks.</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Plant Information:</strong></p><ul><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Scientific Name:</strong>&nbsp;Rotala sp. Spikey</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Family:</strong>&nbsp;Lythraceae</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Origin:</strong>&nbsp;Cultivated variant, likely from Southeast Asia</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Difficulty Level:</strong>&nbsp;Moderate</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Lighting Requirements:</strong>&nbsp;Medium to High</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">CO2 Requirement:</strong>&nbsp;Medium to High</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Temperature Range:</strong>&nbsp;68-82°F (20-28°C)</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">pH Range:</strong>&nbsp;6.0-7.5</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Propagation:</strong>&nbsp;Cuttings</li></ul>', NULL),
('bn_BD', 349, 'Rotala Twilight', '<p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Description:</strong>&nbsp;Rotala Rotundifolia ‘Twilight’ is a captivating aquatic plant known for its unique coloration that transitions from vibrant green to shades of pink and orange. This stunning gradient effect adds a touch of serenity and elegance to freshwater aquariums, making it a popular choice among aquascaping enthusiasts. ‘Twilight’ combines beauty with ease of care, making it suitable for both beginners and experienced aquarists looking to create a visually striking underwater landscape.</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Plant Information:</strong></p><ul><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Scientific Name:</strong>&nbsp;Rotala Rotundifolia ‘Twilight’</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Family:</strong>&nbsp;Lythraceae</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Origin:</strong>&nbsp;Cultivated variant, likely from Southeast Asia</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Difficulty Level:</strong>&nbsp;Easy to Moderate</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Lighting Requirements:</strong>&nbsp;Low to Medium</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">CO2 Requirement:</strong>&nbsp;Low to Medium</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Temperature Range:</strong>&nbsp;68-82°F (20-28°C)</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">pH Range:</strong>&nbsp;6.0-7.5</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Propagation:</strong>&nbsp;Cuttings</li></ul>', NULL),
('bn_BD', 350, 'Rotala Wallichi Red', '<p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">aquatic plant known for its delicate appearance and vibrant coloration. This species belongs to the Lythraceae family and is native to Southeast Asia. With its fine, feathery leaves arranged in whorls along the stem, Rotala Wallichii adds a touch of elegance to freshwater aquariums. The plant’s hues can range from green to pinkish-red, depending on the tank conditions.</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Plant Information:</strong></p><ul><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Scientific Name:</strong>&nbsp;Rotala Wallichii</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Family:</strong>&nbsp;Lythraceae</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Origin:</strong>&nbsp;Southeast Asia</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Difficulty Level:</strong>&nbsp;Moderate to High</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Lighting Requirements:</strong>&nbsp;High</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">CO2 Requirement:</strong>&nbsp;High</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Temperature Range:</strong>&nbsp;72-82°F (22-28°C)</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">pH Range:</strong>&nbsp;5.5-7.5</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Propagation:</strong>&nbsp;Cuttings</li></ul>', NULL),
('bn_BD', 351, 'Sturogyne Porto Velho', '<p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Description:</strong>&nbsp;Staurogyne sp. Porto Velho is an aquatic plant renowned for its vibrant and distinctive foliage, making it a sought-after choice for aquascaping enthusiasts. Belonging to the Acanthaceae family, this species adds a touch of elegance to freshwater aquariums with its unique leaf structure and eye-catching coloration. Originating from the freshwater habitats of Porto Velho in Brazil, this plant has gained popularity for its ornamental qualities and suitability for planted tank setups.</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Plant Information:</strong></p><ul><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Scientific Name:</strong>&nbsp;Staurogyne sp. Porto Velho</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Common Name:</strong>&nbsp;Porto Velho Staurogyne</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Origin:</strong>&nbsp;Freshwater habitats of Porto Velho, Brazil</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Difficulty Level:</strong>&nbsp;Moderate</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Lighting Requirements:</strong>&nbsp;Moderate to High</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">CO2 Requirement:</strong>&nbsp;Moderate</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Temperature Range:</strong>&nbsp;68-82°F (20-28°C)</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">pH Range:</strong>&nbsp;6.0-7.5</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Propagation:</strong>&nbsp;Cuttings, side shoots</li></ul>', NULL),
('bn_BD', 352, 'Tonina belem', '<p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Description:</strong>&nbsp;Tonina sp. Belem, a diminutive yet captivating aquatic plant, is celebrated for its delicate appearance and vibrant green coloration. Hailing from the Eriocaulaceae family, this species is cherished by aquascapers for its intricate structure and ability to add finesse to the foreground of freshwater aquariums. Despite its small size, Tonina sp. Belem commands attention with its graceful presence.</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Plant Information:</strong></p><ul><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Scientific Name:</strong>&nbsp;Tonina sp. Belem</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Common Name:</strong>&nbsp;Belem Tonina</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Origin:</strong>&nbsp;South America</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Difficulty Level:</strong>&nbsp;Advanced</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Lighting Requirements:</strong>&nbsp;High</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">CO2 Requirement:</strong>&nbsp;High</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Temperature Range:</strong>&nbsp;72-82°F (22-28°C)</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">pH Range:</strong>&nbsp;6.0-7.5</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Propagation:</strong>&nbsp;Cuttings</li></ul>', NULL),
('bn_BD', 353, 'Wrinkled', '<p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Description:</strong>&nbsp;Microsorum Pteropus “Wrinkled Leaf,” also known as Wrinkled Leaf Java Fern, is a distinctive variant of the classic Java Fern celebrated for its textured and crinkled foliage. Belonging to the Polypodiaceae family, this fern originates from Southeast Asia and has gained popularity among aquarists for its unique leaf structure. The leaves, characterized by their wrinkled appearance, add a touch of individuality and aquatic elegance to aquarium landscapes.</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Plant Information:</strong></p><ul><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Scientific Name:</strong>&nbsp;Microsorum Pteropus “Wrinkled Leaf”</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Family:</strong>&nbsp;Polypodiaceae</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Origin:</strong>&nbsp;Southeast Asia</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Difficulty Level:</strong>&nbsp;Easy</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Lighting Requirements:</strong>&nbsp;Low to Medium</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">CO2 Requirement:</strong>&nbsp;Low</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Temperature Range:</strong>&nbsp;68-82°F (20-28°C)</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">pH Range:</strong>&nbsp;6.0-7.5</li><li><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Propagation:</strong>&nbsp;Rhizome Division, Adventitious Plantlets</li></ul>', NULL);
INSERT INTO `ec_products_translations` (`lang_code`, `ec_products_id`, `name`, `description`, `content`) VALUES
('bn_BD', 354, 'Sunken Garden Anti Chlorine 200Ml + 30Ml', '<p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">solution for making aquarium water safe. It effectively removes harmful chlorine, chloramine, and heavy metals. Beyond this, this product is enriched with 15 strains of beneficial bacteria, each selected for their role in establishing and maintaining a healthy, balanced, and thriving ecosystem within your aquarium.</p><p class=\"Body\" style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:19.2px;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;\" lang=\"EN-US\">&nbsp;Benefits:</span></p><p class=\"Body\" style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:19.2px;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;\" lang=\"EN-US\">– Rapidly Removes Harmful Chemicals: Instantly neutralises chlorine and chloramine, making tap water safe for your aquatic life.</span></p><p class=\"Body\" style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:19.2px;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;\" lang=\"EN-US\">– Detoxifies Heavy Metals: Actively binds and neutralises heavy metals that can be toxic to fish and plants.</span></p><p class=\"Body\" style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:19.2px;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;\" lang=\"EN-US\">– Promotes Healthy Ecosystem: Introduces a diverse range of beneficial bacteria to establish and support a balanced aquatic environment.</span></p><p class=\"Body\" style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:19.2px;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;\" lang=\"EN-US\">– Enhances Water Quality: Aids in breaking down organic waste and reducing ammonia levels, ensuring clearer and healthier water.</span></p><p class=\"Body\" style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:19.2px;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;\" lang=\"EN-US\">Directions for Use:</span></p><p class=\"Body\" style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:19.2px;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;\" lang=\"EN-US\">Shake well before use.</span></p><p class=\"Body\" style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:19.2px;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;\" lang=\"EN-US\">Add 1ml of Sunken Garden Anti Chlorine for every 10 liters of aquarium water when setting up a new tank or performing water changes.</span></p><p class=\"Body\" style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:19.2px;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;\" lang=\"EN-US\">Distribute evenly around the aquarium for best results.</span></p><p class=\"Body\" style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:19.2px;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;\" lang=\"EN-US\">Do not overdose.</span></p><p class=\"Body\" style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:19.2px;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;\" lang=\"EN-US\">For aquarium use only.</span></p><ul><li><b style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\"><strong>Best Before : 2 Years from the Mfd Date&nbsp;</strong></b></li></ul>', NULL),
('bn_BD', 355, 'Sunken Garden Arowana Fish Water Conditioner 100Ml', '<p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">Delve into the world of majestic Arowana fish with Sunken Garden Arowana Conditioner, meticulously crafted to cater to the unique needs of these regal aquatic giants. This conditioner recreates their natural habitat, ensuring their health, vibrancy, and the impressive beauty that Arowana’s are known for.</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Benefits:</strong></p><ol><li>pH Reducer: Sunken Garden Arowana Conditioner expertly lowers and stabilises pH levels, replicating the slightly acidic and soft water conditions favoured by Arowanas. Transform your aquarium into an authentic representation of their native environment.</li><li start=\"2\">Chlorine Neutraliser: Instantly neutralises harmful chlorine and chloramines from tap water, safeguarding your Arowanas from stress and potential health issues. Create a safe and serene aquatic haven for your majestic Arowanas.</li><li start=\"3\">Beneficial Bacteria Booster: Enriched with specialised strains of beneficial bacteria, this conditioner supports a healthy nitrogen cycle in your aquarium. These microorganisms actively reduce ammonia and nitrite levels, promoting a balanced and thriving ecosystem.</li><li start=\"4\">Stress Relief: Sunken Garden Arowana Conditioner is thoughtfully formulated to keep your Arowanas stress-free and content. By reducing stress, it enhances overall well-being and vitality, allowing your Arowanas to thrive in their natural-inspired environment.</li><li start=\"5\">Bloat Prevention: Protect your Arowanas from common digestive issues, such as bloat. Our conditioner creates a protective shield, ensuring a healthy and secure aquatic environment.</li></ol><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">Elevate your Arowana’s aquatic experience with Sunken Garden Arowana Conditioner – where science&nbsp; &nbsp; blends harmoniously with nature, dedicated to replicating the perfect habitat for these magnificent&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; fish. Your Arowanas deserve nothing but the best. Immerse yourself in a world of vibrant, thriving aquatic life today!</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Directions for use:</strong></p><ul><li>Shake well before use.</li><li>Add 1ml for every 5 litres of water.</li><li>Overdosing does not affect aquatic life.</li><li>Store in a cool, dry place</li></ul>', NULL),
('bn_BD', 356, 'Sunken Garden Arowana Fish Water Conditioner 200Ml + 30Ml Free', '<p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">Delve into the world of majestic Arowana fish with Sunken Garden Arowana Conditioner, meticulously crafted to cater to the unique needs of these regal aquatic giants. This conditioner recreates their natural habitat, ensuring their health, vibrancy, and the impressive beauty that Arowana’s are known for.</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Benefits:</strong></p><ol><li>pH Reducer: Sunken Garden Arowana Conditioner expertly lowers and stabilises pH levels, replicating the slightly acidic and soft water conditions favoured by Arowanas. Transform your aquarium into an authentic representation of their native environment.</li><li start=\"2\">Chlorine Neutraliser: Instantly neutralises harmful chlorine and chloramines from tap water, safeguarding your Arowanas from stress and potential health issues. Create a safe and serene aquatic haven for your majestic Arowanas.</li><li start=\"3\">Beneficial Bacteria Booster: Enriched with specialised strains of beneficial bacteria, this conditioner supports a healthy nitrogen cycle in your aquarium. These microorganisms actively reduce ammonia and nitrite levels, promoting a balanced and thriving ecosystem.</li><li start=\"4\">Stress Relief: Sunken Garden Arowana Conditioner is thoughtfully formulated to keep your Arowanas stress-free and content. By reducing stress, it enhances overall well-being and vitality, allowing your Arowanas to thrive in their natural-inspired environment.</li><li start=\"5\">Bloat Prevention: Protect your Arowanas from common digestive issues, such as bloat. Our conditioner creates a protective shield, ensuring a healthy and secure aquatic environment.</li></ol><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">Elevate your Arowana’s aquatic experience with Sunken Garden Arowana Conditioner – where science&nbsp; &nbsp; blends harmoniously with nature, dedicated to replicating the perfect habitat for these magnificent&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; fish. Your Arowanas deserve nothing but the best. Immerse yourself in a world of vibrant, thriving aquatic life today!</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">&nbsp; &nbsp; Directions for use:</strong></p><ul><li>Shake well before use.</li><li>Add 1ml for every 5 litres of water.</li><li>Overdosing does not affect aquatic life.</li><li>Store in a cool, dry place.</li></ul>', NULL),
('bn_BD', 357, 'Sunken Garden Cichlid Fish Water Conditioner 100Ml', '<p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">Embark on a journey to create the perfect aquatic home for your vibrant cichlid community with Sunken Garden Cichlid Conditioner. Meticulously designed to meet the specific needs of cichlids, this conditioner replicates their natural habitat, ensuring their health, vitality, and the stunning beauty that these fish are known for.</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">&nbsp;Benefits:</strong></p><ol><li>pH Reducer: Sunken Garden Cichlid Conditioner adeptly lowers and stabilises pH levels, recreating the slightly acidic and hard water conditions favoured by cichlids. Transform your aquarium into an authentic representation of their native environment.<ol><li start=\"2\">Chlorine Neutraliser: Instantly neutralises harmful chlorine and chloramines from tap water, safeguarding your cichlids from stress and potential health issues. Create a safe and serene aquatic haven for your prized cichlid community.</li><li start=\"3\">Beneficial Bacteria Booster: Enriched with specialised strains of beneficial bacteria, this conditioner supports a healthy nitrogen cycle in your aquarium. These microorganisms actively reduce ammonia and nitrite levels, promoting a balanced and thriving ecosystem.<ol><li start=\"3\">Stress Relief: Sunken Garden Cichlid Conditioner is thoughtfully formulated to keep your cichlids stress-free and content. By reducing stress, it enhances overall well-being and vitality, allowing your cichlids to thrive in their natural-inspired environment.</li><li start=\"3\">Disease Prevention: Protect your cichlid community from common aquatic diseases, including Tuberculosis (TB) and gill flukes. Our conditioner creates a protective shield, ensuring a disease-free and secure aquatic environment.<strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">&nbsp; Directions for use:</strong><ul><li start=\"3\">Shake well before use.</li><li start=\"3\">Add 1ml for every 5 litres of water.</li><li start=\"3\">Overdosing does not affect aquatic life.</li><li start=\"3\">Consume within 120 days of opening the bottle.</li><li start=\"3\">Store in a cool, dry place.</li></ul></li></ol></li></ol></li></ol>', NULL),
('bn_BD', 358, 'Sunken Garden Cichlid Fish Water Conditioner 200Ml +30Ml Free', '<p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">Embark on a journey to create the perfect aquatic home for your vibrant cichlid community with Sunken Garden Cichlid Conditioner. Meticulously designed to meet the specific needs of cichlids, this conditioner replicates their natural habitat, ensuring their health, vitality, and the stunning beauty that these fish are known for.</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">&nbsp;Benefits:</strong></p><ol><li>pH Reducer: Sunken Garden Cichlid Conditioner adeptly lowers and stabilises pH levels, recreating the slightly acidic and hard water conditions favoured by cichlids. Transform your aquarium into an authentic representation of their native environment.</li><li start=\"2\">Chlorine Neutraliser: Instantly neutralises harmful chlorine and chloramines from tap water, safeguarding your cichlids from stress and potential health issues. Create a safe and serene aquatic haven for your prized cichlid community.</li><li start=\"3\">Beneficial Bacteria Booster: Enriched with specialised strains of beneficial bacteria, this conditioner supports a healthy nitrogen cycle in your aquarium. These microorganisms actively reduce ammonia and nitrite levels, promoting a balanced and thriving ecosystem.</li><li start=\"4\">Stress Relief: Sunken Garden Cichlid Conditioner is thoughtfully formulated to keep your cichlids stress-free and content. By reducing stress, it enhances overall well-being and vitality, allowing your cichlids to thrive in their natural-inspired environment.</li><li start=\"5\">Disease Prevention: Protect your cichlid community from common aquatic diseases, including Tuberculosis (TB) and gill flukes. Our conditioner creates a protective shield, ensuring a disease-free and secure aquatic environment.</li></ol><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Directions for use:</strong></p><ul><li>Shake well before use.</li><li>Add 1ml for every 5 litres of water.</li><li>Overdosing does not affect aquatic life.</li><li>Consume within 120 days of opening the bottle.</li><li>Store in a cool, dry place.</li></ul>', NULL),
('bn_BD', 359, 'Sunken Garden CO2 Booster 100ml', '<p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">Elevate your aquatic plant growth with Sunken Garden Liquid CO2. Designed as a rich source of bioavailable organic carbon, this innovative formula provides the essential fuel that all plants crave. While carbon dioxide (CO2) is traditionally obtained from the atmosphere, our solution offers an alternative by delivering organic carbon derived from simple compounds.</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">Fueling photosynthesis, Sunken Garden Liquid CO2 ensures robust plant development, vibrant colors, and lush greenery. It’s a game-changer for aquatic plant enthusiasts seeking to create a thriving underwater garden.</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">Sunken Garden Liquid CO2 is designed to posses iron-reducing properties, promoting the ferrous state of iron (Fe) over ferric iron (Fe). By doing so, it maximizes iron utilization by plants, further enhancing their growth and vitality.</p>', NULL),
('bn_BD', 360, 'Sunken Garden CO2 Booster 200ml+30ml free', '<p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">Elevate your aquatic plant growth with Sunken Garden Liquid CO2. Designed as a rich source of bioavailable organic carbon, this innovative formula provides the essential fuel that all plants crave. While carbon dioxide (CO2) is traditionally obtained from the atmosphere, our solution offers an alternative by delivering organic carbon derived from simple compounds.</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">Fueling photosynthesis, Sunken Garden Liquid CO2 ensures robust plant development, vibrant colors, and lush greenery. It’s a game-changer for aquatic plant enthusiasts seeking to create a thriving underwater garden.</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">Sunken Garden Liquid CO2 is designed to posses iron-reducing properties, promoting the ferrous state of iron (Fe) over ferric iron (Fe). By doing so, it maximizes iron utilization by plants, further enhancing their growth and vitality.</p>', NULL),
('bn_BD', 361, 'Sunken Garden Discus Fish Water Conditioner 100Ml', '<p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">Dive into the world of captivating discus fish with Sunken Garden Discus Conditioner, meticulously crafted to cater to the unique needs of these mesmerising aquatic treasures. Discus enthusiasts, prepare to unlock the secrets of thriving discus keeping with a conditioner designed to replicate their natural habitat and ensure their health and vitality.</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Benefits:</strong></p><ol><li>pH Reducer: Sunken Garden Discus Conditioner skilfully lowers and stabilises pH levels, recreating the slightly acidic, soft water conditions favoured by discus fish. Transform your aquarium into a haven that closely resembles their native Amazonian environment.</li><li start=\"2\">Chlorine Neutraliser: Instantly neutralises harmful chlorine and chloramines from tap water, shielding your discus fish from stress and potential health issues. Create a safe and serene aquatic haven for your prized discus.</li><li start=\"3\">Beneficial Bacteria Booster: Enriched with specialised strains of beneficial bacteria, this conditioner supports a healthy nitrogen cycle in your aquarium. These microorganisms actively reduce ammonia and nitrite levels, promoting a balanced and thriving ecosystem.</li><li start=\"4\">Stress Relief: Sunken Garden Discus Conditioner is thoughtfully formulated to keep your discus fish stress-free and content. By reducing stress, it enhances overall well-being and vitality, allowing your discus to thrive in their natural-inspired environment.</li><li start=\"5\">Fluke Prevention: Protect your discus fish from common aquatic pests, including flukes. Our conditioner creates a protective shield, ensuring a pest-free and secure aquatic environment.</li></ol><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Directions for use:</strong></p><ul><li>Shake well before use.</li><li>Add 1ml for every 5 litres of water.</li><li>Overdosing does not affect aquatic life.</li><li>Store in a cool, dry place.</li></ul>', NULL),
('bn_BD', 362, 'Sunken Garden Discus Fish Water Conditioner 200Ml +30Ml', '<p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">Dive into the world of captivating discus fish with Sunken Garden Discus Conditioner, meticulously crafted to cater to the unique needs of these mesmerising aquatic treasures. Discus enthusiasts, prepare to unlock the secrets of thriving discus keeping with a conditioner designed to replicate their natural habitat and ensure their health and vitality.</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Benefits:</strong></p><ol><li>pH Reducer: Sunken Garden Discus Conditioner skilfully lowers and stabilises pH levels, recreating the slightly acidic, soft water conditions favoured by discus fish. Transform your aquarium into a haven that closely resembles their native Amazonian environment.</li><li start=\"2\">Chlorine Neutraliser: Instantly neutralises harmful chlorine and chloramines from tap water, shielding your discus fish from stress and potential health issues. Create a safe and serene aquatic haven for your prized discus.</li><li start=\"3\">Beneficial Bacteria Booster: Enriched with specialised strains of beneficial bacteria, this conditioner supports a healthy nitrogen cycle in your aquarium. These microorganisms actively reduce ammonia and nitrite levels, promoting a balanced and thriving ecosystem.</li><li start=\"4\">Stress Relief: Sunken Garden Discus Conditioner is thoughtfully formulated to keep your discus fish stress-free and content. By reducing stress, it enhances overall well-being and vitality, allowing your discus to thrive in their natural-inspired environment.</li><li start=\"5\">Fluke Prevention: Protect your discus fish from common aquatic pests, including flukes. Our conditioner creates a protective shield, ensuring a pest-free and secure aquatic environment.</li></ol><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Directions for use:</strong></p><ul><li>Shake well before use.</li><li>Add 1ml for every 5 litres of water.</li><li>Overdosing does not affect aquatic life.</li><li>Store in a cool, dry place.</li></ul>', NULL),
('bn_BD', 363, 'Sunken Garden Flowerhorn Fish Water Conditioner 100Ml', '<p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">Enter the world of magnificent Flower-horn cichlids with Sunken Garden Flower-horn Conditioner, meticulously designed to cater to the unique needs of these remarkable fish. This conditioner recreates their natural habitat, ensuring their health, vibrancy, and the stunning beauty that Flower-horns are known for.</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Benefits:</strong></p><ol><li>pH Reducer: Sunken Garden Flower-horn Conditioner expertly lowers and stabilizes pH levels, replicating the slightly acidic and soft water conditions favoured by Flower-horns. Transform your aquarium into an authentic representation of their native environment.</li><li start=\"2\">Chlorine Neutraliser: Instantly neutralises harmful chlorine and chloramines from tap water, safeguarding your Flower-horns from stress and potential health issues. Create a safe and serene aquatic haven for your prized Flower-horns.</li><li start=\"3\">Beneficial Bacteria Booster: Enriched with specialised strains of beneficial bacteria, this conditioner supports a healthy nitrogen cycle in your aquarium. These microorganisms actively reduce ammonia and nitrite levels, promoting a balanced and thriving ecosystem.</li><li start=\"4\">Stress Relief: Sunken Garden Flower-horn Conditioner is thoughtfully formulated to keep your Flower-horns stress-free and content. By reducing stress, it enhances overall well-being and vitality, allowing your Flower-horns to thrive in their natural-inspired environment.</li><li start=\"5\">Hexamita Prevention: Protect your Flower-horns from common aquatic diseases, including Hexamita. Our conditioner creates a protective shield, ensuring a disease-free and secure aquatic environment.</li></ol><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Directions for use:</strong></p><ul><li>Shake well before use.</li><li>Add 1ml for every 5 litres of water.</li><li>Overdosing does not affect aquatic life.</li><li>Store in a cool, dry place.</li></ul>', NULL),
('bn_BD', 364, 'Sunken Garden Goldfish Water Conditioner 200Ml + 30Ml Free', '<p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">Transform your aquarium into a vibrant aquatic paradise with Sunken Garden Goldfish Conditioner. Specially formulated to cater to the unique needs of your goldfish, this conditioner is your gateway to a thriving and harmonious underwater world. Enhance the well-being of your goldfish while replicating their natural habitat with ease.</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Benefits:</strong></p><ol><li>pH Balancer: Sunken Garden Goldfish Conditioner elevates and stabilises pH levels, creating an environment that closely mimics the best conditions for your goldfish. This ensures optimal health and comfort for your aquatic companions.</li><li start=\"2\">Chlorine Neutraliser : Instantly neutralises harmful chlorine and chloramines from tap water, safeguarding your goldfish from stress and potential health issues. Say goodbye to water worries and hello to a tranquil aquarium.</li><li start=\"3\">Beneficial Bacteria Booster: Enriched with specialised strains of beneficial bacteria, this conditioner supports a healthy nitrogen cycle in your aquarium. These microbes actively reduce ammonia and nitrite levels, promoting a pristine and balanced ecosystem.</li><li start=\"4\">Stress Relief: Sunken Garden Goldfish Conditioner is expertly designed to keep your goldfish calm and content. By reducing stress, it enhances overall well-being and vitality, allowing your goldfish to thrive in their aquatic haven.</li><li start=\"5\">Parasite Prevention: Guard your goldfish against common aquatic pests such as lice and anchor worms. Our conditioner forms a protective barrier, ensuring a pest-free and secure environment.</li></ol><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Directions for use:</strong></p><ul><li>Shake well before use.</li><li>Add 1ml for every 5 litres of water.</li><li>Overdosing does not affect aquatic life.</li><li>Store in a cool, dry place.</li></ul>', NULL),
('bn_BD', 365, 'Sunken Garden Good Bacteria 200ML+30ML', '<p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">Sunken Garden Good Bacteria 100 ML” appears to be a product designed to introduce beneficial bacteria into an aquatic environment. These bacteria play a crucial role in maintaining a healthy ecosystem within aquariums, ponds, or other aquatic environments.</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">Beneficial bacteria help in breaking down organic waste, such as uneaten fish food, fish waste, and decaying plant matter, into less harmful substances like ammonia and nitrite, which can then be processed further by the aquarium’s filtration system. This helps in keeping the water quality stable and reducing the risk of harmful spikes in ammonia or nitrite levels, which can be harmful to aquatic life.</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Directions for use:</strong></p><ul><li>Add daily after every water change.</li><li>Shake well before use.</li><li>Add 1ml for every 10 litres of water.</li><li>Overdosing does not affect aquatic life.</li><li>Store in a cool, dry place.</li></ul>', NULL);
INSERT INTO `ec_products_translations` (`lang_code`, `ec_products_id`, `name`, `description`, `content`) VALUES
('bn_BD', 366, 'Sunken Garden Koi Fish Water Conditioner 100Ml', '<p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">Description:</strong></p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">Step into the world of serene koi ponds and elevate your Koi’s aquatic experience with Sunken Garden Koi Conditioner. This meticulously crafted conditioner is designed to cater to the unique needs of Koi fish, ensuring their health, vibrancy, and the tranquil beauty that Koi enthusiasts cherish.</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Benefits:</strong></p><ol><li>pH Reducer: Sunken Garden Koi Conditioner expertly lowers and stabilises pH levels, creating a water environment that is ideal for Koi. Replicate the slightly acidic and soft water conditions preferred by Koi, reminiscent of their native habitats.</li><li start=\"2\">Chlorine Neutraliser: Instantly neutralises harmful chlorine and chloramines from tap water, shielding your Koi from stress and potential health issues. Create a safe and serene aquatic haven for your treasured Koi.</li><li start=\"3\">Beneficial Bacteria Booster: Enriched with specialised strains of beneficial bacteria, this conditioner supports a healthy nitrogen cycle in your pond. These microorganisms actively reduce ammonia and nitrite levels, promoting a balanced and thriving ecosystem.</li><li start=\"4\">Stress Relief: Sunken Garden Koi Conditioner is thoughtfully formulated to keep your Koi stress-free and content. By reducing stress, it enhances overall well-being and vitality, allowing your Koi to thrive in their natural-inspired environment.</li><li start=\"5\">Bloat Prevention: Protect your Koi from common digestive issues, such as bloat. Our conditioner creates a protective shield, ensuring a healthy and secure aquatic environment.</li></ol><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">&nbsp;</strong></p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(105, 105, 105);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin-block:0px 0.9rem;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-weight:bolder;\">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Directions for use:</strong></p><ul><li>Shake well before use.</li><li>Add 1ml for every 5 litres of water.</li><li>Overdosing does not affect aquatic life.</li><li>Store in a cool, dry place.</li></ul>', NULL),
